sha":"a625200568c96ee75768533ae5feb3a1167297c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/a625200568c96ee75768533ae5feb3a1167297c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1927579?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zkochan","id":1927579,"login":"zkochan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjc1Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zkochan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/06eab7eae3cf1d389fdf41bc7ddc6ff7fdb51bed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:54:10Z","email":"z@kochan.io","name":"Zoltan Kochan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:54:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: update pnpm (#10767)\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n- Bump `@pnpm/napi` from 12.9.0 to 12.10.0. The lockfile changes only\nthe `@pnpm/napi` entries and its platform packages. It was regenerated\nwith `bit install`.\n- 12.10.0 includes pnpm/pnpm#16631. When `maxSockets` caps the\nconnections to a registry, package metadata requests now go ahead of\nqueued tarball downloads to the same registry. Before, they waited\nbehind every download queued earlier. Bit always passes `maxSockets:\n15`, so its capsule installs hit this. It showed up as hundreds of\n`Request took 10xxxms` warnings in Ripple CI `bit sign` jobs.\n- I measured it locally on internal case (a fresh capsule resolving\n5,554 packages), with the warning threshold lowered to 1s. All three\nruns were back to back:\n\n  | `@pnpm/napi` | metadata requests > 1s | mean | ≥ 10s |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 12.10.0 without the fix (local build) | 3,822 | 8.5s | 1,254 |\n  | 12.10.0 with the fix (local build) | 2,597 | 6.2s | 585 |\n  | 12.10.0 (published) | 2,659 | 7.7s | 817 |\n\nResults vary a lot from run to run, so read these as a direction rather\nthan exact numbers. Some slow requests remain, because the engine''s\nglobal connection pool still reserves half its slots for downloads.\n\n---\nWritten by an agent (Claude Code, claude-opus-5-5).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35851594f3c3b3155a8a6a57c5dcc76747cd8fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/35851594f3c3b3155a8a6a57c5dcc76747cd8fd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/06eab7eae3cf1d389fdf41bc7ddc6ff7fdb51bed","verification":{"payload":"tree 35851594f3c3b3155a8a6a57c5dcc76747cd8fd5\nparent 2500fd984435c82993182e33010e1e187ea6cf4c\nauthor Zoltan Kochan <z@kochan.io> 1791276850 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791276850 +0200\n\nfix: update pnpm (#10767)\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n- Bump `@pnpm/napi` from 12.9.0 to 12.10.0. The lockfile changes only\nthe `@pnpm/napi` entries and its platform packages. It was regenerated\nwith `bit install`.\n- 12.10.0 includes pnpm/pnpm#16631. When `maxSockets` caps the\nconnections to a registry, package metadata requests now go ahead of\nqueued tarball downloads to the same registry. Before, they waited\nbehind every download queued earlier. Bit always passes `maxSockets:\n15`, so its capsule installs hit this. It showed up as hundreds of\n`Request took 10xxxms` warnings in Ripple CI `bit sign` jobs.\n- I measured it locally on internal case (a fresh capsule resolving\n5,554 packages), with the warning threshold lowered to 1s. All three\nruns were back to back:\n\n  | `@pnpm/napi` | metadata requests > 1s | mean | ≥ 10s |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 12.10.0 without the fix (local build) | 3,822 | 8.5s | 1,254 |\n  | 12.10.0 with the fix (local build) | 2,597 | 6.2s | 585 |\n  | 12.10.0 (published) | 2,659 | 7.7s | 817 |\n\nResults vary a lot from run to run, so read these as a direction rather\nthan exact numbers. Some slow requests remain, because the engine''s\nglobal connection pool still reserves half its slots for downloads.\n\n---\nWritten by an agent (Claude Code, claude-opus-5-5).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLcyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADl0QAHmSnhH9hQ7+lC4NsseGKMHJ\nxG+LcRTXCzR4XNNaoaZhlBTqcZ1GdBvdgAFvfbqQtX63Mzx3Kt4gddZx+4EVrq/l\nvOZOvfW00vrIsu6/bMfrUJRYadKPFN454jpfHEGiWCBcCnloMGj8F2CNKaIx8L6u\n19w+BhX6wrpup0yLX/JYVpegyHz87F5Nvm5/sbklT2wVyKt+pfNSr+244hob7uvv\nJYZzb1/A6marmdW/EN08BWE7G/x0QrXxUU4HJaSlycAKIBx03S77DdtHe8VqjGTG\ntjPKxWELxyooSIa/rLiY1C75bQp2wUyAAgRAbtlrtouw0EpQZLZRI7EMU3S7nYP3\nFSNfl903YxLLlPjalYsqALKtZhOlniyfdnam8Sya9VptQkoJjzCi8J41nNzjTkxa\nDz8qTyMNnV1v+hmFXkv9leYlEUsr7Sie+g+H0DPjzZHoSI7dBBgMjnu3JPKmZpOR\nCruvbU63ZVtO8E4T7fh3URj1b2RmKhvcVborzKxDGlbmj28X/K7yMkAszsTYuS3E\nzGytZDXlhmwjN0Wlw31lQuYDQiuZWCdn8QH0nZ/z5zwXLtHuubG7bp/ILm6VUAyN\nDKz7PR/f+/9Mqvswg0pCXbbx84aolTS/WTeWT9af0GxnAGxPZ9OCiuiKs8taeeaw\nsG/9JDUJmua99FZ1KEU+\n=eB2y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T08:54:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url"