/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/f74dfc9dc129976da31dc4ff8965b177f5d13a61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T16:17:51Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T16:17:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(merge): explain why a text file shows as a binary conflict (#10754)\n\n`git merge-file` treats a file as binary when any of its versions has a\nNUL byte, so a corrupted (or UTF-16) source file ends up as a bare\n`unchanged-BINARY-CONFLICT` during checkout/merge/lane switch with no\nhint why.\n\nThe file-changes report now adds a note to binary conflicts: for real\nbinary extensions it says to pick a version manually; for text files it\npoints at NUL bytes / likely corruption or UTF-16 encoding.","tree":{"sha":"3e35be5534efda9b4d05356b7eaf117a8077f399","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/3e35be5534efda9b4d05356b7eaf117a8077f399"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/f74dfc9dc129976da31dc4ff8965b177f5d13a61","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e35be5534efda9b4d05356b7eaf117a8077f399\nparent 18f900e6ad6cfac1e8b344337c04f728abb29d56\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1790957871 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790957871 +0300\n\nfix(merge): explain why a text file shows as a binary conflict (#10754)\n\n`git merge-file` treats a file as binary when any of its versions has a\nNUL byte, so a corrupted (or UTF-16) source file ends up as a bare\n`unchanged-BINARY-CONFLICT` during checkout/merge/lane switch with no\nhint why.\n\nThe file-changes report now adds a note to binary conflicts: for real\nbinary extensions it says to pick a version manually; for text files it\npoints at 