1cd0c20cb0a236cc5abf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/825ff304873ac4216dc89522fed2f0266c320072","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/825ff304873ac4216dc89522fed2f0266c320072","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDgyNWZmMzA0ODczYWM0MjE2ZGM4OTUyMmZlZDJmMDI2NmMzMjAwNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/2626b4381cffb98257508dc795c8b1e50ca69e18","sha":"2626b4381cffb98257508dc795c8b1e50ca69e18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/2626b4381cffb98257508dc795c8b1e50ca69e18"}],"sha":"825ff304873ac4216dc89522fed2f0266c320072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/825ff304873ac4216dc89522fed2f0266c320072"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/2626b4381cffb98257508dc795c8b1e50ca69e18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:22:33Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:22:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(workspace): re-baseline component-loading benchmarks and re-scope phase 2 (#10722)\n\nRe-baselines the component-loading benchmarks after a 3-month gap, and\nre-scopes phase 2 around what measurement actually shows. Doc-only —\nthree candidate quick wins were implemented and measured during this\nwork, and **all three were rejected**.\n\n**Re-baseline** (331 components now, was ~313): `status` −16%, `graph`\n−9%, `show` −29% since June — **with no phase-2 item shipped**. The\ngains came from fixes landed outside this effort. Peak RSS regressed\n(`graph` +339MB, `list` +124MB); no phase targets memory.\n\n**The main finding: the profiler''s aggregate self-time does not predict\nwall-time.**\n\n| experiment | profiler says | wall says | verdict |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| deps-cache fs scan (#10445) | −37% fs syscalls | ~0.3s | closed\nunmerged |\n| forward `loadOpts` on the batch path | `on-load` self-time −52% |\n**−0.07s (noise)**, **+67MB RSS** | rejected |\n| memoize env-component resolution | `workspace.get` calls −75% | −0.14s\n(−1.5%), RSS neutral | rejected, see below |\n\nSpans sum `await` time across concurrently-interleaved async work on one\nJS thread, so dividing by observed concurrency does not recover\nwall-time. Drift is also real — identical code measured 9.43s and 8.99s\ntwenty minutes apart — so all numbers above are medians of 9 interleaved\nruns per variant.\n\n**Why the `workspace.get` 10× count is a red herring:** 80% of the 3349\ncalls are the envs aspect re-resolving one of only **4 distinct envs**.\nMemoizing removes 75% of the calls but moves `workspace.get` self-time\nby just 0.39s — they were already cheap cache hits. The 1.5% wall gain\nwould be bought by adding a 12th ad-hoc cache to the ~11 this effort\nexists to consolidate, so it is recorded as evidence for the §2.4\n`EnvResolver` (phase 5) instead.\n\nConsequences recorded:\n- Perf claims now require an interleaved wall-clock A/B plus peak-RSS\ncomparison. No merges on profiler self-time alone.\n- ~~Phase 3 promoted~~ — **retracted** (§4.5): the component cache holds\none object per id (two keys, same object), so consolidating it saves\nnothing. The +67MB above is unexplained, not a second copy.\n- Prioritize with a V8 CPU profile (`node --cpu-prof`), which sums to\nwall. It found a third of `status` in the object layer, thrashing a\n3,000-object LRU — fixed in #10723, merged (`status` −15% wall, ~−170MB\nRSS; a weak layer over the LRU keeps 3×/5× simulated workspaces 17-24%\nfaster than master instead of regressing).\n- Phase 4 is *not* promoted on the strength of the `legacy-load-deps`\n50% figure, since that figure comes from the metric just shown to be\nunreliable.\n\nAlso records why the deps-cache fs-scan item was dropped (#10445, closed\nunmerged).\n\n\n\n\n**Since then (§4.6-4.7):** the component caches had the same cliff. Warm\n`status` in a simulated larger workspace took 16-31s, because `status`\nre-requests every component while holding them all, so eviction only\nforced rebuilds. A weak layer (#10736) fixed it, after an env-ordering\nbug hidden by those rebuilds was fixed first (#10735). Then three\nprofile follow-ups removed copies that were never read (#10739, #10741,\n#10742). Current master: `status` **6.80s / 927MB**, −28% wall and −25%\nRSS since the September re-baseline. `graph` did not improve and is now\nthe outlier.","tree":{"sha":"d830815797aeab5794914a4915a0783e61560111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/d830815797aeab5794914a4915a0783e61560111"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/2626b4381cffb98257508dc795c8b1e50ca69e18","verification":{"payload":"tree d830815797aeab5794914a4915a0783e61560111\nparent 67d35c4e3918a7e24031fcfa3d6e3d32b8b6b415\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1790878953 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790878953 +0000\n\ndocs(workspace): re-baseline component-loading benchmarks and re-scope phase 2 (#10722)\n\nRe-baselines the component-loading benchmarks after a 3-month gap, and\nre-scopes phase 2 around what measurement actually shows. Doc-only —\nthree candidate quick wins were implemented and measured during this\nwork, and **all three were rejected**.\n\n**Re-baseline** (331 components now, was ~313): `status` −16%, `graph`\n−9%, `show` −29% since June — **with no phase-2 item shipped**. The\ngains came from fixes landed outside this effort. Peak RSS regressed\n(`graph` +339MB, `list` +124MB); no phase targets memory.\n\n**The main finding: the profiler''s aggregate self-time does not predict\nwall-time.**\n\n| experiment | profiler says | wall says | verdict |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| deps-cache fs scan (#10445) | −37% fs syscalls | ~0.3s | closed\nunmerged |\n| forward `loadOpts` on the batch path | `on-load` self-time −52% |\n**−0.07s (noise)**, **+67MB RSS** | rejected |\n| memoize env-component resolution | `workspace.get` calls −75% | −0.14s\n(−1.5%), RSS neutral | rejected, see below |\n\nSpans sum `await` time across concurrently-interleaved async work on one\nJS thread, so dividing by observed concurrency does not recover\nwall-time. Drift is also real — identical code measured 9.43s and 8.99s\ntwenty minutes apart — so all numbers above are medians of 9 interleaved\nruns per variant.\n\n**Why the `workspace.get` 10× count is a red herring:** 80% of the 3349\ncalls are the envs aspect re-resolving one of only **4 distinct envs**.\nMemoizing removes 75% of the calls but moves `workspace.get` self-time\nby just 0.39s — they were already cheap cache hits. The 1.5% wall gain\nwould be bought by adding a 12th ad-hoc cache to the ~11 this effort\nexists to consolidate, so it is recorded as evidence for the §2.4\n`EnvResolver` (phase 5) instead.\n\nConsequences recorded:\n- Perf claims now require an interleaved wall-clock A/B plus peak-RSS\ncomparison. No merges on profiler self-time alone.\n- ~~Phase 3 promoted~~ — **retracted** (§4.5): the component cache holds\none object per id (two keys, same object), so consolidating it saves\nnothing. The +67MB above is unexplained, not a second copy.\n- Prioritize with a V8 CPU profile (`node --cpu-prof`), which sums to\nwall. It found a third of `status` in the object layer, thrashing a\n3,000-object LRU — fixed in #10723, merged (`status` −15% wall, ~−170MB\nRSS; a weak layer over the LRU keeps 3×/5× simulated workspaces 17-24%\nfaster than master instead of regressing).\n- Phase 4 is *not* promoted on the strength of the `legacy-load-deps`\n50% figure, since that figure comes from the metric just shown to be\nunreliable.\n\nAlso records why the deps-cache fs-scan item was dropped (#10445, closed\nunmerged).\n\n\n\n\n**Since then (§4.6-4.7):** the component caches had the same cliff. Warm\n`status` in a simulated larger workspace took 16-31s, because `status`\nre-requests every component while holding them all, so eviction only\nforced rebuilds. A weak layer (#10736) fixed it, after an env-ordering\nbug hidden by those rebuilds was fixed first (#10735). Then three\nprofile follow-ups removed copies that were never read (#10739, #10741,\n#10742). Current master: `status` **6.80s / 927MB**, −28% wall and −25%\nRSS since the September re-baseline. `graph` did not improve and is now\nthe outlier.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvqTpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcOAQACXyxPUAwTUiWXuI4ykXNwmu\n3uohsdXmRukMUQ/EkAEt3V6sqzYUXo1n+wglGWbCBIuFHa5ZBacFqu0eSFrRYhNZ\nRu8GttRAq7QhB/2eu7CjEoQP0NTqOTFJdMkwhYVrzkH+lFlyHQaV0YE9LPPm7+HX\n7Sac70Sn7Wnj6xkNvBuzVYyG2SMj85uAqrcCucYu496szgbSaWwdvcGkUJMNkbeG\n/a+para0vYILFnuM5Sxp5fI5uFUwGUSloadPYvv71IXKjK/iHLBP4zbLFOs1vqQ+\neFAhPDmg6MBS1GLyd+CN6TeQFSUP/Dyk4vALisGpp3MASsHU7pahX8ZGaaj+kiWL\nJtDbvh6Ou3wrFi747E82cXikqpAARIpY5RESjDvrA7rIMWfLxQhZvYNiOUb0/1gQ\nBuUyJENcl+I7RJQbJJ7Wy1jyCpRvmHsfJ9MSSSX3HNyUM614ZqNpoCXiQ5QZ4