avidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/f7e077c779c13114b54385188ae56de54f34d72a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:03:12Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:03:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(install): retry transient fs races when linking components and clearing the deps cache (#10746)\n\nOn Windows, `bit install` can fail with two transient file-system\nerrors. A second run of the command usually succeeds.\n\n- **EEXIST when bit links a component file into `node_modules`.** Bit\nremoves the destination and then links it again. On Windows, a removed\nfile stays \"delete pending\" while a different process (antivirus,\nindexer, IDE) holds it open, so the name is not free yet. Now bit\nremoves the destination again and retries the link up to 5 times, with a\nshort delay between the attempts.\n- **EPERM/EBUSY when bit clears the dependencies cache.** Components\ncontinue to read and write the cache during the removal. The old code\nretried only on ENOTEMPTY (the posix form of this race). Now bit uses\n`fs.rm` with `maxRetries`, which retries ENOTEMPTY, EPERM and EBUSY.","tree":{"sha":"0056236b40d465c6e01109098f2c0cb7b43d976a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/0056236b40d465c6e01109098f2c0cb7b43d976a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/f7e077c779c13114b54385188ae56de54f34d72a","verification":{"payload":"tree 0056236b40d465c6e01109098f2c0cb7b43d976a\nparent e61eac73a9955358ed4d338b47b90bce2c8e64e3\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1790802192 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790802192 -0400\n\nfix(install): retry transient fs races when linking components and clearing the deps cache (#10746)\n\nOn Windows, `bit install` can fail with two transient file-system\nerrors. A second run of the command usually succeeds.\n\n- **EEXIST when bit links a component file into `node_modules`.** Bit\nremoves the destination and then links it again. On Windows, a removed\nfile stays \"delete pending\" while a different process (antivirus,\nindexer, IDE) holds it open, so the name is not free yet. Now bit\nremoves the destination again and retries the link up to 5 times, with a\nshort delay between the attempts.\n- **EPERM/EBUSY when bit clears the dependencies cache.** Components\ncontinue to read and write the cache during the removal. The old code\nretried only on ENOTEMPTY (the posix form of this race). Now bit uses\n`fs.rm` with `maxRetries`, which retries ENOTEMPTY, EPERM and EBUSY.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXkQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAegcQAHp3Bzn21KbxLqSxQtBuT6zw\nd4KCKT/osO8acXgXVuYbWNyZ7PsymCNa4WunpmYGN6tzrnbU2cpuWhBtCUTs9y8H\n1WfwJdJqu4jViuEx+zK/1MAdRrnhX3m0M2WrA23vm2M8Vq8AE1ixXNbjdVD+Eykt\nKMUhaLUpG5oRkUKzp8Mmctkg8eW8yih2zEMsDiS6WBTqqAunmqReg0XHZiDDR1HS\nO8A4rDHrl+8VxSec0VPgKyz7Yi1LdaBbUPES84C5l7VLP9C4htRhCSF7laWjRKcm\nlwZ0WGnFEbcooYCDo8ICf5xX5G9CEv0QtjYxhsULoYVXr6kJ3QTeP8Y/178sxIg5\ne/SqhbA860J9UOEbdIg/1gbT5+intKEw04PX8sfGnQcFHSKhnyDYwrgLdshiEAYM\nl6r