ZmUzYmQxYjhjZjc3N2Y1NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1","sha":"1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1"}],"sha":"391c920a885ddeeab93ef55fe3bd1b8cf777f548","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/391c920a885ddeeab93ef55fe3bd1b8cf777f548"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:37:55Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T14:37:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(objects): filter objects by type from their header in Repository.list (#10730)\n\n`Repository.list(types)` read and inflated every object file in the\nscope just to check its type, then discarded almost all of them — most\nof a scope is file contents, which no caller of `list()` asks for. It\nnow reads the type from the header in the first 512 bytes (the mechanism\n`bit gc` added in #10714) and only reads the full file when the type\nmatches.\n\nThis speeds up every `list()` caller: rebuilding a missing `index.json`\n(on scope load, and after every `bit clear-cache`), `bit cat-scope`, the\nbare-scope garbage collector, `toObjectList` and the doctor''s\norphan-symlink check. On a 254 MB scope (27k objects) the index rebuild\nwent from ~3.1s to ~1.4s; the full read scales with the scope''s bytes\nand the header read with its object count, so the gap grows on larger\nscopes.\n\nWhen a content transformer is registered the header can''t be read on its\nown, so that case keeps the single full read. An object of an\nunregistered type is still skipped rather than thrown on, as before.","tree":{"sha":"e6198f124a1caea5bf622812b6d92ae8f56e3b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/e6198f124a1caea5bf622812b6d92ae8f56e3b8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1","verification":{"payload":"tree e6198f124a1caea5bf622812b6d92ae8f56e3b8f\nparent c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1790260675 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790260675 +0000\n\nperf(objects): filter objects by type from their header in Repository.list (#10730)\n\n`Repository.list(types)` read and inflated every object file in the\nscope just to check its type, then discarded almost all of them — most\nof a scope is file contents, which no caller of `list()` asks for. It\nnow reads the type from the header in the first 512 bytes (the mechanism\n`bit gc` added in #10714) and only reads the full file when the type\nmatches.\n\nThis speeds up every `list()` caller: rebuilding a missing `index.json`\n(on scope load, and after every `bit clear-cache`), `bit cat-scope`, the\nbare-scope garbage collector, `toObjectList` and the doctor''s\norphan-symlink check. On a 254 MB scope (27k objects) the index rebuild\nwent from ~3.1s to ~1.4s; the full read scales with the scope''s bytes\nand the header read with its object count, so the gap grows on larger\nscopes.\n\nWhen a content transformer is registered the header can''t be read on its\nown, so that case keeps the single full read. An object of an\nunregistered type is still skipped rather than thrown on, as before.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtTXDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdTkQAEnfz4m19N/+GFcGJrBvYimW\nKTjnCoBQvegzu3MkKR50kqvZuoyIS2hyVGB7YJ/N5Apc3HB9bsruKxo4CrljkzL/\nE43WKdoGoSK0i3dzAj0qfZbRX/MFO5Z8HGVPWIn+PaDyyf7wLKoIqPmhAf+sAyWG\n/huq9phPzDjzNHa67aGvNEPkTTG+FX0a5jo2dDTAfRBIJSLEYl8HWPSroo6noA0N\nc/PG7nMZFXbSGs7Rq7DPg/GawVZNEHl9AB89NzaeZbkjGADBlQLp0DT/+JwjVJr5\ngGzpECNjNgrbPmX6AQ65YN6ii9l/ZPpLfW915gFrWdivNQXtpWS0s7qF7m+Q0CkL\nuioFQ3DxxBYU3Pnr+UG9BIiJ/DKsBztQjVczl6ZMnWPGYt8e78ji4FDj6H0FEzqp\ncu5jDWjmEoJhct2OBgsHGgF9aD9CmrR6u1zxx05KiX+J26hxYo3QNOqJpVR/fwhk\nIR7ejjxyLv0ztJDjkEPRbH55MCWemz1GomV+IbVmz1nNRG8tflxKbUclL237Aw4n\nqoC+WcAcTF++0a2F/B3aK+9/F1n5VsbOAmqRdV65bGz+QmjdfsfKV7SdmJRCiuKE\nlM1//o6ITGykr/0Vnt4DqPPvF7YrhOybQbBSsZur4rX4q+YJPRXiHi/GqV8u24EW\nWSjK6Ov2SuJ/7audqYBz\n=7Mzs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T14:37:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDFmZGVlYTBjNDFiNzg0YzBmYTJkOTA1Y2MzN2VjY2Q4MDEyMzY2YjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b","sha":"c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b"}],"sha":"1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/1fdeea0c41b784c0fa2d905cc37eccd8012366b1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:02:34Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:02:34Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"message":"bump teambit version to 2.2.60 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"0c4ecc07781c589dcaafbdb8d2eb2befa1f31b67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/0c4ecc07781c589dcaafbdb8d2eb2befa1f31b67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKGMzZTljMzU0NzhmMTM1YmE0MzE1M2FjOTYzZWRhMmE0ZjZmNjkxOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f","sha":"33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f"}],"sha":"c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/c3e9c35478f135ba43153ac963eda2a4f6f6919b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T21:24:42Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T21:24:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(gc): add \"bit gc\" to remove unneeded objects from the local scope (#10714)\n\nA workspace keeps all versions of all components that it imports. Each\nnew version adds its source files, and nothing removes the superseded\nones. The local scope thus grows to many gigabytes.\n\n`bit gc` removes the versions that nothing refers to. It keeps the\nchecked-out version of each component, all heads (of the workspace, of\nits lanes and of the tracked remotes), all local snaps that you did not\nexport yet, and the dependencies of these. Bit fetches a removed version\nagain from the remote when it needs it.\n\nThe command removes a version as a unit: the Version object and its\nSource objects together. `sources.get()` reads only the Version object\nto decide if a version is local. A Version object without its files thus\nmakes the importer skip the fetch, and the command fails later.\n\n`--keep-versions <n>` keeps the last n versions of each workspace\ncomponent. The recent history stays local for `bit log` and `bit blame`.\n\nIn a bare scope the command runs the existing collector that keeps all\nhistory, because a bare scope is the source of truth and not a cache.\n\nOn this repository: 5.3 GB to 254 MB in 45 seconds, or 364 MB with\n`--keep-versions 5`.\n\nOther options: `--dry-run`, `--backup`, `--restore`, `--verbose`,\n`--json`. 11 unit tests cover the collector.","tree":{"sha":"80f19ab06594207dbe1239f107c831ee6fa35f02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/80f19ab06594207dbe1239f107c831ee6fa35f02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f","verification":{"payload":"tree 80f19ab06594207dbe1239f107c831ee6fa35f02\nparent 22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1790198682 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790198682 +0000\n\nfeat(gc): add \"bit gc\" to remove unneeded objects from the local scope (#10714)\n\nA workspace keeps all versions of all components that it imports. Each\nnew version adds its source files, and nothing removes the superseded\nones. The local scope thus grows to many gigabytes.\n\n`bit gc` removes the versions that nothing refers to. It keeps the\nchecked-out version of each component, all heads (of the workspace, of\nits lanes and of the tracked remotes), all local snaps that you did not\nexport yet, and the dependencies of these. Bit fetches a removed version\nagain from the remote when it needs it.\n\nThe command removes a version as a unit: the Version object and its\nSource objects together. `sources.get()` reads only the Version object\nto decide if a version is local. A Version object without its files thus\nmakes the importer skip the fetch, and the command fails later.\n\n`--keep-versions <n>` keeps the last n versions of each workspace\ncomponent. The recent history stays local for `bit log` and `bit blame`.\n\nIn a bare scope the command runs the existing collector that keeps all\nhistory, because a bare scope is the source of truth and not a cache.\n\nOn this repository: 5.3 GB to 254 MB in 45 seconds, or 364 MB with\n`--keep-versions 5`.\n\nOther options: `--dry-run`, `--backup`, `--restore`, `--verbose`,\n`--json`. 11 unit tests cover the collector.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtEOaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPQYQAGCSyqygvwOXyINIe5d0t620\n3PkTmN//jr28GHBYQ6j+qHtITac7k6RrHIKnOw1VmKUZPWjRfH7PxUitcI3yLtJJ\nNcc77FgcAxitRW7zrePpMKtdy0VYrvK4ZRgH0R/LsA7YyePbqIh8hY85K50U60sp\nwpGDn+tM8et7KrhbpdxXu2E12vfxlDes4OODF5MnP9F/+eV7aS8MIolCKaXSUCQT\nnXHyK7ufH5LKwieF0zikAnR90p8bp+qGYqamMX9z3v4RS4PNKC86fDYiSO2/baXg\nL8b8oWgrjdiIPY1CqZ2nfLX6B9GmS3e3NEp/RJBE0cn5uzOf2pk9/Ha/DkcVXIN5\nlAzYCgGHIb2Qzyly99jBAIdyuztzkuYqYxZk/1nmlDGZYX1vLFXfN72zJSLqZj8l\nh2+RGDAy9WsG6qfjMpKAYcYPD+QhgJ2t/lAesMmUuOjncwvkiEWiUh1nohPte/2C\nUN4N2BOYjeJFnzOODZJVjw/bDFlwZgZeral9/PRneE+yWeZDd/V5t3A0yfqtQ0b9\nmRGpFdl9GB851cClZWH+CB3IAnX1/qAAWhGDiwI7WINaZY85PKU1la3GPtZRIv1b\nDSEhHhV2GQyqpcxO/QOze3iSWluFV6JPULIAgQGCRJ7N7m7yfrW8Mf8N9e+b4ewJ\n0BUnvlvqLu/jirk+5/GV\n=Q9D+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T21:24:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDMzMTE2ZWY2ZDU5Y2QzMmFhNTkwZjE1YjdmNDcxNDUxNjdhYzVjMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442","sha":"22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442"}],"sha":"33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/33116ef6d59cd32aa590f15b7f47145167ac5c1f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:44:21Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:44:21Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"message":"bump teambit version to 2.2.59 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"7e759fe4a2ba7a7c151326a20f7b6a6e7c9f5b8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/7e759fe4a2ba7a7c151326a20f7b6a6e7c9f5b8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDIyZGUxYjJhZjM3ZmZlNjQyNjI2ZDVjYjY4NGYwODZjMDk4OTU0NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/7cb93083adbb0931aa0ea6ba1e1610bc822dc375","sha":"7cb93083adbb0931aa0ea6ba1e1610bc822dc375","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/7cb93083adbb0931aa0ea6ba1e1610bc822dc375"}],"sha":"22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/22de1b2af37ffe642626d5cb684f086c09895442"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/7cb93083adbb0931aa0ea6ba1e1610bc822dc375/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:03:56Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T17:03:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: trim redundant e2e tests, move pure logic to unit specs (#10651)\n\nThis PR reduces the number of slow e2e tests. The work goes file by\nfile. Each commit covers one e2e file.\n\n- Remove e2e tests that a unit spec already covers.\n- Remove e2e tests that repeat the same code path as a sibling test.\n- Move tests of pure functions to unit specs. Example: main-file\nresolution now has a unit spec (determine-main-file.spec.ts) with 9\ntests.\n- Keep all tests that need a real workspace or scope.","tree":{"sha":"9aecc8e7d55b28140c7a0733b27c592d41cb1aec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/9aecc8e7d55b28140c7a0733b27c592d41cb1aec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/7cb93083adbb0931aa0ea6ba1e1610bc822dc375","verification":{"payload":"tree 9aecc8e7d55b28140c7a0733b27c592d41cb1aec\nparent 6d3b4d14ece8dc076bf4e914c35f09cefeeb12c6\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1790183036 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790183036 -0400\n\ntest: trim redundant e2e tests, move pure logic to unit specs (#10651)\n\nThis PR reduces the number of slow e2e tests. The work goes file by\nfile. Each commit covers one e2e file.\n\n- Remove e2e tests that a unit spec already covers.\n- Remove e2e tests that repeat the same code path as a sibling test.\n- Move tests of pure functions to unit specs. Example: main-file\nresolution now has a unit spec (determine-main-file.spec.ts) with 9\ntests.\n- Keep all tests that need a real workspace or scope.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtAZ8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGvwQAEJEHVnXu+IWPG2xto154PBx\nbInEcKU544fQNDOHgNEGLJgRaDyCmaojjzKxVI+t/61Gc5z5D2s/moQsudqshWOL\niTERqeP6z1vANb+gzp3jP9yM++OFnBBEOJ+PaeISl98t+q6YmSawItIlxQyg4QH6\nSO3xIUpE63jGCVwk4S3/aFZw7iaXtTz8ZSDOHNB8xkmrIjrcOOIRDujk4gHi+gVk\n297ldmRatI3v+hlok9SfqPFeASED7F7A8lUZpok0LXi8Bz9OoimUOmQpm5Z4ylYv\no7iyTjBfZV4Lkjy0U2kCaXATtSlZwn6b1rbPSvBKE2cWCdTJTShrtQFeqITdVQOb\nhN1jkA4RuIfqVbSZwZSOOo2CCElf1YKZ2PbXa6DCJ6Zco/ulAi6lGOHamuvgOQRG\nzfmbKQBfwK0s7yHsTEBDExvveXAj8CIkJo/Fs+Fg2nT664xPm6xJlCB0iLY9l1+A\nAUS7N2Tu9ukHEoOZFrk4N8+axsfxDOssAQGA6WYjU