:"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/e79885a777de9e6faaaf2691854f6c9aec66387c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:46:44Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:46:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(envs): stop false \"env was not loaded\" warning on partial loads (#10713)\n\nCloses #10505.\n\nBit showed this warning on a healthy workspace:\n\n```\n⚠ environment with ID: <env> configured on component <comp> was not loaded (run \"bit install\")\n```\n\nThe workspace was correct. `bit install` did not remove the warning.\n\nTwo different causes give the same message.\n\n**1. Partial loads.** The workspace loads components in groups. A group\nwith `seeders: false` holds components that the user did not request.\nBit loads them only because another component uses them as an aspect or\nan env. Bit schedules the env of such a component only when the user\nrequests that component. Thus the env is correctly absent from the slot\nduring this pass, and the warning is incorrect. For example, `bit show\n<comp>` warned about the env of the env of `<comp>`. `bit status` did\nnot warn, because it requests all components.\n\n**2. The install flow.** `_installModules` loads the components before\nit loads the envs as aspects. `install()` sets `inInstallContext` to\nmute the warning during this time. But `uninstallDependencies` and\n`updateDependencies` called `_installModules` directly, and they did not\nset the flag. Thus `bit uninstall` and `bit update` showed the warning\nwhile they did the install that the warning recommends.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `EnvsMain.skipNotLoadedWarnings(fn)` mutes the warning for the time of\n`fn`. Use a scope, not a parameter: five aspects calculate the env\nduring the load slot (tester, docs, pkg, compositions, dev-files). If\nyou mute one caller, the warning moves to the next caller.\n- Non-seeder load groups run in that scope.\n- `uninstallDependencies` and `updateDependencies` set\n`inInstallContext`, as `install()` does.\n\n### Results\n\nA healthy workspace shows no warning for `bit show <comp>`, `bit\nuninstall`, `bit status`, `bit list`.\n\nA broken env keeps its report. `bit status` shows the warning and the\ncomponent issues. `bit show <the env>` shows the warning.\n\n`bit show <comp>` no longer warns when the env of the env is broken. The\nenv of `<comp>` loads correctly in this condition. Bit reports the\nbroken env where the user can correct it.\n\nNew unit tests in `environments.main.runtime.spec.ts`.","tree":{"sha":"cca09e8cb361c9653380c112a470dbfc4c9cb442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/cca09e8cb361c9653380c112a470dbfc4c9cb442"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/e79885a777de9e6faaaf2691854f6c9aec66387c","verification":{"payload":"tree cca09e8cb361c9653380c112a470dbfc4c9cb442\nparent c9983b218ed6b89a2cd32f8cf17d03ae4f83b63c\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1789750004 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789750004 -0400\n\nfix(envs): stop false \"env was not loaded\" warning on partial loads (#10713)\n\nCloses #10505.\n\nBit showed this warning on a healthy workspace:\n\n```\n⚠ environment with ID: <env> configured on component <comp> was not loaded (run \"bit install\")\n```\n\nThe workspace was correct. `bit install` did not remove the warning.\n\nTwo different causes give the same message.\n\n**1. Partial loads.** The workspace loads components in groups. A group\nwith `seeders: false` holds components that the user did not request.\nBit loads them only because another component uses them as an aspect or\nan env. Bit schedules the env of such a component only when the user\nrequests that component. Thus the env is correctly absent from the slot\nduring this pass, and the warning is incorrect. For example, `bit show\n<comp>` warned about the env of the env of `<comp>`. `bit status` did\nnot warn, because it requests all components.\n\n**2. The install flow.** `_installModules` loads the components before\nit loads the envs as aspects. `install()` sets `inInstallContext` to\nmute the warning during this time. But `uninstallDependencies` and\n`updateDependencies` called `_installModules` directly, and they did not\nset the flag. Thus `bit uninstall` and `bit update` showed the warning\nwhile they did the install that the warning recommends.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `EnvsMain.skipNotLoadedWarnings(fn)` mutes the warning for the time of\n`fn`. Use a scope, not a parameter: five aspects calculate the env\nduring the load slot (tester, docs, pkg, compositions, dev-files). If\nyou mute one caller, the warning moves to the next caller.\n- Non-seeder load groups run in that scope.\n- `uninstallDependencies` and `updateDependencies` set\n`inInstallContext`, as `install()` does.\n\n### Results\n\nA healthy workspace shows no warning for `bit show <comp>`, `bit\nuninstall`, `bit status`, `bit list`.\n\nA broken env keeps its report. `bit status` shows the warning and the\ncomponent issues. `bit show <the env>` shows the warning.\n\n`bit show <comp>` no longer warns when the env of the env is broken. The\nenv of `<comp>` loads correctly in this condition. Bit reports the\nbroken env where the user can correct it.\n\nNew unit tests in `environments.main.runtime.spec.ts`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrWr0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd7cQACMTvUXEKsv/3hK