s.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/12afa43c9db33fe494b96f101d0026bb316f0539/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:39:17Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:39:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(qodo): scope push reviews to new commits and curb repeated findings (#10717)\n\nTwo changes to how Qodo reviews a PR, both prompted by a long review\ncycle on #10698.\n\n**Push reviews look only at the new commits.**\n`enable_incremental_review` is documented as defaulting to `true`, but\nrounds on #10698 kept raising findings about files the latest commits\nhad not touched. Stating it in the repo puts the setting under version\ncontrol instead of leaving it to a portal default.\n\n**Findings that were answered should not come back.** There is no\nsetting for this on the agentic reviewer - the open-source reviewer has\n`persistent_inline_comments`, but it is not among the hosted agent''s\noptions - so it is asked for in `issues_user_guidelines` instead. The\nsecond rule there addresses a specific case that recurred three times: a\nrequest to move an e2e assertion to a unit test, where the assertion\nreuses a workspace an adjacent case already builds and so costs no extra\nprocess. Moving it would cut coverage and no CI time.\n\nReviews still run on every push; only their scope changes.","tree":{"sha":"ac9da87e86171c7689bb2481fd9d776bb8810cff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/ac9da87e86171c7689bb2481fd9d776bb8810cff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/12afa43c9db33fe494b96f101d0026bb316f0539","verification":{"payload":"tree ac9da87e86171c7689bb2481fd9d776bb8810cff\nparent ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1789677557 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789677557 +0000\n\nchore(qodo): scope push reviews to new commits and curb repeated findings (#10717)\n\nTwo changes to how Qodo reviews a PR, both prompted by a long review\ncycle on #10698.\n\n**Push reviews look only at the new commits.**\n`enable_incremental_review` is documented as defaulting to `true`, but\nrounds on #10698 kept raising findings about files the latest commits\nhad not touched. Stating it in the repo puts the setting under version\ncontrol instead of leaving it to a portal default.\n\n**Findings that were answered should not come back.** There is no\nsetting for this on the agentic reviewer - the open-source reviewer has\n`persistent_inline_comments`, but it is not among the hosted agent''s\noptions - so it is asked for in `issues_user_guidelines` instead. The\nsecond rule there addresses a specific case that recurred three times: a\nrequest to move an e2e assertion to a unit test, where the assertion\nreuses a workspace an adjacent case already builds and so costs no extra\nprocess. Moving it would cut coverage and no CI time.\n\nReviews still run on every push; only their scope changes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrE/1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZlYQAJrsSi7/xg0AbR2XTpqtWWFb\nNmBz3SxQ22D1mBS8h9M8e7etm0mgvlxFTxZuYjnPshPnGFVQLNfYl8e+IJbJe4xp\nVgnk3GtwZhGTFasqnZFO/emBMe1R8VGYxjiXSBbEc0A0wShVI9POCLWz47vNOMEv\nOklri50nYzZrmBo8UJ6blX3H8IonbxquO24rZLg6u8wnb2ZhlKrm2o9J1lQemwy+\nVKH79efDo2Vuc9i2aXhDg4T+xwoEdhBE8fHU3HDG3HLIwIDCPGTZadxnBcaAtuj1\nWPfMFaUVDGyO88PmVbR7jtH9fzpvZSgyZwKT9uDH1m4kFQVenMtUEhX14pUpQ6GJ\nqlA33IpZCRM8Rwvp3yOb5a1D2shIHipFA42xwGMsDGHpbxGHK4tZHWrBlyKYhyJm\nHOPr1tQFz+gK3OWZzFAwM1ZYJ5/ZryqDERvsQulJ/UTXtmIzgPMk26kDGku/d0li\nNaW6iPH/YyvoHNYOi1JbpfFwhXUQuSuViI7wi5V7iI8rwnDPPkYXjML+tFP2JIDw\nxRuXaeKmu6pQ3SadEfDrPkmfc9GIp+QzN2Po5GXeZyi8q8nORIugdUIi9AoO9NLL\nJlYwPAr+7STaDvvQmTVzQb1DSy1yuGi0nL8uNl1MBTX0HeWrcBOIjWDJzhS2FeGX\ni6LW1fYyNoYozhJg0o3h\n=mQKK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T20:39:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/12afa43c9db33fe494b96f101d0026bb316f0539","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDEyYWZhNDNjOWRiMzNmZTQ5NGI5NmYxMDFkMDAyNmJiMzE2ZjA1Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e","sha":"ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e"}],"sha":"12afa43c9db33fe494b96f101d0026bb316f0539","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/12afa43c9db33fe494b96f101d0026bb316f0539"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:10:37Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:10:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(test): scope the root babel config to the e2e suite (#10715)\n\n## Problem\n\nBabel finds `babel.config.js` automatically. The mocha tester in bit\nalso uses `@babel/register`. Thus `bit test` reads this file for every\ncomponent in the workspace.\n\nThe file contains an old rule: `ignore: [''components/*'']`. A commit\nadded this rule in June 2019. At that time, `components/` held two\nunrelated directories. Later refactors moved the legacy source tree into\n`components/`.\n\nBecause of the rule, babel does not transform the spec files below\n`components/`. Node then reads the TypeScript source as an ES module.\nThe command stops with a syntax error.\n\nCI does not show this error. The build pipeline tests the compiled dist\nin a capsule. The capsule is outside the repository root. Thus the rule\ndoes not apply there.\n\n## Solution\n\nRename the file to `babel.e2e.config.js`. Give the path to\n`@babel/register` in `babel-register.js`. Babel no longer finds the file\nautomatically. Only the e2e suite reads it. `bit test` now uses the\nconfig of the env, as CI does.\n\nDo not delete the file. The e2e suite needs it. Without babel, node\nreads each `.ts` file as an ES module. The `@teambit/*` packages then\nresolve to `dist/esm.mjs`. 89 of 198 such packages do not contain this\nfile.\n\nThe renamed file keeps the old `ignore` rule. The behavior of the e2e\nsuite stays the same.\n\n## Result\n\n| | components | tests passed | tester errors |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| before | 64 | 1225/1290 | 11 |\n| after | 74 | 1403/1468 | 1 |\n\n24 spec files across 10 components run again. The one remaining error is\na jest resolver problem in a react component. That error is not related\nto this change, and it is also present before this change.","tree":{"sha":"f6db3d857a066a77e921422d8c781e97bfa52094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/f6db3d857a066a77e921422d8c781e97bfa52094"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e","verification":{"payload":"tree f6db3d857a066a77e921422d8c781e97bfa52094\nparent 721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1789668637 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789668637 +0000\n\nfix(test): scope the root babel config to the e2e suite (#10715)\n\n## Problem\n\nBabel finds `babel.config.js` automatically. The mocha tester in bit\nalso uses `@babel/register`. Thus `bit test` reads this file for every\ncomponent in the workspace.\n\nThe file contains an old rule: `ignore: [''components/*'']`. A commit\nadded this rule in June 2019. At that time, `components/` held two\nunrelated directories. Later refactors moved the legacy source tree into\n`components/`.\n\nBecause of the rule, babel does not transform the spec files below\n`components/`. Node then reads the TypeScript source as an ES module.\nThe command stops with a syntax error.\n\nCI does not show this error. The build pipeline tests the compiled dist\nin a capsule. The capsule is outside the repository root. Thus the rule\ndoes not apply there.\n\n## Solution\n\nRename the file to `babel.e2e.config.js`. Give the path to\n`@babel/register` in `babel-register.js`. Babel no longer finds the file\nautomatically. Only the e2e suite reads it. `bit test` now uses the\nconfig of the env, as CI does.\n\nDo not delete the file. The e2e suite needs it. Without babel, node\nreads each `.ts` file as an ES module. The `@teambit/*` packages then\nresolve to `dist/esm.mjs`. 89 of 198 such packages do not contain this\nfile.\n\nThe renamed file keeps the old `ignore` rule. The behavior of the e2e\nsuite stays the same.\n\n## Result\n\n| | components | tests passed | tester errors |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| before | 64 | 1225/1290 | 11 |\n| after | 74 | 1403/1468 | 1 |\n\n24 spec files across 10 components run again. The one remaining error is\na jest resolver problem in a react component. That error is not related\nto this change, and it is also present before this change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrC0dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqDYQAA3Ts6dYbPaYO5qy8GzjAQZP\n5ssbJk7DG2fj3igtS3386XF6xaKBb0rOnWzPMbDCBX6XrcZn5qe8vgOFjm/vNIbJ\nxKJ0Kc80YQUAxxxi6yDS1p8tj/ind1zTYqqx/6GKWr8h+UIzZWCQTzGWqXnjJxK9\nZwsxEG2+WGBZX8NyEJ0ateyG4Rz2M18bdr2UN6E4DlaFgLqo1gr9SFhBx0eexSwD\ngEL8lrHKMbKgCUPfyk8CYYtJhfCrBSZa86bv4dni02GmYx8WjPf+9UmBpF0Jz6yn\n1tFMrdrOM7FUIry/vnaXh/z3NiXVPf7ZNaMEpr0Cxgdw8rctf0MRaWvj/J+4lGxt\nPWdSB0GEnVE0/0FAdUqGXlBefSRt9gD5HmETZyYv5AtNv+CoRE97lLwmIEOyeC4S\nEdyd9tVoIjU9AuPi0A1a2VU7/jcasd3GRqqcFmmt/vpnsLdhuLXlyU6GDoqp+1zw\nQW19UjWayzQvY0Eel+XtnmApJ/c+kvlYNsvadXkEbALNerMaA5xGUnxz5IJlJ2Uj\nJrnXaEnEWT0T+Qe7xHTuJCtJMhqGeU6puUCbHmQcOHtKN6ijmc0ErHRqJFBs0Zgd\nKx242FinTUKA6ViumFSXHUQefvuIcsTtSLpqBTLd4v+837W+2CwnPwpJfQx0JG1c\n9LtRq9pqwy/KTrs0uF84\n=3icW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T18:10:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKGVkNTRmY2JjMDE4M2E3MGMyNmVjMDYxNDg0MmQ4MWUyNjczMDhkNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a","sha":"721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a"}],"sha":"ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/ed54fcbc0183a70c26ec0614842d81e267308d4e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:42:25Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:42:25Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"message":"bump teambit version to 2.2.53 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"e0f2061928354b6e859863b6420662027aa63742","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/e0f2061928354b6e859863b6420662027aa63742"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDcyMWZiMTdkYzA1Y2JhNDJhZTQzMGNiODU0MGNlN2FmYjMxNjliMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892","sha":"f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892"}],"sha":"721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/721fb17dc05cba42ae430cb8540ce7afb3169b0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:04:15Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:04:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ripple): add ''ripple simulate'' and ''lane updates'' commands (#10712)\n\nThis PR adds three CLI verbs. Agents can use them to find what a lane\nchange breaks in its dependents.\n\n- `bit ripple simulate` starts a Ripple CI simulation for the current\nlane, or for the lane given with `--lane`. Ripple CI builds the\ndependents of the lane components against the lane heads. It does not\nmerge and it does not publish. By default it searches for dependents in\nthe lane scope, because the server cannot resolve the graph without a\nnetwork filter. Use `--scopes`, `--owners` and `--exclude-scopes` to\nwiden or narrow the search. The command rejects main and rejects a lane\nthat was never exported. The mutation returns the job before it is\npersisted, so the command fetches the persisted job by slug to report a\nusable job id.\n- `bit lane updates` lists the dependents that Ripple CI cascaded onto\nthe lane (the hidden `updateDependents` entries). It reads the remote\nlane first. It uses the local lane object only when the remote lane is\nnot available.\n- `bit lane updates --undo` removes these entries. An export does not\nremove hidden entries from the remote, because the remote merge walks\nonly the incoming entries. The command removes them on the remote\nthrough the GraphQL field that the cloud UI uses, and then removes them\nlocally.\n\n`bit ripple list` now marks simulation jobs. Unit tests cover the\nsimulate request shape and command guards with a stubbed fetch, and list\nand undo against a mock bare scope. The simulate command was verified\nagainst bit.cloud on a throwaway lane: the simulation reported the\nplanted compile error in the dependent.","tree":{"sha":"06cfd0529407b8af08c62aec24fb9e08a20c06ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/06cfd0529407b8af08c62aec24fb9e08a20c06ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892","verification":{"payload":"tree 06cfd0529407b8af08c62aec24fb9e08a20c06ce\nparent 7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1789592655 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789592655 +0000\n\nfeat(ripple): add ''ripple simulate'' and ''lane updates'' commands (#10712)\n\nThis PR adds three CLI verbs. Agents can use them to find what a lane\nchange breaks in its dependents.\n\n- `bit ripple simulate` starts a Ripple CI simulation for the current\nlane, or for the lane given with `--lane`. Ripple CI builds the\ndependents of the lane components against the lane heads. It does not\nmerge and it does not publish. By default it searches for dependents in\nthe lane scope, because the server cannot resolve the graph without a\nnetwork filter. Use `--scopes`, `--owners` and `--exclude-scopes` to\nwiden or narrow the search. The command rejects main and rejects a lane\nthat was never exported. The mutation returns the job before it is\npersisted, so the command fetches the persisted job by slug to report a\nusable job id.\n- `bit lane updates` lists the dependents that Ripple CI cascaded onto\nthe lane (the hidden `updateDependents` entries). It reads the remote\nlane first. It uses the local lane object only when the remote lane is\nnot available.\n- `bit lane updates --undo` removes these entries. An export does not\nremove hidden entries from the remote, because the remote merge walks\nonly the incoming entries. The command removes them on the remote\nthrough the GraphQL field that the cloud UI uses, and then removes them\nlocally.\n\n`bit ripple list` now marks simulation jobs. Unit tests cover the\nsimulate request shape and command guards with a stubbed fetch, and list\nand undo against a mock bare scope. The simulate command was verified\nagainst bit.cloud on a throwaway lane: the simulation reported the\nplanted compile error in the dependent.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqwRPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdUEQAHTGBzt0T6zXMypHzXErzfdd\nEv1HUIFkfd7KGPcYx/P0jOW61Z3cpshsOAvxZOp/d7ekDHY2lVA+kZx/+YppiqNz\ngmaaMvs/Z9KQtsUwVf+hwcu1H8VkjNObmksBMnj6GLFY/8AyiXlGM4UwH7HKZlfU\nVe/oojFfwkEbuE5p77DFy9XD325OROQhVqN14F/Cfp190PHIuP67jm+IMCvgf3mw\nAYQi8cwWmXRJBpAEHixRy1dR2fOuvPw1bdAM6J2zOP3np+0scuoZUKfjltehpRBm\n4VfdSouJ9MjPMiQ//SuzICu6z0lD49/i07MTz2lEEh0cdvrEI9LE9BB84r985Q3s\na38uaYnU1mdy0rRniSwledlzVsUtEMsmNfhDGPc3J5UYfU0zeA8sdP2+TcmwBip5\n3AJbJKT7WFUZ0yQ4sE6u6qh6oPbw1MREdu1AHCFyxcLtqzjhF9bX3IFFdSYLnuLx\ny2Hszmd3vre1P6finnvVw/7B98uQo/SUntaD/z86G4/L/5KR8LVilzYbQm0bW8Kl\nSQlMsuBtZyB9/9VO4oSy5VgF7rng54pW+Mr1C4YjWn9TYuPdk1rumbUsM9ISkWFS\nv/UDlij0QsTkwkOZElg9XhENHbzqJPM4jhAAMe5Xvnx+A6RPZAShGgyjgQWH6JnQ\nTWE7FJW66gPvToYzA9fT\n=Y0Rb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T21:04:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKGY5ZWEwMmEwYjQ5YzcwNDExMmI2YzI2NzA2YWZlYjZiMjcxMGI4OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c","sha":"7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c"}],"sha":"f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/f9ea02a0b49c704112b6c26706afeb6b2710b892"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:52:26Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:52:26Z","email":"bit-ci[bot]@bit.cloud","name":"Bit CI"},"message":"bump teambit version to 2.2.52 [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"b3ebc173d26bed6a247bfed791ac1046f99c47f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/b3ebc173d26bed6a247bfed791ac1046f99c47f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c","node_id":"C_kwDOBMB9P9oAKDdlNWEzNjYzYTI4YjVhMWQ5NGYyY2Q0YWNhMDhjMzBjYzY0NmQ5M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/teambit/bit/commit/618dd6a7671f9fb2192a7f3233be5010f81e1ea0","sha":"618dd6a7671f9fb2192a7f3233be5010f81e1ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/618dd6a7671f9fb2192a7f3233be5010f81e1ea0"}],"sha":"7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/7e5a3663a28b5a1d94f2cd4aca08c30cc646d93c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1963573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidfirst","id":1963573,"login":"davidfirst","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjM1NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidfirst","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/commits/618dd6a7671f9fb2192a7f3233be5010f81e1ea0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:16:55Z","email":"davidnet@gmail.com","name":"David First"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:16:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(envs): treat empty-env as a core env so bit install skips its package (#10711)\n\n`teambit.harmony/empty-env` is a core aspect, but it was not in the\ncore-envs list. Because of this, `bit install` handled it as an external\nenv. It added the `@teambit/empty-env` package to the env root and\npulled the whole Bit core into the workspace (3187 packages instead of\n2). The dependency-resolver and dev-files guards also fetched the env\ncomponent from the remote on each load.\n\nThis change adds `empty-env` to `getCoreEnvsIds()`.\n\nThe same line was added and then reverted in July, before #10535 was\nmerged, with the note \"it breaks env loading for the component\". I\nreproduced what the revert saw. In the bit repo itself, `bit show\nteambit.harmony/empty-env` now reports its own env (`core-aspect-env`)\nas \"not loaded\". This is the existing load-groups behavior for every\ncore env in this repo: `bit show teambit.react/react`,\n`teambit.harmony/node` and `teambit.harmony/aspect` report the same\nwarning on master. The component still compiles and builds. The `bit_pr`\njob on this PR compiled and snapped `empty-env` with the other 97\ndependents. The remove-core-envs branch (#10465) returns only\n`empty-env` from `getCoreEnvsIds()` and passes full `bit ci pr --build`\nruns with it.\n\nA unit test in the install aspect makes sure that no env package is\nadded to the env root for `empty-env`. It does not assert anything about\nthe other core envs, so it stays valid after #10465.","tree":{"sha":"bb959af930cf00fc24c1998a4b9915f48875d923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/trees/bb959af930cf00fc24c1998a4b9915f48875d923"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teambit/bit/git/commits/618dd6a7671f9fb2192a7f3233be5010f81e1ea0","verification":{"payload":"tree bb959af930cf00fc24c1998a4b9915f48875d923\nparent 2df38187146fb985bd06b7abaa996977c50d337b\nauthor David First <davidnet@gmail.com> 1789507015 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789507015 +0000\n\nfix(envs): treat empty-env as a core env so bit install skips its package (#10711)\n\n`teambit.harmony/empty-env` is a core aspect, but it was not in the\ncore-envs list. Because of this, `bit install` handled it as an external\nenv. It added the `@teambit/empty-env` package to the env root and\npulled the whole Bit core into the workspace (3187 packages instead of\n2). The dependency-resolver and dev-files guards also fetched the env\ncomponent from the remote on each load.\n\nThis change adds `empty-env` to `getCoreEnvsIds()`.\n\nThe same line was added and then reverted in July, before #10535 was\nmerged, with the note \"it breaks env loading for the component\". I\nreproduced what the revert saw. In the bit repo itself, `bit show\nteambit.harmony/empty-env` now reports its own env (`core-aspect-env`)\nas \"not loaded\". This is the existing load-groups behavior for every\ncore env in this repo: `bit show teambit.react/react`,\n`teambit.harmony/node` and `teambit.harmony/aspect` report the same\nwarning on master. The component still compiles and builds. The `bit_pr`\njob on this PR compiled and snapped `empty-env` with the other 97\ndependents. The remove-core-envs branch (#10465) returns only\n`empty-env` from `getCoreEnvsIds()` and passes full `bit ci pr --build`\nruns with it.\n\nA unit test in the install aspect makes sure that no env package is\nadded to the env root for `empty-env`. It does not assert anything about\nthe other core envs, so it stays valid after #10465.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqbXHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJeMQAJXBlMB6m2POZgZzXd3zD13t\n1PJLu4OtRZ9SIcTJbIbT28V2b+/jpMPHLmIc5vtkhRc6jwk1CMj31LKrhQCD3PQ8\n8GE1sCMeXiDB0QZ3Ge1begYASG2WVJqmS01f5jmWyQ54DC8LwLi0CdsTgVXaP3Pq\nMKiY9pTB84CyT1n9pHVG/bLC1cURhLCHlOV0XzCmxqqP+LWc70wPAgHLxAQvaYMY\n2eWORpr2MvF4s6G06jUQDqvtimnV5Rdta7GNwySIKdU/vXEc7swLsu1snz4+f6WP\n/W+RXe2lRou1t9udQtSnpkYUaqCkjc/wGM46riEHKZQ/kpHbRdnTkzt9RXwUxOgo\nOMnXkX4cEhfGXI7C9tLXLb1G25TJzijA4qhscfLc5s7BJaxL/uYIl4eK9D+vAFom\nQKKZLcNSlRV21ShaeS/TZUFaGocr5N4IkVF9VYSfSuXrR0M020fNvyy/SnyqgeHl\nn931HPdBLElwNPArxo5zPw13ENa5ye/+8K11fuKjD0ZM7g7MY0DBpHVEA80hvbht\nJWW+TCC8eq2DluOlQbX+zmdlJc/0LZAorx7Q2YNK7ys2f9kNawwC0KDQXO1Z97cE\nmSTy9jfypdPreDm