":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commit/4f9af5f1e425c267f95241fce9ca7bfe5020d4b0","node_id":"C_kwDOBNevYdoAKDRmOWFmNWYxZTQyNWMyNjdmOTUyNDFmY2U5Y2E3YmZlNTAyMGQ0YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commit/9c52db8751671f91c6fa63477bfb7e8314d863c4","sha":"9c52db8751671f91c6fa63477bfb7e8314d863c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/9c52db8751671f91c6fa63477bfb7e8314d863c4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commit/fb0a35af47d1994d327099963ab1e388666570f5","sha":"fb0a35af47d1994d327099963ab1e388666570f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/fb0a35af47d1994d327099963ab1e388666570f5"}],"sha":"4f9af5f1e425c267f95241fce9ca7bfe5020d4b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/4f9af5f1e425c267f95241fce9ca7bfe5020d4b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20686545?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom","id":20686545,"login":"miguelperezcolom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg2NTQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/fb0a35af47d1994d327099963ab1e388666570f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:38:52Z","email":"miguelperezcolom@gmail.com","name":"Miguel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:38:52Z","email":"miguelperezcolom@gmail.com","name":"Miguel"},"message":"fix(vaadin): the generated accent strip tiles without a seam\n\nAt the shell''s 10px band height the 1440×24 generated strip scales to a 600px tile repeated with\nrepeat-x, and shapes cut at the tile''s right edge stopped dead where the next tile started afresh\n(seen on ec-demo1''s journey pages).\n\nAccentStrip now draws a periodic SVG: every motif (shape + its dot/dash texture) that crosses the\nright edge is also drawn shifted by -width, and every one crossing the left edge (the walk starts\nat x=-20) shifted by +width, each copy right after its original so overlaps stack the same way on\nboth sides of the seam. The random walk is unchanged, so the original elements are byte-identical;\nonly the wrapped copies are added (default strip 9.2 KB -> 9.3 KB, worst doc example 12.9 KB).\nStretching one tile across the page instead would distort the shapes and only push the seam out,\nso the CSS sizing (background-size: auto <h>, repeat-x) is left as is; hand-declared accentStrip\nimages are untouched.\n\nTests: a render-free seamlessness check (the shapes covering x=width, shifted by -width, equal the\nshapes covering x=0, in drawing order) over colours, seeds and sizes incl. widths narrower than a\ns