tps://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/9adde779b27d2bef869dd939a222b0ba64020c0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:04:08Z","email":"miguelperezcolom@gmail.com","name":"Miguel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:04:08Z","email":"miguelperezcolom@gmail.com","name":"Miguel"},"message":"feat(vaadin): a generated accent strip — @App(accentColor) alone gets a Redwood-style band\n\nAn app with an accent and no strip image used to get a plain line in the accent colour in the\nVaadin shell. Mateu now draws the strip itself: hills, arches, peaks and blocks with a dot/dash\ntexture, in a palette derived from the accent in HLS (port of ec-demo1''s deploy/branding/strip.py).\n\n- io.mateu.core.infra.AccentStrip: palette(), svg(color, seed[, w, h]) and dataUri(); a seeded\n  random walk, deterministic per (colour, seed, size), cached.\n- @App(accentStripSeed, default 7); @App(accentStrip): blank = generated, a URL = the app''s image\n  (as before), \"none\" = plain band.\n- AppDto.accentStrip keeps carrying only what the app declared; the generated strip travels in a\n  new AppDto.generatedAccentStrip, read by the Vaadin shell only — the Redwood renderer and its\n  payload are unchanged (it keeps its own Spectra strips).\n- Vaadin shell: applyAccent accepts a base64 SVG data URI; bundle regenerated.\n- Docs: design-systems/accent-strip (\"Accent colour and strip\"), @App reference updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5bd0c2c0be4c91ce8dcc6ff1aca44006b981605a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/git/trees/5bd0c2c0be4c91ce8dcc6ff1aca44006b981605a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/m