https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commit/8c5aa2455319a6b4864c41263e2c409cb9984d21","node_id":"C_kwDOBNevYdoAKDhjNWFhMjQ1NTMxOWE2YjQ4NjRjNDEyNjNlMmM0MDljYjk5ODRkMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commit/3212670834099c31259182fea56282089aba4c90","sha":"3212670834099c31259182fea56282089aba4c90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/3212670834099c31259182fea56282089aba4c90"}],"sha":"8c5aa2455319a6b4864c41263e2c409cb9984d21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/8c5aa2455319a6b4864c41263e2c409cb9984d21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20686545?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/miguelperezcolom","id":20686545,"login":"miguelperezcolom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjg2NTQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miguelperezcolom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/commits/3212670834099c31259182fea56282089aba4c90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:21:47Z","email":"miguelperezcolom@gmail.com","name":"miguelperezcolom"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:21:47Z","email":"miguelperezcolom@gmail.com","name":"miguelperezcolom"},"message":"feat(listing): multi-line rows — @Line puts a listing column on line 2, 3… of its row\n\nListings with many columns can now show each record on several lines within one\nrow. `@Line(n)` (io.mateu.uidl.annotations, default line 1) assigns a row field\nto a line; it travels as `GridColumn.line` (only lines > 1 go on the wire, so a\nlisting without @Line keeps its exact wire).\n\nWhen a listing has columns beyond line 1:\n- line 1 = the line-1 columns as today (header labels, sorting, widths);\n- line 2+ = the other columns as secondary «Label: value» pairs under line 1,\n  spanning the row.\n\nRenderers\n- Vaadin (mateu-table): line-1 columns are the grid''s columns; the extra lines\n  go in the row-details area, kept open for every row. The @Details toggle keeps\n  its own state (chevron/button read it) and its content goes under the lines;\n  values reuse the column cell renderer (status badge, money, link, editor…).\n  Row click / rowRoute, selection, sorting, paging and group rows keep working.\n- Cards (mateu-table-crud): columns ordered line by line, so the \"first six\"\n  are the line-1 ones.\n- Redwood (listingOf + oj-table): table columns = line 1; a 1px technical column\n  (__rowLines, template cellLines) paints the extra lines in an absolute block\n  spanning the row, in the space mateu-lines-N reserves under each cell.\n\nShared helper libs/mateu listingLines.ts (splitLines/byLine/lineOf). Schemas\n(uidl/specs) and the TS GridColumn DTO carry `line`.\n\nTests: core ListingColumnLineTest, vitest listingLines.test.ts, Redwood poc\ntest \"filas de varias líneas (@Line)\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b1914abe6abc086eb66c32fd03805da2cfef2cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/mateu/git/trees/3b1914abe6abc086eb66c32fd03805da2cfef2cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/miguelperezcolom/m