/api.github.com/users/xitij2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xitij2000","id":118837,"login":"xitij2000","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODgzNw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xitij2000","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/paragon/commits/b46e24186668027657f5e0abcc77800967e0df05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-03T15:21:24Z","email":"kshitij@sobti.in","name":"Kshitij Sobti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-03T15:21:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Better support for multiple themes (#2792)\n\n* feat: Better support for multiple themes\n\nThis change adds support for two CLI options to the build-tokens\ncommand.\n\nThe first, --all-themes makes the build-tokens command process all\nthemes in the source directory as opposed to specifying all the names\nvia --theme.\n\nSecondly, --base-paragon-theme allows you to have multiple themes derived\nfrom the same common base. If specified, you can have a derived theme that\nstill loads tokens from the light theme. For example, you can have a\nsite theme called ''theme-one'' and set the base theme to light so it will\nreuse the core light theme tokens and layer on changes from ''theme-one''.\n\n* fixup! feat: Better support for multiple themes\n\n* fixup! fixup! feat: Better support for multiple themes","tree":{"sha":"bdb169bacb872565b94ef28fb3d7710c6a455606","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/paragon/git/trees/bdb169bacb872565b94ef28fb3d7710c6a455606"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openedx/paragon/git/commits/b46e24186668027657f5e0abcc77800967e0df05","verification":{"payload":"tree bdb169bacb872565b94ef28fb3d7710c6a455606\nparent 04e52615ba76423342dfd27f4eff63cc6a54b85f\nauthor Kshitij Sobti <kshitij@sobti.in> 1762183284 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1762183284 -0500\n\nfeat: Better support for multiple themes (#2792)\n\n* feat: Better support for multiple themes\n\nThis change adds support for two CLI options to the build-tokens\ncommand.\n\nThe first, --all-themes makes the build-tokens command process all\nthemes in the source directory as opposed to specifying all the names\nvia --theme.\n\nSecondly, --base-paragon-theme allows you to have multiple themes derived\nfrom the same common base. If specified, you can have a derived theme that\nstill loads tokens from the light theme. For example, you can have a\nsite theme called ''theme-one'' and set the base theme to light so it will\nreuse the core light theme tokens and layer on changes from ''theme-one''.\n\n* fixup! feat: Better support for multiple themes\n\n* fixup! fixup! feat: Better support for multiple themes","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpCMh0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdDwQAGDDibmrMQwBw01OX/2QmS4+\ny1PkiFsEMTzSqcwvZawCyZRNg90M90JeJsGknVDUYUJpXzMY1Ksf0cesO9QCyp0K\nk7H8vgtmXptVc6FOXpIqsGukObrn7GLA2AvqXJ5OW0ZPCJ1bpSR0PYojQxKASf+g\nrYV8AF/44511nrVfilSdo/h7uQTmEiCVam+QV7T+yKEfVZd3OkNFWC2eTvaZA9hX\n5odciqblRMTd+ksl2dVgUNnS9i2sKsYivOA/+pRy0Ge/sFX14MKJ02UOKV8yzMAn\nBHovH42vyXNp5NEJYYDtF8lv9Y3dYCkWDo90PfcnLUPJbyytmYXmtOREczHnRsr1\nOA0bJRID9/z/vRwt4M0esVYmuXz56SdzflP2f3EEr2MUrxTDPgRTeA8bCBXd0hhV\nGFXRs/ClQGIm2QfV/OLeHA8QmoMcZtx49JOG8c/wC1AIW/Yzn9KoNnTrC4iCNXwf\njf54rsmIAIBV2gS0F0uEA7Ud/u8RD3BOU8EeZacJ4I+9a5vxb1PvOgucObHs/Qrt\n0BUiOGHa/dA4wY340iE6osXrXCQT6QFDPTrnXXqxrWlXedJ+vNT6QW4FDENZrpdT\nMh94/UjgLq2o2CuK2vrjvLvUiDEbzxIGFWyrKAYEUn2H9xWzBesdGEVCMHfHZI8i\n9t4XXshKXZ93DUbAvZ