:"","html_url":"https://github.com/JulianWielga","id":965924,"login":"JulianWielga","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTkyNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulianWielga/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulianWielga/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulianWielga/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulianWielga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulianWielga/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulianWielga","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TouK/nussknacker/commits/0635b69e74da1428bde0cb5e6d0a5b145234c1a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-14T09:48:52Z","email":"j@touk.pl","name":"JulianWielga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-14T09:48:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"local storage scenario draft  (#9290)\n\n* feat: draft hack - save scenario state as sticky note on validation failure\n\nWhen debug.scenario.enableDraftHack user setting is enabled:\n- On save failure, packs nodes/edges/stickyNotes into a draft sticky note and retries\n- On fetch, detects draft sticky note and restores the original scenario graph\n\n* feat: persist scenario drafts in localStorage via storage abstraction\n\nReplace the sticky-note draft hack with a ScenarioDraftStorage interface\n(async get/save/delete) backed by localStorage, wired through a redux\nmiddleware that debounces saves on graph-mutation actions and restores\non DISPLAY_PROCESS when the draft''s base version matches the server.\nSwapping to a remote backend later only requires a new storage impl.\n\n* feat: persist scenario drafts via redux-persist with undoable apply\n\nReplace the sticky-note draft hack with a dedicated persisted scenarioDraft\nslice. A listener driven by state-path predicates (not an action whitelist)\nsyncs edits into the slice; redux-persist handles storage. On scenario load\nthe draft is replayed via a new APPLY_SCENARIO_DRAFT action so the user can\nundo back to the clean loaded scenario. When undo history empties, the\nstored draft is cleared, keeping \"no undoable changes\" in sync with\n\"no stored draft\".\n\n* feat: gate scenario draft persistence behind scenario.enableDraft flag\n\n* feat: skip route-leaving prompt when draft is enabled, flush on exit\n\n* feat: key scenario drafts by processName + baseVersionId\n\n* feat: skip unsaved-changes prompt when draft is enabled (version change, archive)\n\n* feat: show local draft notice in activity panel with discard for current version\n\n* fix: observe activity row size changes so virtualized list reflows\n\n* fix: sync scenario draft actions across tabs to prevent overwrite\n\n* feat: persistent warning when draft is overwritten in another session\n\n* refactor: per-scenario draft backend with (processName, versionId) API\n\nReplace the string-keyed backend with one that takes processName and\nversionId directly; list is scoped to a scenario. Drop the redux-persist\nwrapper in favour of a single draftListener that owns autosave, backend\nI/O, hydrate-on-scenario-change, undoable restore, and cross-tab\noverwrite warning. Reorder middlewares: listenerMiddleware and thunk\nstay as infra; business middlewares sit together in concat.\n\n* refactor: centralise unsaved-changes prompt + reuse useUserSettings/createSelector\n\nAdd useUnsavedChangesPrompt hook that decides between silent flush+proceed\n(when scenario.enableDraft is on and the in-memory graph already matches\nthe persisted draft) and the legacy DISCARD/CANCEL confirm dialog. Use it\nfrom RouteLeavingGuard, useArchiveHelper and ActivityItemHeader. Hide the\nlocal-draft activity-row notice when the draft flag is off. Replace ad-hoc\ndraftEnabled selectors with the existing useUserSettings hook and a\nmemoised createSelector in the draftListener.\n\n* fix: route guard always blocks on unsaved changes; alert when draft writes pending\n\nTrack in-flight / failed backend draft writes in a module-level Set.\nuseUnsavedChangesPrompt treats a pending key as out-of-sync and falls\nback to the confirm dialog instead of silently proceeding.\nuseRouteLeavingGuard always blocks router navigation when there are\nunsaved changes and lets promptOrProceed decide flush-vs-confirm; the\nbeforeunload handler triggers the native alert whenever drafts are off\nor some draft write hasn''t been persisted yet.\n\n* refactor: generic ScenarioDraftBackend carries typed Draft, not JSON strings\n\nMove the Draft shape into draftStorage/types.ts (source of truth) with\na generic DraftBackend API so backend implementations own their own\n(de)serialisation. localStorageBackend now JSON-encodes internally; the\nlistener and reducer hand typed Draft objects around directly. Rename\nthe public field to ''id'' and ''data'' to stay neutral about what the\nbackend stores, with re-exports kept as ScenarioDraft for existing\ncall-sites.\n\n* refactor: type-safe matchers for scenarioDraft listeners; merge SET / add CLEAR sync warnings\n\n* feat: warn about new scenario version created in another session\n\nAfter a successful save dispatch scenarioDraftClear for the pre-save\nbaseVersionId (so the now-persisted draft is removed everywhere) and\nscenarioVersionBumped with the new versionId. Both are broadcast via\nredux-state-sync. Other tabs viewing the same scenario replace the\ndraft-overwritten notification with a sticky version-bump warning that\nnames the new version number.\n\n* refactor: split scenarioDraft actions/creators into scenarioDraftActions","tree":{"sha":"63ba3223e4ceeb876462f3e1a424e0bbe84eefb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TouK/nussknacker/git/trees/63ba3223e4ceeb876462f3e1a424e0bbe84eefb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TouK/nussknacker/git/commits/0635b69e74da1428bde0cb5e6d0a5b145234c1a6","verification":{"payload":"tree 63ba3223e4ceeb876462f3e1a424e0bbe84eefb1\nparent a07645407654178dbcb900137d2edafbbfb80813\nauthor JulianWielga <j@touk.pl> 1776160132 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776160132 +0200\n\nlocal storage scenario draft  (#9290)\n\n* feat: draft hack - save scenario state as sticky note on validation failure\n\nWhen debug.scenario.enableDraftHack user setting is enabled:\n- On save failure, packs nodes/edges/stickyNotes into a draft sticky note and retries\n- On fetch, detects draft sticky note and restores the original scenario graph\n\n* feat: persist scenario drafts in localStorage via storage abstraction\n\nReplace the sticky-note draft hack with a ScenarioDraftStorage interface\n(async get/save/delete) backed by localStorage, wired through a redux\nmiddleware that debounces saves on graph-mutation actions and restores\non DISPLAY_PROCESS when the draft''s base version matches the server.\nSwapping to a remote backend later only requires a new storage impl.\n\n* feat: persist scenario drafts via redux-persist with undoable apply\n\nReplace the sticky-note draft hack with a dedicated persisted scenarioDraft\nslice. A listener driven by state-path predicates (not an action whitelist)\nsyncs edits into the slice; redux-persist handles storage. On scenario load\nthe draft is replayed via a new APPLY_SCENARIO_DRAFT action so the user can\nundo back to the clean loaded scenario. When undo history empties, the\nstored draft is cleared, keeping \"no undoable changes\" in sync with\n\"no stored draft\".\n\n* feat: gate scenario draft persistence behind scenario.enableDraft flag\n\n* feat: skip route-leaving prompt when draft is enabled, flush on exit\n\n* feat: key scenario drafts by processName + baseVersionId\n\n* feat: skip unsaved-changes prompt when draft is enabled (version change, archive)\n\n* feat: show local draft notice in activity panel with discard for current version\n\n* fix: observe activity row size changes so virtualized list reflows\n\n* fix: sync scenario draft actions across tabs to prevent overwrite\n\n* feat: persistent warning when draft is overwritten in another session\n\n* refactor: per-scenario draft backend with (processName, versionId) API\n\nReplace the string-keyed backend with one that takes processName and\nversionId directly; list is scoped to a scenario. Drop the redux-persist\nwrapper in favour of a single draftListener that owns autosave, backend\nI/O, hydrate-on-scenario-change, undoable restore, and cross-tab\noverwrite warning. Reorder middlewares: listenerMiddleware and thunk\nstay as infra; business middlewares sit together in concat.\n\n* refactor: centralise unsaved-changes prompt + reuse useUserSettings/createSelector\n\nAdd useUnsavedChangesPrompt hook that decides between silent flush+proceed\n(when scenario.enableDraft is on and the in-memory graph already matches\nthe persisted draft) and the legacy DISCARD/CANCEL confirm dialog. Use it\nfrom RouteLeavingGuard, useArchiveHelper and ActivityItemHeader. Hide the\nlocal-draft activity-row notice when the draft flag is off. Replace ad-hoc\ndraftEnabled selectors with the existing useUserSettings hook and a\nmemoised createSelector in the draftListener.\n\n* fix: route guard always blocks on unsaved changes; alert when draft writes pending\n\nTrack in-flight / failed backend draft writes in a module-level Set.\nuseUnsavedChangesPrompt treats a pending key as out-of-sync and falls\nback to the confirm dialog instead of silently proceeding.\nuseRouteLeavingGuard always blocks router navigation when there are\nunsaved changes and lets promptOrProceed decide flush-vs-confirm; the\nbeforeunload handler triggers the native alert whenever drafts are off\nor some draft write hasn''t been persisted yet.\n\n* refactor: generic ScenarioDraftBackend carries typed Draft, not JSON strings\n\nMove the Draft shape into draftStorage/types.ts (source of truth) with\na generic DraftBackend API so backend implementations own their own\n(de)serialisation. localStorageBackend now JSON-encodes internally; the\nlistener and reducer hand typed Draft objects around directly. Rename\nthe public field to ''id'' and ''data'' to stay neutral about what the\nbackend stores, with re-exports kept as ScenarioDraft for existing\ncall-sites.\n\n* refactor: type-safe matchers for scenarioDraft listeners; merge SET / add CLEAR sync warnings\n\n* feat: warn about new scenario version created in another session\n\nAfter a successful save dispatch scenarioDraftClear for the pre-save\nbaseVersionId (so the now-persisted draft is removed everywhere) and\nscenarioVersionBumped with the new versionId. Both are broadcast via\nredux-state-sync. Other tabs viewing the same scenario replace the\ndraft-overwritten notification with a sticky version-bump warning that\nnames the new version number.\n\n* refactor: split scenarioDraft actions/creators into scenarioDraftActions","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3g2ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/scQAIuBYh1Fu1Dts+UYITW5ZybY\ny365di6QkiH4hVm7FNB0A/QNGUt8gdtIPbQeFHfa/aJUtMvbfUTnTX8PBYJkBpUp\n9JUOWYwq0WLYFNQppielii/0vCFxYRYrIcC9oa4FZfuDGvXxHCKgy05O7AAuPBo8\nVUvY9w6ldeAMKnYyboYTufJaQNN84bTUrytcAE96EatGjP45kwzGm1QJYwNnaD88\nTFrquCNJFDTk49fVgdHdKHQQFM6McuQStCuD4TB43fzlZAcCC9C4YJ4tqRUrqMah\ndpN/uWoISxc7BalfSUO609THOhe5I4htR2n8HJQfUukGv0OwY8xO49kFWGbZDmrm\nsw236A/VwXsjGtT9pjcFLzWMEYM/WupkkI9Fvgt0ER4opTIzexwA1bk3BXBNN9gD\nQo+D548fzwi250/quZfloSMTlKvivZrLkjc8Ajw48TTz28jlan6FwjnNlut1Nf7i\nSRyel3P6ZAlg7/EOQJOo5Sow5Rngbr7coiI8ZeHkBfPLElWs8S8x4QPI5lC12Mnx\nLDo9KzrOYY1QMQn15fQtLGIc+zyTb72ElztCG0ghY+ZfNUJklsg7stHwtfeg3YXT\nWLIlbg17wtOgVkPvac4A2+ONfMZns24jQ26HXb4D6pscC8awAtYsIkvwdL0xx+aG\nhPYsKq79R5CGe/mu4RVb\n=LPcJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-14T09:48:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"