OBdusrNoAKDkxZGIzYjAyN2Y0ZDVlYmE1ZjIzMDAzN2NjMTkzMzYxOTg1MGJiMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/frontend-permission-toolkit/commit/23ab3055133661116c7ef44620281fd35f9ce088","sha":"23ab3055133661116c7ef44620281fd35f9ce088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/frontend-permission-toolkit/commits/23ab3055133661116c7ef44620281fd35f9ce088"}],"sha":"91db3b027f4d5eba5f230037cc1933619850bb22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/frontend-permission-toolkit/commits/91db3b027f4d5eba5f230037cc1933619850bb22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11871778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ValeriaMaltseva","id":11871778,"login":"ValeriaMaltseva","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODcxNzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/frontend-permission-toolkit/commits/23ab3055133661116c7ef44620281fd35f9ce088/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T18:41:56Z","email":"valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com","name":"Valeriia Maltseva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T18:41:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup) (#138)\n\n* [Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup)\n\nReplaces the committed, expanded src/Resources/public/studio/build/ tree with a single\ncontent-addressed build-dist/build-<id>.zip that studio-ui-bundle''s\nBuildArchiveExtractionTrait reconstructs at cache warmup. 16 committed build\nfiles become one 352K archive, removing the per-build file churn and merge\nconflicts the \"Automatic frontend build\" commits used to cause.\n\n- WebpackEntryPointProvider implements BuildArchiveProviderInterface via the\n  shared trait; the interface_exists() guard is dropped since studio-ui-bundle\n  is a hard composer requirement.\n- rsbuild.config.ts derives the build id from source content (getBuildGroupId +\n  pluginWriteBuildId) instead of a random uuid, and the clean-up step keeps the\n  current build dir because studio-package-build picks the lexicographically\n  greatest .build-id on disk.\n- CI switches to reusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml, watching\n  build-dist/** on push and deliberately not on pull_request, so the workflow''s\n  own archive commit does not retrigger it.\n- composer requires ^2026.2.1, the first release shipping the Build/* classes.\n- No npm change: @pimcore/studio-ui-bundle is already ^2026.2.10, past the\n  ^2026.2.1 that first shipped the Build/* classes, ./bundler/build-id,\n  pluginWriteBuildId and the studio-package-build CLI. package-lock.json is\n  untouched and package.json gains only the package-build script.\n\nSee https://github.com/pimcore/platform-version/issues/247\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Document the entry point array types for PHPStan\n\nDropping the interface_exists() guard means the provider is now a top-level\nclass, so PHPStan analyses it where it previously skipped the conditionally\ndeclared one, and reports \"return type has no value type specified in iterable\ntype array\" for both accessors. Both return lists of entry point names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revise upgrade information for version 2026.2.1\n\nUpdated upgrade information for version 2026.2.1 and removed details for version 2026.1.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"be02edaca2bc6dfa84cbc08c5505ed1eb69cc395","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/frontend-permission-toolkit/git/trees/be02edaca2bc6dfa84cbc08c5505ed1eb69cc395"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/frontend-permission-toolkit/git/commits/23ab3055133661116c7ef44620281fd35f9ce088","verification":{"payload":"tree be02edaca2bc6dfa84cbc08c5505ed1eb69cc395\nparent a0715c30caf232162c03ee44167f8bb0287da8bb\nauthor Valeriia Maltseva <valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com> 1789756916 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789756916 +0200\n\n[Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup) (#138)\n\n* [Studio] Ship frontend build as a committed archive (extracted at cache warmup)\n\nReplaces the committed, expanded src/Resources/public/studio/build/ tree with a single\ncontent-addressed build-dist/build-<id>.zip that studio-ui-bundle''s\nBuildArchiveExtractionTrait reconstructs at cache warmup. 16 committed build\nfiles become one 352K archive, removing the per-build file churn and merge\nconflicts the \"Automatic frontend build\" commits used to cause.\n\n- WebpackEntryPointProvider implements BuildArchiveProviderInterface via the\n  shared trait; the interface_exists() guard is dropped since studio-ui-bundle\n  is a hard composer requirement.\n- rsbuild.config.ts derives the build id from source content (getBuildGroupId +\n  pluginWriteBuildId) instead of a random uuid, and the clean-up step keeps the\n  current build dir because studio-package-build picks the lexicographically\n  greatest .build-id on disk.\n- CI switches to reusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml, watching\n  build-dist/** on push and deliberately not on pull_request, so the workflow''s\n  own archive commit does not retrigger it.\n- composer requires ^2026.2.1, the first release shipping the Build/* classes.\n- No npm change: @pimcore/studio-ui-bundle is already ^2026.2.10, past the\n  ^2026.2.1 that first shipped the Build/* classes, ./bundler/build-id,\n  pluginWriteBuildId and the studio-package-build CLI. package-lock.json is\n  untouched and package.json gains only the package-build script.\n\nSee https://github.com/pimcore/platform-version/issues/247\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Document the entry point array types for PHPStan\n\nDropping the interface_exists() guard means the provider is now a top-level\nclass, so PHPStan analyses it where it previously skipped the conditionally\ndeclared one, and reports \"return type has no value type specified in iterable\ntype array\" for both accessors. Both return lists of entry point names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revise upgrade information for version 2026.2.1\n\nUpdated upgrade information for version 2026.2.1 and removed details for version 2026.1.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrYX0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFD0QAKYOnDpCiQotuvEoBui3YR2g\nsCAFavPozAvDCCP33ZUq+yy8yIo004yGW501k+MUm6uGY1RfVvmkT3EUysVyDGIR\njVQnI+m68Lo5SZtvWCOundUD7WxRW8tVzj1qiW5NUmRbvLbYIp/X3y4akntSA0+7\n0RDBStqZKh+Dy6sl9sfZ2lZ9CadXOi0lCsJKiB2Xv5/G6TB/NkLNhVAds+sbR8mR\nlXUrTaFeZ596nT