08a6d25038fcbdcddb781e","sha":"00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e"}],"sha":"b035653204ab0da12f1c8ea7eceb71c643bca91c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b035653204ab0da12f1c8ea7eceb71c643bca91c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:10:02Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:10:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): resolve critical npm audit advisories (#37334)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe nightly [NPM\nAudit](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/workflows/npm-audit.yml)\nworkflow has failed on master since October 7 ([failing\nrun](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/37706706894/job/113082677130)).\nAdvisories published on October 5 and 6 flag six packages that the\nlockfile resolves below the patched version:\n\n| Package | Advisory | Locked | Patched |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `tinypool` |\n[GHSA-5gmw-xhrv-c9v3](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5gmw-xhrv-c9v3),\n[GHSA-85c8-ppgw-ccpr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-85c8-ppgw-ccpr)\n| 2.1.0 | 2.1.2 |\n| `proxy-addr` |\n[GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h)\n| 2.0.7 | 2.0.8 |\n| `seroval` |\n[GHSA-p6vx-979v-rg4c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-p6vx-979v-rg4c)\n| 1.6.0 | 1.6.2 |\n| `shell-quote` |\n[GHSA-pqg4-j6r4-53mv](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pqg4-j6r4-53mv)\n| 1.8.4 | 1.11.0 |\n| `simple-git` |\n[GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh)\n| 3.36.0 | 4.0.1 |\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` |\n[GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c)\n| 1.1.1 | 2.0.1 |\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe lockfile resolves tinypool 2.2.0, proxy-addr 2.0.8, seroval 1.6.8,\nshell-quote 1.12.0 and simple-git 4.0.2, and the audit reports no\ncritical advisories. The repo formats its files with oxfmt 0.72.0. No\npublished package or generator version changes.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `oxfmt` 0.60.0 pinned `tinypool` to exactly 2.1.0. The repo''s `oxfmt`\nmoves to 0.72.0, which depends on `tinypool` 2.2.0, so `tinypool` needs\nno override.\n- The `seroval` and `shell-quote` overrides already existed, and their\nfloors move to the patched versions. `proxy-addr` gets a new caret\noverride, like the other single-line overrides.\n- `simple-git` gets a caret override to 4.0.2, the first release that\nfixes both advisories. Its only consumer, `@nuxt/devtools`, wants 3.x,\nand 4.x breaks its dev-server module. Nothing in the repo starts a Nuxt\ndev server, and Nuxt workspaces that Nx generates still get 3.x.\n- `oxfmt` 0.72.0 reformats 14 files, and none of them ship in a\npublished package. Six TypeScript files keep a last-argument arrow\nfunction with a return type on the call line, matching Prettier 3.9.\nFour Markdown files and four docs pages change under the new Markdown\nformatter. On the docs deploy preview, those pages show the same\ncontent; only two code examples and one YAML example change layout.\n- #37335 changes the `oxfmt` version that `@nx/js` installs in user\nworkspaces.\n- pnpm flips the `optional` flag on four `bunyan` dependencies, as it\ndid in earlier lockfile updates.","tree":{"sha":"3b881b171d789c1511d82e1c7e9afb7f22143c89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/3b881b171d789c1511d82e1c7e9afb7f22143c89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b881b171d789c1511d82e1c7e9afb7f22143c89\nparent dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1791465002 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791465002 -0400\n\nchore(repo): resolve critical npm audit advisories (#37334)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe nightly [NPM\nAudit](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/workflows/npm-audit.yml)\nworkflow has failed on master since October 7 ([failing\nrun](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/37706706894/job/113082677130)).\nAdvisories published on October 5 and 6 flag six packages that the\nlockfile resolves below the patched version:\n\n| Package | Advisory | Locked | Patched |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `tinypool` |\n[GHSA-5gmw-xhrv-c9v3](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5gmw-xhrv-c9v3),\n[GHSA-85c8-ppgw-ccpr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-85c8-ppgw-ccpr)\n| 2.1.0 | 2.1.2 |\n| `proxy-addr` |\n[GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jqcg-44mw-7w3h)\n| 2.0.7 | 2.0.8 |\n| `seroval` |\n[GHSA-p6vx-979v-rg4c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-p6vx-979v-rg4c)\n| 1.6.0 | 1.6.2 |\n| `shell-quote` |\n[GHSA-pqg4-j6r4-53mv](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pqg4-j6r4-53mv)\n| 1.8.4 | 1.11.0 |\n| `simple-git` |\n[GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh)\n| 3.36.0 | 4.0.1 |\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` |\n[GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c)\n| 1.1.1 | 2.0.1 |\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe lockfile resolves tinypool 2.2.0, proxy-addr 2.0.8, seroval 1.6.8,\nshell-quote 1.12.0 and simple-git 4.0.2, and the audit reports no\ncritical advisories. The repo formats its files with oxfmt 0.72.0. No\npublished package or generator version changes.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `oxfmt` 0.60.0 pinned `tinypool` to exactly 2.1.0. The repo''s `oxfmt`\nmoves to 0.72.0, which depends on `tinypool` 2.2.0, so `tinypool` needs\nno override.\n- The `seroval` and `shell-quote` overrides already existed, and their\nfloors move to the patched versions. `proxy-addr` gets a new caret\noverride, like the other single-line overrides.\n- `simple-git` gets a caret override to 4.0.2, the first release that\nfixes both advisories. Its only consumer, `@nuxt/devtools`, wants 3.x,\nand 4.x breaks its dev-server module. Nothing in the repo starts a Nuxt\ndev server, and Nuxt workspaces that Nx generates still get 3.x.\n- `oxfmt` 0.72.0 reformats 14 files, and none of them ship in a\npublished package. Six TypeScript files keep a last-argument arrow\nfunction with a return type on the call line, matching Prettier 3.9.\nFour Markdown files and four docs pages change under the new Markdown\nformatter. On the docs deploy preview, those pages show the same\ncontent; only two code examples and one YAML example change layout.\n- #37335 changes the `oxfmt` version that `@nx/js` installs in user\nworkspaces.\n- pnpm flips the `optional` flag on four `bunyan` dependencies, as it\ndid in earlier lockfile updates.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5YqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnWQQACLiyOF5NvbTD9lRIuXcygyb\nHEik2fNGVDN0HkjY1ehdto4Qq4cb1i2y8obS5+tRa10uRw9faWc6UrkMsXb5dUMI\n4zwLWSuCC6lJpz4I/cQK1ukTQEKCFQmTgghDYfQvVvpfWtJiOMHbYzoZwFgehiEU\nbOdUm035m/btel9jGzFyvQJZ1X2ewyZU+mmymYmQS6mGEA7s/Bmtz4OtcU+8xHzL\n7B7uDILmCpS/E+l9s2pAfKS7pQtFGF7WXzV83QtVBdVVbWHBHBGtb3l/bkEAo0Fa\nZfdrG9REpMy0+fsmPASHyhWWCyzs6Q9VEchnmt36RteAkBTIip5vNyDcH6scmUI2\nGKMW5bEd8QJSz7RO9TEnZ/O1FkpLu+e6KntNbof0lfi4e089BJg/CFAdWVGuI6KZ\ndYWqc2TEFLPgmsPneKbDUXNlMT6e4u9jmKourXSsdGyFJn1pqbEI6tx9SkZDzTEg\nxMeCk0mHWPqE+QMtd87s7TBmyI/Ki2txmoxpPqp2MqbMQZnb6/VngRCOJ/AZ5YOt\nGCJODb/uL7/A4p+VeysP5HHE7qfLjFefgcNkeKXt7QSSpfZED+6NAwLlsXvR6wJX\nfBn8o9AsNmEZ+3KbE9zVo7PN+Z7g/l6oD/ek9nXV7TlJG6kvW9ksDKf3cGV2DMet\n5CsMGiFItTakWQzOm7+D\n=CISo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:10:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDAwYjkxY2Q2MTc2ZDczMzkxNjA4YTZkMjUwMzhmY2JkY2RkYjc4MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","sha":"dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173"}],"sha":"00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/00b91cd6176d73391608a6d25038fcbdcddb781e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:03:22Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T12:03:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): let dependsOn opt out of a continuous dependency''s inputs (#37246)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWith task-based affected, an atomized e2e task such as\n`app:e2e-ci--src/feature.test.ts` is affected by every lib the app\nbundles. The planner folds every continuous dependency''s inputs\n(`app:serve`) into the dependent''s hash, so a change to `libs/feature2`\nselects a test that only exercises `libs/feature`.\n\nThere''s no way to opt out. `ultracache.ignoredReads` can''t help: it only\nfilters the task''s own recording, and the server''s inputs are appended\nseparately.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`inputs: false` on a `dependsOn` entry drops that continuous\ndependency''s inputs from the dependent''s hash and affected selection:\n\n```jsonc\n\"dependsOn\": [{ \"projects\": [\"app\"], \"target\": \"serve\", \"inputs\": false }]\n```\n\n- Scheduling is unchanged; the server still starts first.\n- Servers reached only through an opted-out edge drop out too. A server\nalso reached through an edge with inputs still counts.\n- Affected and the hash stay in sync, since affected reads the same hash\nplans. The plan memo and task graph fingerprint include the new edges.\n- On a regular (non-continuous) dependency the flag has no effect, since\nthose inputs were never part of the dependent''s hash.\n\nDocs: `reference/inputs.mdoc` and\n`reference/project-configuration.mdoc`.\n\nFollow-ups stacked on this PR: `always` inputs and the `@nx-depends-on`\ntest file directive.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Scope-e2e-tasks-inputs-false-always-inputs-nx-depends-on-094b3973\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc59265c87c36b6a1171769fefbe8710d81739be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/bc59265c87c36b6a1171769fefbe8710d81739be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","verification":{"payload":"tree bc59265c87c36b6a1171769fefbe8710d81739be\nparent f2140568fa2de6ec96fad98a4dd060218a91a4e1\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1791461002 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791461002 -0400\n\nfeat(core): let dependsOn opt out of a continuous dependency''s inputs (#37246)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWith task-based affected, an atomized e2e task such as\n`app:e2e-ci--src/feature.test.ts` is affected by every lib the app\nbundles. The planner folds every continuous dependency''s inputs\n(`app:serve`) into the dependent''s hash, so a change to `libs/feature2`\nselects a test that only exercises `libs/feature`.\n\nThere''s no way to opt out. `ultracache.ignoredReads` can''t help: it only\nfilters the task''s own recording, and the server''s inputs are appended\nseparately.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`inputs: false` on a `dependsOn` entry drops that continuous\ndependency''s inputs from the dependent''s hash and affected selection:\n\n```jsonc\n\"dependsOn\": [{ \"projects\": [\"app\"], \"target\": \"serve\", \"inputs\": false }]\n```\n\n- Scheduling is unchanged; the server still starts first.\n- Servers reached only through an opted-out edge drop out too. A server\nalso reached through an edge with inputs still counts.\n- Affected and the hash stay in sync, since affected reads the same hash\nplans. The plan memo and task graph fingerprint include the new edges.\n- On a regular (non-continuous) dependency the flag has no effect, since\nthose inputs were never part of the dependent''s hash.\n\nDocs: `reference/inputs.mdoc` and\n`reference/project-configuration.mdoc`.\n\nFollow-ups stacked on this PR: `always` inputs and the `@nx-depends-on`\ntest file directive.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Scope-e2e-tasks-inputs-false-always-inputs-nx-depends-on-094b3973\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx4aKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKI8QADdhweXe9pE+ftgtL/EyQMd4\nrLXk/XeDylSvhkF7UZn1Ja0KC3Lgffz2xA3I/UzXVZsqfvhnwsakXA6WEYF+h7aI\nzoauK5RkTzx78/hK5P11m44GeFYAkObmIdctnzHf/mnaO9RGeYN9ALvjPx27TaF2\nSoOTDqPL1+K1rnDnjHSEfMy/bUGfgaTHKNfHXU9cJ7dZKFeUwA+qa2ZL7CdXWGoE\n85gxc+fyB4M97JpLg8ievhs2N/4FH15p49V/r0rOy9wCS7BK5GdDoTwJtnJAroDT\nWeUUVNeO4qYcS92twpX6wqezcXPgtpT3Qz+KhXsPbux/q5jtQJL8jIdY9rsQKEEn\n0XLvzToC851N8xQPeqZUSzGsZY2AWTUNjyeYuUpCnzTDpFogp6gPiScQVciIJRcI\nTZ1Ow2cQJLx/hkCJu+E7BUssOXojgp5DmMvuLTNyKiX0zi2SgdnV/U7i0VrsbiZJ\nx+rIkE97mI4XRCpyUyAYSn6MCs8dx/sqVWdsKpu7qqXAfsx7eoQjCv/L71TaZ5+r\n7fyvxhqEBVqwHPewiuHrY99GWr8BLhCykhpueBLMA2nnSgR/N/EClNgD9YOqd9To\nx5TlaRwkxTkxYCeceLiE2OpJttgxi3QLzJak8e9MmSA9jahyvSEn2BdG3oJU+4vY\n5UbaIeyCIqOaUWxPXa8U\n=QKfN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T12:03:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGRjM2RjMzQyZjQ1YTNhYzcyNzA4ZDBhZTUyODFkZjk5OWE2YjYxNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/f2140568fa2de6ec96fad98a4dd060218a91a4e1","sha":"f2140568fa2de6ec96fad98a4dd060218a91a4e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f2140568fa2de6ec96fad98a4dd060218a91a4e1"}],"sha":"dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/dc3dc342f45a3ac72708d0ae5281df999a6b6173"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6933928?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AgentEnder","id":6933928,"login":"AgentEnder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzM5Mjg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AgentEnder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f2140568fa2de6ec96fad98a4dd060218a91a4e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T22:14:31Z","email":"craigorycoppola@gmail.com","name":"Craigory Coppola"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T22:14:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): stop three specs flaking on temp workspace cleanup and process order (#37309)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\n\nThree specs fail intermittently on a loaded machine. The `@nx/js`\ntypescript plugin spec removes its temp workspace while a background\nwalk is still writing `.nx/workspace-data`, so the cleanup throws\n`ENOTEMPTY`. The file-lock spec depends on which process starts first,\nand the tmp-dir sandbox wording test prints the real workspace path.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\n\nTemp workspace removal retries until the walk is done, the file-lock\nspec no longer depends on start order, and the wording test masks the\npath. CI on PRs that touch `nx` stops failing on these.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes #","tree":{"sha":"7d0618c22bd1f864629e0889dbb268a515aa28b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/7d0618c22bd1f864629e0889dbb268a515aa28b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/f2140568fa2de6ec96fad98a4dd060218a91a4e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d0618c22bd1f864629e0889dbb268a515aa28b4\nparent d502a3d095e3224d7adcdd38dc8db4a8a7f0dce1\nauthor Craigory Coppola <craigorycoppola@gmail.com> 1791411271 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791411271 -0400\n\nfix(core): stop three specs flaking on temp workspace cleanup and process order (#37309)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\n\nThree specs fail intermittently on a loaded machine. The `@nx/js`\ntypescript plugin spec removes its temp workspace while a background\nwalk is still writing `.nx/workspace-data`, so the cleanup throws\n`ENOTEMPTY`. The file-lock spec depends on which process starts first,\nand the tmp-dir sandbox wording test prints the real workspace path.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\n\nTemp workspace removal retries until the walk is done, the file-lock\nspec no longer depends on start order, and the wording test masks the\npath. CI on PRs that touch `nx` stops failing on these.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes #","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxsRHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA90UQAJPca65tNyTgrsDW847jiMMv\nv3NhZKfu4NcVOcgopwMFLARmGVijk1tZ32fn/cr2NDYhflpu+pUxoljd+H8ha9Yl\nlRLtI8HwrOA9YZOPrwxggkGUS20o8kZQZ927FVrzYVUD4lzqEnMzG+4CvWrX3rR7\ng4Nf8YTanZLBru/uhC5sS3p06zo2mv2T1aJ6HnIlNDQXipe5c1bqHIuGQULS+fu8\nrg1jhRs+b+zt6uzyeWUvypIS13BmTu7C3Qxh6MMfD9ZM2FVkuT1GuXOduMdAFSWr\nwFKN4wHLrEeS/LWGgR7rLmbt+idmHsRQ1wSfY5Jtnecz3/+9jYS8rptHw7uWeM6S\nBxnPH3KL9KDVhztJ4HCqsijTUK1wMYnq9epsMA/sSfoNQkpHPCXl2DG9QFWsTjgl\nQMCF1AuO6d0cz4tHH/cr1kMH+WcpvygN2ZF46+ToyeiqCVv0VNtonz599PHNCcrj\niI5BvD2S0840C/US2S+Ua3Zv/4ZsvM5btcfWtpIrp4AuNFYppk5vaAlkR/Mwn7tk\n28gDKI+RI5Xby3bDIM3u3za+fK6A29K+rmi3FQaoJpXEdufMHmsubn6bhEd821uE\nKDtY/2CBiitdKMWmi/Fd/xAL20WlFn76gfTwAl