e":"Craigory Coppola"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T21:24:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): drop the Node 24 ERR_USE_AFTER_CLOSE handlers (#37314)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\n\n`create-nx-workspace`, `nx init` and `nx configure-ai-agents` each\ninstall an `uncaughtException` handler that swallows\n`ERR_USE_AFTER_CLOSE`. It was added for enquirer on Node 24, and all\nthree flows now prompt through `@clack/prompts`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\n\nThe three handlers are removed. A pseudo-TTY spec drives a clack prompt\nand a Ctrl-C and asserts no `ERR_USE_AFTER_CLOSE`.\n\nCI never runs these prompts interactively, so please check on Node 24 by\nrunning `npx create-nx-workspace`, `nx init` and `nx\nconfigure-ai-agents` through to the end, then again with Ctrl-C at a\nprompt.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes NXC-5070","tree":{"sha":"3e04e971962442500bb21e57b6681a16034eb1f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/3e04e971962442500bb21e57b6681a16034eb1f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/57a82fc76bb056eb331c44366fa4516e7803118d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e04e971962442500bb21e57b6681a16034eb1f6\nparent 9ef52d1629162cf2b486d35f172195a9fb1d02e7\nauthor Craigory Coppola <craigorycoppola@gmail.com> 1791408254 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791408254 -0400\n\nfix(core): drop the Node 24 ERR_USE_AFTER_CLOSE handlers (#37314)\n\n<!-- Please make sure you have read the submission guidelines before\nposting an PR -->\n<!--\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-a-pr\n-->\n\n<!-- Please make sure that your commit message follows our format -->\n<!-- Example: `fix(nx): must begin with lowercase` -->\n\n<!-- If this is a particularly complex change or feature addition, you\ncan request a dedicated Nx release for this pull request branch. Mention\nsomeone from the Nx team or the `@nrwl/nx-pipelines-reviewers` and they\nwill confirm if the PR warrants its own release for testing purposes,\nand generate it for you if appropriate. -->\n\n## Current Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we have today -->\n\n`create-nx-workspace`, `nx init` and `nx configure-ai-agents` each\ninstall an `uncaughtException` handler that swallows\n`ERR_USE_AFTER_CLOSE`. It was added for enquirer on Node 24, and all\nthree flows now prompt through `@clack/prompts`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n<!-- This is the behavior we should expect with the changes in this PR\n-->\n\nThe three handlers are removed. A pseudo-TTY spec drives a clack prompt\nand a Ctrl-C and asserts no `ERR_USE_AFTER_CLOSE`.\n\nCI never runs these prompts interactively, so please check on Node 24 by\nrunning `npx create-nx-workspace`, `nx init` and `nx\nconfigure-ai-agents` through to the end, then again with Ctrl-C at a\nprompt.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n<!-- Please link the issue being fixed so it gets closed when this is\nmerged. -->\n\nFixes NXC-5070","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxrh+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4AQQACyTTLTVuhU6KYQhM/r1HzEF\nC0GyAlAshy6+EFMKJ7AwGdh7uxkkC0ORXgVSBI4gvOGpVS3YfcgiY3grIy1jUfB