om/u/7008670?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomasboni","id":7008670,"login":"thomasboni","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDg2NzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomasboni","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f7adc8667ad7872ea3bd8b50d72a5096981131d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:20:46Z","email":"thomasboni13@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Boni"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T17:20:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): harden the release and publish workflows (#36599)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n**1. `dawidd6/action-download-artifact` is pinned to v2, which is in an\nadvisory range.** `issue-notifier.yml` uses it to download an artifact\nfrom a different workflow run with `search_artifacts`. Versions before\nv6 are affected by\n[GHSA-5xr6-xhww-33m4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5xr6-xhww-33m4)\n(artifact poisoning, high), where the action can be made to unpack an\nartifact uploaded by an untrusted run into the workspace. That is the\npattern this step uses.\n\n**2. The release build''s cargo cache key is shared across branches.** In\n`publish.yml`, the job that builds the published native binaries\nrestores a cargo cache keyed only on the target triple, so every branch\nthat runs the job shares one entry per target.\n\n**3. Four workflows declare no `permissions:` block.** `ci.yml`,\n`do-not-merge.yml`, `generate-embeddings.yml` and `publish.yml` fall\nback to the repository default token scope for every job, including the\njobs that build and publish the native binaries.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n**1.** Bumped to v21, the current release. It keeps every input used\nhere (`name`, `path`, `search_artifacts`, `allow_forks`), so this is a\npin change and nothing else.\n\n**2.** The ref is added to the cache key, so a release build only\nrestores what that same ref produced. Canary releases from `master` keep\nhitting the cache exactly as before, since the ref does not change. The\n`cache: pnpm` line on the x86 Windows `setup-node` step has no\nequivalent key to scope, so it is dropped. That matrix leg is currently\ncommented out, so it only matters if it is switched back on.\n\n**3.** Scopes are read off what each job actually does rather than\napplied uniformly:\n\n- `ci.yml` checks out and builds, with no API calls anywhere in the\nfile, so `contents: read`.\n- `do-not-merge.yml` reads labels from the event payload and never\nchecks out, so it needs no token.\n- `generate-embeddings.yml` checks out and talks to Supabase and OpenAI\nthrough their own secrets, so `contents: read`.\n- `publish.yml` takes `contents: read` as the default.\n`resolve-required-data` adds `pull-requests: read` because\n`publish-resolve-data.js` calls `pulls.get`, and the two Slack reporters\nget an empty block since they only use the Slack bot token. The\n`publish` and `pr_failure_comment` jobs already scope themselves and are\nuntouched.\n\nOne thing worth knowing if you use a repository-level Actions allowlist:\nentries written as tag patterns (`owner/action@v1`) stop matching once a\nworkflow pins a SHA, and every workflow using that action then fails at\nstartup. Nothing here changes an existing pin, so it should not bite,\nbut the fix is `owner/action@*` in settings.\n\nFound and fixed by [Plumber](https://github.com/getplumber/plumber)''s\nanalysis, reviewed and submitted by me.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNo existing issue, this came out of reading the workflows. Happy to open\none first if you prefer that for changes like this.","tree":{"sha":"a477127bc76aa487b56e5d05d701e880bf304e3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/a477127bc76aa487b56e5d05d701e880bf304e3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/f7adc8667ad7872ea3bd8b50d72a5096981131d7","verification":{"payload":"tree a477127bc76aa487b56e5d05d701e880bf304e3a\nparent 2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8\nauthor Thomas Boni <thomasboni13@gmail.com> 1791393646 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791393646 -0400\n\nchore(repo): harden the release and publish workflows (#36599)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n**1. `dawidd6/action-download-artifact` is pinned to v2, which is in an\nadvisory range.** `issue-notifier.yml` uses it to download an artifact\nfrom a different workflow run with `search_artifacts`. Versions before\nv6 are affected by\n[GHSA-5xr6-xhww-33m4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5xr6-xhww-33m4)\n(artifact poisoning, high), where the action can be made to unpack an\nartifact uploaded by an untrusted run into the workspace. That is the\npattern this step uses.\n\n**2. The release build''s cargo cache key is shared across branches.** In\n`publish.yml`, the job that builds the published native binaries\nrestores a cargo cache keyed only on the target triple, so every branch\nthat runs the job shares one entry per target.\n\n**3. Four workflows declare no `permissions:` block.** `ci.yml`,\n`do-not-merge.yml`, `generate-embeddings.yml` and `publish.yml` fall\nback to the repository default token scope for every job, including the\njobs that build and publish the native binaries.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n**1.** Bumped to v21, the current release. It keeps every input used\nhere (`name`, `path`, `search_artifacts`, `allow_forks`), so this is a\npin change and nothing else.\n\n**2.** The ref is added to the cache key, so a release build only\nrestores what that same ref produced. Canary releases from `master` keep\nhitting the cache exactly as before, since the ref does not change. The\n`cache: pnpm` line on the x86 Windows `setup-node` step has no\nequivalent key to scope, so it is dropped. That matrix leg is currently\ncommented out, so it only matters if it is switched back on.\n\n**3.** Scopes are read off what each job actually does rather than\napplied uniformly:\n\n- `ci.yml` checks out and builds, with no API calls anywhere in the\nfile, so `contents: read`.\n- `do-not-merge.yml` reads labels from the event payload and never\nchecks out, so it needs no token.\n- `generate-embeddings.yml` checks out and talks to Supabase and OpenAI\nthrough their own secrets, so `contents: read`.\n- `publish.yml` takes `contents: read` as the default.\n`resolve-required-data` adds `pull-requests: read` because\n`publish-resolve-data.js` calls `pulls.get`, and the two Slack reporters\nget an empty block since they only use the Slack bot token. The\n`publish` and `pr_failure_comment` jobs already scope themselves and are\nuntouched.\n\nOne thing worth knowing if you use a repository-level Actions allowlist:\nentries written as tag patterns (`owner/action@v1`) stop matching once a\nworkflow pins a SHA, and every workflow using that action then fails at\nstartup. Nothing here changes an existing pin, so it should not bite,\nbut the fix is `owner/action@*` in settings.\n\nFound and fixed by [Plumber](https://github.com/getplumber/plumber)''s\nanalysis, reviewed and submitted by me.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNo existing issue, this came out of reading the workflows. Happy to open\none first if you prefer that for changes like this.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxn9uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9+YQAJ7mvAqT0ypxRe0yeGRbU5at\n/O99rOkC5+K9E2/REGHNVr8sKgNYbmOMc6r+s8mxtSx57uEfeGyWMkWDq49D/svf\nGo8oBpDzKC1JOWy2j7L3Ex0AKiCDDWJ+Ajlt0raNboyzkbWcJVyWVfHHy0Yd06Fa\nylDI+Zwd7XyyvZ+Ai3EwW5dlvQBLyotWO/4F1XK/gdUDt7SJBORRrxFN6mdcwWeX\nZWLMCd4PscsctqshjLZoMy6f7Nj7cUwje+GcYQ04CISosNufNjiWtndhPXbiOkUY\n3jys5Z6+TlO3qnQfR1DyE9QTtha4cjsps28MiDCs2lY4o1KeMj8PHeY+nuVbgdEM\nB3OPdUq1Azf74CkDCw0uBZMGhK/g1y2eTwLx0NIpgnNR85s0dPJrM4W9Ok1VrNrz\n7CGn1JWAEo8nFx8s6+Xz3ypNK6a3eXS3YYgAUivFV8At01UIvYkLQjSaEH94wM64\nITUPgo9TOzaqLeZDohwk5GFSHEzpE7X4cOHcNwvWf1TU5cWoAey7Yv48cVmwoWTY\namD3+qSn9yYMuvD85Py6y1Sgfk5oca+ZAglyBtls8ZKlWjIOKT0VJPlNlqIpq0M/\niRyqAgpnmTxMJI7IkcIoJc3C5TPkXaarCfQAy82R6qtK5zSkTYVqHBTwPGB8wt5P\nQqLQva86lmP6qq92tnY0\n=iz51\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T17:20:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/f7adc8667ad7872ea3bd8b50d72a5096981131d7","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGY3YWRjODY2N2FkNzg3MmVhM2JkOGI1MGQ3MmE1MDk2OTgxMTMxZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8","sha":"2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8"}],"sha":"f7adc8667ad7872ea3bd8b50d72a5096981131d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f7adc8667ad7872ea3bd8b50d72a5096981131d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:37:08Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:37:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): accept --final-validation with a migrate CLI pinned below 23.2.0 (#37294)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only affects the hidden `--final-validation` flag, which acts only\nin orchestrated runs (`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR=true`). The refusal\nhappens when `NX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION` pins nx below 23.2.0.\n\nnx refuses the command below. The error says the flag ships in nx 23.2.0\nor newer, but no released version has it yet. The same command without\nthe flag runs fine.\n\n```shell\nNX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION=23.1.0 nx migrate --run-migrations --no-final-validation\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nnx accepts `--final-validation` and `--no-final-validation` whatever\nversion `NX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION` pins, and the workspace''s nx reads\nthem. The flags that choose which migrate path runs keep the 23.2.0\ncheck.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5074\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `nx migrate` runs through a temporary install of nx: latest, or the\nversion `NX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION` pins. An older temporary nx ignores\nflags it doesn''t know and runs a different migrate path. The check\nguards against that.\n- `--final-validation` only matters after `--run-migrations`, which\nevery version understands. The temporary nx hands the command line\nunchanged to the workspace''s nx, which reads the flag. Versions back to\n21.0.0 do the same.\n- The comment above the flag list states which flags belong in it.","tree":{"sha":"30f320765c48965e4fb85281e1ee4673fa3bb4a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/30f320765c48965e4fb85281e1ee4673fa3bb4a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 30f320765c48965e4fb85281e1ee4673fa3bb4a0\nparent d133deb462d7fa9ea257afb5cf3a0d8bf75a310b\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1791380228 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791380228 -0400\n\nfix(core): accept --final-validation with a migrate CLI pinned below 23.2.0 (#37294)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only affects the hidden `--final-validation` flag, which acts only\nin orchestrated runs (`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR=true`). The refusal\nhappens when `NX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION` pins nx below 23.2.0.\n\nnx refuses the command below. The error says the flag ships in nx 23.2.0\nor newer, but no released version has it yet. The same command without\nthe flag runs fine.\n\n```shell\nNX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION=23.1.0 nx migrate --run-migrations --no-final-validation\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nnx accepts `--final-validation` and `--no-final-validation` whatever\nversion `NX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION` pins, and the workspace''s nx reads\nthem. The flags that choose which migrate path runs keep the 23.2.0\ncheck.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5074\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `nx migrate` runs through a temporary install of nx: latest, or the\nversion `NX_MIGRATE_CLI_VERSION` pins. An older temporary nx ignores\nflags it doesn''t know and runs a different migrate path. The check\nguards against that.\n- `--final-validation` only matters after `--run-migrations`, which\nevery version understands. The temporary nx hands the command line\nunchanged to the workspace''s nx, which reads the flag. Versions back to\n21.0.0 do the same.\n- The comment above the flag list states which flags belong in it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxksECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI5sQADuoDWRR+VfIbp7f4KeOqSTC\nOTdSWzLvxFh/0yBIxG/lxbcM8LAQdSIZXnNUZD8BZDmTnWaeIT9pKiH5zoWpN7yw\nETPEWz66FJNIEPzmgCIMupSAqVbswpTb7K5CoAgE02FO4ZA0Qwf8rjk/5Jg3jVOK\nr20l8NFqHdjvqKfiOjVhGrVlh7eNj3/JkXoJpURoBMK6mEvoeJ0CfSm9vvX1UB9z\n9M1uWsm8SvtcW2uE6h1WOJs1w4UEyrFCQ0mS3YiNNPiCxeqUmMIsr6OBDQ9dSfqL\n0eTZW0+Ao3yNCHYkxpNR6hsEAv0XsNe282vKFeReu10t5NrVcaMzgJjxBUZtVzcS\nrFHo5j9WiLtU5W2bf4s5eYBEtOlL+eE4Ai0RnMvHOlF/XKkJrqweMXG9cp9oQZtf\nS3/TWPXrsUmeR4NSFz4Bw8mkwLGzPW7lW9etHvV02HM3guQd2+ed18mXf4qRpqlb\nrnYilXClzt3aYl4BfNYrJEGLNBRSL9z74N6vHsQjn0wmAMqsXNhfIH0ZbVpp848D\nV/VjukUi/Hw9dA9OAIyeklHcKPYQUhEtIgmqgx1cBvS8ntcybFB/jjMjK945Vw+6\nY9vrolhIQauY3e+Sh5TRnHSbmf+6S3HyF1a+Ca1C1VEe66LqYqUqwtp9BM6Ett25\nJ63UayPdYK9whMkqL0Jl\n=tsg4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T13:37:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDJiMzA1ZWU4NWI4ZGIwMzNlNGFiOTk4ZjMxMjgyY2JmZjY2YWMyYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/d133deb462d7fa9ea257afb5cf3a0d8bf75a310b","sha":"d133deb462d7fa9ea257afb5cf3a0d8bf75a310b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d133deb462d7fa9ea257afb5cf3a0d8bf75a310b"}],"sha":"2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/2b305ee85b8db033e4ab998f31282cbff66ac2a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/326263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vizanto","id":326263,"login":"vizanto","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNjI2Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vizanto","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d133deb462d7fa9ea257afb5cf3a0d8bf75a310b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:13:25Z","email":"git@danny.prime.vc","name":"Danny Wilson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:13:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): size the default cache bound from its own filesystem (#37269)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWhen `nx.json` sets no `maxCacheSize` (and `NX_MAX_CACHE_SIZE` is\nunset), `resolveMaxCacheSize` calls the native\n`getDefaultMaxCacheSize(cacheDir)`. It runs\n`sysinfo::Disks::new_with_refreshed_list()` to find the disk holding the\ncache and returns a tenth of its total space.\n\nThat refresh lists every mounted filesystem. On macOS it calls\n`getfsstat` and then, per mount, IOKit (`IOServiceGetMatchingService`)\nand CacheDelete over mach IPC. A `sample` of the call shows nearly all\nof its time waiting in `mach_msg2_trap` under\n`IOServiceGetMatchingService` and `getfsstat_b` (CacheDelete). The call\nis synchronous on the client''s main thread. `DbCache` makes it while\n`TaskOrchestrator` is being constructed, after the hashes come back and\nbefore the first task is scheduled, so every task run that uses the\ndefault bound waits for it.\n\nMeasured on macOS 26 (arm64, 57 mounts), `nx@23.2.1`:\n\n- about 80 ms per call on a quiet host;\n- 0.3–1.2 s per call while one real APFS disk-image test (attach, write,\nresize, detach) runs alongside;\n- up to 2.3 s per call during a loop of `hdiutil attach` / write /\n`detach` of a small sparse image.\n\nThe value also depends on mount order. The first disk whose mount point\nis a prefix of the cache path wins, and `/` is listed first. So a cache\non a separately mounted volume is bounded by the root container''s size,\nnot by the size of the volume it is on.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nSize the default bound from the cache directory''s own filesystem:\n`fs4::total_space` (statvfs) of the nearest ancestor that exists,\nbecause the cache directory may not exist yet. `fs4` is already a\ndependency of this crate on the targets that build `cache.rs`. The\nnumber is unchanged when the cache is on the root container (same `total\n* 0.1`, truncated). On a separately mounted volume, it is now that\nvolume''s. If the filesystem cannot be queried for any reason other than\na missing path, the error is returned instead of the silent 100 GiB.\n\nI applied the equivalent change to the published 23.2.1 `dist`\n(`resolveMaxCacheSize` computes the default with `fs.statfsSync` on the\nnearest existing ancestor) as a package patch. It returns the same\nvalues as this Rust version on the same paths (`~/.nx/<missing>/cache`\nand `$TMPDIR/<missing>`: 799849922560; a path on a mounted 100 GiB\nimage: 10737418240). In a loop running alongside the same attach/detach\nchurn, it averaged 58 µs per call where the native call averaged 275 ms.\nA fixture task run with the native `getDefaultMaxCacheSize` replaced by\na throwing stub fails on unpatched 23.2.1 and passes with the patch.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNone found. Searched for `getDefaultMaxCacheSize` and slow default cache\nsize.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"8463b92716718daec6b69d165011e32bc544ff6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/8463b92716718daec6b69d165011e32bc544ff6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/d133deb462d7fa9ea257afb5cf3a0d8bf75a310b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8463b92716718daec6b69d165011e32bc544ff6c\nparent fa2fbb653adc0e0b6c5919c883c4aff872511f21\nauthor Danny Wilson <git@danny.prime.vc> 1791378805 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791378805 -0400\n\nfix(core): size the default cache bound from its own filesystem (#37269)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWhen `nx.json` sets no `maxCacheSize` (and `NX_MAX_CACHE_SIZE` is\nunset), `resolveMaxCacheSize` calls the native\n`getDefaultMaxCacheSize(cacheDir)`. It runs\n`sysinfo::Disks::new_with_refreshed_list()` to find the disk holding the\ncache and returns a tenth of its total space.\n\nThat refresh lists every mounted filesystem. On macOS it calls\n`getfsstat` and then, per mount, IOKit (`IOServiceGetMatchingService`)\nand CacheDelete over mach IPC. A `sample` of the call shows nearly all\nof its time waiting in `mach_msg2_trap` under\n`IOServiceGetMatchingService` and `getfsstat_b` (CacheDelete). The call\nis synchronous on the client''s main thread. `DbCache` makes it while\n`TaskOrchestrator` is being constructed, after the hashes come back and\nbefore the first task is scheduled, so every task run that uses the\ndefault bound waits for it.\n\nMeasured on macOS 26 (arm64, 57 mounts), `nx@23.2.1`:\n\n- about 80 ms per call on a quiet host;\n- 0.3–1.2 s per call while one real APFS disk-image test (attach, write,\nresize, detach) runs alongside;\n- up to 2.3 s per call during a loop of `hdiutil attach` / write /\n`detach` of a small sparse image.\n\nThe value also depends on mount order. The first disk whose mount point\nis a prefix of the cache path wins, and `/` is listed first. So a cache\non a separately mounted volume is bounded by the root container''s size,\nnot by the size of the volume it is on.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nSize the default bound from the cache directory''s own filesystem:\n`fs4::total_space` (statvfs) of the nearest ancestor that exists,\nbecause the cache directory may not exist yet. `fs4` is already a\ndependency of this crate on the targets that build `cache.rs`. The\nnumber is unchanged when the cache is on the root container (same `total\n* 0.1`, truncated). On a separately mounted volume, it is now that\nvolume''s. If the filesystem cannot be queried for any reason other than\na missing path, the error is returned instead of the silent 100 GiB.\n\nI applied the equivalent change to the published 23.2.1 `dist`\n(`resolveMaxCacheSize` computes the default with `fs.statfsSync` on the\nnearest existing ancestor) as a package patch. It returns the same\nvalues as this Rust version on the same paths (`~/.nx/<missing>/cache`\nand `$TMPDIR/<missing>`: 799849922560; a path on a mounted 100 GiB\nimage: 10737418240). In a loop running alongside the same attach/detach\nchurn, it averaged 58 µs per call where the native call averaged 275 ms.\nA fixture task run with the native `getDefaultMaxCacheSize` replaced by\na throwing stub fails on unpatched 23.2.1 and passes with the patch.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNone found. Searched for `getDefaultMaxCacheSize` and slow default cache\nsize.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxkV1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANNMQAHqbWISPPgaOY6imcd7+nTsu\ncxvFurlW/1sFG8eXb4QJdT3ZhG3HTFUgigW5AN3nPls80yLD6tzM/CHOpBZROquH\nLvkQQn1vu9eexpsWdkY1rFizODgDKZQgV2b2w27UczLOkkqUPa5GU1gPqZtKGeR4\nQKT6T6Ls1p1zMigvNVAanTiyH1gUtPgwtuoemYdJMZ6GNJYGywk2/gLsdFADOo9o\nHn5r5+0N+pPLYU2Re6vfqe/LPuMkoQkFJ2TLVo9gDTcW5Jg3uOmIMZPELHDVPY24\noOod3qoXtk17qBsADzPajJYHfI5pY66XUreVBmWJUDbNj6N09kZTcLZb5KEbrjxZ\nZFPIp8708hquvuobAR+80EWi24U1A4vw6FOLyPfheQoq+03r0NeGS7Si60zlwE1P\nqEl5wFVtuyfXl2spfNAils5P/uxSw3GovV6ifzr/HMTNcR5FNMcp63DGoc0JuJs2\nalSq7tiXPuDRPkOJauhmdCqA02JR7KWrwc02rpoXlKE9JqfiCJH8OmoVt6PmlaEC\nX02l5xOKP9P+O2cOIgiBJTYl9+A9vVtM1quvcKFyH1L9nSMkZP+H2IqPa1pcMKEm\nsMhkFtZ+EYYUhqdrPx59lErwZFYRgNVhzGvme9XCJESkMZh8Fn0cDrP7r6VvbVm5\nan4waKbFUaV9wHCHNoMQ\n=eg1p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T13:13:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.co