.githubusercontent.com/u/59180449?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Optischa","id":59180449,"login":"Optischa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MTgwNDQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Optischa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b23c118c58642131612889a0c307cb01d26c46fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:18:36Z","email":"59180449+Optischa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Optischa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:18:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(core): update brace-expansion for CVE-2026-102277 (#37291)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe workspace pins the `brace-expansion` override to the exact version\n`5.0.9` in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. That version is affected by\nCVE-2026-102277, CVE-2026-102278 and CVE-2026-102276, and the exact pin\nstops pnpm from picking up later patch releases.\n\n  ## Expected Behavior\n\nThe `brace-expansion` override is `^5.0.12`, and the lockfile resolves\nto `5.0.12`, which contains the fixes for the CVEs above. Using a caret\nrange matches how comparable overrides in the file are declared\n(`minimatch`, `minimist`, `underscore`), so future patch releases within\n5.x can be picked up by a\n  lockfile update.\n\n  ## Related Issue(s)\n\n  <!-- No issue; this is a dependency security update. -->","tree":{"sha":"0d828afff76ea73cc3301fbfd4707bcb1b0d4c25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/0d828afff76ea73cc3301fbfd4707bcb1b0d4c25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/b23c118c58642131612889a0c307cb01d26c46fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d828afff76ea73cc3301fbfd4707bcb1b0d4c25\nparent 53c247cd9134da0f2e296c46a2249c787e47a02c\nauthor Optischa <59180449+Optischa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791281916 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791281916 +0200\n\nchore(core): update brace-expansion for CVE-2026-102277 (#37291)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe workspace pins the `brace-expansion` override to the exact version\n`5.0.9` in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. That version is affected by\nCVE-2026-102277, CVE-2026-102278 and CVE-2026-102276, and the exact pin\nstops pnpm from picking up later patch releases.\n\n  ## Expected Behavior\n\nThe `brace-expansion` override is `^5.0.12`, and the lockfile resolves\nto `5.0.12`, which contains the fixes for the CVEs above. Using a caret\nrange matches how comparable overrides in the file are declared\n(`minimatch`, `minimist`, `underscore`), so future patch releases within\n5.x can be picked up by a\n  lockfile update.\n\n  ## Related Issue(s)\n\n  <!-- No issue; this is a dependency security update. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxMr8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy2YQAFvn17Sdkg+EXGZBodDEXBVb\nBTvRL0PWb8dS6BvbVaoKeHa4gK9J3solpL3hpyQqw91uBIG1C1Ano12uk8/l79R4\nYmi17I75Biq2ddujxbS+wUDqEYtrt8Hlgo2Zk776dkz/FnN9b/zzAHDTzgLUILrf\nErugKlcVlodBe6lQQAKQb9IJcLk6UEL16jzUesKrjKPJZ6qd5B9XZzcZJnFzrYh6\nfTBBrrMb8y9aDWRHE54mwTFkpJgDSMfBMgY3J7uaisF+s4zWQEdpP29ysHXS/Sx5\niIQkX9jakGVVvDYxhZXm86Tzri2fmGi8I5E+0DZBeb02Ba80M+fPZOJkn2LrcjgS\nF9fF6DX95Wj5T+snzvMZdXaFwtT2igclvHbKUaSt9iAU6mR3K4XUjLzWbbFcC/n/\nZ3u8YfW983wZFGVKwT6dTgu30Qz5XOET48AEI/UvDoRR/NlvuTetDOy393esoO5/\nC2d741e4jrhFdg95YkaCVMuAOYhhtC1bXQecn7JV9ANLe3in19V