_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/53c247cd9134da0f2e296c46a2249c787e47a02c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:33:33Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:33:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): add a Codex counterpart to the review-pr skill (#37228)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nOnly Claude can review a pull request in this repository. The\n`review-pr` skill and the sandbox CLI it drives both live under\n`.claude/`, so a Codex session has no review skill here. A Codex one\nexists, but it is maintained outside the repo and carries its own fork\nof the sandbox CLI. That fork has drifted from this copy in both\ndirections.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nA Codex `review-pr` skill ships in the repository: the skill under\n`.agents/skills/review-pr`, five reviewer roles under `.codex/agents`.\nCodex loads both only from a trusted project.\n\nIt writes its review to `~/.nx-pr-reviews/<PR>.md`, the file and layout\nClaude''s `review-pr` already writes. Both tools use the same section\nheadings, and the outbox can tell which tool wrote a draft. So\n`review-pending-pr-reviews` posts a draft from either tool, evaluates\nits findings with the maintainer first, and a re-review carries the\nother''s history forward.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4849\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Both skills drive one CLI instead of two copies, now at\n`tools/review-sandbox/sandbox` with the fork''s nine fixes folded in.\n- `stop` and `prune` prove a review left nothing behind, and both could\nexit clean after reclaiming nothing. Each failure now names the subtree,\ncontainer or host it could not reach. A stopped host is named as\nskipped, not failed, and a later prune sweeps it.\n- Snapshotting a PR runs `git archive` on the host, so the override\nunsets `filter` and four byte-rewriting conversions. A PR cannot make\nthe host run a driver from the maintainer''s config.\n- The record quotes the PR''s body and comments inside a fence. A PR\ncannot open a section there, such as the one saying a human evaluated\nthe draft.\n- Sharing the record forces four changes in Claude''s skills. Its\n`review-pr` keeps sections its template omits, moves the grill record\nwith the draft it graded, and drops the writer key on a rewrite. Its\noutbox reads that key, then compares the draft against that tool''s\nconstant.\n- Three fixes in Claude''s `review-pr` are independent of the port. A\nre-review refreshes the criteria stamp and clears the posting fields\nthat hid every re-review of a posted PR. It fetches the prior head by\nURL, since the shared object store carries no `origin`.\n- Not handled: a superseded shared host stays running when an image\nrebuild changes the image ID. That predates this PR and affects both\nskills. `prune --host` reclaims it.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/nxc-4849-99e04a8b\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"e98f3014087c16c36492cf0539023af3c26a5b69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/e98f3014087c16c36492cf0539023af3c26a5b69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/53c247cd9134da0f2e296c46a2249c787e47a02c","verification":{"payload":"tree e98f3014087c16c36492cf0539023af3c26a5b69\nparent a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1791246813 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791246813 -0400\n\nchore(repo): add a Codex counterpart to the review-pr skill (#37228)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nOnly Claude can review a pull request in this repository. The\n`review-pr` skill and the sandbox CLI it drives both live under\n`.claude/`, so a Codex session has no review skill here. A Codex one\nexists, but it is maintained outside the repo and carries its own fork\nof the sandbox CLI. That fork has drifted from this copy in both\ndirections.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nA Codex `review-pr` skill ships in the repository: the skill under\n`.agents/skills/review-pr`, five reviewer roles under `.codex/agents`.\nCodex loads both only from a trusted project.\n\nIt writes its review to `~/.nx-pr-reviews/<PR>.md`, the file and layout\nClaude''s `review-pr` already writes. Both tools use the same section\nheadings, and the outbox can tell which tool wrote a draft. So\n`review-pending-pr-reviews` posts a draft from either tool, evaluates\nits findings with the maintainer first, and a re-review carries the\nother''s history forward.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4849\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Both skills drive one CLI instead of two copies, now at\n`tools/review-sandbox/sandbox` with the fork''s nine fixes folded in.\n- `stop` and `prune` prove a review left nothing behind, and both could\nexit clean after reclaiming nothing. Each failure now names the subtree,\ncontainer or host it could not reach. A stopped host is named as\nskipped, not failed, and a later prune sweeps it.\n- Snapshotting a PR runs `git archive` on the host, so the override\nunsets `filter` and four byte-rewriting conversions. A PR cannot make\nthe host run a driver from the maintainer''s config.\n- The record quotes the PR''s body and comments inside a fence. A PR\ncannot open a section there, such as the one saying a human evaluated\nthe draft.\n- Sharing the record forces four changes in Claude''s skills. Its\n`review-pr` keeps sections its template omits, moves the grill record\nwith the draft it graded, and drops the writer key on a rewrite. Its\noutbox reads that key, then compares the draft against that tool''s\nconstant.\n- Three fixes in Claude''s `review-pr` are independent of the port. A\nre-review refreshes the criteria stamp and clears the posting fields\nthat hid every re-review of a posted PR. It fetches the prior head by\nURL, since the shared object store carries no `origin`.\n- Not handled: a superseded shared host stays running when an image\nrebuild changes the image ID. That predates this PR and affects both\nskills. `prune --host` reclaims it.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/nxc-4849-99e04a8b\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEHdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2PYQACJ8FRvtlU05iH8Yp9NPkljq\nBW10WF2FDF2gcM85at8Iid1O7LhNyMSDO8k2ursDV2bhWMOzmMFL6dZrpUV2sUUX\nBM1VNmWpANLF+BkVwzZsd53GY7ly5uEFDkWP/o+Yh9k2NauSGJkB9JcYbLbxOmQg\ncsngbcuylgSXrR8iIwj4PkGndNIgUA2PSrw5dMmxBKVgFWrUDiqHS7tippUoRHZs\niPlvT6/3FBMD4A1en5yZclgYXOlV8WLTuSKZGDuSR7BAQ/uw739xGeelZNRgoZ++\nipoZZ7P9DJEUwXxuVwrSiY+KfWo8xKoxC8B9nvJFlvSlD2QeJ42qZUGrJblzv3UZ\nNN0+rCSBePia12ijADC2kr5WGxbCqL5bLoJTOSggGKoOQUv0updX9+DF6ywVDmU1\nlNGlCnwJu8DJ6i5saEdG4XVlcGjrV1yA24D5cw3R8V8z1LYRatsV7f0hDeRrgY9n\nRAq04ixyRs7BiAs3WeFc8Exec1CK6fNPwX5RL47tjZKUwsBogj51k+C/HwAv61ka\n18gwiYWbVddy+uhQ38Y6rLQPqadvhjjbCTePKDVmRM6Ct/WqY8CzGTvOCatYIArT\n/LnUeH88E42KqOiY697nL7CxO0AZZ3vyHU+OqaNFYVezf6Af0cn16lIt46ncTCdl\nGILK+D2UNLdDMHkVWp2X\n=o0Zn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T00:33:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/53c247cd9134da0f2e296c46a2249c787e47a02c","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDUzYzI0N2NkOTEzNGRhMGYyZTI5NmM0NmEyMjQ5Yzc4N2U0N2EwMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c","sha":"a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c"}],"sha":"53c247cd9134da0f2e296c46a2249c787e47a02c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/53c247cd9134da0f2e296c46a2249c787e47a02c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:44:21Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:44:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): answer daemon output tracking from the workspace context (#37217)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWith the daemon on, the next run after a cache restore can copy\nunchanged outputs back from the cache (#37086), and a real edit under an\noutput can be missed. Two causes in\n`packages/nx/src/daemon/server/outputs-tracking.ts`:\n\n- **Arrival-time window.** A watch event under a recorded output drops\nits hash if it arrives more than 2s after the record, and is ignored\ninside that window. Slow machines drop hashes on a restore''s own late\nevents and re-copy. Fast machines miss real writes, which is why `cache\n› should support using globs as outputs` flaked under pnpm 12 and #37151\nhad to add 2s waits to it.\n- **A rescan clears everything.** `handle-outputs-changes.ts` called\n`clearRecordedOutputsHashes()` on dropped events, so an overflowed watch\nmid-restore forgot every record.\n\nThe tracker also never looked at output contents (\"unchanged\" meant \"no\nevent arrived\"), and it read outputs with its own expansion\n(`get_files_for_outputs`), which disagrees with the cache''s\n(`_expand_outputs`): it ignored `!` exclusions (and read an excluded\ndirectory twice), and skipped `node_modules` inside an output that the\ncache stores.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nOutput tracking lives in the workspace context and compares file stamps,\nagainst one definition of a task''s output files.\n\n**One definition of output files.** A task''s output files are exactly\nwhat the cache copies: `_expand_outputs`, with each folder copied whole\n(including `node_modules`, links to files, no linked directories).\n`get_files_for_outputs` is now that definition (`output_files_via` with\nfolders read by `copied_files`, which mirrors the copy), so tracking and\nthe cache agree by construction. Outputs are normalized the same way on\nboth sides (`normalize_outputs`: an absolute output made\nworkspace-relative; one outside the workspace is skipped by tracking and\nrefused by the cache).\n\n**Record** (`WorkspaceContext.recordOutputs`) keeps each output file''s\n`(mtime, size)`, plus a content hash only for a whole-second mtime from\nthe record''s own second (coarse filesystems such as HFS+ or FAT).\n- `put` and `copyFilesFromCache` report the files they write, with\nstamps, and the orchestrator records after caching and passes that list\nalong, so the daemon records without walking. A restore stamps its files\nonce the (parallel) copy is done, so a link is never stamped before its\ntarget is written.\n- `put`''s list is always the full set. A restore''s list is passed only\nwhen every output is a path and each one present was replaced from the\ncache; a glob, a negation or an output the artifact lacks can leave\nother files in place, so those record from disk.\n\n**Check** (`WorkspaceContext.outputsUnchanged`) lists the output files\nthrough the definition with folders answered from the `IgnoredIndex`,\nre-reads from disk if that set differs from the record (a listing can\nlag a write, or skip what the index never lists), then compares every\nstamp in parallel.\n\n**Watch events only keep the listings current.** A late event for a\ntask''s own write, or a rescan, no longer drops a record; an edit whose\nevent was lost is still caught by its stamp. The 2s window,\n`processFileChangesInOutputs`, the rescan wipe and\n`collapseExpandedOutputs` are removed; the daemon''s\n`outputs-tracking.ts` delegates to the context.\n\n**Faster glob expansion.** `_expand_outputs` walked the whole workspace\nfor a glob output; it now walks only under each glob''s literal root\n(`nx_walker_sync_under`), yielding the same paths (tested against the\nfull walk, including links, vetoed folders and pruned parents; roots\nkeep the case they are given). This speeds up the cache''s own copies\ntoo.\n\nHow this covers both causes in #37086:\n\n- **Arrival-time window:** gone. Event timing plays no part in the\ncheck; a late event only makes the index re-list, and a real write\nchanges the stamp however soon it lands.\n- **Rescan wipe:** gone. A rescan reseeds the listings; records are\nchecked against stamps on disk.\n\nBehavior changes:\n\n- A file an output glob does not name is no longer an output. In\n`cache.test.ts`, an unrelated `dist/apps/c.ts` next to glob outputs now\nreports \"existing outputs match the cache\"; the 2s waits #37151 added to\nthat spec are removed. (`c.ts` was added as an unrelated file in #18242;\nthe restore there came from the directory collapse, per #35204.)\n- With `.next` and `!.next/cache`, writes to `.next/cache` no longer\ntrigger a restore. With `!.next/cache/**`, the cache still copies that\nfolder, so writes there still count.\n- `node_modules` inside an output is part of it, as the cache stores it.\n\nKnown gaps:\n\n- Records live in the workspace context, so the daemon''s rare\n`resetWorkspaceContext` path drops them: one extra restore per task, not\nwrong outputs.\n- A new file in a folder the index never lists (`node_modules`, `.git`,\n`.nx/cache`, `.yarn/cache`) inside an output, where the record has none,\nis not seen. Master has the same blind spot.\n\nVerified locally:\n\n- Rust: 14 output-tracking tests (stamps, edits/new/deleted files,\nsame-size and same-second rewrites, late events, rescans, lagging\nlistings, given lists, escaped and negated outputs, `node_modules`\ninside an output), the restricted walk against the full walk, and the\n`expand_outputs`, `file_ops`, cache and `ignored_index` suites (119\npass). `check-wasm-target.sh`, clippy, `cargo fmt` and prepush are\nclean.\n- Vitest: `put`''s file list equals `getFilesForOutputs` for 7 output\nshapes (folders, exclusions, `!x/**`, globs, `node_modules`, links) and\nfor absolute outputs; a restore''s list includes links to files the same\nrestore writes; restores return a list only when complete; the\norchestrator records after `put` and after a restore with their files.\nThe daemon, native, task-orchestrator, cache and workspace-context\nsuites pass.\n- Repro of #37086 (macOS, 965 tasks × 77 files, daemon on): `rm -rf\ndist`, restore everything, build again at once, three times, then once\nmore after 60s. On master, each restore burst overflowed FSEvents and\neach rescan wiped every record, so 1–2 of every 3 rebuilds re-copied all\n965 tasks. With this PR: 0 re-copies in every pass, through 4–10 rescans\nper run.\n\n| Quiet machine, averages of 3 rounds | master-style walk | this PR |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Daemon record time per run | 7.2s | 1.1s |\n| Daemon check time per run | 0.42s | 0.47s |\n| Restore build | 10.2s | 9.4–9.9s |\n\nNot yet verified: Windows (CI runs no Rust tests there), the\n`cache.test.ts` e2e itself (CI), and a full `packages/nx` Vitest run.\n\nFollow-ups (not in this PR):\n\n- Glob outputs: each check walks the glob root on disk, since\n`_expand_outputs` matches globs against the disk; matching them against\nthe index''s listing of the glob root would avoid it. Outputs holding a\nlink to a file outside the workspace always fall through to the disk\nread, since the index does not list such links.\n- Skip the stat for roots the watcher reports as quiet (per-root change\ncounters); it trades safety on filesystems without reliable events.\n- The cache copies a folder excluded as `!x/**` whole, and an outputs\nlist of only exclusions copies the whole workspace.\n\nLinear: NXC-5028.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37086\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Export-NodeExecutorOptions-from-nx-js-executors-b3cb0c6d\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"270decf87f8efbee08e8446e9901ba658b89f02d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/270decf87f8efbee08e8446e9901ba658b89f02d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c","verification":{"payload":"tree 270decf87f8efbee08e8446e9901ba658b89f02d\nparent 3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1791243861 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791243861 +0000\n\nfix(core): answer daemon output tracking from the workspace context (#37217)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWith the daemon on, the next run after a cache restore can copy\nunchanged outputs back from the cache (#37086), and a real edit under an\noutput can be missed. Two causes in\n`packages/nx/src/daemon/server/outputs-tracking.ts`:\n\n- **Arrival-time window.** A watch event under a recorded output drops\nits hash if it arrives more than 2s after the record, and is ignored\ninside that window. Slow machines drop hashes on a restore''s own late\nevents and re-copy. Fast machines miss real writes, which is why `cache\n› should support using globs as outputs` flaked under pnpm 12 and #37151\nhad to add 2s waits to it.\n- **A rescan clears everything.** `handle-outputs-changes.ts` called\n`clearRecordedOutputsHashes()` on dropped events, so an overflowed watch\nmid-restore forgot every record.\n\nThe tracker also never looked at output contents (\"unchanged\" meant \"no\nevent arrived\"), and it read outputs with its own expansion\n(`get_files_for_outputs`), which disagrees with the cache''s\n(`_expand_outputs`): it ignored `!` exclusions (and read an excluded\ndirectory twice), and skipped `node_modules` inside an output that the\ncache stores.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nOutput tracking lives in the workspace context and compares file stamps,\nagainst one definition of a task''s output files.\n\n**One definition of output files.** A task''s output files are exactly\nwhat the cache copies: `_expand_outputs`, with each folder copied whole\n(including `node_modules`, links to files, no linked directories).\n`get_files_for_outputs` is now that definition (`output_files_via` with\nfolders read by `copied_files`, which mirrors the copy), so tracking and\nthe cache agree by construction. Outputs are normalized the same way on\nboth sides (`normalize_outputs`: an absolute output made\nworkspace-relative; one outside the workspace is skipped by tracking and\nrefused by the cache).\n\n**Record** (`WorkspaceContext.recordOutputs`) keeps each output file''s\n`(mtime, size)`, plus a content hash only for a whole-second mtime from\nthe record''s own second (coarse filesystems such as HFS+ or FAT).\n- `put` and `copyFilesFromCache` report the files they write, with\nstamps, and the orchestrator records after caching and passes that list\nalong, so the daemon records without walking. A restore stamps its files\nonce the (parallel) copy is done, so a link is never stamped before its\ntarget is written.\n- `put`''s list is always the full set. A restore''s list is passed only\nwhen every output is a path and each one present was replaced from the\ncache; a glob, a negation or an output the artifact lacks can leave\nother files in place, so those record from disk.\n\n**Check** (`WorkspaceContext.outputsUnchanged`) lists the output files\nthrough the definition with folders answered from the `IgnoredIndex`,\nre-reads from disk if that set differs from the record (a listing can\nlag a write, or skip what the index never lists), then compares every\nstamp in parallel.\n\n**Watch events only keep the listings current.** A late event for a\ntask''s own write, or a rescan, no longer drops a record; an edit whose\nevent was lost is still caught by its stamp. The 2s window,\n`processFileChangesInOutputs`, the rescan wipe and\n`collapseExpandedOutputs` are removed; the daemon''s\n`outputs-tracking.ts` delegates to the context.\n\n**Faster glob expansion.** `_expand_outputs` walked the whole workspace\nfor a glob output; it now walks only under each glob''s literal root\n(`nx_walker_sync_under`), yielding the same paths (tested against the\nfull walk, including links, vetoed folders and pruned parents; roots\nkeep the case they are given). This speeds up the cache''s own copies\ntoo.\n\nHow this covers both causes in #37086:\n\n- **Arrival-time window:** gone. Event timing plays no part in the\ncheck; a late event only makes the index re-list, and a real write\nchanges the stamp however soon it lands.\n- **Rescan wipe:** gone. A rescan reseeds the listings; records are\nchecked against stamps on disk.\n\nBehavior changes:\n\n- A file an output glob does not name is no longer an output. In\n`cache.test.ts`, an unrelated `dist/apps/c.ts` next to glob outputs now\nreports \"existing outputs match the cache\"; the 2s waits #37151 added to\nthat spec are removed. (`c.ts` was added as an unrelated file in #18242;\nthe restore there came from the directory collapse, per #35204.)\n- With `.next` and `!.next/cache`, writes to `.next/cache` no longer\ntrigger a restore. With `!.next/cache/**`, the cache still copies that\nfolder, so writes there still count.\n- `node_modules` inside an output is part of it, as the cache stores it.\n\nKnown gaps:\n\n- Records live in the workspace context, so the daemon''s rare\n`resetWorkspaceContext` path drops them: one extra restore per task, not\nwrong outputs.\n- A new file in a folder the index never lists (`node_modules`, `.git`,\n`.nx/cache`, `.yarn/cache`) inside an output, where the record has none,\nis not seen. Master has the same blind spot.\n\nVerified locally:\n\n- Rust: 14 output-tracking tests (stamps, edits/new/deleted files,\nsame-size and same-second rewrites, late events, rescans, lagging\nlistings, given lists, escaped and negated outputs, `node_modules`\ninside an output), the restricted walk against the full walk, and the\n`expand_outputs`, `file_ops`, cache and `ignored_index` suites (119\npass). `check-wasm-target.sh`, clippy, `cargo fmt` and prepush are\nclean.\n- Vitest: `put`''s file list equals `getFilesForOutputs` for 7 output\nshapes (folders, exclusions, `!x/**`, globs, `node_modules`, links) and\nfor absolute outputs; a restore''s list includes links to files the same\nrestore writes; restores return a list only when complete; the\norchestrator records after `put` and after a restore with their files.\nThe daemon, native, task-orchestrator, cache and workspace-context\nsuites pass.\n- Repro of #37086 (macOS, 965 tasks × 77 files, daemon on): `rm -rf\ndist`, restore everything, build again at once, three times, then once\nmore after 60s. On master, each restore burst overflowed FSEvents and\neach rescan wiped every record, so 1–2 of every 3 rebuilds re-copied all\n965 tasks. With this PR: 0 re-copies in every pass, through 4–10 rescans\nper run.\n\n| Quiet machine, averages of 3 rounds | master-style walk | this PR |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Daemon record time per run | 7.2s | 1.1s |\n| Daemon check time per run | 0.42s | 0.47s |\n| Restore build | 10.2s | 9.4–9.9s |\n\nNot yet verified: Windows (CI runs no Rust tests there), the\n`cache.test.ts` e2e itself (CI), and a full `packages/nx` Vitest run.\n\nFollow-ups (not in this PR):\n\n- Glob outputs: each check walks the glob root on disk, since\n`_expand_outputs` matches globs against the disk; matching them against\nthe index''s listing of the glob root would avoid it. Outputs holding a\nlink to a file outside the workspace always fall through to the disk\nread, since the index does not list such links.\n- Skip the stat for roots the watcher reports as quiet (per-root change\ncounters); it trades safety on filesystems without reliable events.\n- The cache copies a folder excluded as `!x/**` whole, and an outputs\nlist of only exclusions copies the whole workspace.\n\nLinear: NXC-5028.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37086\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Export-NodeExecutorOptions-from-nx-js-executors-b3cb0c6d\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxDZVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZIEQAGkW/1MB2Oxs+KaJWAWz9z+y\nFmoOx/oTGcNatcrM2oOTeBTAlaiHdRaRUBxlR9mpA4UYmk4P6d4yD9K+2DuHcTNU\nM7nV6mumBeZSeX3Q4Rd9uveh6Uwv4JY+4a3hPcQyVfiyGXImDIckCov5eoQszrgm\nMbnniZVmOBiHg2M3XpjnG/w/qS//cV2hacBp3P06jF/9z0RHJ3fKAzSvx5Fopw2g\nZkHhkdVa0v/7R14p+MWUgAN0R6G39NDXwPJJdYS9+ZGREpqzPZ43Qogu7TWX1CNw\n8fROjYeNxWZvGlp7pEQD6JpHKZeTE/fpGIE6WiTJJi1WnuSyABIPXDfLSIEFkrbO\n40SWiVuw6xT0OTJ1GDcaLP5lJbqGJHzDX7bbGXIq995Ae7c7Gqhxe2NFvywVOh2D\niDjZSW6P4gEhvOfAjLIbRishD2d8DxlS+BsOSngruKxIbNu0IfP8cUh6YdpaCZlz\nG2VW47zRfi6X+2dpKPrHdlgsP3xjBIpHjiDEdzeNZ+uIuGcnq2o/YncCpef+/I9R\nzX7PNsTVTYx9EKQlsWZYdbM9Ay3vzrnR64d56TpznjTUlm4ojL7IIH2RzAVNXttP\nz8JCApHmb2PLSE9b8aapU7aaqWi1GaDJBLD1KcYpXPTenI9GBDNE9t3A60VHPdNj\nG/LIjPaznv8qAB6d/RCe\n=vEGX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T23:44:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGEyNjY0NGJiMTIxOTExYzNjNTU3MGU1YWEwM2U1MjE0N2Y2OGMzNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc","sha":"3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc"}],"sha":"a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a26644bb121911c3c5570e5aa03e52147f68c36c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:53:49Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:53:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): keep ultracache exclusions with the globs they trim (#37285)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nNx splits a task''s Ultracache configuration into one file group per\nproject, and an exclusion only applies inside its own group. Exclusions\nwere put in the group of the project that owns their own path, not the\ngroup of the glob they trim:\n\n- `libs/**/*.md` lands in one project''s group and\n`!libs/parent/README.md` in `parent`''s group, so `README.md` is hashed\nanyway.\n- Exclusions that trim nothing (e.g. `!packages/nx/src/native/*.node`\nfor angular:oxlint) form groups with no globs to trim, which is noise in\nhash details.\n\nGroups also hold the configuration''s globs after brace expansion, so\n`packages/angular/**/*.{ts,mts,cts,js,mjs,cjs,tsx,jsx}` becomes 8 globs.\nGroups over 8 globs show in hash details as `files:[37 paths\n#<digest>]`, which says nothing about what they hold.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- Each group takes the exclusions that overlap its globs. Exclusions\nthat overlap no glob are dropped.\n- Groups keep the globs as recorded. A brace glob is split only when its\nalternatives belong to different projects or name a file the always-on\nset already hashes. `expand_globs` expands braces itself, so hashing\ndoes the same work.\n- Globs come first, then exclusions, so hash details read like the\nconfiguration.\n- Groups over 8 globs list their first 8 positive globs and count the\nrest: `files:[libs/a/**/*.ts,libs/a/**/*.json (+5 excluded)]`. Labels\nare unique within a task, since a task''s groups never share a positive\nglob. They can repeat across tasks, so the files expansion cache is now\nkeyed by instruction id.\n\nangular:oxlint goes from three groups (one of them 37 globs, one only\nexclusions) to:\n\n- `files:[.eslintignore,.oxlintrc.json,tsconfig.base.json]`\n-\n`files:[packages/angular/**/*.json,packages/angular/**/*.{ts,mts,cts,js,mjs,cjs,tsx,jsx},!packages/angular/**/*.{di,impl,migrator}.d.ts,…]`\n(7 globs)\n\nHashes of tasks with an Ultracache configuration change once.\n\nThe \"moves a task hash by a changed read\" spec could re-import the same\ncommit within one millisecond, and plans are memoized per (commit, fetch\nmillisecond), so the second hash sometimes reused the first plan. It now\nwaits for the clock to move on between imports.\n\n### Performance\n\nExclusion roots are computed once per configuration and matched by\nbinary search over each group''s sorted roots. `literal_segment` skips\nthe parser for segments with no glob syntax, which makes\n`walk_root`/`partition_glob` cheap everywhere they run, not only here.\n\nBenchmarked on this repo''s 333 `lint`/`test` tasks with fabricated\nconfigurations, master vs this branch, alternating builds (medians of 5\nruns, last two of three rounds):\n\n| All 333 tasks | master | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Plan: globifier-style globs over each project and its deps | 163–183\nms | 95–141 ms |\n| Plan: 3,000 literal paths + 40 exclusions per project | 3.4–4.9 s |\n0.71–0.73 s |\n| Plan: globs + 40 exclusions per project | 480–484 ms | 165–171 ms |\n| Single-task hash, literal-path configurations | 41–49 ms | 16 ms |\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/NXC-4846-snapshot-resolution-in-Nx-core-618d13d8\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"4e49d3edf027e1010e53114cd6d335c79922cf08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/4e49d3edf027e1010e53114cd6d335c79922cf08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e49d3edf027e1010e53114cd6d335c79922cf08\nparent af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1791240829 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791240829 +0000\n\nfix(core): keep ultracache exclusions with the globs they trim (#37285)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nNx splits a task''s Ultracache configuration into one file group per\nproject, and an exclusion only applies inside its own group. Exclusions\nwere put in the group of the project that owns their own path, not the\ngroup of the glob they trim:\n\n- `libs/**/*.md` lands in one project''s group and\n`!libs/parent/README.md` in `parent`''s group, so `README.md` is hashed\nanyway.\n- Exclusions that trim nothing (e.g. `!packages/nx/src/native/*.node`\nfor angular:oxlint) form groups with no globs to trim, which is noise in\nhash details.\n\nGroups also hold the configuration''s globs after brace expansion, so\n`packages/angular/**/*.{ts,mts,cts,js,mjs,cjs,tsx,jsx}` becomes 8 globs.\nGroups over 8 globs show in hash details as `files:[37 paths\n#<digest>]`, which says nothing about what they hold.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- Each group takes the exclusions that overlap its globs. Exclusions\nthat overlap no glob are dropped.\n- Groups keep the globs as recorded. A brace glob is split only when its\nalternatives belong to different projects or name a file the always-on\nset already hashes. `expand_globs` expands braces itself, so hashing\ndoes the same work.\n- Globs come first, then exclusions, so hash details read like the\nconfiguration.\n- Groups over 8 globs list their first 8 positive globs and count the\nrest: `files:[libs/a/**/*.ts,libs/a/**/*.json (+5 excluded)]`. Labels\nare unique within a task, since a task''s groups never share a positive\nglob. They can repeat across tasks, so the files expansion cache is now\nkeyed by instruction id.\n\nangular:oxlint goes from three groups (one of them 37 globs, one only\nexclusions) to:\n\n- `files:[.eslintignore,.oxlintrc.json,tsconfig.base.json]`\n-\n`files:[packages/angular/**/*.json,packages/angular/**/*.{ts,mts,cts,js,mjs,cjs,tsx,jsx},!packages/angular/**/*.{di,impl,migrator}.d.ts,…]`\n(7 globs)\n\nHashes of tasks with an Ultracache configuration change once.\n\nThe \"moves a task hash by a changed read\" spec could re-import the same\ncommit within one millisecond, and plans are memoized per (commit, fetch\nmillisecond), so the second hash sometimes reused the first plan. It now\nwaits for the clock to move on between imports.\n\n### Performance\n\nExclusion roots are computed once per configuration and matched by\nbinary search over each group''s sorted roots. `literal_segment` skips\nthe parser for segments with no glob syntax, which makes\n`walk_root`/`partition_glob` cheap everywhere they run, not only here.\n\nBenchmarked on this repo''s 333 `lint`/`test` tasks with fabricated\nconfigurations, master vs this branch, alternating builds (medians of 5\nruns, last two of three rounds):\n\n| All 333 tasks | master | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Plan: globifier-style globs over each project and its deps | 163–183\nms | 95–141 ms |\n| Plan: 3,000 literal paths + 40 exclusions per project | 3.4–4.9 s |\n0.71–0.73 s |\n| Plan: globs + 40 exclusions per project | 480–484 ms | 165–171 ms |\n| Single-task hash, literal-path configurations | 41–49 ms | 16 ms |\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/NXC-4846-snapshot-resolution-in-Nx-core-618d13d8\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCp9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnAoQAKeUtiksbUgcFSnpeP4Ez7Kq\nHnu8DoFKd54NUYU9O7ot4VQu9NNvloMf112cbPLP9Gj0OIdxJwlFzLknWRh3fdUR\n0yivLKvx/NdDaiMmJtv2Tv/OPMnsWvmaCiA/pX4s/a862BIhvMfadWjRvEBxVUnq\nDRCLRQROOIYW1sN7ExeD2MdbLccL9d/0/XCwQGi9/WZ9W6hQQMAOiDoUVaEdGxbq\n4EcCV2vPw+Ky+msDUnWfUKKa570m0kgaFD3p0/4ERzOSFF23ffIVoV31qY3Hl6gK\n47oK3sPvAVlnh3XiYGVX/BirI4AqvxZxRoXdausa15dA46ObAVdv6g2+jGvH5cV8\nbY4nNa4iFuUboczaUkf6O/nDSqryJnto0pz8Rdp9fdeHpSf3GUqoIR+4u7ureLip\nn8DzDNaFAJM3FIdusPhfmD9ayoo+d87emwF2WO2UbBFBjTu9+vDn/RU0MbkUwvto\nqxR4q4UGSC03A0eCWsYzPhrqsO2lEf2Wqhd4RGPTwrdCGz8Dfm2UDLaK/wkaB+4K\n+mJdWKgvOwg+/Tl0RyY0lT0I2d6Chr9KDqwXR9Tp5pb/ObGzH0Q4IYmcll94n3Jz\nTc/GMqGVrFL00/qynwHHsEuXwv3m6VXSLR1mVG5aWoOUFZcMtjjDE2z/vVItXRjF\nIaol8SKDQKEVXVP1QyFl\n=6JP6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T22:53:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDNlYzA2MGZmOTJjYTdjNjFjNGNiN2Q3MGE5OTE1ODdjMDhiOGE3YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82","sha":"af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82"}],"sha":"3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/3ec060ff92ca7c61c4cb7d70a991587c08b8a7bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:15:33Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:15:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): run a final agent validation pass at the end of an orchestrated migrate run (#37069)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nThe agent validates each migration on its own, scoped to what that\nmigration meant to do. Breakage that no single migration owns falls\nthrough. A package bump can break a build, or two migrations can break\nsomething only together. nx reports the run as complete and the user\nfinds the broken workspace afterwards.\n\nIssues the agent deferred or gave up on stay listed in the completion\nreport with nobody left to act on them.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nOnce every migration is done, nx hands the agent one more step: a\nvalidation pass over the whole workspace. The agent runs lint, build and\nunit tests on the projects the upgrade touched, fixes breakage the\nupgrade caused, and leaves everything else alone. Deferred and\nunresolved issues go to this step by default, so the agent sees them\nbefore the run ends.\n\nThe pass ends like any other step. nx commits its result when the run\ncommits and a failure offers the same retry choices. The completion\nreport counts it. The pass is on by default and a run can opt out when\nit starts.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4617\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The pass is a step of its own kind in the run state, planned last. It\nhas no worker command: the reconcile parks it as awaiting the agent and\nwrites an instructions file the agent reads. Its handoff goes through\nthe same fold as a migration prompt.\n- The instructions name the ref the run started from (`gitRefAtInit`,\nHEAD before the checkpoint commit when one landed) so `nx affected\n--base <sha>` covers the upgrade''s changes, the package.json and\nlockfile changes the checkpoint captured included. Without a recorded\nref they fall back to `nx run-many`. A package bump committed before the\nrun starts is outside that diff; the run has no record of the commit\nthat carried it.\n- The pass may update any unresolved issue without a claim; migration\nsteps still need one. Resolved issues land on the pass''s ledger entry by\nid, not on the migrations that raised them.\n- `--final-validation` is hidden like the other orchestrator flags,\nsince nothing about the orchestrator is documented yet. An opted-out run\nplans no pass step, so its tallies and progress line count migrations\nonly. A parked pass blocks the resume-time checkpoint retry, because a\nlate checkpoint would absorb its edits.\n- Run files from before this change have no pass step and complete as\nbefore.\n- The completion analytics event counts migration steps only; the\nprinted tally counts the pass as well.\n- The runbook renders its pass guidance from the planned steps, so an\nopted-out run, or a run planned before the pass existed, gets a runbook\nthat promises no pass even when a missing runbook is re-rendered.\n- Headless behavior comes from the master session''s existing prompt\ngate; nothing is pass-specific.\n- The spawned agent session drops `NX_BASE` and `NX_HEAD`, which CI\nexports for its own `nx affected` runs; inherited, `NX_HEAD` would pin\nthe pass''s selection to that commit and drop uncommitted files. A\nworkspace that sets them in its env files gets them back on every nx\ncommand, and a session started by hand keeps its shell''s values. Whether\n`nx affected` should honour an environment head next to an explicit\n`--base` is a follow-up on the ticket.\n- The e2e scenarios opt out except the two that exercise the pass, so\nthe existing ones keep their step count.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9f2a4908e437363119be19a9fe41faca5522ddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/d9f2a4908e437363119be19a9fe41faca5522ddf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82","verification":{"payload":"tree d9f2a4908e437363119be19a9fe41faca5522ddf\nparent f7d64bbc4fe57ff4f0c29f6c2307a6eedd32e799\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1791238533 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791238533 -0400\n\nfeat(core): run a final agent validation pass at the end of an orchestrated migrate run (#37069)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nThe agent validates each migration on its own, scoped to what that\nmigration meant to do. Breakage that no single migration owns falls\nthrough. A package bump can break a build, or two migrations can break\nsomething only together. nx reports the run as complete and the user\nfinds the broken workspace afterwards.\n\nIssues the agent deferred or gave up on stay listed in the completion\nreport with nobody left to act on them.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nOnce every migration is done, nx hands the agent one more step: a\nvalidation pass over the whole workspace. The agent runs lint, build and\nunit tests on the projects the upgrade touched, fixes breakage the\nupgrade caused, and leaves everything else alone. Deferred and\nunresolved issues go to this step by default, so the agent sees them\nbefore the run ends.\n\nThe pass ends like any other step. nx commits its result when the run\ncommits and a failure offers the same retry choices. The completion\nreport counts it. The pass is on by default and a run can opt out when\nit starts.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4617\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The pass is a step of its own kind in the run state, planned last. It\nhas no worker command: the reconcile parks it as awaiting the agent and\nwrites an instructions file the agent reads. Its handoff goes through\nthe same fold as a migration prompt.\n- The instructions name the ref the run started from (`gitRefAtInit`,\nHEAD before the checkpoint commit when one landed) so `nx affected\n--base <sha>` covers the upgrade''s changes, the package.json and\nlockfile changes the checkpoint captured included. Without a recorded\nref they fall back to `nx run-many`. A package bump committed before the\nrun starts is outside that diff; the run has no record of the commit\nthat carried it.\n- The pass may update any unresolved issue without a claim; migration\nsteps still need one. Resolved issues land on the pass''s ledger entry by\nid, not on the migrations that raised them.\n- `--final-validation` is hidden like the other orchestrator flags,\nsince nothing about the orchestrator is documented yet. An opted-out run\nplans no pass step, so its tallies and progress line count migrations\nonly. A parked pass blocks the resume-time checkpoint retry, because a\nlate checkpoint would absorb its edits.\n- Run files from before this change have no pass step and complete as\nbefore.\n- The completion analytics event counts migration steps only; the\nprinted tally counts the pass as well.\n- The runbook renders its pass guidance from the planned steps, so an\nopted-out run, or a run planned before the pass existed, gets a runbook\nthat promises no pass even when a missing runbook is re-rendered.\n- Headless behavior comes from the master session''s existing prompt\ngate; nothing is pass-specific.\n- The spawned agent session drops `NX_BASE` and `NX_HEAD`, which CI\nexports for its own `nx affected` runs; inherited, `NX_HEAD` would pin\nthe pass''s selection to that commit and drop uncommitted files. A\nworkspace that sets them in its env files gets them back on every nx\ncommand, and a session started by hand keeps its shell''s values. Whether\n`nx affected` should honour an environment head next to an explicit\n`--base` is a follow-up on the ticket.\n- The e2e scenarios opt out except the two that exercise the pass, so\nthe existing ones keep their step count.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCGFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXnUQAHGsglWPDoMD0W0QLGGLK05E\nYz0kfOt6u7RzWhuoyTUPCApzgNnsq83FNf4RObj4ZjtS2paDOWerEqn1VTKrJ5aX\n4uFG87LhUJiuAYlcG1yLqDIyNyaUJCNdnJJ3tK9xr7vHmVlpF8R4e5hs+IfzSVHD\nrLaDhkn33DXVi7KM4R06FZaUYrAPQnydmmIw2IMzGngVw/3ShpjvV3rsSBGnM8gO\nX273lkW3WUwjew5KcoiOTRs0vuKxLwAty4sVqymSRzfTdZEf/BS1ujvnI7aOGKiC\nGWb9eZ1Psy6RiIDSAlh0xqce+Vt/sHzGyx10Lm+xKNkijYbs982JoHfbEjnN1o4e\npj5fiL3pam6e+eagWojUnVE0zCpu3ux8bThD5is2mrgZis0CXJ9W4X3S2T32sQrW\nbJ1OakIbGMF7SNxVtKcG77FtZlRJQGS2vIVjDp4i6EWMSfIbXAM3EnLzXD435qB+\n5DU2yuOJnAF69mlKkBLBpClHkIZlvCVeWjtN33+EqknnY+d4t13vaiKJC3wps9h2\n6VBP0GCXEAi5b46cu+fEDXysqwyKbxcRCG8DyrBZ6pK65tf0U9HYS/WUDEv90Br6\nN0L4kOg8Du7CXDYcWJaCMA3mRc+aR+nuV+nGetmGSzfyEqKebkMPttPqw0Xr58vq\n8kviss9LBIlmgrsjJVQD\n=b5wl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T22:15:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGFmMGI0ZmJlNzc4OWVjNTYxODA1N2NhZWU1ODMxNjcwNjRmYTZjODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/f7d64bbc4fe57ff4f0c29f6c2307a6eedd32e799","sha":"f7d64bbc4fe57ff4f0c29f6c2307a6eedd32e799","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f7d64bbc4fe57ff4f0c29f6c2307a6eedd32e799"}],"sha":"af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/af0b4fbe7789ec5618057caee583167064fa6c82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23272162?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/barbados-clemens","id":23272162,"login":"barbados-clemens","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjcyMTYy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbados-clemens","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f7d64bbc4fe57ff4f0c29f6c2307a6eedd32e799/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:30:53Z","email":"caleb@nrwl.io","name":"Caleb Ukle"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:30:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(nx-cloud): make the public api reference easier to use (#37241)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nthe deployed openapi spec defines the public api, but nx docs lack an\nendpoint reference and practical guidance for clients.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nclients can find the deployed contract and usage guidance in one place.\nlive loading prevents the docs from claiming a version the service does\nnot serve, and one model keeps the page and plain-text exports\nconsistent.\n\n- production currently serves v0-beta. deploy v1 and rebuild the docs to\nrefresh the reference.\n- secondary response-code link styling remains a cosmetic follow-up.\n- preview screenshots:\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/pull/37241#issuecomment-5935396949\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\ncloses: DOC-696","tree":{"sha":"705a97315e4ca9c4e7bfdf179e61758ae61c78d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/705a97315e4ca9c4e7bfdf179e61758ae61c78d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/f7d64bbc4fe57ff4f0c29f6c2307a6eedd32e799","verification":{"payload":"tree 705a97315e4ca9c4e7bfdf179e61758ae61c78d2\nparent ab845a8298971eeed8752b2f41b06bbbf13cce82\nauthor Caleb Ukle <caleb@nrwl.io> 1791235853 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791235853 +0000\n\ndocs(nx-cloud): make the public api reference easier to use (#37241)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nthe deployed openapi spec defines the public api, but nx docs lack an\nendpoint reference and practical guidance for clients.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nclients can find the deployed contract and usage guidance in one place.\nlive loading prevents the docs from claiming a version the service does\nnot serve, and one model keeps the page and plain-text exports\nconsistent.\n\n- production currently serves v0-beta. deploy v1 and rebuild the docs to\nrefresh the reference.\n- secondary response-code link styling remains a cosmetic follow-up.\n- preview screenshots:\nhttps://github.com/nrwl/nx/pull/37241#issuecomment-5935396949\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\ncloses: DOC-696","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxBcNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuX8QACcpSVx5XGQsQyde8EKrkBp3\ngIvVzLKqq2Xdi6STvxihM4BmeMe8lPMDGa3M3MKcFBRA55gpE+fsw+G8VlsO/naM\nYHGkRNEHVv7mpANH/hIcMBUfPi1mwzI77+M0hEFVgiBu83ZI10KSA9Rz0D6K50/z\nW0iJOz/YSBrunjHzWwympRVYMYcGbzCZPb0mbrxhMPAEj3H07pbP3BBADT4cfS2y\n/YI2Lj4XZ5BHiQ0JovKudMbsnZ6bdXSaqd+2ZFDWwRq98BKep1tgg2bDXeJF3994\nqYYDTYjtL1HV+eKKEd/Drx4IqXoPsxEB72YJ92yL7rLJCzsSwXwBoSWfc9FnZYfX\nmZ5m/Hgwou5bH4utDPwYLPh7QAgpU61KDc/vbXOCMG5Ausz9HhIspG1mpowuGq9/\nIOJgxNBzwK+KWxTMylKIARVaWhPreNjLBbxix3P1GraETGdsW5OICHHwWI2tjwAO\nLl4LlHSz4oeQq+q0n++JFoQfgwFJzHfRLo