witch is https://github.com/nrwl/ocean/pull/14118.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://snapshot.app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/69cdc268b6aa527e4129c2b4/sessions/Enable-chunked-DTE-task-graph-storage-V2-cb2863b9\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvlT8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWuoQAFdRizBo2MgqB02/uy9RAEsd\nKbHilWP3xorAMBJPR3Cb/Rowdr3EY/ZD2NnqUJEw0j9o54sNFGLpS2LPyiTOOxC5\ny0XZvTjcIIjc2oPcqAl22p96AqiMf8z2yY3moa/hcHATio1VLhMSCVnyKIN03qyC\n5W8gBrMvjLn4OozJ7cxg4bFDE1TIabY7wMnplOPkUprGZzdGZq5pl3msNOY4xGIA\nWyHmZVR9+NZD1o8E60wuMFA1PZ+8YzdFUrxySIIZLFVwvphtUOGR34X7+//LX1tF\nhq9mW91XY9m7smFO+ss97VtdU7WMrqC/hnsY6eq6/g/sqRWbSqgp4pzQF8POVAU8\nGSWiHUUjSFavMs6LQU4Cfk6IDZInDLb7IG4lhwCyDTw0jFHnYR2fx9HIvRVjjUlV\nSn2DXRqIStjQAd7bxaStU68BEuoy0P1qU0hobwFyM3UefURr5jwR4n0vIDXQR1D4\nTj3awpIzd/z0Tv6EO5z+htdB/Xy5nJnmW16ezPPzFr2EGvuaFtpy/IJLanETB5vT\ne1GMlwPgR8rPTDCibA06Cwm2ZKne42+3BUA4YVLgUcy+JZ/c2jwTjnp9fmaXEQTR\nObrukKT9r2I9Q+629n0qRW1Ee1Pg03zUFuxnsTIV+OGHbL7gCWdWshCoH+VmIh40\nm/LCJ0mgSWVyqjjdHdR2\n=W5Eq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:41:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/5c91c94976a02595f1c61bbf2fd45117a21a93fb","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDVjOTFjOTQ5NzZhMDI1OTVmMWM2MWJiZjJmZDQ1MTE3YTIxYTkzZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/1d08795d3b5589fa2a562d16c29a1ef77269ff72","sha":"1d08795d3b5589fa2a562d16c29a1ef77269ff72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1d08795d3b5589fa2a562d16c29a1ef77269ff72"}],"sha":"5c91c94976a02595f1c61bbf2fd45117a21a93fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/5c91c94976a02595f1c61bbf2fd45117a21a93fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/542149?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/comp615","id":542149,"login":"comp615","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MjE0OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/comp615","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1d08795d3b5589fa2a562d16c29a1ef77269ff72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:39:58Z","email":"ccroom@squareup.com","name":"Charlie Croom"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:39:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(release): preserve private dev-only workspace dependencies (#37193)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n#36334 correctly made Nx Release resolve local workspace protocols for\ndependencies outside the current version set. This prevents publish\nmanifests from retaining unresolved `workspace:` versions and allows\nconfigured projects that are not being versioned to use their concrete\ncurrent version.\n\nThe manifest-wide scan also reaches private, dev-only workspace\ndependencies. When one of those projects is intentionally excluded from\nNx Release, there is no configured version resolver, so releasing the\nconsuming project now fails. This affects private build tooling that\ndoes not need a publishable version and cannot be published as a runtime\ndependency.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nKeep #36334''s resolution behavior for publish-relevant and resolvable\ndependencies, but preserve an unresolved local protocol when all of\nthese conditions hold:\n\n- the dependency is dev-only;\n- its target manifest is explicitly private;\n- it is absent from dependencies, peerDependencies, and\noptionalDependencies; and\n- resolution failed specifically because the target is not configured\nfor Nx Release.\n\nThe dependency resolver now marks that specific failure with\n`NX_RELEASE_PROJECT_NOT_CONFIGURED`. The `@nx/js` version action\nrecognizes the structural error code and applies the narrow manifest\npolicy without matching message text or depending on a public error\nconstructor. Public packages, runtime/peer/optional dependencies,\nmissing or malformed manifests, configured private projects, and\nunrelated resolver failures remain strict.\n\nRegression coverage includes `workspace:` and `file:` protocols and\nverifies each strict boundary, including mixed dependency collections\nand malformed target manifests.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37192\n\nFollow-up to #36334. Related prior reports: #28695, #29602, and #30670.\n\n🤖 Drafted and implemented with AI assistance.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>","tree":{"sha":"082d8fabf5f7e4ac6a36aa03779ef3e1b82b91a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/082d8fabf5f7e4ac6a36aa03779ef3e1b82b91a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/1d08795d3b5589fa2a562d16c29a1ef77269ff72","verification":{"payload":"tree 082d8fabf5f7e4ac6a36aa03779ef3e1b82b91a1\nparent 0b8bab7f0977db85130edd82f7c5ea8a80bc5b3a\nauthor Charlie Croom <ccroom@squareup.com> 1790858398 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790858398 +0000\n\nfix(release): preserve private dev-only workspace dependencies (#37193)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n#36334 correctly made Nx Release resolve local workspace protocols for\ndependencies outside the current version set. This prevents publish\nmanifests from retaining unresolved `workspace:` versions and allows\nconfigured projects that are not being versioned to use their concrete\ncurrent version.\n\nThe manifest-wide scan also reaches private, dev-only workspace\ndependencies. When one of those projects is intentionally excluded from\nNx Release, there is no configured version resolver, so releasing the\nconsuming project now fails. This affects private build tooling that\ndoes not need a publishable version and cannot be published as a runtime\ndependency.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nKeep #36334''s resolution behavior for publish-relevant and resolvable\ndependencies, but preserve an unresolved local protocol when all of\nthese conditions hold:\n\n- the dependency is dev-only;\n- its target manifest is explicitly private;\n- it is absent from dependencies, peerDependencies, and\noptionalDependencies; and\n- resolution failed specifically because the target is not configured\nfor Nx Release.\n\nThe dependency resolver now marks that specific failure with\n`NX_RELEASE_PROJECT_NOT_CONFIGURED`. The `@nx/js` version action\nrecognizes the structural error code and applies the narrow manifest\npolicy without matching message text or depending on a public error\nconstructor. Public packages, runtime/peer/optional dependencies,\nmissing or malformed manifests, configured private projects, and\nunrelated resolver failures remain strict.\n\nRegression coverage includes `workspace:` and `file:` protocols and\nverifies each strict boundary, including mixed dependency collections\nand malformed target manifests.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37192\n\nFollow-up to #36334. Related prior reports: #28695, #29602, and #30670.\n\n🤖 Drafted and implemented with AI assistance.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvlSeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGBQQABlPl5+gNLD3gbK1FlQ2QZJ7\nd1TnAA/jTfsoH1/hZaiq+aRPKHcYq3cyiIxnAdPB2f/iqnRDNbrqT5ntnVBGh4se\nW4v/4oaNtHuNJzfrq7X1rC1vXUVAWWEOJlJlF/jzdi4vKI1SDmD2JDqZ+Q0VowbF\na+E0nOL12CM8n4KS61ma8KykIiaYFaBzCWizVh7V5hGhv9t3KmGc+15rJhQ+6Pbc\nD2BR1/deZJ1bCg5PpeMqzFVB+rTdgpcZYn4edcR9liGa9xBRCq65GpT2BR3u51Jg\nGZA9mCGwgBSxuxlU2tCGQFLPJ4a25vPbIB2bbFEz3nBbo11BS+kPJSqJNQ8CbZIm\nkmXLUFbBHW6E4xxY+4sqwIAFu9ICesS5cFElYnREy2g3n5lp2EiaIeiP4IDmjQgG\nrUlVPCvRIEQuGE2daWNrRZarrjtcW3b7z5A4zKzGiuTENxQtIR9gA1N8sf9yrO85\nBp23kDyTP2wCr1UeuLL2EXyli1YT0pSO5YA/MfDdDPFTzsSCIKT59oK6S7MwGUk6\n63/4FFqFwucOYrlxXhMw90LeVbw7GddyQ9wTXMo4NLF5VhnBM9pWOAlGiHItxFcg\nUH9og+fmAi+NWQGp6S4/h9eXiypW69cVdWjz2J4gxqR64DdYRf8urKK7o3WH2eNf\n76iYnA6zyf2RlIfIcJDR\n=ZL6W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:39:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_i