9c1c","sha":"da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c"}],"sha":"70dab9ed69f997780f53932837924d2ca13fa71f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/70dab9ed69f997780f53932837924d2ca13fa71f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:27:53Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:27:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): tighten task inputs for nx-dev, astro-docs, angular and e2e-utils (#37230)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n- `nx-dev` `next:build` uses `\"...\"`, so it inherits `default` /\n`^default` from `@nx/next`. Any spec or test config change in nx-dev or\nits dependencies invalidates the build.\n- Any lockfile change marks every project as affected.\n- The `e2e-ci` and `e2e-ci--**/**` target defaults replace the inferred\ne2e inputs instead of extending them.\n- `astro-docs` `prebuild-banner`, `prebuild-agent-skills` and `preview`\ndeclare no inputs, although they read files and env vars outside the\ndefault set.\n- `astro-docs` `test` is an `nx:noop`, but it gets the default inputs,\nso any change in the project changes its hash.\n- `angular` `build-ng` declares no inputs, so it falls back to Nx''s\nbroad default.\n- `e2e-utils` depends on `@nx/angular` only to read\n`angularDevkitVersion`. That puts Angular and its dependencies into the\n`^production` inputs of every e2e project.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- `nx-dev` `next:build` uses `production`, `^production` and\n`externalDependencies: [\"next\"]`, plus its existing dependent-output and\nenv inputs.\n- It also declares the spec/test/stories files in each folder that\n`styles/main.css` lists with `@source`. Tailwind''s PostCSS plugin passes\neach of those folders to Turbopack as a `dir-dependency` glob without\nthe `@source not` exclusions, so `next build` reads those files (the\nsandbox flagged `feed-answer.spec.tsx`, `heading.schema.spec.ts` and\n`transform-image-path.spec.ts`). `^production` leaves them out.\n- `nx.json`:\n- `pluginsConfig[\"@nx/js\"].projectsAffectedByDependencyUpdates: \"auto\"`,\nso a lockfile change only affects projects that use the updated\npackages.\n- `\"...\"` added to the `e2e-ci` and `e2e-ci--**/**` inputs, so they keep\nthe inferred inputs.\n- `astro-docs` declares what each target reads:\n  - `prebuild-banner`: its script and the `BANNER_URL` env var.\n  - `prebuild-agent-skills`: its script and the `NETLIFY` env var.\n- `preview`: `default`, the `packages/*` JSON files the sidebar reads\nwhen `astro.config.mjs` loads, the `astro` package, and the build\noutput.\n- `test` (an `nx:noop` that only aggregates `validate-links` and\n`format`): no inputs, since the noop reads nothing.\n- `angular` `build-ng` uses `production` / `^production`, matching the\nrepo''s `build` target default.\n- `e2e-utils` reads the default Angular CLI version for `runNgNew` from\nthe installed `@angular/cli` (the `angular` catalog keeps it on the same\nline as `angularDevkitVersion`), and no longer depends on `@nx/angular`.\n- This only narrows the 6 e2e projects that don''t reach `@nx/js`\n(lerna-smoke-tests, graph-client, docker, dotnet, gradle, maven). The\nothers still reach every framework through `@nx/js` → `@nx/workspace`,\nwhose `implicitDependencies` list the lazy-loaded plugins.\n\n**Testing**\n- `nx show target inputs nx-dev:next:build --check …` confirms the three\nflagged spec files are inputs, and that `nx-dev/ui-podcast`, which\n`main.css` doesn''t list, is not.\n- Tailwind''s PostCSS plugin (4.1.11 and the latest 4.3.3) emits\n`dir-dependency` globs for the `@source` folders that match those spec\nfiles. `@source not` only affects Tailwind''s own scan.\n- `e2e-utils` typecheck and oxlint pass, and `create-project-utils.ts`\nloads with the new version lookup. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`\npasses.\n- Not yet verified: `nx-dev` `next:build` and `astro-docs` `preview`\nunder the sandbox, and the Angular e2e tests that use `runNgNew`\n(`ng-add`, `nx-init-angular`).\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Tighten-task-inputs-for-Next.js-builds-and-affected-0a2e52fc\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"d27b45eba10ff5cae0cf47d14d16827fdc968694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/d27b45eba10ff5cae0cf47d14d16827fdc968694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c","verification":{"payload":"tree d27b45eba10ff5cae0cf47d14d16827fdc968694\nparent 5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790774873 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790774873 -0400\n\nchore(repo): tighten task inputs for nx-dev, astro-docs, angular and e2e-utils (#37230)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n- `nx-dev` `next:build` uses `\"...\"`, so it inherits `default` /\n`^default` from `@nx/next`. Any spec or test config change in nx-dev or\nits dependencies invalidates the build.\n- Any lockfile change marks every project as affected.\n- The `e2e-ci` and `e2e-ci--**/**` target defaults replace the inferred\ne2e inputs instead of extending them.\n- `astro-docs` `prebuild-banner`, `prebuild-agent-skills` and `preview`\ndeclare no inputs, although they read files and env vars outside the\ndefault set.\n- `astro-docs` `test` is an `nx:noop`, but it gets the default inputs,\nso any change in the project changes its hash.\n- `angular` `build-ng` declares no inputs, so it falls back to Nx''s\nbroad default.\n- `e2e-utils` depends on `@nx/angular` only to read\n`angularDevkitVersion`. That puts Angular and its dependencies into the\n`^production` inputs of every e2e project.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- `nx-dev` `next:build` uses `production`, `^production` and\n`externalDependencies: [\"next\"]`, plus its existing dependent-output and\nenv inputs.\n- It also declares the spec/test/stories files in each folder that\n`styles/main.css` lists with `@source`. Tailwind''s PostCSS plugin passes\neach of those folders to Turbopack as a `dir-dependency` glob without\nthe `@source not` exclusions, so `next build` reads those files (the\nsandbox flagged `feed-answer.spec.tsx`, `heading.schema.spec.ts` and\n`transform-image-path.spec.ts`). `^production` leaves them out.\n- `nx.json`:\n- `pluginsConfig[\"@nx/js\"].projectsAffectedByDependencyUpdates: \"auto\"`,\nso a lockfile change only affects projects that use the updated\npackages.\n- `\"...\"` added to the `e2e-ci` and `e2e-ci--**/**` inputs, so they keep\nthe inferred inputs.\n- `astro-docs` declares what each target reads:\n  - `prebuild-banner`: its script and the `BANNER_URL` env var.\n  - `prebuild-agent-skills`: its script and the `NETLIFY` env var.\n- `preview`: `default`, the `packages/*` JSON files the sidebar reads\nwhen `astro.config.mjs` loads, the `astro` package, and the build\noutput.\n- `test` (an `nx:noop` that only aggregates `validate-links` and\n`format`): no inputs, since the noop reads nothing.\n- `angular` `build-ng` uses `production` / `^production`, matching the\nrepo''s `build` target default.\n- `e2e-utils` reads the default Angular CLI version for `runNgNew` from\nthe installed `@angular/cli` (the `angular` catalog keeps it on the same\nline as `angularDevkitVersion`), and no longer depends on `@nx/angular`.\n- This only narrows the 6 e2e projects that don''t reach `@nx/js`\n(lerna-smoke-tests, graph-client, docker, dotnet, gradle, maven). The\nothers still reach every framework through `@nx/js` → `@nx/workspace`,\nwhose `implicitDependencies` list the lazy-loaded plugins.\n\n**Testing**\n- `nx show target inputs nx-dev:next:build --check …` confirms the three\nflagged spec files are inputs, and that `nx-dev/ui-podcast`, which\n`main.css` doesn''t list, is not.\n- Tailwind''s PostCSS plugin (4.1.11 and the latest 4.3.3) emits\n`dir-dependency` globs for the `@source` folders that match those spec\nfiles. `@source not` only affects Tailwind''s own scan.\n- `e2e-utils` typecheck and oxlint pass, and `create-project-utils.ts`\nloads with the new version lookup. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`\npasses.\n- Not yet verified: `nx-dev` `next:build` and `astro-docs` `preview`\nunder the sandbox, and the Angular e2e tests that use `runNgNew`\n(`ng-add`, `nx-init-angular`).\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Tighten-task-inputs-for-Next.js-builds-and-affected-0a2e52fc\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQ5ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADTcQAAVCyS4KIxqPhEZIdRFdrWhy\nb4DxhcvAgfxaSd2bCwlyx1lX0TA3b8YslxeyZri9kVdvLHFaSsC72kUPNJoOxPK8\nvVpEvqYSdE/LNVbCfYzptRYQl5f1ZHl8jG3qweY8MpPV9K56xkx7/5hC/H/0yYOr\n+L6WtRBdwjU+yqGyZL/r70Q/ekBG2A25HuVXhnbBpwXhcZcJkMvS60QFGOngDmXD\nANTu8xLIUwtLghasVohihItPjxs9nxbLXzQytdy6YU6duhHFIqV9knpxmi7Kpek5\n0C2Pii3HkYGKZG1sTWTNgPAu8YygNezHdcprHl3nO+IKoHa2xgA+F24w0MFQU5An\nmlTUAOEi4GGI7wMeTXedkyNih/Jiadzc+a2LzL/eO20sE+9UembzAQB0h9kGsHMX\nPZhIRamQ484tzdkdcA7dmvmbh6W4qUetiODaPp1/uYdzmE/ffhr62/QIgd2pivsT\n4a5oN2hL06dh3Cf72n0xbjxoNXZJ/vsnBm63jSu+VVhEM78Ty48CN0EZl9j6mENi\n4tkOiVNUUlbq4Jgmgbcb7agYFRtecpVVmdGXtto8uoPycFVDdMTAwiGsNMm8RUah\neGKWzZ8zxbaZrOf6/kK1Q0l+6nYkyI0T9J11ebC2ASHef5Zn5Eln2HSAWLgpWUOE\nfB5mzK7fJyX49DUMYCmd\n=74XA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:27:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGRhMzY2YjFiYzZmNDZlNTM2ODFhZjI3YTExNGNmNjgxNzJhZTljMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4","sha":"5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4"}],"sha":"da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/da366b1bc6f46e53681af27a114cf68172ae9c1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/231424177?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy","id":231424177,"login":"alexandrucojocaru-creatopy","node_id":"U_kgDODctAsQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexandrucojocaru-creatopy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:25:02Z","email":"alexandru.cojocaru@thebrief.ai","name":"alexandrucojocaru-creatopy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T08:25:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): traverse past module-format package.json stubs when locating npm dependencies (#36985)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`TargetProjectLocator.readPackageJson` returns `null` when the directly\nresolvable `<pkg>/package.json` is a module-format stub\n(`{\"type\":\"commonjs\"}`) without `name`/`version`, and again at the first\nsuch stub during the upward traversal. A wildcard export (`\"./*\":\n\"./dist/cjs/*\"`) with no explicit `./package.json` export produces\nexactly that stub (e.g. `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `react-router-dom`,\n`recharts`, `react-markdown`).\n\nThe import then only matches through the unversioned `npm:<name>` node,\nwhich exists solely for the hoisted (root-level) version. When the\npackage is declared by projects but not by the root `package.json`, and\nmore than one version exists, the project loses its edge to the package:\n`nx graph` shows none, and `@nx/dependency-checks` reports the\ndependency as unused (its `--fix` then deletes a real dependency).\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAs the method''s JSDoc already states: keep traversing past a stub until\na package.json with `name` and `version` is found, then match the\nversioned node (`npm:@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.28.0`).\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #36984\n\nRelated: #30342 (fixed by #30511, which added the traversal and its\ncomment but kept both early returns).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `readPackageJson`: the directly-resolvable branch falls through to the\ntraversal when the manifest lacks `name`/`version`; the traversal caches\na stub as `null` and continues upward instead of returning.\n- Spec: new case `@rerouted/pkg` with a rerouted `package.json` and a\n**versioned-only** external node (`npm:@rerouted/pkg@2.0.0`). The\nexisting `@json2csv/plainjs` case is unchanged; it passes through the\nunversioned fallback node and never reached the traversal.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Minimal pnpm workspace (two libs on `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.28.0\nand 1.29.0, root does not declare it): before, both projects have no\nedge; after, `npm:@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.28.0` and `@1.29.0`\nrespectively.\n- Applied as a pnpm patch to `nx@23.1.0` in a 119-project workspace:\n`@nx/dependency-checks` false positive gone, and the project graph keeps\nevery project-to-package edge it had while the root manifest still\nhoisted everything.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"3bf73ff06051418a198e968921418716df986d60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/3bf73ff06051418a198e968921418716df986d60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 3bf73ff06051418a198e968921418716df986d60\nparent 9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca\nauthor alexandrucojocaru-creatopy <alexandru.cojocaru@thebrief.ai> 1790756702 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790756702 +0200\n\nfix(core): traverse past module-format package.json stubs when locating npm dependencies (#36985)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`TargetProjectLocator.readPackageJson` returns `null` when the directly\nresolvable `<pkg>/package.json` is a module-format stub\n(`{\"type\":\"commonjs\"}`) without `name`/`version`, and again at the first\nsuch stub during the upward traversal. A wildcard export (`\"./*\":\n\"./dist/cjs/*\"`) with no explicit `./package.json` export produces\nexactly that stub (e.g. `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, `react-router-dom`,\n`recharts`, `react-markdown`).\n\nThe import then only matches through the unversioned `npm:<name>` node,\nwhich exists solely for the hoisted (root-level) version. When the\npackage is declared by projects but not by the root `package.json`, and\nmore than one version exists, the project loses its edge to the package:\n`nx graph` shows none, and `@nx/dependency-checks` reports the\ndependency as unused (its `--fix` then deletes a real dependency).\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAs the method''s JSDoc already states: keep traversing past a stub until\na package.json with `name` and `version` is found, then match the\nversioned node (`npm:@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.28.0`).\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #36984\n\nRelated: #30342 (fixed by #30511, which added the traversal and its\ncomment but kept both early returns).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `readPackageJson`: the directly-resolvable branch falls through to the\ntraversal when the manifest lacks `name`/`version`; the traversal caches\na stub as `null` and continues upward instead of returning.\n- Spec: new case `@rerouted/pkg` with a rerouted `package.json` and a\n**versioned-only** external node (`npm:@rerouted/pkg@2.0.0`). The\nexisting `@json2csv/plainjs` case is unchanged; it passes through the\nunversioned fallback node and never reached the traversal.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Minimal pnpm workspace (two libs on `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.28.0\nand 1.29.0, root does not declare it): before, both projects have no\nedge; after, `npm:@modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.28.0` and `@1.29.0`\nrespectively.\n- Applied as a pnpm patch to `nx@23.1.0` in a 119-project workspace:\n`@nx/dependency-checks` false positive gone, and the project graph keeps\nevery project-to-package edge it had while the root manifest still\nhoisted everything.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvMdeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH74QACd9X+5xNtobKV3q4PPigg4m\nnkWtKpd2ipRL0h/Z9BETXHfmGl9F1gTwtYErBzfNLnYywrp/b7fUw2rLLejbUX7p\nVofSG7qtC9Q03QvDY1B/V8YagJcbB/yW6gkWugPZmuSDmjesWy+eFaDa0AIok15v\nKRaTBulxbQUx5JJWoWyV40BuWa6fWS09KsGpTIdk5FFazlQFh98qW5XknhTFfSPG\nBsQ5qQdZTgDP3eBxPsac0bM4Lb/JpD8qN/CtW/VJuk3wi7MBkyCM/NlFAGt7HzXp\nqKD/V/qm6z/lfd0lWh0sXZjC0TfzDDujfJE/c7bc2QwJsplxWwT4ouWBlMoLbokr\n3T/9yJY/RT4hsPrsP8g2Ir6XDXx9zkEFlJfLrXTn5lj+VuWvhspUdgdPcC3FP59W\nPJTooMF6q1naD/tnqPPnd7rayQI9fJlkpRuCpLTdWWleKi+sBjEZ/WelTETpfBBQ\n+og1bnm+KfX+ArC/x1ifDxFxXfbyBOh2vNyoXEF1DCohc5wKBf3dNUMgH/u5OMr8\nJIOvosOb7bgtFYw5XUqNp3kxyIRRKMjc3mUiH8Ut8853o4CvHMHYJIeMX2uWs7gG\nIRcSYBw8R0fSg0ZwGEE0FKRzOuyAdZaVnuWETVqyOeJqDAiv/pZCKf+X+kG0nWH6\nplQzhq7+teMvEyv01IIo\n=+Tug\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T08:25:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDVmNmM1MTdlNTZhNzYxZTNlNzA5YjgxNmUzZmM2OGZjZGY2MmE4YzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca","sha":"9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca"}],"sha":"5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/5f6c517e56a761e3e709b816e3fc68fcdf62a8c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:46:06Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:46:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): migrate to nx 23.3.0-beta.7 (#37202)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe repo runs its own tooling on nx `23.3.0-beta.5`. CI selects affected\nwork by whole project and hashes tasks from declared inputs only.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- Bumps nx and `@nx/*` to `23.3.0-beta.7`. There are no migrations from\nbeta.5.\n- Sets `NX_LEGACY_AFFECTED=false` in the root `.env`, so `nx affected`\nselects tasks whose inputs changed (#36825). Every nx command loads that\nfile, so local runs match CI. `.gitignore` gets a `!/.env` exception.\n- Sets `NX_CLOUD_USE_IO_SNAPSHOTS=true` in the CI workflow env and in\nthe Nx Agents env. Nx Cloud records I/O snapshots, and Nx hashes tasks\nfrom them (ultracache, #37165).\n\nbeta.7 includes #37212, which fixes the agent crash beta.6 hit with\nsnapshots on.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nPart of a linked migration across nx, ocean, nx-labs, nx-examples and\nnx-console.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Migrate-to-nx-23.3.0-beta.6-with-ultracache-and-task-based-affected-f4012f97\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"80b92ac9bb52ebe47ea9e5b342b789eb9b64cc61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/80b92ac9bb52ebe47ea9e5b342b789eb9b64cc61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca","verification":{"payload":"tree 80b92ac9bb52ebe47ea9e5b342b789eb9b64cc61\nparent 03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790725566 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790725566 -0500\n\nchore(repo): migrate to nx 23.3.0-beta.7 (#37202)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe repo runs its own tooling on nx `23.3.0-beta.5`. CI selects affected\nwork by whole project and hashes tasks from declared inputs only.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- Bumps nx and `@nx/*` to `23.3.0-beta.7`. There are no migrations from\nbeta.5.\n- Sets `NX_LEGACY_AFFECTED=false` in the root `.env`, so `nx affected`\nselects tasks whose inputs changed (#36825). Every nx command loads that\nfile, so local runs match CI. `.gitignore` gets a `!/.env` exception.\n- Sets `NX_CLOUD_USE_IO_SNAPSHOTS=true` in the CI workflow env and in\nthe Nx Agents env. Nx Cloud records I/O snapshots, and Nx hashes tasks\nfrom them (ultracache, #37165).\n\nbeta.7 includes #37212, which fixes the agent crash beta.6 hit with\nsnapshots on.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nPart of a linked migration across nx, ocean, nx-labs, nx-examples and\nnx-console.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Migrate-to-nx-23.3.0-beta.6-with-ultracache-and-task-based-affected-f4012f97\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvE2+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuZMQAHSoM4RU9E+sfoG8Iu+DjbGx\naAKef3ydMPJrLLVtHT83UPZeW9gMlJOOO7nhgixAeRYbBeNXMoeWB6oDUa2Nmu63\nKhMjl1ORw4UBajHutLnXjwIQnTuH26YJslUtUcQCcSM773Dvg56bfJSun8FKBdgL\nfVQWCwUtFI+Nb/ByI2WjGfkEZTwJlHobByj24uu+9YgvAfG9zT8BrJ+rZJxBle3+\nwvvlGr4RF8qwZQMcoDdYbhnDi1GRffb3CZL+NRny9ry9H2EGsu281sYULPf5MsZ9\n1aROV2pVUE4l0iy+khxZvbH2kBjitXi8GR+MpEDVs0nKAk41uHDKhsGSgGAM+MKE\nvsJ1ytnEFBGd1U2m7UVEUjP7qDWcmoENx0pO0cHs+tJ9wnpObEXGvFSS3sIbDCsc\nkC6kncwAZe/GDkYvaxZX42xkgcx1AgU4XKScUrI/QYLkI6WZicouzpqnLcM94m6m\nI1/h5Mp3UtD0Dn2oLgDek2iw+YwF8BRi2g2Dk4WkEnaYej/s8kTp5HpK5ki9iARY\ngVCJEEJvv8qinWJ7pukJp1f+JuCxmWwhFGcOA72rbBsgD3AzxRIjp+5G9ALOGHaT\nUHIx+bsmyFHSP9Efgskqnf9KN3C+SlfLSW3wcQpdu9NSCohYMpqEWvGcyMNaK6ng\nim3OL2q/ANwIjbiGuOim\n=dQPX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T23:46:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDlkODExMzUzNTk3Nzk5ZTJmMjk5ZDVkNzRjYWUyYWEyMDlhYWViY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28","sha":"03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28"}],"sha":"9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9d811353597799e2f299d5d74cae2aa209aaebca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:12:19Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:12:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): report abandoned, revisited and resumed orchestrated migrate runs and their dispense ordinals (#36989)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nAn orchestrated run is many short nx calls driven by an agent. The agent\ncan stop calling nx at any point. Nothing runs at the end to say so. In\nanalytics an abandoned run only shows up as a start event with no\ncompletion event. The classic loop never had this gap, because one\nprocess sends both its start and its end.\n\nWhen a session continues an existing run, or finds one and reports it,\nanalytics sees nothing either. The start event is sent once per run, so\na restarted session leaves no trace.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAnalytics can tell how orchestrated runs end and how far they got. The\nabandonment, existing-run and resume events carry the run''s tallies:\napplied, skipped, given up on, and steps handed out.\n\n- nx started the agent and the run is still active when the agent exits:\nan abandonment event, with the agent id.\n- nx finds an existing run and reports it instead of starting one: an\nexisting-run event. It says whether another nx migrate process was\nworking on the run at the time, so a revisit of an idle run can be told\nfrom a collision with a live one.\n- A session continues an existing run: a resume event.\n- nx hands a new step to the agent: a step event with the step''s\nposition (the handed-out count) and attempt. Counting these per position\nshows where runs stop.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4818\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- A run id dimension was the first plan and was dropped. The GA property\nhas no BigQuery export, so an undeclared parameter cannot be read. GA\ncollapses unique-id dimensions into an \"(other)\" row past a few hundred\nvalues a day. The new events reuse the existing dimensions; no Rust\nchange.\n- The existing per-response dispense event now carries the same step\nposition, but it repeats until the step moves. It feeds the action mix\nper position, not the survival curve.\n`migrate_orchestrator_step_dispensed` fires once per durable step\nhandout and is the curve.\n- `runTallies()` in `state-machine.ts` derives the event tallies from\n`tallySteps()`, so the completion summary, the completion event and the\nthree run-level events share one step classification. The step and\ndispense events take only their position from the same dispense count.\nAdopted steps count as applied. The given-up count rides\n`majors_crossed`, a declared numeric dimension no orchestrator event\nused.\n- A bare `--run-id` reconcile is not a resume: nothing in run state\nmarks the first call after a lost session. The existing-run report\noffers the continue in the resume shape on both paths, so a revisit that\ncontinues sends the existing-run event and then a resume.\n- A session that failed to start its agent with the run left active\nsends both the error event and the abandonment event. That fall-through\norder predates this change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"24df94b6b890bc1538cd0c204d608a2319c25324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/24df94b6b890bc1538cd0c204d608a2319c25324"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28","verification":{"payload":"tree 24df94b6b890bc1538cd0c204d608a2319c25324\nparent d73fb1b70068eea5646a2443e34720ca01fb3ae0\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1790719939 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790719939 -0400\n\nfeat(core): report abandoned, revisited and resumed orchestrated migrate runs and their dispense ordinals (#36989)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nAn orchestrated run is many short nx calls driven by an agent. The agent\ncan stop calling nx at any point. Nothing runs at the end to say so. In\nanalytics an abandoned run only shows up as a start event with no\ncompletion event. The classic loop never had this gap, because one\nprocess sends both its start and its end.\n\nWhen a session continues an existing run, or finds one and reports it,\nanalytics sees nothing either. The start event is sent once per run, so\na restarted session leaves no trace.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAnalytics can tell how orchestrated runs end and how far they got. The\nabandonment, existing-run and resume events carry the run''s tallies:\napplied, skipped, given up on, and steps handed out.\n\n- nx started the agent and the run is still active when the agent exits:\nan abandonment event, with the agent id.\n- nx finds an existing run and reports it instead of starting one: an\nexisting-run event. It says whether another nx migrate process was\nworking on the run at the time, so a revisit of an idle run can be told\nfrom a collision with a live one.\n- A session continues an existing run: a resume event.\n- nx hands a new step to the agent: a step event with the step''s\nposition (the handed-out count) and attempt. Counting these per position\nshows where runs stop.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4818\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- A run id dimension was the first plan and was dropped. The GA property\nhas no BigQuery export, so an undeclared parameter cannot be read. GA\ncollapses unique-id dimensions into an \"(other)\" row past a few hundred\nvalues a day. The new events reuse the existing dimensions; no Rust\nchange.\n- The existing per-response dispense event now carries the same step\nposition, but it repeats until the step moves. It feeds the action mix\nper position, not the survival curve.\n`migrate_orchestrator_step_dispensed` fires once per durable step\nhandout and is the curve.\n- `runTallies()` in `state-machine.ts` derives the event tallies from\n`tallySteps()`, so the completion summary, the completion event and the\nthree run-level events share one step classification. The step and\ndispense events take only their position from the same dispense count.\nAdopted steps count as applied. The given-up count rides\n`majors_crossed`, a declared numeric dimension no orchestrator event\nused.\n- A bare `--run-id` reconcile is not a resume: nothing in run state\nmarks the first call after a lost session. The existing-run report\noffers the continue in the resume shape on both paths, so a revisit that\ncontinues sends the existing-run event and then a resume.\n- A session that failed to start its agent with the run left active\nsends both the error event and the abandonment event. That fall-through\norder predates this change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvDfDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFQYQAKLCRfME+10AuLI4JZkmMS5A\n1aiAL3Kg+Vv0yvBoSR2TTYtxzVXoCyEJ2/PJnKw56qF5+LG3fmTH7Rmcd+1DE0pm\n67PRAye2H3afpNej/+72viIDFOOUqVZC7Wzi4X5ushgsoInIm4ytAduD00yfCLTf\nXTjbCKtIRK/nzNLLjcI/WZ43XBDP3rEVeM9r6o4d1z93WtrU1Hz/o/UUk/8REKqI\nhaFLJXq2mtF/AwWU4RAtC1wwO/BIWdHOSHm2Xs349/CFnHVTVpKCdyNps16qQJ4Q\n2rHUJrlhdqc6KoPUOhR2jMRpYQDdJ0bBhLO6EpOI1hXkVBcro3gOcHHQ4uqnxOF0\n24mMEnk68HPPxuWfP74QOo+7MThRzgUgSid1IPlfWt3zUmQjiVXaNfssPYJtWWX8\nF3tKoe2vzwJysQVM6RgOCX3b5GxcW3tI+qySsSj6ECpjGnb2fTIR4Tq2rrcXGNnO\nufkuOkx372e2xV63cl/SeJAKqIeVhMqQlzp3ce5d/tvPmMvzk7FDOkZU9ogiYpvM\niVyoAfv20HOcAq4ghAr/6/Hv7MNW8Nao5PadNjLbf/E1Vkcbrlx7As0MoajyfBtw\nDWOj0no52UoToRCUQLFbcU8jzwOqSY+51yA7o/U3lc0nGWSu2b573DjVKL1r7pmj\nvtbkFelxLG54K3rBhMXk\n=oRbi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T22:12:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDAzZmFjZWVlMDg0ZDAyYTc2MjczYWNhODJiOWFhZjEzMjRhNThiMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/d73fb1b70068eea5646a2443e34720ca01fb3ae0","sha":"d73fb1b70068eea5646a2443e34720ca01fb3ae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d73fb1b70068eea5646a2443e34720ca01fb3ae0"}],"sha":"03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/03faceee084d02a76273aca82b9aaf1324a58b28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d73fb1b70068eea5646a2443e34720ca01fb3ae0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:12:18Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:12:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): report an active orchestrated migrate run instead of resuming it (#36988)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nWhen a run is already on disk, `nx migrate --run-migrations` either\npicks it up silently (same plan) or stops with a plan-mismatch error.\nThe user learns nothing about that run. Picking it up can dispense past\nsteps whose work is gone from the tree. It can open a second agent\nsession over a parked run, so two agents edit the same workspace.\nDropping a run means deleting its directory by hand, even while another\nnx process is still working on it.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nnx reports the run and starts nothing. The report lists:\n\n- the run id and its age\n- the branch then and now\n- progress, and the commit and install policy the run recorded\n- whether its commits are still reachable from HEAD\n- open issues, live workers, other nx migrate processes on the run, and\nother runs on disk\n- how many applied migrations the new plan would apply again\n\nThen it gives two commands. `--run-migrations --agentic --run-id=<id>`,\nwith the recorded policy flags, continues the run. `--run-migrations\n--start-fresh --run-id=<id>` deletes that run''s record and starts over;\nwhen the newest active run is another, nx reports it instead. Both need\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR=true` set, and the report says so.\n\nInside an agent, the report goes out as an `existing-run` block for the\nagent to show the user. When nx started the agent itself, it asks in the\nterminal: continue, start fresh, or abort. When it cannot ask, it prints\nboth commands and exits 1. Without a terminal, or with\n`--no-interactive`, `--agentic` falls back to the classic loop,\nunchanged; NXC-4817 owns that loop''s answer to an active run.\n\nA continue over rewritten history warns and proceeds. While another nx\nmigrate process holds the run, nx refuses to continue or start fresh,\nnames that process, and skips the terminal prompt. `--start-fresh`\nrefuses when the id names no active run, when a sibling run directory\ncannot be read, and when another run is active on disk.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4769\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Continuing is its own entry point, `runOrchestratorResume`; init never\nresumes. Bare `--agentic` inside an agent continues in place;\n`--agentic=<id>` outside respawns the agent session on that run. It\nkeeps the recorded policy, since a resume under another policy is\nrefused. The agent path used to print the bare reconcile instead, which\nnever retries a failed checkpoint; the resume does.\n- Every process acting on a run holds a native file lock under the run\ndirectory''s `activity/` folder, named by its pid, which the kernel\nreleases when the process dies. Deletion refuses while one is held; a\ncontinue takes an exclusive hold that refuses while any other process\nholds the run. An unreadable folder fails closed. Under WASM there is no\nnative lock: deletion refuses outright, the prompt is skipped, and a\ncontinue proceeds.\n- The deletion refusals run before the prompt and the checkpoint commit,\nand again under the creation lock right before the record goes. That\nsame locked section reserves the replacement''s directory without\n`run.json`. The checkpoint commits outside the lock while the\nreservation stands, so a git hook re-entering nx migrate cannot\ndeadlock, and an init that meets a live reservation exits at once. Until\n`run.json` lands under the lock afterwards, neither run can be found,\ncontinued or held. The report and the start confirmation hold the run\ntoo, so a concurrent start-fresh cannot delete it under the prompt.\n- A start-fresh naming a run that is no longer active refuses before any\nside effect, and again under the creation lock. A completed run means\nthe plan already ran, so a new run would apply every migration again.\n- A continue holds the run before its pre-flight install. It releases\nthe hold before handing off to the workspace-local nx, whose own\nexclusive hold would refuse.\n- A continue checks only the newest recorded commit, so the warning\nstops once the next step commits on the new history.\n- Rendered commands carry the package manager prefix and a non-default\nmigrations path, shell-quoted on POSIX. A path that needs quoting on\nWindows, or holds a line break anywhere, is named in prose: cmd and\nPowerShell quote differently, and the command goes out on one line.\n- A landed commit with no recorded sha counts as unchecked, not dropped.\n- Not handled: a colleague who pulls a branch that already carries a\nrun''s commits has no run state and starts at step one. The run directory\nis gitignored, so no check based on it can see this.\n- `--run-id` and `--start-fresh` are checked against\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR` before the pre-flight install, which a refused\ncommand has no use for. Without either flag the install still runs\nbefore the report.\n- Run rounds no longer record a plan hash; nothing read it once an init\nreports any active run. A `run.json` written by this nx reads as corrupt\nto nx 23.2.x if the workspace-local nx is downgraded mid-run. No format\nbump: runs are not supported across Nx versions while the orchestrator\nis dark.\n- The rendered recovery commands do not carry\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR=true`. cmd and PowerShell share no one-line\nform for a variable prefix. Printing it, or letting a run id stand in\nfor it, is scaffolding that goes away with the flag. The report and the\ncontinue hint name the variable in prose instead.","tree":{"sha":"33a05b3ce69d1e8982281d9969b2ba0afcfbf9ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/33a05b3ce69d1e8982281d9969b2ba0afcfbf9ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/d73fb1b70068eea5646a2443e34720ca01fb3ae0","verification":{"payload":"tree 33a05b3ce69d1e