in":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/75b913e0ea9f820e3096247325d1975a5c92b572","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDc1YjkxM2UwZWE5ZjgyMGUzMDk2MjQ3MzI1ZDE5NzVhNWM5MmI1NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/0ea74af9ad31b9b87de861bd53ca6c021cc9cf1e","sha":"0ea74af9ad31b9b87de861bd53ca6c021cc9cf1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0ea74af9ad31b9b87de861bd53ca6c021cc9cf1e"}],"sha":"75b913e0ea9f820e3096247325d1975a5c92b572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/75b913e0ea9f820e3096247325d1975a5c92b572"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0ea74af9ad31b9b87de861bd53ca6c021cc9cf1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:33:59Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:33:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): build the daemon''s ignore rules from the file scan (#37220)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWhen the daemon creates its watching `WorkspaceContext`, the constructor\nwalks the whole workspace for `.gitignore` and `.nxignore` files before\nthe file scan starts. That walk only skips the hardcoded directories, so\nit also enters gitignored build output such as `dist` or `.next`. The\ndaemon does not start listening until it finishes. The file scan then\nwalks the workspace a second time, with ignore rules applied.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe daemon walks the workspace once. The file scan records the\n`.gitignore` and `.nxignore` of every directory it enters, and the\nignore rules are built from that list when the scan finishes. Nothing\nreads the rules before then: watch events queue during the scan, and\ncallers that need an answer wait for it.\n\n- A self-ignoring `.gitignore` (the `*` file pytest, ruff and mypy write\ninto their caches) is applied by the walk but never listed, so it is\nfound by checking each directory, not by filtering the file list.\n- Only a watching context asks its walk for ignore files. Other contexts\nwalk exactly as before.\n- When the files come from another process''s archive instead of a walk,\nthe existing rules are kept. If there are none yet, the rules come from\nthe same pruned walk the scan uses, on the scan thread.\n- Ignore files inside gitignored directories are no longer read. The\nwalk never reads them, and neither does git: a `!keep.js` in\n`dist/.gitignore` under a gitignored `dist/` used to admit a file the\nwalk never lists.\n\nThe separate ignore-file walk (`watch/git_utils.rs`) is removed. So is\nthe `use_ignore` parameter on the watch session, which was `false` in\nevery production call: the watch stream never applies ignore files.\n`create_filter` takes the ignore files directly (`None` for the stream).\n\n## Measurements\n\n`nx show projects` starting the daemon, 9 alternating runs per build,\nmedians, graph caches cleared (file archive kept). macOS, measured at\nd9a7c5cae9 against master ff94a98fa3. Times come from the daemon''s\n`NX_PERF_LOGGING` output.\n\n| Workspace | `workspace context init` | init + graph (daemon to first\ngraph) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2k files + 150k gitignored `dist` files | 113 -> 5 ms | 533 -> 431 ms\n|\n| large-monorepo (110 projects, 80k files) | 481 -> 6 ms | 1468 -> 1150\nms |\n| large-monorepo + 100k gitignored `.next` files | 553 -> 4 ms | 1702 ->\n1522 ms |\n\n- `init` dropped in every run on every workspace.\n- The graph step alone looks slower (for example 987 -> 1144 ms) because\nits timer now starts earlier: the scan used to get a head start during\n`init`. The sum is the daemon''s time to its first graph.\n- Wall time of the client command is dominated by plugin worker startup\n(~1.3 s, varying by about 1 s between runs), so its medians are too\nnoisy to read small differences from.\n- Both builds produced the same project list and file map in every run.\n\nOn Linux (6 CPUs, Docker VM), the saving is small: the constructor went\nfrom 912 to 860 ms on large-monorepo. The ignore-file walk only cost\n20-60 ms there. Registering inotify watches per directory (~750 ms for\n27k directories) dominates startup, and is left for a follow-up.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5060\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Build-the-daemons-ignore-rules-from-the-file-scan-NXC-5060-19c4b50f\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1bea3d0de42773045de5d55f2ef4683d1f3b14c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/d1bea3d0de42773045de5d55f2ef4683d1f3b14c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/0ea74af9ad31b9b87de861bd53ca6c021cc9cf1e","verification":{"payload":"tree d1bea3d0de42773045de5d55f2ef4683d1f3b14c\nparent b8beaaaab2522a103d08bab96d1ff808a82f099b\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790714039 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790714039 +0000\n\nfix(core): build the daemon''s ignore rules from the file scan (#37220)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWhen the daemon creates its watching `WorkspaceContext`, the constructor\nwalks the whole workspace for `.gitignore` and `.nxignore` files before\nthe file scan starts. That walk only skips the hardcoded directories, so\nit also enters gitignored build output such as `dist` or `.next`. The\ndaemon does not start listening until it finishes. The file scan then\nwalks the workspace a second time, with ignore rules applied.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe daemon walks the workspace once. The file scan records the\n`.gitignore` and `.nxignore` of every directory it enters, and the\nignore rules are built from that list when the scan finishes. Nothing\nreads the rules before then: watch events queue during the scan, and\ncallers that need an answer wait for it.\n\n- A self-ignoring `.gitignore` (the `*` file pytest, ruff and mypy write\ninto their caches) is applied by the walk but never listed, so it is\nfound by checking each directory, not by filtering the file list.\n- Only a watching context asks its walk for ignore files. Other contexts\nwalk exactly as before.\n- When the files come from another process''s archive instead of a walk,\nthe existing rules are kept. If there are none yet, the rules come from\nthe same pruned walk the scan uses, on the scan thread.\n- Ignore files inside gitignored directories are no longer read. The\nwalk never reads them, and neither does git: a `!keep.js` in\n`dist/.gitignore` under a gitignored `dist/` used to admit a file the\nwalk never lists.\n\nThe separate ignore-file walk (`watch/git_utils.rs`) is removed. So is\nthe `use_ignore` parameter on the watch session, which was `false` in\nevery production call: the watch stream never applies ignore files.\n`create_filter` takes the ignore files directly (`None` for the stream).\n\n## Measurements\n\n`nx show projects` starting the daemon, 9 alternating runs per build,\nmedians, graph caches cleared (file archive kept). macOS, measured at\nd9a7c5cae9 against master ff94a98fa3. Times come from the daemon''s\n`NX_PERF_LOGGING` output.\n\n| Workspace | `workspace context init` | init + graph (daemon to first\ngraph) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2k files + 150k gitignored `dist` files | 113 -> 5 ms | 533 -> 431 ms\n|\n| large-monorepo (110 projects, 80k files) | 481 -> 6 ms | 1468 -> 1150\nms |\n| large-monorepo + 100k gitignored `.next` files | 553 -> 4 ms | 1702 ->\n1522 ms |\n\n- `init` dropped in every run on every workspace.\n- The graph step alone looks slower (for example 987 -> 1144 ms) because\nits timer now starts earlier: the scan used to get a head start during\n`init`. The sum is the daemon''s time to its first graph.\n- Wall time of the client command is dominated by plugin worker startup\n(~1.3 s, varying by about 1 s between runs), so its medians are too\nnoisy to read small differences from.\n- Both builds produced the same project list and file map in every run.\n\nOn Linux (6 CPUs, Docker VM), the saving is small: the constructor went\nfrom 912 to 860 ms on large-monorepo. The ignore-file walk only cost\n20-60 ms there. Registering inotify watches per directory (~750 ms for\n27k directories) dominates startup, and is left for a follow-up.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5060\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Build-the-daemons-ignore-rules-from-the-file-scan-NXC-5060-19c4b50f\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvCC3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsmIQAA0WXExwbdx0gIT1JYZ+c6GD\n59aH8dmEuj0qBV+iSdtVfyWYfzOQ/mYKJJ/PdZYsI/8mebnjd7sfWDBeQiIAr1XZ\nMo+u5O5pYdzrXCWwlnQIVGg3gfo1MSP4IJhhVAz0UARla9D4xw8pEhuw+hp7LWqD\n7taOkQ0wNrIHEP1jIx8bYN40dIChuzDAqDt0yuhvWd2w+k3OXvSXH7rAZTKbvaYh\nXLfHJIrYA542MxOIOsGcQSSvSrUJJrBnzxrGSeu3KDZmpJ5YkiBK18ukWSakbWHU\nRzJLdg7lUPLRr/6t6f3Dq1yzysJ4aXJVIAnepzPTkbaVgxUTT4MkUYghMX5OfvyD\nCKB8NeOB4ShvMkpY/YtNc3aBvmpS6Ix6//cvHiLwHCYXfE6zHsrnyBBu7gjw2AC4\nR1gwCl5oSyTGt4Ds/Fh4mkgG35pCVJGG07xb1TDOueIP7FuAxsoO7s2A2TcSaaW+\nG6Kg2u7sRMh3IcsR9v0VxH/ZS5g1Sr/x8wU8m1C4bHEr2s46JrgFLTw/5/0qVQis\nV7GCitjauF6CSkjVYTK6OmKrDALnXj2L+H3ZGeFdN1mueGVhHyZSiBGdKCVlpN4D\nf9EY8yqYjW5AdrZ7j4iNclqoYTCntbAiTdBZwgoqrlI6SlwqofFdQb3HVyXsYANK\nKu7qlkTJR22Wa/ekhpB6\n=Lh59\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T20:34:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subsc