https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1361436aa6e80eeda8e8146f7d5f375bcc471943/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:45:45Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:45:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): make glob escapes work the same on every platform (#37215)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nA glob can mean different things on different operating systems, and\nsome escapes don''t work anywhere:\n\n| Glob | macOS / Linux | Windows |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `app/(marketing)/page.tsx` | `(marketing)` is a group | same |\n| `app/\\(marketing\\)/page.tsx` | no match: the extglob parser still\nopens a group at `(` | no match: `\\` is a path separator |\n| `app/[(]marketing[)]/page.tsx` | no match: the `(` inside the class\nstill opens a group | same |\n| `libs\\app\\**` | `\\a` escapes `a`, matches nothing | matches\n`libs/app/**` |\n\nglobset defaults `backslash_escape` to off on Windows, and Nx mirrored\nthat with Windows-only `\\` → `/` rewrites. Because of that, several\nfirst-party plugins build output globs with the platform\n`path.relative`/`path.join` (vite, vitest, webpack, rspack, rsbuild,\nnuxt, gradle v1). On Windows they produce\n`{workspaceRoot}/dist\\apps\\app`. Outputs are part of the task hash, so\nthose targets never share remote cache between Windows and macOS/Linux.\n\nFor I/O snapshots, a recorded read of a path with parentheses hashes\nnothing, and a root-level name that needs escaping (`\\!notes.md`) is\nrefused, so the Nx Cloud client has to reject those reports today.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nGlobs use `/` as the separator and `\\` as the escape on every platform,\nlike minimatch and picomatch:\n\n- **`\\` escapes** everywhere: `build_glob_set` enables\n`backslash_escape`, and the extglob parser keeps `\\` plus the next\ncharacter as text, so `\\(`, `\\)`, `\\!`, `\\?`, `\\+`, `\\@`, `\\{,` and `\\\\`\nare literal. The Windows-only rewrites (`common_glob_prefix`,\n`classify`) and the lexer''s `cfg(not(windows))` gate are removed.\n- **`[(]` works too**: a closed `[...]` class is parsed whole, so `(`\nand `)` inside it are members.\n- **Root-level names with glob symbols hash from snapshots**:\n`escapes_workspace` refused any snapshot glob starting with `\\`, so a\nroot file like `!notes.md` (escaped `\\!notes.md`) or `(group)` never\nused its snapshot. A leading escape of a glob symbol (`* ? [ ] { } ( )\n!`) is now allowed, since it cannot form an absolute path; `\\/etc`,\n`\\\\server` and `\\C:` stay refused.\n- **Outputs never leave the workspace**: allowing a leading escape means\na snapshot output like `\\!Backup` is kept, and on Windows\n`workspace_root.join` resolves it to `C:\\!Backup`. `cache.rs`''s\n`escapes_workspace` (a `..` climb, or a root or drive prefix) moves to\n`utils/path.rs` and now also guards output hashing\n(`normalize_output_entry`), the daemon''s output walk\n(`get_files_for_outputs`) and snapshot `observed_outputs`, which report\nsuch an output as unusable instead of adding it to the task.\n- **An escape can''t disguise `.git`, `node_modules` or `.nx`**:\n`observed_outputs` compared raw text split on `/` and `\\`, so a snapshot\noutput like `.gi\\t/config` passed although Nx reads it as `.git/config`,\nwhich a cache restore would then write. It now splits on `/` only and\nlets the glob matcher read any escaped segment, as it already did for\n`.gi[t]`-style disguises. This was already possible on macOS and Linux.\n- **Plugins write `/`**: the seven plugins above normalize inferred\noutputs with `normalizePath`/`joinPathFragments`, so their hashes match\nacross operating systems. Windows users see a one-time cache miss for\nthose targets.\n- **Plugin globs use `/`**: jest (`testMatch`) and cypress\n(`specPattern`/`excludeSpecPattern`) join spec globs onto the project\nroot with `posix.join`, so Windows no longer produces\n`libs\\app\\**\\*.spec.ts`, which would now match nothing and leave the\natomized CI targets empty. `posix.join` leaves a user''s `\\(` escape in\nthe pattern intact. Angular''s and cypress''s inferred outputs are also\nwritten with `/`, so output checks find the real outputs.\n- **Create-nodes hashing globs with `/`**: `@nx/devkit`''s\n`calculateHashForCreateNodes` and `calculateHashesForCreateNodes` joined\n`projectRoot` and `**/*` with the platform path, so on Windows the glob\nread `libs\\a\\**\\*`, which now matches nothing. The hash would stop\nchanging and plugins would serve stale inferred targets. They join with\nposix now, as does gradle''s version-catalog search.\n- **Docs**: `reference/inputs.mdoc` gains a \"Glob syntax\" section (use\n`/` on every OS, `\\` escapes, with a route-group example), and\n`kb/configure-outputs.mdoc` links to it.\n\n### Intentional behavior change\n\nThis PR deliberately changes how some globs are read, and it can break\npeople who rely on the old reading:\n\n- **Windows globs that use `\\` as a separator** in `project.json`,\n`nx.json` or third-party plugins (for example `{projectRoot}\\src\\**`, or\nan output built with `path.join`) now read `\\` as an escape and match\nnothing. For an input that means edits no longer change the task hash;\nfor an output it means nothing is cached or restored.\n- **A `\\` before `+`, `!`, `?`, `@` or `(`** now escapes that character\non every platform instead of starting an extglob. Off Windows this\nchanges two globs in the recorded corpus (`e2e\\react\\**\\+(…)`,\n`e2e\\react\\!(*.test).ts`).\n\nWe accept this because those globs were never portable: the same `\\`\nglob already matched nothing on macOS and Linux, and a workspace''s\ninputs and outputs are shared across machines and the remote cache. The\nfix for anyone affected is to write `/` in globs. First-party plugins\nare updated here; third-party plugins that build globs with the platform\n`path` module need the same change.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Parser specs: `\\(`, `\\)`, `\\!` parse as `Escaped` parts; classes\nholding `(`/`)` parse as `Class` parts. Backslash specs now run on every\nplatform.\n- `build_glob_set` specs: `app/\\(marketing\\)/**` and\n`app/[(]marketing[)]/**` match the real directory only; `\\\\` matches a\nliteral backslash; `\\{,b\\}` stays literal.\n- Escape round-trip spec: 27 names full of glob symbols, escaped the way\nthe Nx Cloud client does, each match only their own path.\n- `escapes_workspace` spec: leading `\\!`, `\\(`, `\\[`, `\\*`, `\\{`\nallowed; `\\/etc/passwd`, `\\\\server\\share`, `\\C:/Windows`, `\\../x`\nrefused.\n- `escapes_workspace` (paths) spec: `../x`, `/etc/passwd` escape\neverywhere, `\\!Backup` and `C:x` only on Windows;\n`get_files_for_outputs` reads nothing for `../outside.txt`; a root-level\nescaped snapshot write is kept off Windows and dropped on Windows.\n- `observed_outputs` spec: `.gi\\t/config`, `node_module\\s/x`,\n`.GI\\T/hooks/x`, `apps/\\.nx/cache/x` dropped; `libs/\\!notes.md`,\n`dist/a\\(b\\).js`, `a\\\\b/x` kept.\n- `calculate-hash-for-create-nodes.spec.ts`: with `path` mocked as\n`path.win32`, the project glob is still `libs/a/**/*` (it was\n`libs\\a\\**\\*` before).\n- Snapshot hashing specs: `libs/child/[(]group[)]/page.md` and\n`libs/child/\\(group\\)/page.md` hash that file (both hash nothing on\nmaster); root-level `\\!root.md`, `\\(root\\)/page.md`, `\\[id\\].md` and\n`\\{a,b\\}.md` hash their file.\n\n### Performance\n\nMeasured against master on the same base commit (`0188776ea0`), both\nrelease builds of the native binding loaded directly (`pnpm nx` in this\nrepo runs the published nx, not the source). 25 rounds, alternating\nmaster and branch, macOS arm64. Times are medians with the interquartile\nrange.\n\n| Measurement | master | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Parse and build all 101 corpus globs, cold, fresh process | 8.28 ms\n(8.04–8.55) | 8.61 ms (8.17–9.82) |\n| `WorkspaceContext.glob`, 6 input sets over the nx repo (4,149 files\nfor `packages/**/*.ts`) | 6.70 ms (6.52–7.11) | 6.75 ms (6.70–7.33) |\n| `hashFilesMatchingGlob`, same 6 sets | 6.29 ms (6.07–6.87) | 6.35 ms\n(6.20–6.95) |\n| `getFilesForOutputsBatch` (daemon output walk), 5 real output entries\n| 69.69 ms (68.66–74.81) | 70.58 ms (68.58–74.25) |\n\nThe medians differ by 4% or less, and every master median falls inside\nthis PR''s interquartile range. The largest gap is the cold parse, 0.33\nms over 101 globs (about 3 µs per glob). Parsing costs about 85 µs per\nglob, once per unique glob per process, since `build_glob_set` caches\nthe result. Both builds matched the same files and rejected the same 6\ninvalid corpus globs. Windows could not be measured.\n\nVerified: full `packages/nx` vitest suite (8298 tests; `moves a task\nhash by a changed read` is flaky on master too), Rust tests (916\npassed), `lint-native`, `check-native-wasm`, and `test`/`lint` for\ndevkit, vite, vitest, webpack, rspack, rsbuild, nuxt, gradle, jest,\ncypress and angular. Not run on Windows.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nImplements NXC-5054. Lets the Nx Cloud client write any path into I/O\nsnapshots for nx versions with this fix. Related: nrwl/ocean#14037.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Migrate-to-nx-23.3.0-beta.6-with-ultracache-and-task-based-affected-f4012f97\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"0134f2edb0b8130814bd4c5de9418a1a9c8fa473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/0134f2edb0b8130814bd4c5de9418a1a9c8fa473"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/1361436aa6e80eeda8e8146f7d5f375bcc471943","verification":{"payload":"tree 0134f2edb0b8130814bd4c5de9418a1a9c8fa473\nparent 87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790700345 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790700345 +0000\n\nfix(core): make glob escapes work the same on every platform (#37215)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nA glob can mean different things on different operating systems, and\nsome escapes don''t work anywhere:\n\n| Glob | macOS / Linux | Windows |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `app/(marketing)/page.tsx` | `(marketing)` is a group | same |\n| `app/\\(marketing\\)/page.tsx` | no match: the extglob parser still\nopens a group at `(` | no match: `\\` is a path separator |\n| `app/[(]marketing[)]/page.tsx` | no match: the `(` inside the class\nstill opens a group | same |\n| `libs\\app\\**` | `\\a` escapes `a`, matches nothing | matches\n`libs/app/**` |\n\nglobset defaults `backslash_escape` to off on Windows, and Nx mirrored\nthat with Windows-only `\\` → `/` rewrites. Because of that, several\nfirst-party plugins build output globs with the platform\n`path.relative`/`path.join` (vite, vitest, webpack, rspack, rsbuild,\nnuxt, gradle v1). On Windows they produce\n`{workspaceRoot}/dist\\apps\\app`. Outputs are part of the task hash, so\nthose targets never share remote cache between Windows and macOS/Linux.\n\nFor I/O snapshots, a recorded read of a path with parentheses hashes\nnothing, and a root-level name that needs escaping (`\\!notes.md`) is\nrefused, so the Nx Cloud client has to reject those reports today.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nGlobs use `/` as the separator and `\\` as the escape on every platform,\nlike minimatch and picomatch:\n\n- **`\\` escapes** everywhere: `build_glob_set` enables\n`backslash_escape`, and the extglob parser keeps `\\` plus the next\ncharacter as text, so `\\(`, `\\)`, `\\!`, `\\?`, `\\+`, `\\@`, `\\{,` and `\\\\`\nare literal. The Windows-only rewrites (`common_glob_prefix`,\n`classify`) and the lexer''s `cfg(not(windows))` gate are removed.\n- **`[(]` works too**: a closed `[...]` class is parsed whole, so `(`\nand `)` inside it are members.\n- **Root-level names with glob symbols hash from snapshots**:\n`escapes_workspace` refused any snapshot glob starting with `\\`, so a\nroot file like `!notes.md` (escaped `\\!notes.md`) or `(group)` never\nused its snapshot. A leading escape of a glob symbol (`* ? [ ] { } ( )\n!`) is now allowed, since it cannot form an absolute path; `\\/etc`,\n`\\\\server` and `\\C:` stay refused.\n- **Outputs never leave the workspace**: allowing a leading escape means\na snapshot output like `\\!Backup` is kept, and on Windows\n`workspace_root.join` resolves it to `C:\\!Backup`. `cache.rs`''s\n`escapes_workspace` (a `..` climb, or a root or drive prefix) moves to\n`utils/path.rs` and now also guards output hashing\n(`normalize_output_entry`), the daemon''s output walk\n(`get_files_for_outputs`) and snapshot `observed_outputs`, which report\nsuch an output as unusable instead of adding it to the task.\n- **An escape can''t disguise `.git`, `node_modules` or `.nx`**:\n`observed_outputs` compared raw text split on `/` and `\\`, so a snapshot\noutput like `.gi\\t/config` passed although Nx reads it as `.git/config`,\nwhich a cache restore would then write. It now splits on `/` only and\nlets the glob matcher read any escaped segment, as it already did for\n`.gi[t]`-style disguises. This was already possible on macOS and Linux.\n- **Plugins write `/`**: the seven plugins above normalize inferred\noutputs with `normalizePath`/`joinPathFragments`, so their hashes match\nacross operating systems. Windows users see a one-time cache miss for\nthose targets.\n- **Plugin globs use `/`**: jest (`testMatch`) and cypress\n(`specPattern`/`excludeSpecPattern`) join spec globs onto the project\nroot with `posix.join`, so Windows no longer produces\n`libs\\app\\**\\*.spec.ts`, which would now match nothing and leave the\natomized CI targets empty. `posix.join` leaves a user''s `\\(` escape in\nthe pattern intact. Angular''s and cypress''s inferred outputs are also\nwritten with `/`, so output checks find the real outputs.\n- **Create-nodes hashing globs with `/`**: `@nx/devkit`''s\n`calculateHashForCreateNodes` and `calculateHashesForCreateNodes` joined\n`projectRoot` and `**/*` with the platform path, so on Windows the glob\nread `libs\\a\\**\\*`, which now matches nothing. The hash would stop\nchanging and plugins would serve stale inferred targets. They join with\nposix now, as does gradle''s version-catalog search.\n- **Docs**: `reference/inputs.mdoc` gains a \"Glob syntax\" section (use\n`/` on every OS, `\\` escapes, with a route-group example), and\n`kb/configure-outputs.mdoc` links to it.\n\n### Intentional behavior change\n\nThis PR deliberately changes how some globs are read, and it can break\npeople who rely on the old reading:\n\n- **Windows globs that use `\\` as a separator** in `project.json`,\n`nx.json` or third-party plugins (for example `{projectRoot}\\src\\**`, or\nan output built with `path.join`) now read `\\` as an escape and match\nnothing. For an input that means edits no longer change the task hash;\nfor an output it means nothing is cached or restored.\n- **A `\\` before `+`, `!`, `?`, `@` or `(`** now escapes that character\non every platform instead of starting an extglob. Off Windows this\nchanges two globs in the recorded corpus (`e2e\\react\\**\\+(…)`,\n`e2e\\react\\!(*.test).ts`).\n\nWe accept this because those globs were never portable: the same `\\`\nglob already matched nothing on macOS and Linux, and a workspace''s\ninputs and outputs are shared across machines and the remote cache. The\nfix for anyone affected is to write `/` in globs. First-party plugins\nare updated here; third-party plugins that build globs with the platform\n`path` module need the same change.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Parser specs: `\\(`, `\\)`, `\\!` parse as `Escaped` parts; classes\nholding `(`/`)` parse as `Class` parts. Backslash specs now run on every\nplatform.\n- `build_glob_set` specs: `app/\\(marketing\\)/**` and\n`app/[(]marketing[)]/**` match the real directory only; `\\\\` matches a\nliteral backslash; `\\{,b\\}` stays literal.\n- Escape round-trip spec: 27 names full of glob symbols, escaped the way\nthe Nx Cloud client does, each match only their own path.\n- `escapes_workspace` spec: leading `\\!`, `\\(`, `\\[`, `\\*`, `\\{`\nallowed; `\\/etc/passwd`, `\\\\server\\share`, `\\C:/Windows`, `\\../x`\nrefused.\n- `escapes_workspace` (paths) spec: `../x`, `/etc/passwd` escape\neverywhere, `\\!Backup` and `C:x` only on Windows;\n`get_files_for_outputs` reads nothing for `../outside.txt`; a root-level\nescaped snapshot write is kept off Windows and dropped on Windows.\n- `observed_outputs` spec: `.gi\\t/config`, `node_module\\s/x`,\n`.GI\\T/hooks/x`, `apps/\\.nx/cache/x` dropped; `libs/\\!notes.md`,\n`dist/a\\(b\\).js`, `a\\\\b/x` kept.\n- `calculate-hash-for-create-nodes.spec.ts`: with `path` mocked as\n`path.win32`, the project glob is still `libs/a/**/*` (it was\n`libs\\a\\**\\*` before).\n- Snapshot hashing specs: `libs/child/[(]group[)]/page.md` and\n`libs/child/\\(group\\)/page.md` hash that file (both hash nothing on\nmaster); root-level `\\!root.md`, `\\(root\\)/page.md`, `\\[id\\].md` and\n`\\{a,b\\}.md` hash their file.\n\n### Performance\n\nMeasured against master on the same base commit (`0188776ea0`), both\nrelease builds of the native binding loaded directly (`pnpm nx` in this\nrepo runs the published nx, not the source). 25 rounds, alternating\nmaster and branch, macOS arm64. Times are medians with the interquartile\nrange.\n\n| Measurement | master | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Parse and build all 101 corpus globs, cold, fresh process | 8.28 ms\n(8.04–8.55) | 8.61 ms (8.17–9.82) |\n| `WorkspaceContext.glob`, 6 input sets over the nx repo (4,149 files\nfor `packages/**/*.ts`) | 6.70 ms (6.52–7.11) | 6.75 ms (6.70–7.33) |\n| `hashFilesMatchingGlob`, same 6 sets | 6.29 ms (6.07–6.87) | 6.35 ms\n(6.20–6.95) |\n| `getFilesForOutputsBatch` (daemon output walk), 5 real output entries\n| 69.69 ms (68.66–74.81) | 70.58 ms (68.58–74.25) |\n\nThe medians differ by 4% or less, and every master median falls inside\nthis PR''s interquartile range. The largest gap is the cold parse, 0.33\nms over 101 globs (about 3 µs per glob). Parsing costs about 85 µs per\nglob, once per unique glob per process, since `build_glob_set` caches\nthe result. Both builds matched the same files and rejected the same 6\ninvalid corpus globs. Windows could not be measured.\n\nVerified: full `packages/nx` vitest suite (8298 tests; `moves a task\nhash by a changed read` is flaky on master too), Rust tests (916\npassed), `lint-native`, `check-native-wasm`, and `test`/`lint` for\ndevkit, vite, vitest, webpack, rspack, rsbuild, nuxt, gradle, jest,\ncypress and angular. Not run on Windows.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nImplements NXC-5054. Lets the Nx Cloud client write any path into I/O\nsnapshots for nx versions with this fix. Related: nrwl/ocean#14037.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Migrate-to-nx-23.3.0-beta.6-with-ultracache-and-task-based-affected-f4012f97\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+s5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANrIQABPSv5wQuOFZh+BOBWnV/NMf\nvYmWRBwvMPXpOafcXgZ0lx0ngXwYc61CKrnM9MI8HPzri3nKK/DNvSdN0cYzNGQq\nei8LHz5XhdFnti1wbhTQSSs4Qrukw6Gi89MY14H17g38bEiFIcf3IlgrbkbgVM8U\njwGQ0p1Q+vKV0SbtsBG8+xmxXgorLnpFjpjxyo/oq9BnibNUVnOGPJRHWMg5dupf\ny0MJ+IwvUgpxygj5eGSc9cwKxe+UYLfJDAHSYh2xiTGmtQc9Ptr+JwJG+7MsAbtv\nKclsFlJXqVksBZxkR51x8MYJF9rodhoEFayDrP1FIRIpt5czBJLWjGFYDaazq9k8\n0faAhTNphNNwQ8OqGmjHNSrDNlQPmIB+IWS9UsOXk4TA3XWaJeLTW4GHtY9ZAKer\nQu157lEdODLlhoc3C/mfoibSKPxoznWk/BbVWGIV0qAmP1TT6v/T9EkW9m/IpnO8\n54tOtVBHqRnlwuZ1hp6KpxNg/EL7CdfBuLM1n56x4kxZRZmd5uFdjgtfSxTSUX5M\nJt09KF7DfTlpSGgOqsg+x+RFeLqAmoO35qC5EVnga4Y1wmsrSh3UvIdr4ABewtSg\n+yUmbWt2kj/kCUh/WvkEKQ4Jy1v/nI1kiSgl53UoW98ABli/zokwRYlP9Y8Rm8VH\nAW7zSVkrlD5MvEhYdcC/\n=FmZf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:45:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/1361436aa6e80eeda8e8146f7d5f375bcc471943","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDEzNjE0MzZhYTZlODBlZWRhOGU4MTQ2ZjdkNWYzNzViY2M0NzE5NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41","sha":"87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41"}],"sha":"1361436aa6e80eeda8e8146f7d5f375bcc471943","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1361436aa6e80eeda8e8146f7d5f375bcc471943"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:14:46Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:14:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): record unresolved migrations and cap retries in orchestrated migrate runs (#36986)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nWhen a migration fails, nx offers the agent three choices: retry, retry\nover a clean tree, or skip. A dead worker gets a fourth choice, adopt,\nwhich keeps the working tree as the result. Nothing lets the agent say\n\"this migration is not going to work, move on\". Nothing lets it keep a\nfix it applied by hand after a plain failure. A skip pretends the\nmigration did not apply to the workspace, which is wrong for both cases.\n\nThe agent can retry a failing migration forever. Each retry costs time\nand the failure is usually the same.\n\nThe only way past a migration that will not work is skip. The run then\ncompletes as if the migration did not apply. The user gets no list of\nwhat was given up, and a session nx started for the run exits 0.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAfter a failure or death the menu gains:\n\n- `adopt` after a plain failure: the tree as left is the result,\ncommitted under the migration''s name.\n- `unresolved`: the agent gives the migration up and nx files the\nfailure as a run issue. Safely discardable changes are reset; others\nstay and, with commits on, land under the migration''s name marked\nunresolved.\n\nA migration whose commit landed, or was started and never recorded, gets\nadopt instead of skip and unresolved. A retry resumes the remaining work\nwithout reapplying the generator.\n\nnx refuses third retries.\n\nThe completion report counts applied, adopted, skipped and unresolved\nmigrations and lists each given-up one''s failure. A session nx started\nexits 1 on a given-up migration or open issue.\n\nWith no user to ask, the agent gives a stuck migration up and continues.\nWhere that is withheld, it adopts only after finishing the migration, or\nstops.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4819\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `unresolved` is terminal, so a resumed run never re-dispenses a\ngiven-up migration.\n- A give-up resets the tree only when the generator never completed and\na clean retry would be safe. A commit of the migration on record or\nstarted withholds it. Nx runs the reset under the tree reservation and\nrefuses the give-up until the tree is clean. Everything else is kept:\nhand-made edits are never dropped.\n- A give-up that commits is one operation under one tree reservation,\nrun by the process that holds the tree. It checks that no other commit\nof the migration is on record, commits, and settles the step, issue and\nledger entry in one write. Split across two processes, the transition\nfound the give-up''s own commit and refused it.\n- In a session the parent answers a `give-up` request with that\noperation. An install failure, or a commit that failed once git ran,\nstill settles the step with its debt. A crash between git and the\nsettling write leaves the commit-started mark, so only adopt is offered\nafterwards.\n- A died worker''s adopt reuses the worker''s commit request until its\ncommit is recorded, so that commit is not made twice.\n- The retry cap is two rearms per migration, refused at acceptance\nrather than withheld from the menu.\n- The run-state format stays at v1 and the feature goes public at v1.\nRuns written under the flag are not supported across Nx versions.\n- The multi-repo migrate skill lists the new options.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"26d0a956874725e14286c3104e4a6ae43c833ac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/26d0a956874725e14286c3104e4a6ae43c833ac0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41","verification":{"payload":"tree 26d0a956874725e14286c3104e4a6ae43c833ac0\nparent 9d666d1f5c7f67d61d6fdb1e344d23ac90dfc538\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1790698486 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790698486 -0400\n\nfeat(core): record unresolved migrations and cap retries in orchestrated migrate runs (#36986)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThis only applies to orchestrated migrate runs, behind\n`NX_MIGRATE_ORCHESTRATOR`.\n\nWhen a migration fails, nx offers the agent three choices: retry, retry\nover a clean tree, or skip. A dead worker gets a fourth choice, adopt,\nwhich keeps the working tree as the result. Nothing lets the agent say\n\"this migration is not going to work, move on\". Nothing lets it keep a\nfix it applied by hand after a plain failure. A skip pretends the\nmigration did not apply to the workspace, which is wrong for both cases.\n\nThe agent can retry a failing migration forever. Each retry costs time\nand the failure is usually the same.\n\nThe only way past a migration that will not work is skip. The run then\ncompletes as if the migration did not apply. The user gets no list of\nwhat was given up, and a session nx started for the run exits 0.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAfter a failure or death the menu gains:\n\n- `adopt` after a plain failure: the tree as left is the result,\ncommitted under the migration''s name.\n- `unresolved`: the agent gives the migration up and nx files the\nfailure as a run issue. Safely discardable changes are reset; others\nstay and, with commits on, land under the migration''s name marked\nunresolved.\n\nA migration whose commit landed, or was started and never recorded, gets\nadopt instead of skip and unresolved. A retry resumes the remaining work\nwithout reapplying the generator.\n\nnx refuses third retries.\n\nThe completion report counts applied, adopted, skipped and unresolved\nmigrations and lists each given-up one''s failure. A session nx started\nexits 1 on a given-up migration or open issue.\n\nWith no user to ask, the agent gives a stuck migration up and continues.\nWhere that is withheld, it adopts only after finishing the migration, or\nstops.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4819\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `unresolved` is terminal, so a resumed run never re-dispenses a\ngiven-up migration.\n- A give-up resets the tree only when the generator never completed and\na clean retry would be safe. A commit of the migration on record or\nstarted withholds it. Nx runs the reset under the tree reservation and\nrefuses the give-up until the tree is clean. Everything else is kept:\nhand-made edits are never dropped.\n- A give-up that commits is one operation under one tree reservation,\nrun by the process that holds the tree. It checks that no other commit\nof the migration is on record, commits, and settles the step, issue and\nledger entry in one write. Split across two processes, the transition\nfound the give-up''s own commit and refused it.\n- In a session the parent answers a `give-up` request with that\noperation. An install failure, or a commit that failed once git ran,\nstill settles the step with its debt. A crash between git and the\nsettling write leaves the commit-started mark, so only adopt is offered\nafterwards.\n- A died worker''s adopt reuses the worker''s commit request until its\ncommit is recorded, so that commit is not made twice.\n- The retry cap is two rearms per migration, refused at acceptance\nrather than withheld from the menu.\n- The run-state format stays at v1 and the feature goes public at v1.\nRuns written under the flag are not supported across Nx versions.\n- The multi-repo migrate skill lists the new options.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu+P2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi7AQADHJ7vi0pm8s17EZvB17KiNQ\nQvWtmB+u3UUuXKNb5bmvJ8xRSI1y8Y1wHn+uy0mymbLnL3+pq3VRWE9Bnw+rGoHm\nxaibeote8eK3pfHuHTdXffIGSuw6e7ofvm9cuP+LmoEdUkB4O8QZQMDLCUWkZJUf\nxQWMuUr0OtyO6iUb3GSsFFKwxnwU3q0MrTee44VWFDCCPEWe19DXGjYkcKfg3EjX\nRKAM8VM13hKuR+IFBX8dSUwB0EL8IgChYXJOsDPfzy5Qhr/uDT9IUpQo1Er39NTZ\n2lqcldgKc8rFNSouu44zFpaIfs0+0nz7ONmvB5nete31+0b1VwdCJijTHuQgGJIT\nnloVcSF3dLNsA/KBWiMRGY/jkSFwIwYM8N6ze5c7Np3W50aCK4am2NDo4Pbhh7X9\nzmVqffyhU7aNxrNqya5wA/1bsobZ19Kf1EWtKvPGDfoh9+D8DGkbrViW1Gyf4LpU\nE74409FrOWa1g8BB09K2yZAi7Q3SkeDuHvvjxS2CypSw/DHGZbhyP4vxvHGg/xK6\nzK8abD3fDPvDXdEP1HxrD7tbrZybOHmLFgM+FEQeh+M+cuBUI0RAPHFf7j1FEt6z\nylhLqG6uyytaKF7bevloCPh0MTv32DncptyAeG2lDpCcSDm5/JPI/YK42fkDLXrY\nwGaODHYDNqIKAi7L39Sj\n=gCEq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T16:14:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDg3NTI1ZDY4MGRkMjBjMjg4ZDYyNmMyNmI2ZGUzYzU4NWFlYWRiNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/9d666d1f5c7f67d61d6fdb1e344d23ac90dfc538","sha":"9d666d1f5c7f67d61d6fdb1e344d23ac90dfc538","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9d666d1f5c7f67d61d6fdb1e344d23ac90dfc538"}],"sha":"87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/87525d680dd20c288d626c26b6de3c585aeadb41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53559?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jaysoo","id":53559,"login":"jaysoo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTU5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9d666d1f5c7f67d61d6fdb1e344d23ac90dfc538/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:07:01Z","email":"jack.hsu@gmail.com","name":"Jack Hsu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:07:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): remove axios from the published nx package (#36706)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe published `nx` package depends on Axios for Nx Cloud requests and\nremote releases.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nUse fetch for these requests and Undici for proxy environment variables.\nPreserve request timeouts, streamed downloads, and HTTP error details\nwithout exposing Axios types.\n\nNx Cloud client downloads no longer use `customProxyConfigPath`;\naffected users receive guidance to configure proxy environment variables\nand certificates. The downloaded client bundle continues to handle its\nown proxy configuration.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4743\n\nProxy documentation:\n[DOC-727](https://linear.app/nxdev/issue/DOC-727/document-proxy-settings-for-nx-cloud).","tree":{"sha":"ccdf9f01b3fabfa839399c229ca19658c56ec125","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/ccdf9f01b3fabfa839399c229ca19658c56ec125"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/9d666d1f5c7f67d61d6fdb1e344d23ac90dfc538","verification":{"payload":"tree ccdf9f01b3fabfa839399c229ca19658c56ec125\nparent 0440632fb8fb93827483289fbc59aa337db87cf2\nauthor Jack Hsu <jack.hsu@gmail.com> 1790694421 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790694421 -0400\n\nfix(core): remove axios from the published nx package (#36706)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe published `nx` package depends on Axios for Nx Cloud requests and\nremote releases.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nUse fetch for these requests and Undici for proxy environment variables.\nPreserve request timeouts, streamed downloads, and HTTP error details\nwithout exposing Axios types.\n\nNx Cloud client downloads no longer use `customProxyConfigPath`;\naffected users receive guidance to configure proxy environment variables\nand certificates. The downloaded client bundle continues to handle its\nown proxy configuration.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4743\n\nProxy documentation:\n[DOC-727](https://linear.app/nxdev/issue/DOC-727/document-proxy-settings-for-nx-cloud).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu9QVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvYEQAE3ArLi8EpaUlr4pGBKv+Tji\nrOFslT57zAPCAsEWz46vfPQmrM0iUhKbEEh/U8Pjh8rKpvS/DLB4k/njoRtsjUhr\nu89I7xzN8+muU07gPsxoWF1jEry4mgMNtifYI1t8aJv8pv7zSe+LjXFjFIcpB44n\nLqaDzj357GY8sB2QF1OnsB2sT4Okt5okQSRx4MtSEzlC9qk+/PYA06mgRTIDp0dX\nl/HywrxqoWenCmMKJ7dOb/ofZ+WGUy1sA1XlvV3N2BtMhLH6FMUoAXdVbArQ2Efp\nBTkMeNuQCwVbRMrV0Q4DoT6wS3tE/9XL5b28M2WV2v3BAlTdtG6/Hwf7WFPSM1DQ\nhZ2/bRxxyKiv6T21auRCdBZdJmgfE0X8MxD7hucQSk/UtXBBwiR+f0ndRTGV5rqd\nlxljpIysxnIZPFisxqhs+Nmm9PAklusFaCClDNMkAHiCYn62dWapqMZacfS1TXfX\nmYc+dTa/9QvbjIbkFyQiKqjw/RI/E1CfEzUrQnT7KflBwk9ZcZS++bNVCGYLmJUU\nWNfFxCZSHy42muvsy9BgnKzGvg5RjbP/adFrh/cnP2b0F3Mb1/7M15BjA1FUCgxo\nMJtTU4xj29R+eoyfo/6xdsU/7s1akQKBVs0V7QOdIH9SnB1PoAr0R9tz9fGjwGCM\naBXx+5Dpdm/EiNA8UeBe\n=e+wc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:07:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followe