hub.com/users/jaysoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaysoo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0440632fb8fb93827483289fbc59aa337db87cf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:06:21Z","email":"jack.hsu@gmail.com","name":"Jack Hsu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:06:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vitest): support vitest 5 (#37142)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nGenerators template vitest `~4.1.0` and there is no migration path to\nv5.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nNew scaffolds default to vitest 5, with version selection falling back\nto the highest major the workspace can actually resolve. A hybrid\nmigration moves existing workspaces.\n\n## Preview\n\n\nhttps://deploy-preview-37142--nx-docs.netlify.app/docs/technologies/test-tools/vitest/introduction\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5032\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"071d1a9100ec9164e04aaa2b7faacbc548e7449d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/071d1a9100ec9164e04aaa2b7faacbc548e7449d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/0440632fb8fb93827483289fbc59aa337db87cf2","verification":{"payload":"tree 071d1a9100ec9164e04aaa2b7faacbc548e7449d\nparent a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c\nauthor Jack Hsu <jack.hsu@gmail.com> 1790694381 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790694381 -0400\n\nfeat(vitest): support vitest 5 (#37142)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nGenerators template vitest `~4.1.0` and there is no migration path to\nv5.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nNew scaffolds default to vitest 5, with version selection falling back\nto the highest major the workspace can actually resolve. A hybrid\nmigration moves existing workspaces.\n\n## Preview\n\n\nhttps://deploy-preview-37142--nx-docs.netlify.app/docs/technologies/test-tools/vitest/introduction\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5032\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu9PtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA420QALG3ild5/QveFZiKBxN5zqbk\nOzSgKvyI1yV34I6Ys3KL1bbmfYVveczB+p+XWfIG4puWKMQZVEmcD3fDWK6E/Yy+\n4maia5sRAVaVHVU3o3jRFyYvnkf/ClxYN5E2QYoOZV4zjV6L1fmKOD1RDqOxQ/34\nRPVf8gIJXJV3E346R4rhZTkey3kX7qHUmivg8g44YH+si1UWifsJ4A33RHEibl08\n/c+Ke/+S9TB6N/sEeGzvmx0779vz7Tfz1ZpTP3sK4LnZVnuI9yrW8NGek08u6/y0\n/ckep9QggO8V/FcKTwtVgWlgzOk9Co4NK5y1/HYHKLDb4k/oLMb7h0mxNKA7/eM3\ncJMEM8WeoPxdR9YiUGx5lFVBZASlmHyXGnnfYFf/mnodm9iwbBHHZK/jvOau/WSp\nkUUL5xHyFt4dYS3QL4/Ro80E7iESy5Bp0hzI84ySVyVUiPUqP3V+FzPHnDRVBi7x\nCarMzY6bIzuljXLxft2hfsoBwqV/UZmmkj5adLggSUYzrA9WSgwjW/dMaLjdEOvw\nWtQ7axyRt38yZYsF/HOj3Ze/1Utmracd4TdkUussNnwKqWUxq1vXEuJhTOPSaK3n\n1IsXrxyR/lasYOEzuqbn6BoWP8qV6vYl4fuF9pBWtZ+2K604nODQCedXZBVylwdX\nxzL/X3zJ2S1Oqgez9iou\n=WIJJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:06:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/0440632fb8fb93827483289fbc59aa337db87cf2","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDA0NDA2MzJmYjhmYjkzODI3NDgzMjg5ZmJjNTlhYTMzN2RiODdjZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c","sha":"a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c"}],"sha":"0440632fb8fb93827483289fbc59aa337db87cf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0440632fb8fb93827483289fbc59aa337db87cf2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/636020?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdjayna","id":636020,"login":"sdjayna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNjAyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:54:25Z","email":"sdjayna@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jupiter Jayna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:54:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): copy cached outputs into the workspace in parallel (#37085)\n\nRestoring outputs from the local cache copies one file at a time, so a\nrestore is bound by per-file latency while the disk sits idle. This\nchange copies the entries of each directory in parallel on a small pool\nand cuts the copy of a 77,642-file restore from 61 s to 14 s on a\nWindows laptop. Stale outputs are removed exactly as before, with one\n`fs::remove_dir_all` per output.\n\n| Machine, tree | Copy, master | Copy, this PR | Remove and copy, master\n| Remove and copy, this PR |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Windows 11 laptop, 24 threads, real `dist`, 77,642 files, 1.69 GB |\n60.6 s | 13.9 s (4.4x) | 75.0 s | not re-run since the removal change,\nsee below |\n| M4 Mac, 16 cores, APFS, synthetic tree, 77,001 files, 1.97 GB | 10.9 s\n| 3.8 s (2.9x) | 14.5 s | 7.8 s (1.9x) |\n\nMedians of three interleaved rounds, master and patched binaries\nalternating. The Mac row is a fresh run of the current code on 28 Sep\n(release test binary calling `copy_outputs_into_workspace` directly), so\nit is not comparable with the Mac numbers in the earlier revision of\nthis description, which used a different harness. Every restore was\nchecked against the cache entry for file count, directory count and byte\ntotal, and the stale file and the extra file planted in the workspace\nwere gone afterwards. The Windows copy column stands: the copy code has\nnot changed since it was measured. The Windows remove-and-copy figure\nfor this PR was measured with a parallel removal that has since been\ndropped, so it is withdrawn; the removal is now master''s, which measured\nabout 14 s on that tree, so the expected total is that plus the 13.9 s\ncopy.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`NxCache.copyFilesFromCache` is a synchronous napi method, so the\n`Promise.all` in `finalizeCacheHits` runs the restores one after\nanother, and inside it `copy_dir_all`\n(`packages/nx/src/native/cache/file_ops.rs`) walks the tree on one\nthread with one `fs::copy` per file. Every file open passes through the\nfilesystem filter drivers on the machine, and the cost is paid serially:\nduring the Windows master run the disk was 5.7% busy and the copying\nprocess used 0.87 cores while Defender used 1.40.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`copy_dir_all` copies the entries of each directory in parallel on a\ndedicated rayon pool, recursing into subdirectories on the same pool.\nThe same function serves the restore, the store of outputs into the\ncache (`_copy` from `cache.rs`) and the exported `copy` binding, so all\nthree run in parallel; only the restore was measured.\n\nSemantics preserved: symlinks are recreated as links and never followed;\na file copy on restore first unlinks a pre-existing destination symlink;\nthe destination directory exists before any of its entries are copied,\nso nothing races `create_dir_all`; the first error still fails the call,\nthough when two entries fail at once which error is reported is no\nlonger determined by directory order. Removal of stale outputs is\nuntouched: `remove_path` passes the output to `fs::remove_dir_all`,\nwhich opens the directory once and unlinks a symlink at that path rather\nthan traversing its target.\n\nPool size: `cmp::max(available_parallelism().map_or(2, |n| n.get()) / 3,\n2)`, a third of the available parallelism and never below two, the\nderivation `workspace/files_hashing.rs` already uses. A fraction because\nthe copy is latency-bound and more threads than that only contend in the\nfilesystem: on the Mac a fixed pool of eight was slower than five in the\nearlier measurements, and a pool of the CPU count was slower than the\nsequential copy. The division gives 8 threads on the 24-thread laptop\nand 5 on the 16-core Mac.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Removal stays serial. An earlier revision removed the top-level\nsubdirectories of a stale output in parallel by path. That resolves\n`dist/sub` through `dist` at call time, so a symlink swapped in at\n`dist` between the listing and the removal redirects the deletion to the\nlink''s target. A stress test racing `remove_path` against a thread that\nrenames the output away and drops a symlink in its place deleted every\nfile behind the link in 1 of 1,000 swaps with that revision, and 0 of\n1,300 with `fs::remove_dir_all`. On the Windows tree the parallel\nremoval was no faster anyway (14 s serial, 15 s parallel), so nothing\nmeasured is lost.\n- Container CPU quotas. `available_parallelism` reports host CPUs;\n`detect_effective_cpu_count` in `metrics/collector.rs` is\ncontainer-aware but private to that module and used by nothing else.\nSharing it crate-wide would let this pool, the walker and the file\nhashing respect a quota; this PR does not change its visibility.\n- Not in this PR: making `copyFilesFromCache` a napi async task so that\nrestores of different tasks overlap and the main thread stays free.\n- Tests. Seven added in `file_ops.rs`: a wide tree copied byte for byte\nwith empty directories preserved; a restore over stale outputs; nested\nsymlinks recreated without being followed; a nested directory symlink\nunlinked rather than followed on removal; a stale escaping symlink\nreplaced on restore; a file in the way of a directory; an unreadable\nsource. 16 pass on macOS; on Windows 8 run and pass, the rest being\nunix-gated. `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy` adds no warning.\n`src/native/tests/cache.spec.ts`, `src/tasks-runner/cache.spec.ts` and\n`src/tasks-runner/task-orchestrator.spec.ts` under Vitest against the\nrebuilt binding: 70 pass.\n- End to end (earlier revision, copy code unchanged since). The `e2e-nx`\ncache, cache-no-daemon, affected-graph and run suites against a locally\npublished build: 111 passed, 4 skipped (pre-existing `xit`), 1 failed.\nThe failure, `cache › should support using globs as outputs`, reproduces\non master: the test writes a new output within two seconds of the hash\nbeing recorded, inside the window where the daemon ignores watcher\nevents for that output; #37087 removes that window and the test passes\nwith it. No restore runs in that step.\n- Sampled during the Windows runs at 1 s: master, CPU 12.9% of 24 cores,\ndisk 5.7% busy, copying process 0.87 cores, Defender 1.40 cores; this\nPR, CPU 27.9%, disk 13.3%, copying process 2.47 cores, Defender 2.46\ncores.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37090. #35172 parallelised cache lookups; the copy was untouched.","tree":{"sha":"11b9be82be90416e08b48e97303ba76f64b19953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/11b9be82be90416e08b48e97303ba76f64b19953"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c","verification":{"payload":"tree 11b9be82be90416e08b48e97303ba76f64b19953\nparent 0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba\nauthor Jupiter Jayna <sdjayna@users.noreply.github.com> 1790679265 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790679265 +0200\n\nfix(core): copy cached outputs into the workspace in parallel (#37085)\n\nRestoring outputs from the local cache copies one file at a time, so a\nrestore is bound by per-file latency while the disk sits idle. This\nchange copies the entries of each directory in parallel on a small pool\nand cuts the copy of a 77,642-file restore from 61 s to 14 s on a\nWindows laptop. Stale outputs are removed exactly as before, with one\n`fs::remove_dir_all` per output.\n\n| Machine, tree | Copy, master | Copy, this PR | Remove and copy, master\n| Remove and copy, this PR |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Windows 11 laptop, 24 threads, real `dist`, 77,642 files, 1.69 GB |\n60.6 s | 13.9 s (4.4x) | 75.0 s | not re-run since the removal change,\nsee below |\n| M4 Mac, 16 cores, APFS, synthetic tree, 77,001 files, 1.97 GB | 10.9 s\n| 3.8 s (2.9x) | 14.5 s | 7.8 s (1.9x) |\n\nMedians of three interleaved rounds, master and patched binaries\nalternating. The Mac row is a fresh run of the current code on 28 Sep\n(release test binary calling `copy_outputs_into_workspace` directly), so\nit is not comparable with the Mac numbers in the earlier revision of\nthis