 once and unlinks a symlink at that path rather\nthan traversing its target.\n\nPool size: `cmp::max(available_parallelism().map_or(2, |n| n.get()) / 3,\n2)`, a third of the available parallelism and never below two, the\nderivation `workspace/files_hashing.rs` already uses. A fraction because\nthe copy is latency-bound and more threads than that only contend in the\nfilesystem: on the Mac a fixed pool of eight was slower than five in the\nearlier measurements, and a pool of the CPU count was slower than the\nsequential copy. The division gives 8 threads on the 24-thread laptop\nand 5 on the 16-core Mac.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Removal stays serial. An earlier revision removed the top-level\nsubdirectories of a stale output in parallel by path. That resolves\n`dist/sub` through `dist` at call time, so a symlink swapped in at\n`dist` between the listing and the removal redirects the deletion to the\nlink''s target. A stress test racing `remove_path` against a thread that\nrenames the output away and drops a symlink in its place deleted every\nfile behind the link in 1 of 1,000 swaps with that revision, and 0 of\n1,300 with `fs::remove_dir_all`. On the Windows tree the parallel\nremoval was no faster anyway (14 s serial, 15 s parallel), so nothing\nmeasured is lost.\n- Container CPU quotas. `available_parallelism` reports host CPUs;\n`detect_effective_cpu_count` in `metrics/collector.rs` is\ncontainer-aware but private to that module and used by nothing else.\nSharing it crate-wide would let this pool, the walker and the file\nhashing respect a quota; this PR does not change its visibility.\n- Not in this PR: making `copyFilesFromCache` a napi async task so that\nrestores of different tasks overlap and the main thread stays free.\n- Tests. Seven added in `file_ops.rs`: a wide tree copied byte for byte\nwith empty directories preserved; a restore over stale outputs; nested\nsymlinks recreated without being followed; a nested directory symlink\nunlinked rather than followed on removal; a stale escaping symlink\nreplaced on restore; a file in the way of a directory; an unreadable\nsource. 16 pass on macOS; on Windows 8 run and pass, the rest being\nunix-gated. `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy` adds no warning.\n`src/native/tests/cache.spec.ts`, `src/tasks-runner/cache.spec.ts` and\n`src/tasks-runner/task-orchestrator.spec.ts` under Vitest against the\nrebuilt binding: 70 pass.\n- End to end (earlier revision, copy code unchanged since). The `e2e-nx`\ncache, cache-no-daemon, affected-graph and run suites against a locally\npublished build: 111 passed, 4 skipped (pre-existing `xit`), 1 failed.\nThe failure, `cache › should support using globs as outputs`, reproduces\non master: the test writes a new output within two seconds of the hash\nbeing recorded, inside the window where the daemon ignores watcher\nevents for that output; #37087 removes that window and the test passes\nwith it. No restore runs in that step.\n- Sampled during the Windows runs at 1 s: master, CPU 12.9% of 24 cores,\ndisk 5.7% busy, copying process 0.87 cores, Defender 1.40 cores; this\nPR, CPU 27.9%, disk 13.3%, copying process 2.47 cores, Defender 2.46\ncores.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37090. #35172 parallelised cache lookups; the copy was untouched.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu5jhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaL8QAJ3Y5yI1dXh5arCwkL/k28mW\n5dGvphZ6B/t5+Dtih+IQE3LQcf1FIGhnCp7clp4ThWrwPdfUMcojhcb6dPk7qsqc\npKPXXF8DM9aw1Sv0j61enRBOkqnbKYU0R0FiZK06ryB44jhiOW5S1Z15LUw1g4tL\nVdD+mA5tSl7jKHuLk2u1JNgMyvzFThUpZRzJaey5UoDS0xDsIQMB8WccLBrs4g9h\nV3jJj1HJ3dyofgjINMgTRVpavNzgXI9OQiInUsmCeA1L2i1xDt+/yqEmKjNwrRaj\nB2zrl+L8+FPRf5gWyhWYXcuS/1Dmg9kb2h6zQV435uIoEa7gWhj2Nf5KVm5TLB4w\nr/ZCXIom/n3sJ+LiiJuYHTglQ1fYlIIHSUxb2CNRYqBgSMUzYIMOP2Mxq6r8h3Vn\n6jdqVX102thJ8II5KQpzjDUTblmehQkRg91W0gB7MQGFQn/mlO29/UepBo21kVSX\nTPnkB7DUuwstl1TerQGQKprrAXzw+fDceB3KjptCJnVocfkzj3klfwmaWSg6FkGU\nQ5Yn82da7a7lY2V6z8GTcfqzhRoIrXEfR5Kj9qJjUdAwRBAsSXJYM2JiGnfswhs/\nsjN62ik2zWJ9aiRQpBnHJ9ACDgARbij7xfQg3iyZmAeMZAyi8SzXZbjQlu1HHn23\np4eJUm7Gd99NHBfOBfbh\n=99US\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:54:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGExMWVhNDlmZDMyMzE1NTZiMzQ0MGI5MmE0MjkwNTk2ZDc1YTAwM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba","sha":"0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba"}],"sha":"a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a11ea49fd3231556b3440b92a4290596d75a003c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28018309?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xItsSky","id":28018309,"login":"xItsSky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MDE4MzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xItsSky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:00:41Z","email":"emo.quentin@gmail.com","name":"Quentin Emo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:00:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(module-federation): skip undeclared default packages when sharing (#37223)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`DEFAULT_ANGULAR_PACKAGES_TO_SHARE` names `@angular/animations`, but the\nAngular generators never install it. Every freshly generated Module\nFederation host therefore logs this on each serve:\n\n```\nCould not find a version for \"@angular/animations\" in the root \"package.json\" when collecting shared packages for the Module Federation setup. The package will not be shared.\n```\n\nThe warning comes from `getNpmPackageSharedConfig`, which receives only\na package name and a version, so it cannot tell a package the user asked\nto share from a default-list entry.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nNo warning for a default the workspace does not declare, and no change\nto what actually gets shared.\n\n`buildModuleFederationConfig` now filters the framework default list\nagainst the root `package.json` before handing it to `sharePackages`. A\ndefault the workspace declares is still shared exactly as before. One it\ndoes not declare is dropped without a warning, because it was never\nshared in the first place: `getNpmPackageSharedConfig` already returned\n`undefined` for it after warning. Packages the project genuinely depends\non still warn when their version is missing, so a real misconfiguration\nstays visible.\n\n`@angular/animations` stays in the default list, so workspaces that\nstill install it keep sharing it. Removing it from the list instead\nwould have traded the warning for a silent change in sharing behavior.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37108","tree":{"sha":"93d7d04bffe346608b31adf42a1ccab3598ea059","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/93d7d04bffe346608b31adf42a1ccab3598ea059"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba","verification":{"payload":"tree 93d7d04bffe346608b31adf42a1ccab3598ea059\nparent a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf\nauthor Quentin Emo <emo.quentin@gmail.com> 1790676041 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790676041 +0200\n\nfix(module-federation): skip undeclared default packages when sharing (#37223)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`DEFAULT_ANGULAR_PACKAGES_TO_SHARE` names `@angular/animations`, but the\nAngular generators never install it. Every freshly generated Module\nFederation host therefore logs this on each serve:\n\n```\nCould not find a version for \"@angular/animations\" in the root \"package.json\" when collecting shared packages for the Module Federation setup. The package will not be shared.\n```\n\nThe warning comes from `getNpmPackageSharedConfig`, which receives only\na package name and a version, so it cannot tell a package the user asked\nto share from a default-list entry.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nNo warning for a default the workspace does not declare, and no change\nto what actually gets shared.\n\n`buildModuleFederationConfig` now filters the framework default list\nagainst the root `package.json` before handing it to `sharePackages`. A\ndefault the workspace declares is still shared exactly as before. One it\ndoes not declare is dropped without a warning, because it was never\nshared in the first place: `getNpmPackageSharedConfig` already returned\n`undefined` for it after warning. Packages the project genuinely depends\non still warn when their version is missing, so a real misconfiguration\nstays visible.\n\n`@angular/animations` stays in the default list, so workspaces that\nstill install it keep sharing it. Removing it from the list instead\nwould have traded the warning for a silent change in sharing behavior.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFixes #37108","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu4xJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdkkQAHUYLSX6MRLQzu0CVNSiGjJ/\nBQNkPha0hxcoisgJnmm3yzAyKeEHjccL90FeNwcKP3+uG3x+G72sO4c1hJ1RKhYp\nh8AiSi+CzvtpF9JK8WMLZSHe1yuFzT0oR4UnSxMfMblvAGO1fec1fCD22KGzMJO0\ngFuB7MlDRxGoP8LhBnDUsET6KXioY/L/2S6XpS5he/qsJuSkh1PgNBK4ONcCbT3i\n1Ng6d8Q2wr7Tuiyfw9k5/805g7sVPP1g1+qj+xP7EooC9xrtce/pTL+5aBGClVOI\n5WREnVEzTfc6fvIE+upEQAakcGELGCVVQg4tBJheWYlmdfC8sSowYPPQpth/w9cn\nDnba03IPDkUZ6IetaaN7OIJbqHDlROHqlw4pEYkdtcZqGXWg/RDXjA1aj1DqiIhC\n6smP05+eu9RWIZm4xBzibg0GL+dnh6545+kW4DTHg6zyPX8BrJ1dtEKEf/RnYcPv\nX4lK7K9s0suXMrqftH6e6lGM5s9jkPwQWAIEK8mQL6nCxBLTPksHSZrGcYwjUTC6\nkge3xJjgaU7JClIzVAiXd5mNDzibuwU+g9wRr3a5QujKT5K4I/Yz2Ag4HYziFt60\n3XGwJQW9PHQEzSwS+Kut8vEQ2/AiqOyBx45yjQp6/hfOSZ0fn/d7La0xBGO73XuE\nFpY/B5C2F6qlVEvDyuti\n=Zdlu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:00:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDBkNmIyMDljZjQ5MzQxNmMwZTMxNDk5OTY2NGZjNGVlMzNhMDA4YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf","sha":"a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf"}],"sha":"0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0d6b209cf493416c0e314999664fc4ee33a008ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/636020?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdjayna","id":636020,"login":"sdjayna","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNjAyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdjayna","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:49:31Z","email":"sdjayna@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jupiter Jayna"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:49:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(bundling): clear typescript update timer when a rollup build closes its watch program (#37196)\n\n**Fixes the `react-package.test.ts` flake: a rollup build finishes,\nprints `created …`, and its process never exits, so the e2e times out at\n300 s. It fails about one `master` run in 25 and has been failing PRs\nthat have nothing to do with rollup.** **Cause: TypeScript leaves a\nprogram-update timer armed when `@rollup/plugin-typescript` closes its\nwatch program at the end of the build. This change clears it; the hang\nwent from 11 of 53 runs to 0 of 41.**\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n### What fails, and why it matters\n\n`e2e-react` fails with `Command timed out after 300s: build childlib…`\nwhile the output already ends in `created ../../dist/libs/childlib… in\n1.4s`. The build is done; the process is still there. Every such run is\na red CI for a change that did nothing wrong, and a re-run.\n\n| Failed because of it | When |\n|---|---|\n| `master` | 3 of the last 30 runs (24 Sep 13:39 and 13:44, 25 Sep\n14:58); #36794 measured it at about 4% of `master` runs since August |\n| #37113 (daemon lockfile check) | main-linux, 25 Sep ([run\n36133475462](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/36133475462)) |\n| #37085 (parallel cache restore) | main-linux, 18 Sep, then green on\nre-run |\n\n#36794 found from a CI dump that the `rollup -c` child is what stays\nalive after its last output, and added a handle dump to find out why.\nThis PR is the why.\n\n### Why the process does not exit\n\n1. `withNx` adds\n[`@rollup/plugin-typescript`](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/0d8fca1b245ce2700b240008140d3eaef49eebb1/packages/rollup/src/plugins/with-nx/with-nx.ts#L262).\nThe plugin runs the TypeScript compiler as a **watch program** even for\na one-shot build, and closes it in\n[`buildEnd`](https://github.com/rollup/plugins/blob/639f45638234c1c3fabfb13615c78bebaef89ef2/packages/typescript/src/index.ts#L196-L200).\n2. A watch program reacts to file changes by arming a 250 ms timer\n([`timerToUpdateProgram`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8/src/compiler/watchPublic.ts#L881-L891)).\nTypeScript''s\n[`close()`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8/src/compiler/watchPublic.ts#L562-L598)\nstops the file watchers but does not cancel that timer.\n3. So if any watched file changes in the last 250 ms of the build, the\ntimer fires after the program is closed, rebuilds it, and creates a\nfresh set of file watchers that nothing will ever close. Every hung\nprocess we caught holds 192 `FSEventWrap` and 13 `StatWatcher` handles;\na healthy one holds none.\n4. Rollup''s CLI does not call `process.exit`, so those watchers keep it\nalive.\n[`nx:run-commands`](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/0d8fca1b245ce2700b240008140d3eaef49eebb1/packages/nx/src/executors/run-commands/running-tasks.ts#L457)\nwaits for the child to close, the\n[e2e](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/0d8fca1b245ce2700b240008140d3eaef49eebb1/e2e/utils/command-utils.ts#L477)\nwaits for nx, and the test times out.\n\nOn CI a build phase runs 5 to 12 s on a shared runner with the daemon\nrecomputing the graph beside it, so the window for a stray file event is\nfar wider than 250 ms. Which event lands in it on CI does not matter to\nthe fix.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe process exits when the build is done.\n\n**The change:**\n`packages/rollup/src/plugins/with-nx/watch-program-timers.ts` (+51\nlines) gives the plugin a TypeScript whose watch programs remember the\ntimers they arm and cancel them on `close()`. `withNx` passes it as the\nplugin''s `typescript` option (+2 lines). Watch mode is untouched: the\nprogram is never closed there.\n\n**Proof:** `rollup -c` on a generated React library, with one `touch` of\na source file at a fixed offset. The process normally exits at about\n1,050 ms, and `buildEnd` falls in the 650 to 850 ms band.\n\n| | runs | still alive 20 s after `created …` |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `@nx/rollup` 23.2.1, touch at 650 to 850 ms | 30 | **11** |\n| `@nx/rollup` 23.2.1, touch later or none | 23 | 0 |\n| this branch, touch at 650 to 850 ms | 30 | **0** |\n| this branch, touch later or none | 11 | 0 |\n\nTests: 4 new specs pass (timer cleared on close, timer still fires while\nopen, host without timers untouched, module otherwise unchanged); `nx\nrun rollup:test` 188 pass; lint and format clean.\n\n**Where the bug really lives:** in TypeScript''s `close()`, and the\nplugin could also clear the timers itself (rollup/plugins#2025). This PR\nfixes every `withNx` build now, on every installed TypeScript, whichever\nof those lands.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. `npx create-nx-workspace proj --preset=apps --pm=npm`, `npm i -D\n@nx/react`, `nx g @nx/react:library libs/childlib --bundler=rollup\n--unitTestRunner=jest`, then `nx show projects` once to cache the graph.\n2. In `libs/childlib`: `NX_TASK_TARGET_PROJECT=@proj/childlib\nNX_TASK_TARGET_TARGET=build NX_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$PWD/../.. npx rollup -c\nrollup.config.cjs & sleep 0.7; touch src/lib/childlib.tsx; wait` (try\noffsets between 0.65 and 0.85 s; about one run in three hangs).\n3. `rollup` prints `created dist in …` and does not exit. With this\nchange it exits at every offset.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\n#36794 (diagnostics for this timeout). Runs it failed: #37113\n([36133475462](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/36133475462)),\n#37085 on 18 Sep.","tree":{"sha":"c94c9abe6d1403999c2d680513fef51e69e09299","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/c94c9abe6d1403999c2d680513fef51e69e09299"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf","verification":{"payload":"tree c94c9abe6d1403999c2d680513fef51e69e09299\nparent ff94a98fa3f7e6d0dec3900e2bca33a762953755\nauthor Jupiter Jayna <sdjayna@users.noreply.github.com> 1790671771 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790671771 +0200\n\nfix(bundling): clear typescript update timer when a rollup build closes its watch program (#37196)\n\n**Fixes the `react-package.test.ts` flake: a rollup build finishes,\nprints `created …`, and its process never exits, so the e2e times out at\n300 s. It fails about one `master` run in 25 and has been failing PRs\nthat have nothing to do with rollup.** **Cause: TypeScript leaves a\nprogram-update timer armed when `@rollup/plugin-typescript` closes its\nwatch program at the end of the build. This change clears it; the hang\nwent from 11 of 53 runs to 0 of 41.**\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n### What fails, and why it matters\n\n`e2e-react` fails with `Command timed out after 300s: build childlib…`\nwhile the output already ends in `created ../../dist/libs/childlib… in\n1.4s`. The build is done; the process is still there. Every such run is\na red CI for a change that did nothing wrong, and a re-run.\n\n| Failed because of it | When |\n|---|---|\n| `master` | 3 of the last 30 runs (24 Sep 13:39 and 13:44, 25 Sep\n14:58); #36794 measured it at about 4% of `master` runs since August |\n| #37113 (daemon lockfile check) | main-linux, 25 Sep ([run\n36133475462](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/36133475462)) |\n| #37085 (parallel cache restore) | main-linux, 18 Sep, then green on\nre-run |\n\n#36794 found from a CI dump that the `rollup -c` child is what stays\nalive after its last output, and added a handle dump to find out why.\nThis PR is the why.\n\n### Why the process does not exit\n\n1. `withNx` adds\n[`@rollup/plugin-typescript`](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/0d8fca1b245ce2700b240008140d3eaef49eebb1/packages/rollup/src/plugins/with-nx/with-nx.ts#L262).\nThe plugin runs the TypeScript compiler as a **watch program** even for\na one-shot build, and closes it in\n[`buildEnd`](https://github.com/rollup/plugins/blob/639f45638234c1c3fabfb13615c78bebaef89ef2/packages/typescript/src/index.ts#L196-L200).\n2. A watch program reacts to file changes by arming a 250 ms timer\n([`timerToUpdateProgram`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8/src/compiler/watchPublic.ts#L881-L891)).\nTypeScript''s\n[`close()`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/blob/050880ce59e30b356b686bd3144efe24f875ebc8/src/compiler/watchPublic.ts#L562-L598)\nstops the file watchers but does not cancel that timer.\n3. So if any watched file changes in the last 250 ms of the build, the\ntimer fires after the program is closed, rebuilds it, and creates a\nfresh set of file watchers that nothing will ever close. Every hung\nprocess we caught holds 192 `FSEventWrap` and 13 `StatWatcher` handles;\na healthy one holds none.\n4. Rollup''s CLI does not call `process.exit`, so those watchers keep it\nalive.\n[`nx:run-commands`](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/0d8fca1b245ce2700b240008140d3eaef49eebb1/packages/nx/src/executors/run-commands/running-tasks.ts#L457)\nwaits for the child to close, the\n[e2e](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/blob/0d8fca1b245ce2700b240008140d3eaef49eebb1/e2e/utils/command-utils.ts#L477)\nwaits for nx, and the test times out.\n\nOn CI a build phase runs 5 to 12 s on a shared runner with the daemon\nrecomputing the graph beside it, so the window for a stray file event is\nfar wider than 250 ms. Which event lands in it on CI does not matter to\nthe fix.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe process exits when the build is done.\n\n**The change:**\n`packages/rollup/src/plugins/with-nx/watch-program-timers.ts` (+51\nlines) gives the plugin a TypeScript whose watch programs remember the\ntimers they arm and cancel them on `close()`. `withNx` passes it as the\nplugin''s `typescript` option (+2 lines). Watch mode is untouched: the\nprogram is never closed there.\n\n**Proof:** `rollup -c` on a generated React library, with one `touch` of\na source file at a fixed offset. The process normally exits at about\n1,050 ms, and `buildEnd` falls in the 650 to 850 ms band.\n\n| | runs | still alive 20 s after `created …` |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `@nx/rollup` 23.2.1, touch at 650 to 850 ms | 30 | **11** |\n| `@nx/rollup` 23.2.1, touch later or none | 23 | 0 |\n| this branch, touch at 650 to 850 ms | 30 | **0** |\n| this branch, touch later or none | 11 | 0 |\n\nTests: 4 new specs pass (timer cleared on close, timer still fires while\nopen, host without timers untouched, module otherwise unchanged); `nx\nrun rollup:test` 188 pass; lint and format clean.\n\n**Where the bug really lives:** in TypeScript''s `close()`, and the\nplugin could also clear the timers itself (rollup/plugins#2025). This PR\nfixes every `withNx` build now, on every installed TypeScript, whichever\nof those lands.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. `npx create-nx-workspace proj --preset=apps --pm=npm`, `npm i -D\n@nx/react`, `nx g @nx/react:library libs/childlib --bundler=rollup\n--unitTestRunner=jest`, then `nx show projects` once to cache the graph.\n2. In `libs/childlib`: `NX_TASK_TARGET_PROJECT=@proj/childlib\nNX_TASK_TARGET_TARGET=build NX_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$PWD/../.. npx rollup -c\nrollup.config.cjs & sleep 0.7; touch src/lib/childlib.tsx; wait` (try\noffsets between 0.65 and 0.85 s; about one run in three hangs).\n3. `rollup` prints `created dist in …` and does not exit. With this\nchange it exits at every offset.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\n#36794 (diagnostics for this timeout). Runs it failed: #37113\n([36133475462](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/36133475462)),\n#37085 on 18 Sep.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu3ubCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL8QQAKEUEDtHtN7rZs7qw0TkBqYz\nnlpw4eUVrX21mw69dXiH1jf8agchyjvBMAHj1yU2lBWNVNxkgNlb4UgQ+bkH803H\nqfNkXXVMEK8y9F1Qpjl7lg44jmyanrqBTLtl50pWHt3/c9Pk7bojzZtdX1SInuO/\n/53R5P/NO2wl