7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/a7498da252a03db4277a788c672c64a42f9e3bcf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/ff94a98fa3f7e6d0dec3900e2bca33a762953755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:39:29Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T19:39:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(testing): hold the Cypress 16 migration only when a Vite component testing project resolves Vite 7 (#37123)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe Cypress 16 package update in `@nx/cypress` 23.3 never runs in a\nworkspace whose root `node_modules` holds a Vite below 8. Angular\nreleases before 22.1 pin a Vite below 8 in `@angular/build`, and npm\nhoists it to the root. `nx migrate` reads that copy, treats the update\nas incompatible, and keeps the workspace on Cypress 15 without saying\nso. Once `@nx/cypress` is on 23.3, later migrate runs never retry the\nupdate. This holds for workspaces that run no Vite component tests at\nall.\n\n```\n$ npx nx migrate latest   # Angular 22.0 workspace, cypress 15\n# @nx/cypress moves to 23.3.x, cypress stays on 15, no message\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`nx migrate` moves a Cypress 15 workspace to Cypress 16 unless one of\nits Vite component testing configs would run on a Vite below 8. A\ntransitive Vite hoisted to the root does not hold the bump when only e2e\nor webpack component testing projects can reach it. When the bump is\nheld, nx prints which config resolved which Vite and the commands to\nrerun once Vite is on 8. The Cypress 16 config, `overwriteQuery` and\n`cypress/angular` rewrites still run, and the AI instructions still\ncover the remaining source changes.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5020\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The `23.3.0-cypress-16` package update group is replaced by the\n`upgrade-to-cypress-16` migration, gated on `cypress >=15 <16`. It reads\neach config''s `component` block and resolves `vite` from the config''s\ndirectory through Node module resolution, as the Cypress binary does, so\nYarn PnP workspaces resolve too. It bumps `cypress` and the declared\n`@cypress/*-dev-server` packages when no Vite component testing config\nresolves a Vite below 8.\n- The migration bumps a `cypress` declared as a range, `latest` or\n`next`. For a `file:`, git, URL or `npm:` alias declaration, or an\nunresolved catalog reference, it keeps Cypress 15 and prints the\nmanual-bump steps.\n- The migration checks every `cypress.config.*` in the workspace and\nevery config path an `@nx/cypress:cypress` target sets. Target paths get\n`nx.json` target defaults merged in (executor, target-name and filtered\nentries) and `{workspaceRoot}`, `{projectRoot}` and `{projectName}`\nexpanded. An absolute path inside the workspace is read through its\nrelative path. The shared `cypressProjectConfigs` helper carries the\ntarget paths, so the other Cypress migrations get them too.\n- The migration does not check a config with a custom name that no\n`@nx/cypress:cypress` target references, such as one run through\n`nx:run-commands`. Finding it would mean parsing commands. On Vite 7\nsuch a config moves to Cypress 16 and fails until Vite is on 8. The\nmigration docs and AI instructions name the gap.\n- Detection follows same-file spreads and variables, quoted, shorthand\nand computed keys, and the four Nx presets. A config it cannot read or\nclassify with certainty counts as unknown. It holds the bump when a Vite\nbelow 8 resolves from its directory.\n- The held and the manual-bump messages print a two-step recovery that\nneeds no root `migrations.json`: `nx migrate @nx/cypress@<installed>\n--from=@nx/cypress@23.3.0-beta.0` re-collects only the 23.3 Cypress 16\nmigrations (the bound is exclusive and sits below the earliest one,\nchecked against the Migrator), then\n`--run-migration=@nx/cypress:upgrade-to-cypress-16` once Vite is on 8,\nor `--run-migrations` after a manual move to Cypress 16 so the four\n`requires: cypress >=16` migrations run.\n- A pnpm catalog entry is bumped inside the catalog. Known limit,\npre-existing for every catalog bump made by a migration: the migrate\nrunner installs only when the package.json dependency lists change, so a\ncatalog-only bump leaves the lockfile and the installed Cypress on 15\nuntil the next install. Tracked on NXC-5020 for a separate core change.\n- The migration calls the three Cypress 16 rewrite generators itself and\nreuses the Cypress 16 prompt. The `requires: cypress >=16` entries are\nnot collected while Cypress 15 is installed; they stay for workspaces\nalready on Cypress 16.\n- The four `>=16` entries, first shipped in `23.3.0-beta.1`, share the\nnew migration''s `23.3.0-beta.7` stamp. Beta workspaces already on\nCypress 16 run them again, which is accepted for prereleases. Upgrades\nfrom 23.2.x are unaffected.\n- Validated on nx-examples with the built package. Covered: the bump and\nagentic prompt, the hold on a fabricated Vite 7 component testing\nproject, the dev-server bump on Vite 8, and the rewrites on a fabricated\ne2e project.\n\n## Migration coverage\n\n- Vite floor for Cypress 16 component testing: generator, a per-config\ncheck replacing the root-level `incompatibleWith`.\n- `cypress` and `@cypress/*-dev-server` bumps: generator, declared\npackages only, catalog aware.\n- Renamed and removed config options, `overwriteQuery`,\n`cypress/angular` import: existing generators, called from the new\nmigration.\n- Removed runtime APIs (`Cypress.env()`, `cy.exec()`, `.end()`, `env`\ntest overrides, `Cypress.config()` writes): existing prompt, reused.\nEach replacement depends on where the value comes from, so a generator\ncannot guarantee a correct rewrite.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/nxc-5020-a2a94585\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"514d5ccc4503a032a735c7c8d2786b6ae34c657f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/514d5ccc4503a032a735c7c8d2786b6ae34c657f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/ff94a98fa3f7e6d0dec3900e2bca33a762953755","verification":{"payload":"tree 514d5ccc4503a032a735c7c8d2786b6ae34c657f\nparent 0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1790624369 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790624369 +0000\n\nfix(testing): hold the Cypress 16 migration only when a Vite component testing project resolves Vite 7 (#37123)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe Cypress 16 package update in `@nx/cypress` 23.3 never runs in a\nworkspace whose root `node_modules` holds a Vite below 8. Angular\nreleases before 22.1 pin a Vite below 8 in `@angular/build`, and npm\nhoists it to the root. `nx migrate` reads that copy, treats the update\nas incompatible, and keeps the workspace on Cypress 15 without saying\nso. Once `@nx/cypress` is on 23.3, later migrate runs never retry the\nupdate. This holds for workspaces that run no Vite component tests at\nall.\n\n```\n$ npx nx migrate latest   # Angular 22.0 workspace, cypress 15\n# @nx/cypress moves to 23.3.x, cypress stays on 15, no message\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`nx migrate` moves a Cypress 15 workspace to Cypress 16 unless one of\nits Vite component testing configs would run on a Vite below 8. A\ntransitive Vite hoisted to the root does not hold the bump when only e2e\nor webpack component testing projects can reach it. When the bump is\nheld, nx prints which config resolved which Vite and the commands to\nrerun once Vite is on 8. The Cypress 16 config, `overwriteQuery` and\n`cypress/angular` rewrites still run, and the AI instructions still\ncover the remaining source changes.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5020\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The `23.3.0-cypress-16` package update group is replaced by the\n`upgrade-to-cypress-16` migration, gated on `cypress >=15 <16`. It reads\neach config''s `component` block and resolves `vite` from the config''s\ndirectory through Node module resolution, as the Cypress binary does, so\nYarn PnP workspaces resolve too. It bumps `cypress` and the declared\n`@cypress/*-dev-server` packages when no Vite component testing config\nresolves a Vite below 8.\n- The migration bumps a `cypress` declared as a range, `latest` or\n`next`. For a `file:`, git, URL or `npm:` alias declaration, or an\nunresolved catalog reference, it keeps Cypress 15 and prints the\nmanual-bump steps.\n- The migration checks every `cypress.config.*` in the workspace and\nevery config path an `@nx/cypress:cypress` target sets. Target paths get\n`nx.json` target defaults merged in (executor, target-name and filtered\nentries) and `{workspaceRoot}`, `{projectRoot}` and `{projectName}`\nexpanded. An absolute path inside the workspace is read through its\nrelative path. The shared `cypressProjectConfigs` helper carries the\ntarget paths, so the other Cypress migrations get them too.\n- The migration does not check a config with a custom name that no\n`@nx/cypress:cypress` target references, such as one run through\n`nx:run-commands`. Finding it would mean parsing commands. On Vite 7\nsuch a config moves to Cypress 16 and fails until Vite is on 8. The\nmigration docs and AI instructions name the gap.\n- Detection follows same-file spreads and variables, quoted, shorthand\nand computed keys, and the four Nx presets. A config it cannot read or\nclassify with certainty counts as unknown. It holds the bump when a Vite\nbelow 8 resolves from its directory.\n- The held and the manual-bump messages print a two-step recovery that\nneeds no root `migrations.json`: `nx migrate @nx/cypress@<installed>\n--from=@nx/cypress@23.3.0-beta.0` re-collects only the 23.3 Cypress 16\nmigrations (the bound is exclusive and sits below the earliest one,\nchecked against the Migrator), then\n`--run-migration=@nx/cypress:upgrade-to-cypress-16` once Vite is on 8,\nor `--run-migrations` after a manual move to Cypress 16 so the four\n`requires: cypress >=16` migrations run.\n- A pnpm catalog entry is bumped inside the catalog. Known limit,\npre-existing for every catalog bump made by a migration: the migrate\nrunner installs only when the package.json dependency lists change, so a\ncatalog-only bump leaves the lockfile and the installed Cypress on 15\nuntil the next install. Tracked on NXC-5020 for a separate core change.\n- The migration calls the three Cypress 16 rewrite generators itself and\nreuses the Cypress 16 prompt. The `requires: cypress >=16` entries are\nnot collected while Cypress 15 is installed; they stay for workspaces\nalready on Cypress 16.\n- The four `>=16` entries, first shipped in `23.3.0-beta.1`, share the\nnew migration''s `23.3.0-beta.7` stamp. Beta workspaces already on\nCypress 16 run them again, which is accepted for prereleases. Upgrades\nfrom 23.2.x are unaffected.\n- Validated on nx-examples with the built package. Covered: the bump and\nagentic prompt, the hold on a fabricated Vite 7 component testing\nproject, the dev-server bump on Vite 8, and the rewrites on a fabricated\ne2e project.\n\n## Migration coverage\n\n- Vite floor for Cypress 16 component testing: generator, a per-config\ncheck replacing the root-level `incompatibleWith`.\n- `cypress` and `@cypress/*-dev-server` bumps: generator, declared\npackages only, catalog aware.\n- Renamed and removed config options, `overwriteQuery`,\n`cypress/angular` import: existing generators, called from the new\nmigration.\n- Removed runtime APIs (`Cypress.env()`, `cy.exec()`, `.end()`, `env`\ntest overrides, `Cypress.config()` writes): existing prompt, reused.\nEach replacement depends on where the value comes from, so a generator\ncannot guarantee a correct rewrite.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/nxc-5020-a2a94585\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqusJxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFtYQALDSrPtivcPVGYjfJw+b/pj7\nuXhT6AJsliypcG3VMPfeKX2Ny7yq0IIrvebajEhTm5fv8+Au7dMWv0KTlM80E2QQ\nyM2dq2POMPWXfHtWlZiJgo1c/Z539yzjdTFnk8A3frZC9KI2O/XE7eyl1b5nEAtm\nI0OK+GAhR/6NYGaWF24dKR1lBypj1YNV28eZ12eVnYiK1sZjh852HB1X4a+Ccb/Q\nfbMVvlhyrIHDnr7WDnJgaqP2yjbflfN5z/IpdXLXl9zmX5QM64ibtAw01N2PXH0G\ndWTK6igQa3tzdoKLMB4C+VmZ65wElgOl6P4UHpdglSBSo9W8U5p2HbiphEn4q1Fv\nXXeF9VtRFhag/HdbkOF8J3qxT2xVuopq+gxg8HCbUU+RfKkvvRUKWiW7o2FzFp1q\nrFYQoIJtF3wDDJg/l6nR6u7gdhQL+dtnsit3fvHdNy6SEa6J8QNTUJX1sDmN7a2L\njEBMdrlh8gjlpuTGWaGm13vO3b7V0sPJjNhuhrplCqiwGU9Ne+OrWcUxWXHEdL4T\nwB/est02fJ6zL/nI/U5WXh5qNoOoxGiFqS7zB4Ezgo1AKE4TtgeFj/r5vtOCTS9Q\nOwNt0ZAH24tmTIuURBG+0qq1FzUo3/b+IQoHj5h0OS5EXF1DkppsBiJXfcR9eb22\nGhXE0wZAlJSC/EVZqnWm\n=kZP5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T19:39:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/ff94a98fa3f7e6d0dec3900e2bca33a762953755","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGZmOTRhOThmYTNmN2U2ZDBkZWMzOTAwZTJiY2EzM2E3NjI5NTM3NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806","sha":"0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806"}],"sha":"ff94a98fa3f7e6d0dec3900e2bca33a762953755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/ff94a98fa3f7e6d0dec3900e2bca33a762953755"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:19:11Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:19:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): speed up daemon start by collecting ignore files in one walk (#37211)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nBefore the daemon starts listening, its file watcher collects every\n`.gitignore` and `.nxignore` file in the workspace. It walked the\nworkspace twice, once per file name, on a single thread. Each walk\nskipped only dependency, git and Nx cache directories, so it entered\ngitignored build output such as `dist`. A command that starts the daemon\nwaited for both walks before the daemon took its graph request.\n\nWhen the workspace root''s own path ended in one of those skipped names,\nsuch as `node_modules`, the watcher found no ignore files at all. The\ncollection walk skipped the root itself, while the workspace file walk\nnever skips its root. The daemon then tracked changes to files that the\nfile walk leaves out.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe daemon collects both kinds of ignore file in one walk that runs on\nseveral threads. It finds the same files, so its file map and graph\ndon''t change. It answers its first graph request sooner: 4.3% sooner in\nthis repo''s checkout, where the walk takes 61% less time. Only the\ndaemon runs this walk, and Nx turns the daemon off in CI and Docker\nunless `NX_DAEMON=true`.\n\nThe daemon applies the ignore files of a workspace whose root path ends\nin a skipped name, matching the workspace file walk.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The walk reuses the workspace file walk''s parallel walker,\n`create_walker(root, false)`. The source shrinks by 25 lines and adds no\ndependency.\n\nMedians of 5 alternating `nx show projects` runs that start the daemon,\ngraph caches cleared:\n\n| | This checkout (138k entries) | Private workspace (21k entries) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Start to graph ready | 19.36 -> 18.53 s (-4.3%) | 4.81 -> 4.68 s\n(-2.7%) |\n| Daemon graph construction | 17.73 -> 17.69 s (unchanged) | 4.23 ->\n4.22 s (unchanged) |\n| `workspace context init` (the walk) | 1.20 -> 0.47 s (-61%) | 0.20 ->\n0.08 s (-60%) |\n\n- Graph ready was faster in every pair. The saving comes from init,\nwhich the graph request waits for.\n- Walk cost follows entries walked, not project or file count. This\ncheckout tracks fewer files (9.8k vs 12.5k), but gitignored build output\nadds 102k entries. The saving grows with it.\n- Both builds found the same ignore files and daemon file maps, across\n13 edits per workspace.\n- Wall time is left out: sync generators delayed 4 of 10\nprivate-workspace runs by 2.7 s, in both builds.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bec5323b3dba0e886de736a1ced17029a90011a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/9bec5323b3dba0e886de736a1ced17029a90011a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bec5323b3dba0e886de736a1ced17029a90011a\nparent 21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1790619551 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790619551 -0400\n\nfix(core): speed up daemon start by collecting ignore files in one walk (#37211)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nBefore the daemon starts listening, its file watcher collects every\n`.gitignore` and `.nxignore` file in the workspace. It walked the\nworkspace twice, once per file name, on a single thread. Each walk\nskipped only dependency, git and Nx cache directories, so it entered\ngitignored build output such as `dist`. A command that starts the daemon\nwaited for both walks before the daemon took its graph request.\n\nWhen the workspace root''s own path ended in one of those skipped names,\nsuch as `node_modules`, the watcher found no ignore files at all. The\ncollection walk skipped the root itself, while the workspace file walk\nnever skips its root. The daemon then tracked changes to files that the\nfile walk leaves out.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe daemon collects both kinds of ignore file in one walk that runs on\nseveral threads. It finds the same files, so its file map and graph\ndon''t change. It answers its first graph request sooner: 4.3% sooner in\nthis repo''s checkout, where the walk takes 61% less time. Only the\ndaemon runs this walk, and Nx turns the daemon off in CI and Docker\nunless `NX_DAEMON=true`.\n\nThe daemon applies the ignore files of a workspace whose root path ends\nin a skipped name, matching the workspace file walk.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The walk reuses the workspace file walk''s parallel walker,\n`create_walker(root, false)`. The source shrinks by 25 lines and adds no\ndependency.\n\nMedians of 5 alternating `nx show projects` runs that start the daemon,\ngraph caches cleared:\n\n| | This checkout (138k entries) | Private workspace (21k entries) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Start to graph ready | 19.36 -> 18.53 s (-4.3%) | 4.81 -> 4.68 s\n(-2.7%) |\n| Daemon graph construction | 17.73 -> 17.69 s (unchanged) | 4.23 ->\n4.22 s (unchanged) |\n| `workspace context init` (the walk) | 1.20 -> 0.47 s (-61%) | 0.20 ->\n0.08 s (-60%) |\n\n- Graph ready was faster in every pair. The saving comes from init,\nwhich the graph request waits for.\n- Walk cost follows entries walked, not project or file count. This\ncheckout tracks fewer files (9.8k vs 12.5k), but gitignored build output\nadds 102k entries. The saving grows with it.\n- Both builds found the same ignore files and daemon file maps, across\n13 edits per workspace.\n- Wall time is left out: sync generators delayed 4 of 10\nprivate-workspace runs by 2.7 s, in both builds.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquq+fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk1MQABICxVrA04vhA3C46TnsyO2Y\n/1sgd/xvM4p+jWKqA0/wQku4u+u9Z9B7Uxft0N74/rJJFjcvmwOviJDc0HaYkAsn\nmlFrVb+nKIWqK9rMgx8ItfuImuhRJVZcofzjOWsrNm1142KRKxiTpWjy0MN+H66r\n+4JU83SWGc8qwd2sb/Lkg4AdNNoh1E3X/i5JMl68QeigBFp20vWWmdSyN9QzbdeF\nAO0JvDrPQDfijBpFAA2ue57tp1gMqYJffSwM+L2MeDYPFlpQR/d5lA1fa3iq0bs1\nbRAYCFinDWqehf0ILm25tBLRfRddt46CfHer7lOFBscX0u1dXGrfBx7jE96vwLbD\nOtPGE3f9CEX+q7LtftVRaqG3NMB1oaxS3qWE2Y5hBe+za7dDHmsh1x3dLazyhUvJ\nPn9gEV6jsnx4wNzg7lDcR8iwqdaSTqA5xIohG4woIIs2NMixsRTEKC8Fvoyh96ss\n3/iy5DiP8M8TR8y0Cep4FME7Ayi4MmBleMssHMgWw0khnI5pQVphaAxiZCWDDfBw\n7s4D3Mkp8RhsXdvXfOoI79fPCRJgIW1t6aTFBlsEIeKcZ4wiLMKHc5ux9FsrHblO\noHkEwhMIjQWXcN0TMw49WumYx9apYbICu9+c0LcCYeuFTOgZbF2FRTWVyIX88mEZ\ntK61GYPM77qnkiftO4V2\n=xg5S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T18:19:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDAxODg3NzZlYTAwNWQwZDI1M2RhZTA2YWRhZDJmNjk3Mjg1YjM4MDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de","sha":"21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de"}],"sha":"0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/0188776ea005d0d253dae06adad2f697285b3806"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:33:34Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:33:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): pass only ultracache config to the snapshot eligibility walk (#37212)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nOn Nx Cloud agents with I/O snapshots on, every task crashes the agent\nworker:\n\n```\nNX   V4 worker encountered a fatal error\nFailed to convert JavaScript value `Null` into rust type `String` on Task.hash on TaskGraph.tasks\n    at applyIoSnapshotOutputs (nx/dist/src/io-snapshots/outputs.js:22:64)\n    at createOrchestrator (nx/dist/src/tasks-runner/init-tasks-runner.js:44:46)\n    at runDiscreteTasks (...)\n```\n\nThe Cloud agent clears an assigned task''s `hash` to `null` so nx\nrehashes it on the agent (it has done this since 2025). #37036 added\n`applyIoSnapshotOutputs(projectGraph, taskGraph, …)` in\n`createOrchestrator`, and `taskGraph` there holds that nulled task.\n`getObservedIoSnapshotOutputs` takes a whole `TaskGraph`, so napi\ndecodes every field of every task. napi maps only `undefined` to `None`\nfor optional `#[napi(object)]` fields, so `null` goes to the `String`\ndecoder and throws.\n\nThe eligibility walk never reads `hash`. From each task it reads only\nthe id and the `ultracache` config.\n\nThis breaks CI for nrwl/nx and nrwl/ocean on 23.3.0-beta.6.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`getObservedIoSnapshotOutputs` and `getIoSnapshotReport` take\n`Record<taskId, TaskUltracacheConfiguration | null>` instead of a\n`TaskGraph`. JS builds the map with `getUltraCacheConfig(taskGraph)`, so\nno other task field crosses into Rust. Map values go through napi''s\n`Option` decoder, which accepts `null`. The helper sends `null`, not\n`undefined`, for a task with no config, because napi''s map decoder drops\n`undefined` keys.\n\nInside Rust, `resolve` takes an iterator of `(task id, ultracache\nconfig)` pairs. The two napi functions pass their map''s entries, and the\nhash planner passes references into its own graph for the tasks it\nplans, so nothing is cloned. `resolve_scoped` is folded into `resolve`,\nso there is still one eligibility walk. The walk no longer sorts task\nids: only the report needs ordered diagnostics, so `report()` sorts them\nby task id (a stable sort, so the output is unchanged).\n`getIoSnapshotDeferredTaskIds` still takes the graph, because it walks\ndependencies and outputs.\n\nA new spec runs an agent-shaped task (`hash: null`, `hashDetails: null`)\nthrough `applyIoSnapshotOutputs` against the real native binding. It\nfails on master with the error above.\n\nVerified: full `packages/nx` vitest suite (8287 passed), `test-native`\n(904 passed), `lint-native`, `check-native-wasm`, lib typecheck.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFound while migrating nrwl repos to 23.3.0-beta.6 (e.g. #37202).\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Migrate-to-nx-23.3.0-beta.6-with-ultracache-and-task-based-affected-f4012f97\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"03e02c8d2a04da8bf961f876a0fc42e8b2fb23b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/03e02c8d2a04da8bf961f876a0fc42e8b2fb23b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de","verification":{"payload":"tree 03e02c8d2a04da8bf961f876a0fc42e8b2fb23b0\nparent 473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790613214 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790613214 +0000\n\nfix(core): pass only ultracache config to the snapshot eligibility walk (#37212)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nOn Nx Cloud agents with I/O snapshots on, every task crashes the agent\nworker:\n\n```\nNX   V4 worker encountered a fatal error\nFailed to convert JavaScript value `Null` into rust type `String` on Task.hash on TaskGraph.tasks\n    at applyIoSnapshotOutputs (nx/dist/src/io-snapshots/outputs.js:22:64)\n    at createOrchestrator (nx/dist/src/tasks-runner/init-tasks-runner.js:44:46)\n    at runDiscreteTasks (...)\n```\n\nThe Cloud agent clears an assigned task''s `hash` to `null` so nx\nrehashes it on the agent (it has done this since 2025). #37036 added\n`applyIoSnapshotOutputs(projectGraph, taskGraph, …)` in\n`createOrchestrator`, and `taskGraph` there holds that nulled task.\n`getObservedIoSnapshotOutputs` takes a whole `TaskGraph`, so napi\ndecodes every field of every task. napi maps only `undefined` to `None`\nfor optional `#[napi(object)]` fields, so `null` goes to the `String`\ndecoder and throws.\n\nThe eligibility walk never reads `hash`. From each task it reads only\nthe id and the `ultracache` config.\n\nThis breaks CI for nrwl/nx and nrwl/ocean on 23.3.0-beta.6.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`getObservedIoSnapshotOutputs` and `getIoSnapshotReport` take\n`Record<taskId, TaskUltracacheConfiguration | null>` instead of a\n`TaskGraph`. JS builds the map with `getUltraCacheConfig(taskGraph)`, so\nno other task field crosses into Rust. Map values go through napi''s\n`Option` decoder, which accepts `null`. The helper sends `null`, not\n`undefined`, for a task with no config, because napi''s map decoder drops\n`undefined` keys.\n\nInside Rust, `resolve` takes an iterator of `(task id, ultracache\nconfig)` pairs. The two napi functions pass their map''s entries, and the\nhash planner passes references into its own graph for the tasks it\nplans, so nothing is cloned. `resolve_scoped` is folded into `resolve`,\nso there is still one eligibility walk. The walk no longer sorts task\nids: only the report needs ordered diagnostics, so `report()` sorts them\nby task id (a stable sort, so the output is unchanged).\n`getIoSnapshotDeferredTaskIds` still takes the graph, because it walks\ndependencies and outputs.\n\nA new spec runs an agent-shaped task (`hash: null`, `hashDetails: null`)\nthrough `applyIoSnapshotOutputs` against the real native binding. It\nfails on master with the error above.\n\nVerified: full `packages/nx` vitest suite (8287 passed), `test-native`\n(904 passed), `lint-native`, `check-native-wasm`, lib typecheck.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nFound while migrating nrwl repos to 23.3.0-beta.6 (e.g. #37202).\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Migrate-to-nx-23.3.0-beta.6-with-ultracache-and-task-based-affected-f4012f97\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqupbeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUhsQAIbj8VDKbQk64iUXmWhO8iOO\njX4kNbTGZKcxCtagbLE3yjpA6dHj4zQI3IH0lmQOmU+wPfRQqnykNZF/0VI+BDi3\n+US9OoXaQkU42Qg/mDHl1FhFOqzmAFQYzjekSthD0Tp0nk3TXJonoAqCdXmVOC55\nDKdzp4ydSmEua78k7ZUgyh8ghA8s6/aF3Cd+W6ZrI2lhuE5mo9nzwtbrncY+ZZqG\ntUhHdx3Cl9z5egTNtU+48dbnftDAhZWIt9tKKNtLtacGostpYkycz53i6HfsbpWs\nC8VJST285CP4Jq/G2OtgUTYD51KZRHAPf69ZDkjs6Wn7nBJmTLkaiEVpmzoPnSqd\n7/vCe64xQmWTjWH3vfWcmwyT1KpIjcXRe3eHS/V+g4WWiknMaUyv2Yh00bNABDzs\n7RP+eD2/rNjMTjqq2Vum0/gAwMNzHIDVbv1Quu8Jk0E957qQOULzXmLg+jJbINdX\nUnGthd0QV7iTe0h/4mCjZfkUXiFXm0GAM5ngGN2VpA22Q0R8FLaexOyj7g4h+NUJ\nEgDQCehCSqOnIXUSdmoN9QnJdq49Rfvg5c+a1TWPSjvdvjnJcPpU3WMhZQpYxIJ5\nB++5AeNuAOGMeYYbvYjk8aHEcSHjG2EQzA9/4r9YSORP0XHQC56cR9j08wtLaj+/\njkuBJ+qtYRAW9o9Sx27o\n=RNxf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T16:33:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDIxMDY5ZjExZWFkNjk1YmQ1MTM1NmZkNzAxMGYzMmYzNTA2NmM2ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f","sha":"473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f"}],"sha":"21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/21069f11ead695bd51356fd7010f32f35066c6de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T15:22:18Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T15:22:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): prevent stale lockfile caches from breaking the project graph (#37210)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe project graph can fail with `Target project does not exist:\nnpm:<package>@<version>` when a package install overlaps a graph\ncomputation. It is a race, so it rarely triggers. Once it does, every\nlater build fails until the lockfile changes or someone runs `nx reset`.\n\nIn CI it showed up as an intermittent e2e failure after a generator''s\ninstall. It was reported after the move to pnpm 12, but a pnpm 11 run\nbefore the upgrade failed the same way. Logs show one hit in 96 nightly\ne2e runs.\n\nFor pnpm, a package''s node is `npm:<package>` when that version sits at\nthe root of `node_modules`, and `npm:<package>@<version>` otherwise. The\nplugin keyed its lockfile dependencies cache on the lockfile alone. A\ncomputation that overlapped an install could cache dependencies built\nfor old names, which later builds reused.\n\nThe cache had two more races:\n\n- The key and the data lived in separate files, so concurrent runs could\npair one run''s key with another''s data. A reader could crash on a\nhalf-written file.\n- The plugin read the lockfile once per step. An install that added a\npackage in between failed the graph with `TypeError: Cannot read\nproperties of undefined (reading ''forEach'')`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe graph builds when an install lands during or between graph\ncomputations. The plugin reuses cached dependencies only when the\nlockfile and the external node names both match. A half-written cache\nfile counts as a cache miss. Dependencies come from the same lockfile\nread as the external nodes.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5053\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The dependencies cache key adds the external node names to the\nlockfile hash. Hashing the names costs about 2 ms at 5k nodes and 10 ms\nat 50k.\n- Each cache file stores its key next to its data, so both come from one\nread. Checking the key parses the whole cache file, about 5 ms for this\nrepo''s 2 MB files.\n- The cache files have new names. Older Nx versions keep reading their\nown files, so a downgrade never parses the new format. Old files stay in\n`.nx/workspace-data` until `nx reset`.\n- The plugin keeps the lockfile it read in memory between the two steps,\n2.3 MB for this repo. Both parsers follow that file''s name, so Bun''s\nbinary and text lockfiles never swap parsers mid-computation.\n- The external nodes cache is still keyed by the lockfile alone, so node\nnames can lag behind a reinstall that leaves the lockfile unchanged.\nNodes and dependencies still agree, so the graph stays valid. Revisit if\nstale names show up in a reported graph or a pruned lockfile.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/nxc-5053-0362daab\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"75880269f42c84c1037663f5fdafebe4ef47113d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/75880269f42c84c1037663f5fdafebe4ef47113d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f","verification":{"payload":"tree 75880269f42c84c1037663f5fdafebe4ef47113d\nparent 116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1790608938 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790608938 +0000\n\nfix(core): prevent stale lockfile caches from breaking the project graph (#37210)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe project graph can fail with `Target project does not exist:\nnpm:<package>@<version>` when a package install overlaps a graph\ncomputation. It is a race, so it rarely triggers. Once it does, every\nlater build fails until the lockfile changes or someone runs `nx reset`.\n\nIn CI it showed up as an intermittent e2e failure after a generator''s\ninstall. It was reported after the move to pnpm 12, but a pnpm 11 run\nbefore the upgrade failed the same way. Logs show one hit in 96 nightly\ne2e runs.\n\nFor pnpm, a package''s node is `npm:<package>` when that version sits at\nthe root of `node_modules`, and `npm:<package>@<version>` otherwise. The\nplugin keyed its lockfile dependencies cache on the lockfile alone. A\ncomputation that overlapped an install could cache dependencies built\nfor old names, which later builds reused.\n\nThe cache had two more races:\n\n- The key and the data lived in separate files, so concurrent runs could\npair one run''s key with another''s data. A reader could crash on a\nhalf-written file.\n- The plugin read the lockfile once per step. An install that added a\npackage in between failed the graph with `TypeError: Cannot read\nproperties of undefined (reading ''forEach'')`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe graph builds when an install lands during or between graph\ncomputations. The plugin reuses cached dependencies only when the\nlockfile and the external node names both match. A half-written cache\nfile counts as a cache miss. Dependencies come from the same lockfile\nread as the external nodes.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5053\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- The dependencies cache key adds the external node names to the\nlockfile hash. Hashing the names costs about 2 ms at 5k nodes and 10 ms\nat 50k.\n- Each cache file stores its key next to its data, so both come from one\nread. Checking the key parses the whole cache file, about 5 ms for this\nrepo''s 2 MB files.\n- The cache files have new names. Older Nx versions keep reading their\nown files, so a downgrade never parses the new format. Old files stay in\n`.nx/workspace-data` until `nx reset`.\n- The plugin keeps the lockfile it read in memory between the two steps,\n2.3 MB for this repo. Both parsers follow that file''s name, so Bun''s\nbinary and text lockfiles never swap parsers mid-computation.\n- The external nodes cache is still keyed by the lockfile alone, so node\nnames can lag behind a reinstall that leaves the lockfile unchanged.\nNodes and dependencies still agree, so the graph stays valid. Revisit if\nstale names show up in a reported graph or a pruned lockfile.\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/nxc-5053-0362daab\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquoYqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgawQAHdRlOeuOk5zKg4hYBr7fKSa\n1r4K+3pqH7JLbL7mViXJVcFBlp/dTjgqsu/m6g+S+ZKL1V4CxgIxkTlfaXQs9i19\njOItEIbUciK7xAuH4RWvAjjS/xUIEF0fcuoAxIGnVGekj6/PsbID5gRsV50sOEiv\nwUKyIoXFFuC4e9cPeikcgqzSwRhkD2jR9WJrXSJrXPrp9mnwG5MxtQwlOomv+NGm\niZPthFRSFHJGCepGAJ17y6NdGmWMjKhVYE8inOQawyO0wxKZ/dUnZ4Jv7sVL1lmn\nR+/lmWKRCABB6PaARKuE/daTREVzDtIkSgVGV33MKnJ8DP90ntssTfaOctvP/tzO\nsh19ELboKjI/AAPonMzJ1VCMRaboLOTJp/lyjO7YRuRELgg+BWiHRUEXxuSVdfxP\nVOR1ukGulZZ3Etj5I8vCDU8EprI0dbx5sBCdTcvq1I9iOysio2eQjWwjzVv4DXQ3\n/VPHp0R3jLx0IGxq2LoESeho+NeWRT/YO4q1hWAEIigmcRQiHhBpPFXAOyRFrnS/\nwjKdiJyJBy+AU2KV70KJ92Ug5il/EpfwxjBhNWkCyC8wR662c4vtIWhBlMycZ62H\nU4qZpE4nmpWRK6d9PIxlfIPtAYEtkGR6XnKLNjJ9K3vVLmMsTlshy2Pw7yNud+bY\nGWc1y0OFOW5Kea2wnS2v\n=EdXI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T15:22:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDQ3MzU1MmMyMjhhM2FhOTU4M2U1YWIyY2VhZTRjNTM4OWE2Mzg5MGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c","sha":"116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c"}],"sha":"473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/473552c228a3aa9583e5ab2ceae4c5389a63890f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89645338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/simpleqt","id":89645338,"login":"simpleqt","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5NjQ1MzM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpleqt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:41:23Z","email":"89645338+simpleqt@users.noreply.github.com","name":"陈志谦"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T14:41:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): pin lock-threads to v6.0.2 to fix token validation failure (#37163)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe scheduled Lock Threads workflow fails on every run — most recently\n[run 35937513465](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/35937513465)\n(2026-09-24), and on each preceding scheduled execution.\n\nThe failure comes from inside the action:\n\n```\n##[error]\"github-token\" length must be less than or equal to 100 characters long\n```\n\nThe pinned revision (pre-v6.0.0 commit 6548363) still carries the\nupstream `github-token` validation schema that caps the input at 100\ncharacters. The automatically-injected `GITHUB_TOKEN` now exceeds that\nlength, so the action rejects its default input before locking anything\n— closed threads have stopped being locked.\n\nUpstream fixed the validation schema in\n[v6.0.2](https://github.com/dessant/lock-threads/releases/tag/v6.0.2)\n(\"update github-token validation schema\", closes\n[dessant/lock-threads#55](https://github.com/dessant/lock-threads/issues/55)).\n\n## Fix\n\nRe-pin the action to the v6.0.2 release commit (`89ae32b0`). None of the\ninputs used in this workflow changed between the pinned revision and\nv6.0.2, so lock behaviour stays identical once the workflow can run\nagain.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: 金豆 <jindou@jindoudeMacBook-Air.local>","tree":{"sha":"33099ef72a9e631cce507ed3085227c673dfc41b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/33099ef72a9e631cce507ed3085227c673dfc41b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c","verification":{"payload":"tree 33099ef72a9e631cce507ed3085227c673dfc41b\nparent b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d\nauthor 陈志谦 <89645338+simpleqt@users.noreply.github.com> 1790606483 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790606483 -0400\n\nchore(repo): pin lock-threads to v6.0.2 to fix token validation failure (#37163)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe scheduled Lock Threads workflow fails on every run — most recently\n[run 35937513465](https://github.com/nrwl/nx/actions/runs/35937513465)\n(2026-09-24), and on each preceding scheduled execution.\n\nThe failure comes from inside the action:\n\n```\n##[error]\"github-token\" length must be less than or equal to 100 characters long\n```\n\nThe pinned revision (pre-v6.0.0 commit 6548363) still carries the\nupstream `github-token` validation schema that caps the input at 100\ncharacters. The automatically-injected `GITHUB_TOKEN` now exceeds that\nlength, so the action rejects its default input before locking anything\n— closed threads have stopped being locked.\n\nUpstream fixed the validation schema in\n[v6.0.2](https://github.com/dessant/lock-threads/releases/tag/v6.0.2)\n(\"update github-token validation schema\", closes\n[dessant/lock-threads#55](https://github.com/dessant/lock-threads/issues/55)).\n\n## Fix\n\nRe-pin the action to the v6.0.2 release commit (`89ae32b0`). None of the\ninputs used in this workflow changed between the pinned revision and\nv6.0.2, so lock behaviour stays identical once the workflow can run\nagain.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: 金豆 <jindou@jindoudeMacBook-Air.local>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqunyTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxjoQACORY9m8aznVK7AxWobMmNk9\nCfsuSHzu9o38fxBp2s77w2551bPncxAAq3rFILOFVnsm5tSEp2OSnhUVoAi5RJT9\nnkc3TLei/1K54mRrSmoGPiPa3lR6oXEATzU/AcokW0R5s4xLBAVrZFc3aDamVl5C\n7Tg9pyY7yB5S8Llhy2XAmlSUy9nHl77AOSIfgBHpaaVDIHG6Uq1ZxOrTBtZZvm4t\n1+HzII294H58u9RbDgejammNzZ3GkuBE1UemTCT4utNsWAPwAChFQye924XtPHFn\nh+nnG/ako+/CO0GxMTyANbDupmCjcjD0FgD+xLJgNr6UDMbwj56GLpNL7EaRd/4R\nnjmkSlI0/xLDP/uCzgsWdrHI1qblKmNArdUcY9wSv2o2YjmlJ6d4U8fIV7nbwCsW\nH1G3ZFkgqi+lnbTPRSwrcogF1uSLoQ7zVKc3MED0Mhyt6aS/dOlvO5XyWa6Jh2Oy\n87hTBpAmAlFwMLXKhv2YSfGq1YWao/aJAaD8tmqhr8uy8MjPc6OZROmK+aYVbKZW\no8ULWLuEskSnonyoRmS521vhcDKa0d95IMgyv7P5PmR0yAdsr3is+/4t4w22ArMY\nkr3vDbtcf61y278cppS68g+MyynnclaZmxvhRowvtJaMKQ6MQTHdsdRZ63SinisU\njJydjfVG6u4m+BScooqp\n=SwBN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T14:41:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDExNmJlZTkxMjMyMzc0ZmY0ZjljYzk5YTgzMDllMzJkNDFiYzU3M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d","sha":"b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d"}],"sha":"116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/116bee91232374ff4f9cc99a8309e32d41bc573c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:12Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(detox): run detox unit tests with vitest (#37189)\n\nStacked on #37188.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/detox` unit tests run on Jest through `jest.preset.js`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`@nx/detox` unit tests run on Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from\n`packages/detox/vitest.config.mts`. The config reuses the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`;\nnothing shared changed. `jest.config.cts` is removed (its only extra was\n`verbose: true`, a reporter preference, not reproduced).\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 88 (12 files) | 88 (12 files) |\n| `nx test detox` wall (median of 3) | 17.49s | 3.81s |\n| Runner-reported time (median of 3) | 16.07s | 2.74s |\n\nTiming method: 3 rounds alternating Jest (detached checkout of the base\nbranch) and Vitest (this branch), `nx test detox --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on and warmed by two `nx show\nprojects` runs after each checkout. 1-minute load during the rounds:\n12.78 / 11.91, 9.32 / 8.52, 7.49 / 7.05 (jest / vitest).\n\nRaw: jest 17.54s / 17.49s / 17.17s wall (16.37s / 16.07s / 16.07s\nrunner); vitest 3.86s / 3.81s / 3.75s wall (2.81s / 2.74s / 2.67s\nrunner).\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- `convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`: the `nx/src/devkit-internals` mock\nreturned a `Proxy` that called `jest.requireActual` lazily. The codemod\nonly converts factory-level `requireActual`, so the lazy calls were left\nreferencing `jest`. The factory is now `async` and loads both actual\nmodules with `vi.importActual`, the same shape `packages/react-native`''s\nconvert-to-inferred spec uses.\n\nDetox generates Jest-based e2e projects, so the application/create-files\nspecs and `create-files.ts` assert on `jest.config.*` text; those\nstrings were left untouched (the codemod only ran on\n`convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`).\n\n### Snapshots\n\nNo `.snap` files, and no inline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,copy-assets,build-base -p detox\njest --skip-nx-cache` green (`jest` is the still-on-Jest canary)\n- `nx sync:check` clean\n- two repeat `nx test detox --skip-nx-cache` runs green at 88/88; a\nsingle-file run works\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"cb52dfd912f9eeeba5f26f802296b4e53a6c4b88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/cb52dfd912f9eeeba5f26f802296b4e53a6c4b88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d","verification":{"payload":"tree cb52dfd912f9eeeba5f26f802296b4e53a6c4b88\nparent 54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438952 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438952 -0400\n\nchore(detox): run detox unit tests with vitest (#37189)\n\nStacked on #37188.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/detox` unit tests run on Jest through `jest.preset.js`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`@nx/detox` unit tests run on Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from\n`packages/detox/vitest.config.mts`. The config reuses the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`;\nnothing shared changed. `jest.config.cts` is removed (its only extra was\n`verbose: true`, a reporter preference, not reproduced).\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 88 (12 files) | 88 (12 files) |\n| `nx test detox` wall (median of 3) | 17.49s | 3.81s |\n| Runner-reported time (median of 3) | 16.07s | 2.74s |\n\nTiming method: 3 rounds alternating Jest (detached checkout of the base\nbranch) and Vitest (this branch), `nx test detox --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on and warmed by two `nx show\nprojects` runs after each checkout. 1-minute load during the rounds:\n12.78 / 11.91, 9.32 / 8.52, 7.49 / 7.05 (jest / vitest).\n\nRaw: jest 17.54s / 17.49s / 17.17s wall (16.37s / 16.07s / 16.07s\nrunner); vitest 3.86s / 3.81s / 3.75s wall (2.81s / 2.74s / 2.67s\nrunner).\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- `convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`: the `nx/src/devkit-internals` mock\nreturned a `Proxy` that called `jest.requireActual` lazily. The codemod\nonly converts factory-level `requireActual`, so the lazy calls were left\nreferencing `jest`. The factory is now `async` and loads both actual\nmodules with `vi.importActual`, the same shape `packages/react-native`''s\nconvert-to-inferred spec uses.\n\nDetox generates Jest-based e2e projects, so the application/create-files\nspecs and `create-files.ts` assert on `jest.config.*` text; those\nstrings were left untouched (the codemod only ran on\n`convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`).\n\n### Snapshots\n\nNo `.snap` files, and no inline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,copy-assets,build-base -p detox\njest --skip-nx-cache` green (`jest` is the still-on-Jest canary)\n- `nx sync:check` clean\n- two repeat `nx test detox --skip-nx-cache` runs green at 88/88; a\nsingle-file run works\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+pMQAK1NeutJ6IgfBUuJ8DUCVi00\noDQMyKNU5MNAIJ5Z0pMk319+0OYeRx/JfN6amdTcGfaTst0J+kDVLrHfHLndNnBz\n5ThnDykVhOXtdL4cj6gRjmmHjFvUQ+7KtmCJ9+REpxULF3tV4MgI+HfJPQ6jD2Ag\nvARkvF49AMaBYWGVuwqg1zSbLn1/Y15OZxnw1VFHezeoIggfT6H6mZ54Ac4nBUi0\n4QpAPV4RAw5wq0ltzK21nXzbYkDpx/Ntryr1qKBtw1hwYmkUIL4ulatx4A0z0Eii\nYy9T+IknWz4YXTLDnPa9uPfwOpwIzTvOWHjQ66x3QlRSLwaaIkyMH1s8KC4v81fr\njxO9a+XjkFts4GeERys3NLMeG/QM1gQ0cSDZLW5Fzv7/e/KtBHSHssFdd3vwI4Cw\nJ4h7yyjcQ48AmCcaelAwxXySbXGcay4P035gs6FNyVuUg8w769qURgdInUYi5OFu\nhl5ogDkunfwfM4kciY6VuRo4FFMvSRDulKLgOFIyRj/r3rtPNpaa/+KtZ1ZwDvRH\n9U7LIQOfgagWSj3ZcJHUMSBleY+Aa2clLJ3BaU5vsO+vBXdfSOLtcyNXX4YQ3i16\nt3iVwygKh/ezTbkYvDHVOh1cKWxJXdYFPftGMiga6HozMOlYl2pVQvzSgmoL0ir9\nJnSiULTq1cQ/4gRI/foI\n=NXvb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGI5NGJlZGVlZDQ1NDU3N2VkMzExNTQzZDMyMzk1Y2M0MTcwNTZkNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6","sha":"54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6"}],"sha":"b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b94bedeed454577ed311543d32395cc417056d6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): run node, express, docker and nest unit tests with vitest (#37188)\n\nStacked on #37187.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/node`, `@nx/express`, `@nx/docker` and `@nx/nest` run their unit\ntests with Jest through `jest.preset.js`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAll four run on Vitest 4, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from a\n`vitest.config.mts` in each package. They reuse the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`\nunchanged, and each `project.json` declares those shared files as `test`\ninputs.\n\n| Package | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall (jest → vitest) |\nRunner time (jest → vitest) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| node | 137 → 137 | 95.9s → 5.6s | 94.8s → 4.2s |\n| express | 15 → 15 | 8.6s → 2.9s | 7.6s → 2.0s |\n| docker | 139 → 139 | 5.1s → 2.4s | 4.1s → 1.5s |\n| nest | 98 + 1 skipped → 98 + 1 skipped | 66.6s → 6.2s | 65.5s → 5.3s |\n\nTiming method: medians of 3 alternating rounds of `nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on. Jest ran\non a detached checkout of the base branch, Vitest on this branch, and\nthe daemon was warmed after each checkout. Load average stayed between 3\nand 8 for the whole run.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **node, nest: spying on `require(''@nx/devkit'')` never intercepted.**\nThe generators import `formatFiles` through ESM, so the `--skipFormat`\nspecs now spy on `import * as devkit from ''@nx/devkit''`. That covers 1\nspec in node and 4 in nest.\n- **node `create-targets.spec.ts`: `jest.requireMock`.** The\n`stringifyPnpmLockfile` spy is created with `vi.hoisted` and shared with\nthe `pnpm-parser` mock factory. A direct import of\n`nx/src/plugins/js/...` would fail `oxlint`''s restricted-import rule.\n- **docker `release-publish.impl.spec.ts`:** `mockImplementation()` with\nno argument becomes an explicit `() => {}` no-op.\n- **nest `resource.spec.ts`:** `xdescribe` is not defined in Vitest, so\nit becomes `describe.skip`. The suite is still skipped, same as on Jest.\n- **nest `test-setup.ts` deleted, not ported.** Its only job was to mock\n`createProjectGraphAsync` on `nx/src/project-graph/project-graph` with\nan empty graph. The shared setup already does the same thing on both the\nESM and the CJS channels.\n\n`@nx/docker` release specs set `NX_DRY_RUN=true`, so no spec runs the\n`docker` CLI.\n\n### Snapshots\n\nThe `.snap` files for node (5 keys) and nest (10 keys) were regenerated\nfrom pristine copies. A parsed key/value diff, with the ` > ` separator\nnormalized, shows 0 value differences. Only the key separator changed.\nNo inline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p node express docker nest\njest --skip-nx-cache` passes. `jest` is the still-on-Jest canary (437\ntests).\n- `nx sync:check` passes.\n- Two more runs of each suite were green with the same counts.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"44efa129b537536f2bcb65cc74433152f5ee61cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/44efa129b537536f2bcb65cc74433152f5ee61cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6","verification":{"payload":"tree 44efa129b537536f2bcb65cc74433152f5ee61cc\nparent 1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438951 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438951 -0400\n\nchore(repo): run node, express, docker and nest unit tests with vitest (#37188)\n\nStacked on #37187.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/node`, `@nx/express`, `@nx/docker` and `@nx/nest` run their unit\ntests with Jest through `jest.preset.js`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAll four run on Vitest 4, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from a\n`vitest.config.mts` in each package. They reuse the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`\nunchanged, and each `project.json` declares those shared files as `test`\ninputs.\n\n| Package | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall (jest → vitest) |\nRunner time (jest → vitest) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| node | 137 → 137 | 95.9s → 5.6s | 94.8s → 4.2s |\n| express | 15 → 15 | 8.6s → 2.9s | 7.6s → 2.0s |\n| docker | 139 → 139 | 5.1s → 2.4s | 4.1s → 1.5s |\n| nest | 98 + 1 skipped → 98 + 1 skipped | 66.6s → 6.2s | 65.5s → 5.3s |\n\nTiming method: medians of 3 alternating rounds of `nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on. Jest ran\non a detached checkout of the base branch, Vitest on this branch, and\nthe daemon was warmed after each checkout. Load average stayed between 3\nand 8 for the whole run.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **node, nest: spying on `require(''@nx/devkit'')` never intercepted.**\nThe generators import `formatFiles` through ESM, so the `--skipFormat`\nspecs now spy on `import * as devkit from ''@nx/devkit''`. That covers 1\nspec in node and 4 in nest.\n- **node `create-targets.spec.ts`: `jest.requireMock`.** The\n`stringifyPnpmLockfile` spy is created with `vi.hoisted` and shared with\nthe `pnpm-parser` mock factory. A direct import of\n`nx/src/plugins/js/...` would fail `oxlint`''s restricted-import rule.\n- **docker `release-publish.impl.spec.ts`:** `mockImplementation()` with\nno argument becomes an explicit `() => {}` no-op.\n- **nest `resource.spec.ts`:** `xdescribe` is not defined in Vitest, so\nit becomes `describe.skip`. The suite is still skipped, same as on Jest.\n- **nest `test-setup.ts` deleted, not ported.** Its only job was to mock\n`createProjectGraphAsync` on `nx/src/project-graph/project-graph` with\nan empty graph. The shared setup already does the same thing on both the\nESM and the CJS channels.\n\n`@nx/docker` release specs set `NX_DRY_RUN=true`, so no spec runs the\n`docker` CLI.\n\n### Snapshots\n\nThe `.snap` files for node (5 keys) and nest (10 keys) were regenerated\nfrom pristine copies. A parsed key/value diff, with the ` > ` separator\nnormalized, shows 0 value differences. Only the key separator changed.\nNo inline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p node express docker nest\njest --skip-nx-cache` passes. `jest` is the still-on-Jest canary (437\ntests).\n- `nx sync:check` passes.\n- Two more runs of each suite were green with the same counts.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2mIQAHXr12udxc171VGtpilNNUtq\n1Gc9lN6sGc1Ms8G1aBmcBGuiyq1o1942glRl7ORIqT15MYNBb/EI5jgXhpwuSIvs\n9tjUGzYmco3kihqwEgTc6AtE6Du+wWILnDT3b8BZLX6TYqs4DGRK75l5EFgXZa8G\nW05s1PHM5g6GndSyQjWT46OZ9apJp/O4DO6ueLArXJMyQEU5Q6hHyVZPXZh69QnR\nhzjzbhngshDOwHiT3MBWbd9dsvmnaWnflk1Kb3UhQ+qC2jXLnxSq2sFOCSsqM6uL\nHWNvp1JsiL3ZYBTdnYi+Mu/PJk0fi6XQeRFEQAm1PraSKuoE4zgU10uXXxdgEI/E\nMrrucMSasqLC7o/NtLmmJGLCNKWcUgv4aND2EMUXy9Gnsqj8Ub/LFVF2hP31OZI3\nBIzw2vN2xSTWG5mgxeToRgoubglQULy4IoVk2Q6IYzh2ccy7orY8ILkCqGlCvc3p\n8oaCob2Hw3qX9L69yVMGATMxGBNh5zCM7BtD5m4VxLod5aLOi2yROAL5ftOI5nu1\nYWuFhKSL8Leu1VDnDGmZQZ70tpgRJAZgZ6w2DBMI6Nr2NVonJt1R7pZ85/FHFM8+\nYb0mxT+ZiC43N78d+u4EBM2CyRwV8EoeRqlTiZGHBz2mQGHkMG2NidSppE4NhiVx\nbU4o+gtrDqDBHMmvJhWC\n=04T4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDU0YzdhNjRhMzhhNTc1ZjdjNzBiNzc2N2JmYjZmMTdiMjkzYzY3YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026","sha":"1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026"}],"sha":"54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/54c7a64a38a575f7c70b7767bfb6f17b293c67b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): run create-nx-workspace and create-nx-plugin unit tests with vitest (#37187)\n\nStacked on #37186.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`create-nx-workspace` and `create-nx-plugin` run their unit tests with\nJest through `jest.preset.js`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run on Vitest through the inferred `@nx/vitest` target.\nThey reuse the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`. `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is\nunchanged.\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| create-nx-workspace tests | 175 (13 files, 20 inline snapshots) | 175\n(13 files, 20 inline snapshots) |\n| create-nx-workspace `nx test` wall, median of 3 | 1.74s | 1.80s |\n| create-nx-workspace runner time, median of 3 | 0.76s | 0.69s |\n| create-nx-plugin | 0 specs, passes with `--passWithNoTests` | 0 specs,\npasses with `--passWithNoTests` |\n| create-nx-plugin `nx test` wall, median of 3 | 0.96s | 0.92s |\n\nHow I timed it: 3 rounds, alternating Jest (a detached checkout of the\nbase branch) and Vitest (this branch). Each run used `nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on and warmed\nfirst. Load average was about 9.5 in round 1 and 15 to 17 in rounds 2\nand 3. The suite is tiny, so this is parity rather than a speedup. The\nnumbers only show the switch does not slow it down.\n\n### create-nx-plugin\n\nThe package has a `jest.config.cts` but no spec files. It keeps a test\ntarget through a `vitest.config.mts`. It does not lose the target. Here\nis why:\n\n- Under Jest, the inferred target existed and passed with \"No tests\nfound\". This was because `nx.json` gives the `@nx/jest/plugin` targets\n`--passWithNoTests`.\n- `nx.json` gives the `@nx/vitest` targets the same `--passWithNoTests`\narg, so the inferred target still passes. Without the flag, `vitest run`\nexits 1 with \"No test files found\". I checked this.\n- If the target were removed, a spec added later would never run in CI,\nand nothing would warn about it. With the config in place, a new spec\ngets the shared setup and runs.\n- Nothing refers to `create-nx-plugin:test`. I checked `.github`,\n`nx.json` and the other configs. `nx show project create-nx-plugin`\nlists the same targets before and after. Only the runner changes, from\njest to vitest.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **yargs alias** in `vitest.config.mts`. `bin/create-nx-workspace.ts`\ncalls `yargs.terminalWidth()` through a namespace import. The yargs ESM\nentry only exposes `default`, so the alias pins `yargs` to `index.cjs`.\n`packages/nx` does the same.\n- **Import mocked modules instead of `require()`-ing them**\n(`prompts.spec.ts`, `bin/create-nx-workspace.spec.ts`). The specs pulled\n`isCI`, `isAiAgent` and `output` out of `require(...)` to change the\nmock''s return values. In Vitest, `require` goes through the CJS channel,\nwhich `vi.mock` does not touch. So it returned the real modules and\n`.mockReturnValue` was undefined. Importing the bindings gets the mocked\nones. Before this fix, the real `isAiAgent` read the caller''s agent env\nvars.\n- **`ab-testing.spec.ts`**: `jest.resetModules()` +\n`jest.requireActual`/`require` becomes `vi.resetModules()` + `await\nimport(''./ab-testing'')`. The module reads env vars at load time, so each\ntest needs a fresh copy.\n- **Jest-only globals**: `fail(...)` becomes `expect.unreachable(...)`.\n`test.each` `%p` becomes `%j`, because Vitest has no `%p`.\n\n### No installs, clones or network\n\nThe specs never install, clone or reach the network.\n`download-template.spec.ts` stubs `globalThis.fetch`. `git.spec.ts`\nspies on `execAndWait`. The `createWorkspace` spec fails before it\ndownloads anything. Both runners count 175 tests with the AI-agent\ndetection env vars removed and with `CI` set or unset. So the counts\ndon''t depend on the environment the suite runs in.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,build-base,copy-assets -p\ncreate-nx-workspace create-nx-plugin jest --skip-nx-cache` passes. The\n`jest` project is the still-on-Jest canary, with 437 tests.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean. Two more `--skip-nx-cache` runs passed. A\nsingle-file run works: `nx run create-nx-workspace:test --\nsrc/utils/unparse.spec.ts`.\n- The inline snapshots pass unchanged, and neither package has `.snap`\nfiles.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"48e5e95e33e9273e9300adc3c988bee45f066044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/48e5e95e33e9273e9300adc3c988bee45f066044"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026","verification":{"payload":"tree 48e5e95e33e9273e9300adc3c988bee45f066044\nparent b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438951 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438951 -0400\n\nchore(repo): run create-nx-workspace and create-nx-plugin unit tests with vitest (#37187)\n\nStacked on #37186.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`create-nx-workspace` and `create-nx-plugin` run their unit tests with\nJest through `jest.preset.js`.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run on Vitest through the inferred `@nx/vitest` target.\nThey reuse the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`. `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is\nunchanged.\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| create-nx-workspace tests | 175 (13 files, 20 inline snapshots) | 175\n(13 files, 20 inline snapshots) |\n| create-nx-workspace `nx test` wall, median of 3 | 1.74s | 1.80s |\n| create-nx-workspace runner time, median of 3 | 0.76s | 0.69s |\n| create-nx-plugin | 0 specs, passes with `--passWithNoTests` | 0 specs,\npasses with `--passWithNoTests` |\n| create-nx-plugin `nx test` wall, median of 3 | 0.96s | 0.92s |\n\nHow I timed it: 3 rounds, alternating Jest (a detached checkout of the\nbase branch) and Vitest (this branch). Each run used `nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on and warmed\nfirst. Load average was about 9.5 in round 1 and 15 to 17 in rounds 2\nand 3. The suite is tiny, so this is parity rather than a speedup. The\nnumbers only show the switch does not slow it down.\n\n### create-nx-plugin\n\nThe package has a `jest.config.cts` but no spec files. It keeps a test\ntarget through a `vitest.config.mts`. It does not lose the target. Here\nis why:\n\n- Under Jest, the inferred target existed and passed with \"No tests\nfound\". This was because `nx.json` gives the `@nx/jest/plugin` targets\n`--passWithNoTests`.\n- `nx.json` gives the `@nx/vitest` targets the same `--passWithNoTests`\narg, so the inferred target still passes. Without the flag, `vitest run`\nexits 1 with \"No test files found\". I checked this.\n- If the target were removed, a spec added later would never run in CI,\nand nothing would warn about it. With the config in place, a new spec\ngets the shared setup and runs.\n- Nothing refers to `create-nx-plugin:test`. I checked `.github`,\n`nx.json` and the other configs. `nx show project create-nx-plugin`\nlists the same targets before and after. Only the runner changes, from\njest to vitest.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **yargs alias** in `vitest.config.mts`. `bin/create-nx-workspace.ts`\ncalls `yargs.terminalWidth()` through a namespace import. The yargs ESM\nentry only exposes `default`, so the alias pins `yargs` to `index.cjs`.\n`packages/nx` does the same.\n- **Import mocked modules instead of `require()`-ing them**\n(`prompts.spec.ts`, `bin/create-nx-workspace.spec.ts`). The specs pulled\n`isCI`, `isAiAgent` and `output` out of `require(...)` to change the\nmock''s return values. In Vitest, `require` goes through the CJS channel,\nwhich `vi.mock` does not touch. So it returned the real modules and\n`.mockReturnValue` was undefined. Importing the bindings gets the mocked\nones. Before this fix, the real `isAiAgent` read the caller''s agent env\nvars.\n- **`ab-testing.spec.ts`**: `jest.resetModules()` +\n`jest.requireActual`/`require` becomes `vi.resetModules()` + `await\nimport(''./ab-testing'')`. The module reads env vars at load time, so each\ntest needs a fresh copy.\n- **Jest-only globals**: `fail(...)` becomes `expect.unreachable(...)`.\n`test.each` `%p` becomes `%j`, because Vitest has no `%p`.\n\n### No installs, clones or network\n\nThe specs never install, clone or reach the network.\n`download-template.spec.ts` stubs `globalThis.fetch`. `git.spec.ts`\nspies on `execAndWait`. The `createWorkspace` spec fails before it\ndownloads anything. Both runners count 175 tests with the AI-agent\ndetection env vars removed and with `CI` set or unset. So the counts\ndon''t depend on the environment the suite runs in.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,build-base,copy-assets -p\ncreate-nx-workspace create-nx-plugin jest --skip-nx-cache` passes. The\n`jest` project is the still-on-Jest canary, with 437 tests.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean. Two more `--skip-nx-cache` runs passed. A\nsingle-file run works: `nx run create-nx-workspace:test --\nsrc/utils/unparse.spec.ts`.\n- The inline snapshots pass unchanged, and neither package has `.snap`\nfiles.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWW0QAA/RaR5FTcMcVKqTb5R4mo+h\ncYcpF8lZI2xbrsUK1LLU31wK0H2Mpp2SEPspyl9KCC9T0gqI3cIgZSEihqL8h69w\nRpE2oqenA1Wq9kC6OqaRcGfEc1BayihnjWeCxgIkrZExuBYHuP/cgklmY7ALeCyt\nNHmZS05NJZ1kcKnGlgLTr7tSeRveDDh26TclSoHnrpAKkUKSJMR0+DDD/mrJduAT\niJyk+QlO9iWK4rCZ/1bEoc58TMjpiBcUrUgSqVurojM+WsC7HklEnauemhcseUM9\npGex0w8VMLttD+R2J20DEMuAMwqNk1VZ+CpJzji8eEyrIBGJPCCmNha6/1MTVmBr\nk0yv/3QP3xTwi4VZnYSNApIPukgXVjMdMlOSVlsGEeAi/PNsa1jifvgJJnjnbk48\nyAs5HY6ifDcDXyVE1dIKJlM8JT61T3771nILthzLsBYl+RCJGa64tFxCIk+UhMaT\nKpZu/IbosmebJHdnORyNjitBPPQKijsU/eC7o0uLEyLVY6ONijYai8vGsxjViQnk\nXfd1/HLl1lD758Te6swq/pwLSVQHv/oyUoboXewId6YFqck4iJJ2o23i5iQWBADn\nMEyYpoWtiopVYY8ByynAb/wVFwEGZZJioUtIk1YCyjQPFqF31cjf+oeYLDmY5d9n\nzlIqurKQv9oe2tKepzDO\n=/5gR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDFiYWNjOTMxY2Q1YjQyNTAxMzU4NjEzNWRiNjA2NmM3MGU2ZjcwMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d","sha":"b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d"}],"sha":"1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/1bacc931cd5b425013586135db6066c70e6f7026"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(module-federation): run module-federation unit tests with vitest (#37186)\n\nStacked on #37185.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/module-federation` unit tests run on Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`@nx/module-federation` unit tests run on Vitest 4 through the inferred\n`@nx/vitest` target, using the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts` (no shared-setup changes).\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 94 passed + 1 skipped (95) | 94 passed + 1 skipped (95) |\n| `nx test` wall time (median) | 3.11s | 3.20s |\n| Runner-reported time (median) | 2.02s | 1.99s |\n\nTiming: 3 alternating rounds (jest on a detached checkout of the base\nbranch, vitest on this branch), daemon warmed with two `nx show\nprojects` after each checkout, one `nx test module-federation\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` each. Load average 7.5-10.\nRaw wall: jest 3.29 / 3.10 / 3.11s, vitest 3.07 / 3.30 / 3.20s. The\nsuite is small (13 files, ~0.3s of test time), so the two runners are at\nparity.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **`fs` mocks** (`get-dynamic-manifest-file`, `share`, `typescript`\nspecs): the factories called `jest.requireActual(''fs'')` inside `vi.fn`s;\nthey now read the actual module once in an async factory. The specs\ngrabbed `fs` / `@nx/devkit` with `require()`, which returns the real CJS\nmodule rather than the `vi.mock`ed one, so they now use `import * as`.\n- **`get-remotes.spec.ts`**: `vi.spyOn` on the frozen `fs` namespace\nthrows, so `fs` is mocked in spy mode (`vi.mock(''fs'', { spy: true })`).\n- **`share.spec.ts`**: `vi.mock(''./typescript'', () =>\njest.requireActual(...))` became `vi.mock(''./typescript'', { spy: true\n})` so `vi.spyOn(tsUtils, ...)` works. `xit` became `it.skip`.\n- **`typescript.spec.ts`**: `readTsConfig` loads `typescript` with a\nlazy `require()`, which `vi.mock` cannot reach, so the fake is\nregistered with `mockCjsModule`.\n- **`share.spec.ts` workspace root**: jest''s root (`tmp/unit`) could\nresolve the repo''s `node_modules`. The shared setup''s per-worker temp\nroot cannot, so secondary entry points were never found. The spec now\npoints `@nx/devkit`''s `workspaceRoot` and `readModulePackageJson`''s\ndefault require paths at the repo root. The `fs` mock also reaches nx''s\n`node:fs` imports, so `readNxJson` sees `existsSync() === true`. The\nspec writes an empty `nx.json` into the worker''s temp root for the\nfile''s duration and removes it afterwards.\n- `rewrite-internal-subpath-imports.spec.ts` mentions `jest.mock(...)`\nonly inside strings (it tests a codemod), so it was left out of the\ncodemod.\n\nNo snapshot files; no inline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,build-base,copy-assets,lint,oxlint -p\nmodule-federation jest --skip-nx-cache` passes (`jest` is the\nstill-on-jest canary). The one lint warning is `jest/no-disabled-tests`\non the already-skipped test, which was an `xit` before.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two repeat `nx test module-federation --skip-nx-cache` runs are green,\nwith the same count.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"894e9d3435edf0c29a36e37540fe6fe4a8c75afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/894e9d3435edf0c29a36e37540fe6fe4a8c75afe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d","verification":{"payload":"tree 894e9d3435edf0c29a36e37540fe6fe4a8c75afe\nparent 49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438951 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438951 -0400\n\nchore(module-federation): run module-federation unit tests with vitest (#37186)\n\nStacked on #37185.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/module-federation` unit tests run on Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`@nx/module-federation` unit tests run on Vitest 4 through the inferred\n`@nx/vitest` target, using the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts` (no shared-setup changes).\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 94 passed + 1 skipped (95) | 94 passed + 1 skipped (95) |\n| `nx test` wall time (median) | 3.11s | 3.20s |\n| Runner-reported time (median) | 2.02s | 1.99s |\n\nTiming: 3 alternating rounds (jest on a detached checkout of the base\nbranch, vitest on this branch), daemon warmed with two `nx show\nprojects` after each checkout, one `nx test module-federation\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` each. Load average 7.5-10.\nRaw wall: jest 3.29 / 3.10 / 3.11s, vitest 3.07 / 3.30 / 3.20s. The\nsuite is small (13 files, ~0.3s of test time), so the two runners are at\nparity.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **`fs` mocks** (`get-dynamic-manifest-file`, `share`, `typescript`\nspecs): the factories called `jest.requireActual(''fs'')` inside `vi.fn`s;\nthey now read the actual module once in an async factory. The specs\ngrabbed `fs` / `@nx/devkit` with `require()`, which returns the real CJS\nmodule rather than the `vi.mock`ed one, so they now use `import * as`.\n- **`get-remotes.spec.ts`**: `vi.spyOn` on the frozen `fs` namespace\nthrows, so `fs` is mocked in spy mode (`vi.mock(''fs'', { spy: true })`).\n- **`share.spec.ts`**: `vi.mock(''./typescript'', () =>\njest.requireActual(...))` became `vi.mock(''./typescript'', { spy: true\n})` so `vi.spyOn(tsUtils, ...)` works. `xit` became `it.skip`.\n- **`typescript.spec.ts`**: `readTsConfig` loads `typescript` with a\nlazy `require()`, which `vi.mock` cannot reach, so the fake is\nregistered with `mockCjsModule`.\n- **`share.spec.ts` workspace root**: jest''s root (`tmp/unit`) could\nresolve the repo''s `node_modules`. The shared setup''s per-worker temp\nroot cannot, so secondary entry points were never found. The spec now\npoints `@nx/devkit`''s `workspaceRoot` and `readModulePackageJson`''s\ndefault require paths at the repo root. The `fs` mock also reaches nx''s\n`node:fs` imports, so `readNxJson` sees `existsSync() === true`. The\nspec writes an empty `nx.json` into the worker''s temp root for the\nfile''s duration and removes it afterwards.\n- `rewrite-internal-subpath-imports.spec.ts` mentions `jest.mock(...)`\nonly inside strings (it tests a codemod), so it was left out of the\ncodemod.\n\nNo snapshot files; no inline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,build-base,copy-assets,lint,oxlint -p\nmodule-federation jest --skip-nx-cache` passes (`jest` is the\nstill-on-jest canary). The one lint warning is `jest/no-disabled-tests`\non the already-skipped test, which was an `xit` before.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two repeat `nx test module-federation --skip-nx-cache` runs are green,\nwith the same count.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWoAQAJeBslrtm5dyOECzLpo37+rQ\n3qjwhOZP8sfHd7mFn+NaLI+dPo4lND6E/x5ogycO8rS2GQF78/3DLu7eQG6AXigq\nWBbKgAyAGBevH4BchOAIJ5PU8Gr2KKwt7QhfFqMdRUGniBbGM9ZxHl8amV/Rx2oz\n+R32QFI6m+zsXNQ5milVdazPAAbBKbDqHWJK53TkPlqqiNGO2l8xo440ju5bDCzy\n8ax/Jo5d7go680dqvWXRSPaGHZ3AzdWOC+rpv4ZcfiK152xJzIT3rBB5pT9Ed7p0\nnNz6a8f5+9yBXUszvc05xG1DWgGqkyhBfVkDQaWp1Y/IyI113g2RqY2kg/hxo4at\nkTnSjJDGdq2dlqXssRTWL3LfRgLLzStfmziUWG3ca1RG9wqAhtFKXrJNGNKm0xvg\ncBcBAVFNriPcOOl8P9jsAwHhrXce4vYxc6wFhN9gAiEOeVlIrRFNeTIepndF2y2V\nEfKd2DuhoCtOct2Ot3Ij+0M90xpq8nyirLmtzMGpuRYo1wWic43QFj63rKvXL3ZP\nNSH/ly/iaLJ834HCoqTzIL62QdaRrdUWMkWmvVoVGNBan1DK12q+3DJxxfPEtwsN\nZzX32wiDkCbJQ+CG3S5SOSukZM0cIF1LCgUJcKsFSOrkERQqJi7Shkiv70S/nlmI\n1QAi66rKIF7CzXJl1gGl\n=xp3s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGIzOTkyMGJiMWU2MDVhMWVlNDlmNWI2Yzg2ZjEzMTQwMTMyOWExN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b","sha":"49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b"}],"sha":"b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/b39920bb1e605a1ee49f5b6c86f131401329a17d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): run vue and nuxt unit tests with vitest (#37185)\n\nStacked on #37180.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/vue` (`packages/vue`) and `@nx/nuxt` (`packages/nuxt`) run their\nunit tests with Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run their unit tests with Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest`\nfrom a `vitest.config.mts` that reuses the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`.\n`jest.config.cts` is deleted in both.\n\n| Package | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median | Runner\ntime, median | Quiet round (round 2) wall |\n| ------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| vue | 85 → 85 (11 files) | 242.0s → 9.1s | 240.4s → 7.7s | 97.9s →\n8.5s |\n| nuxt | 113 → 113 (9 files) | 270.3s → 9.0s | 266.1s → 7.5s | 131.1s →\n8.7s |\n\nTiming method: 3 rounds alternating jest (detached checkout of the base\nbranch) and vitest (this branch), `nx test <p> --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon warmed by two `nx show\nprojects` after each checkout. The machine was shared with other work:\n1-minute load was 94 / 21 in round 1 and 25 / 24 in round 3, so those\njest numbers are inflated. Round 2 was the only quiet round (load 5–13)\nand is the fair comparison: roughly 11x (vue) and 15x (nuxt).\n\n### Changes\n\n- `vitest.config.mts` per package, copied from `packages/react` (node\nenvironment, forks pool, shared setup).\n- `project.json`: `test.inputs` names the shared vitest setup and the\n`@clack/prompts` stub.\n- `tsconfig.spec.json`: `vitest/globals` types, includes\n`vitest.config.mts`.\n- Codemod `jest.*` → `vi.*` (vue: 5 files, nuxt: 2 files). Template\nstrings that mention `jest` (e.g. `env: { jest: true }` in generated\neslint config) were left alone.\n- Snapshots regenerated for vitest''s `>` key separator.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- `hookTimeout: 35000` in both configs. Jest''s `testTimeout` (35s in\n`jest.preset.js`) also bounds hooks, while vitest''s `hookTimeout`\ndefaults to 10s. Under heavy machine load the `beforeEach` in `vue`\n`component-story.spec.ts` (it generates a whole library) timed out at\n10s once. No spec changes were needed.\n- `nuxt` `plugin.spec.ts` mocks `loadConfigFile` from\n`@nx/devkit/internal`; the plugin imports it through ESM, so a plain\n`vi.mock` applies (no CJS-channel mock needed). The mocked `buildDir`\nshows up unchanged in the snapshots.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\nSnapshot values compared key by key against the jest originals after\nnormalizing the separator: vue 39 keys in 7 files, nuxt 44 keys in 5\nfiles, 0 value diffs, 0 missing, 0 extra. No inline snapshot changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t\ntest,build,build-base,build-deps,copy-assets,lint,oxlint -p vue nuxt\njest --skip-nx-cache` green (`jest` is the still-on-jest canary: 437\ntests).\n- Two more repeat `nx test` runs of both packages green with the same\ncounts.\n- `nx sync:check` clean.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"1eed7debef5c46adc7224e25cd6439766426ce62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/1eed7debef5c46adc7224e25cd6439766426ce62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1eed7debef5c46adc7224e25cd6439766426ce62\nparent 36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438950 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438950 -0400\n\nchore(repo): run vue and nuxt unit tests with vitest (#37185)\n\nStacked on #37180.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/vue` (`packages/vue`) and `@nx/nuxt` (`packages/nuxt`) run their\nunit tests with Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run their unit tests with Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest`\nfrom a `vitest.config.mts` that reuses the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`.\n`jest.config.cts` is deleted in both.\n\n| Package | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median | Runner\ntime, median | Quiet round (round 2) wall |\n| ------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |\n------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| vue | 85 → 85 (11 files) | 242.0s → 9.1s | 240.4s → 7.7s | 97.9s →\n8.5s |\n| nuxt | 113 → 113 (9 files) | 270.3s → 9.0s | 266.1s → 7.5s | 131.1s →\n8.7s |\n\nTiming method: 3 rounds alternating jest (detached checkout of the base\nbranch) and vitest (this branch), `nx test <p> --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon warmed by two `nx show\nprojects` after each checkout. The machine was shared with other work:\n1-minute load was 94 / 21 in round 1 and 25 / 24 in round 3, so those\njest numbers are inflated. Round 2 was the only quiet round (load 5–13)\nand is the fair comparison: roughly 11x (vue) and 15x (nuxt).\n\n### Changes\n\n- `vitest.config.mts` per package, copied from `packages/react` (node\nenvironment, forks pool, shared setup).\n- `project.json`: `test.inputs` names the shared vitest setup and the\n`@clack/prompts` stub.\n- `tsconfig.spec.json`: `vitest/globals` types, includes\n`vitest.config.mts`.\n- Codemod `jest.*` → `vi.*` (vue: 5 files, nuxt: 2 files). Template\nstrings that mention `jest` (e.g. `env: { jest: true }` in generated\neslint config) were left alone.\n- Snapshots regenerated for vitest''s `>` key separator.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- `hookTimeout: 35000` in both configs. Jest''s `testTimeout` (35s in\n`jest.preset.js`) also bounds hooks, while vitest''s `hookTimeout`\ndefaults to 10s. Under heavy machine load the `beforeEach` in `vue`\n`component-story.spec.ts` (it generates a whole library) timed out at\n10s once. No spec changes were needed.\n- `nuxt` `plugin.spec.ts` mocks `loadConfigFile` from\n`@nx/devkit/internal`; the plugin imports it through ESM, so a plain\n`vi.mock` applies (no CJS-channel mock needed). The mocked `buildDir`\nshows up unchanged in the snapshots.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\nSnapshot values compared key by key against the jest originals after\nnormalizing the separator: vue 39 keys in 7 files, nuxt 44 keys in 5\nfiles, 0 value diffs, 0 missing, 0 extra. No inline snapshot changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t\ntest,build,build-base,build-deps,copy-assets,lint,oxlint -p vue nuxt\njest --skip-nx-cache` green (`jest` is the still-on-jest canary: 437\ntests).\n- Two more repeat `nx test` runs of both packages green with the same\ncounts.\n- `nx sync:check` clean.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjRYQAG7zDgGSVNKvN+QhVFEFvcHh\nzC7TiCmsQYAqJz5hnKUSXLsGB0t9MWJJHbY6Oclnc6uXJ003K3eX2Ea3eTWCaLQa\nZg2MyPstY0OmC4swJZjEAfufKPrD/223Y8ghUvoaOoKS1z60NaFOHq141hIVu/to\naqxtEPpwkftBkf739q8rTlJSvWQBLg5QmQc+XiJm+bTxW4SEMkee593OFc9gGmrO\napTsN4KHKE8Jzh+/ymjhSMDivdZqRJisb3AK23vK0XGW2hdwgX5j1d3oL5hgkARv\nLuy4etHoqGAPiQK8bGbVYvpDSD/ptmD0Y5xm8rhVKwAV05Sim8lgKBfNI4w9Mf8R\nlr6U1u0N8/l453lpYQK8YVl3DhIq/4YABUIEy65WQYJ+xQrScJKmTbjxiCdVWtUJ\niKYuKWQletsFHrmSvrlyrRGsQ5R7R4IXPU6lgLxX8BFmD9LQp3EZ6NiarBLN1X9c\n0YF7i2H9PCRgLRiOGt4aGR7Az5zP1XbKYgu27UeAJhTnz9tlL0DdAQ8aCu5uHm5I\nSjkx5UA/hufoIesdjzhdC29AD6x+8+kloqVlmKWLpK7lXV6ov3o/Bvf3JUtnTPf5\njWAElWTAYzSut17JvkwcnHpo/poAGNYAE3IGm1qWbCAEP0RaxO3x3Ii+dRrZen7w\nrRhu8+WpSQsdeFUIG7SL\n=4BBi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDQ5YmE5MDI0ZjJlYjJjNzAzMTU5NTg4ODFkNDQ3ZDc4YWUxNzM3M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460","sha":"36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460"}],"sha":"49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/49ba9024f2eb2c70315958881d447d78ae17373b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): run gradle, dotnet and maven unit tests with vitest (#37180)\n\nStacked on #37179.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`gradle`, `dotnet` and `@nx/maven` run their unit tests with Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nTheir unit tests run with Vitest. Each package reuses the shared setup\n(`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`).\nOnly the TypeScript plugin projects move. The Kotlin, Java and C#\nsub-projects (`:gradle-batch-runner`, `:gradle-project-graph`,\n`maven-batch-runner`, `nx-maven-plugin`, `maven-shared`,\n`MsbuildAnalyzer`) are untouched.\n\n| project | tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median (jest →\nvitest) | runner time, median (jest → vitest) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| gradle | 294 → 294 | 15.61s → 5.55s | 14.38s → 4.37s |\n| dotnet | 60 → 60 | 3.81s → 2.15s | 2.80s → 1.26s |\n| @nx/maven | 87 → 87 | 5.88s → 2.41s | 4.90s → 1.51s |\n\nHow I timed it: 3 rounds, alternating Jest (a detached checkout of the\nbase branch) and Vitest (this branch). Each run was `nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on and warmed\nafter every checkout. Load average was 3.7 to 7.2 during the runs.\n\n### Config\n\n- `gradle`: Jest''s `modulePathIgnorePatterns` for `batch-runner/` and\n`project-graph/` is now a Vitest `exclude`. Those folders hold the\nKotlin/Gradle projects. `vitest list` confirms nothing under them is\ncollected.\n- `dotnet` and `maven`: their Jest configs had nothing beyond the\npreset.\n- Each `project.json` declares the shared `test.inputs`\n(`tools/vitest/**/*`, `scripts/jest-mocks/clack-prompts.js`).\n- I deleted `packages/maven/src/test-setup.ts`. It was a Jest-only file\nthat silenced console output, but no Jest config ever loaded it.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- `gradle` `exec-gradle.spec.ts`: the spec called\n`vi.doMock(''@nx/devkit/internal'')` and then loaded the module with\n`require(''./exec-gradle'')`. A `require()` goes through the CommonJS\nchannel, and `vi.doMock` never reaches it. So the real `safeSpawn` ran\nand tried to start `/ws/gradlew` (ENOENT). The spec now uses `await\nimport(''./exec-gradle'')`. `vi.doUnmock` in `afterEach` clears the\nregistration, because `vi.resetModules()` keeps it.\n- `dotnet` `analyzer-client.spec.ts`: the same `require()` problem. The\nmodule is now loaded with `await import()` in an async `beforeEach`.\n- `dotnet` `analyzer-client.spec.ts`: the `PluginCache` mock was\n`vi.fn(() => ({...}))`. The source calls it with `new`, and an arrow\nfunction can''t be a constructor. It is now `vi.fn(function () { return\n{...}; })`.\n\nBefore this change, the gradle and dotnet specs only worked because\nJest''s `require` went through the mocked registry.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\n`.snap` files were regenerated from pristine copies. Compared by value\n(after normalizing the ` > ` key separator): gradle 8 keys, dotnet 4,\nmaven 10. Every package had 0 value diffs, 0 missing and 0 extra. No\ninline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,typecheck -p gradle dotnet\n@nx/maven jest --skip-nx-cache` passed. That covers every target the\nthree projects list except `nx-release-publish`, `watch-deps` and\ndotnet''s C#-only `format-native`. `jest` is the canary that stays on\nJest.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two more test runs of all three projects were green, with the same\ncounts.\n- I also ran all three suites with fake\n`gradle`/`gradlew`/`mvn`/`mvnw`/`dotnet`/`java` binaries first on\n`PATH`. None of them was called, so no spec runs a real build tool.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"6466fc9549cdaa4911b5734fc731aa458b4569be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/6466fc9549cdaa4911b5734fc731aa458b4569be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460","verification":{"payload":"tree 6466fc9549cdaa4911b5734fc731aa458b4569be\nparent fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438950 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438950 -0400\n\nchore(repo): run gradle, dotnet and maven unit tests with vitest (#37180)\n\nStacked on #37179.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`gradle`, `dotnet` and `@nx/maven` run their unit tests with Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nTheir unit tests run with Vitest. Each package reuses the shared setup\n(`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`).\nOnly the TypeScript plugin projects move. The Kotlin, Java and C#\nsub-projects (`:gradle-batch-runner`, `:gradle-project-graph`,\n`maven-batch-runner`, `nx-maven-plugin`, `maven-shared`,\n`MsbuildAnalyzer`) are untouched.\n\n| project | tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median (jest →\nvitest) | runner time, median (jest → vitest) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| gradle | 294 → 294 | 15.61s → 5.55s | 14.38s → 4.37s |\n| dotnet | 60 → 60 | 3.81s → 2.15s | 2.80s → 1.26s |\n| @nx/maven | 87 → 87 | 5.88s → 2.41s | 4.90s → 1.51s |\n\nHow I timed it: 3 rounds, alternating Jest (a detached checkout of the\nbase branch) and Vitest (this branch). Each run was `nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` with the daemon on and warmed\nafter every checkout. Load average was 3.7 to 7.2 during the runs.\n\n### Config\n\n- `gradle`: Jest''s `modulePathIgnorePatterns` for `batch-runner/` and\n`project-graph/` is now a Vitest `exclude`. Those folders hold the\nKotlin/Gradle projects. `vitest list` confirms nothing under them is\ncollected.\n- `dotnet` and `maven`: their Jest configs had nothing beyond the\npreset.\n- Each `project.json` declares the shared `test.inputs`\n(`tools/vitest/**/*`, `scripts/jest-mocks/clack-prompts.js`).\n- I deleted `packages/maven/src/test-setup.ts`. It was a Jest-only file\nthat silenced console output, but no Jest config ever loaded it.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- `gradle` `exec-gradle.spec.ts`: the spec called\n`vi.doMock(''@nx/devkit/internal'')` and then loaded the module with\n`require(''./exec-gradle'')`. A `require()` goes through the CommonJS\nchannel, and `vi.doMock` never reaches it. So the real `safeSpawn` ran\nand tried to start `/ws/gradlew` (ENOENT). The spec now uses `await\nimport(''./exec-gradle'')`. `vi.doUnmock` in `afterEach` clears the\nregistration, because `vi.resetModules()` keeps it.\n- `dotnet` `analyzer-client.spec.ts`: the same `require()` problem. The\nmodule is now loaded with `await import()` in an async `beforeEach`.\n- `dotnet` `analyzer-client.spec.ts`: the `PluginCache` mock was\n`vi.fn(() => ({...}))`. The source calls it with `new`, and an arrow\nfunction can''t be a constructor. It is now `vi.fn(function () { return\n{...}; })`.\n\nBefore this change, the gradle and dotnet specs only worked because\nJest''s `require` went through the mocked registry.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\n`.snap` files were regenerated from pristine copies. Compared by value\n(after normalizing the ` > ` key separator): gradle 8 keys, dotnet 4,\nmaven 10. Every package had 0 value diffs, 0 missing and 0 extra. No\ninline snapshots changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,typecheck -p gradle dotnet\n@nx/maven jest --skip-nx-cache` passed. That covers every target the\nthree projects list except `nx-release-publish`, `watch-deps` and\ndotnet''s C#-only `format-native`. `jest` is the canary that stays on\nJest.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two more test runs of all three projects were green, with the same\ncounts.\n- I also ran all three suites with fake\n`gradle`/`gradlew`/`mvn`/`mvnw`/`dotnet`/`java` binaries first on\n`PATH`. None of them was called, so no spec runs a real build tool.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKJsQAEn8/bCO3Gjd7zsgC8J74k2e\nhKpSWoa4V2IkeFWm51xO2zAlXCSwUZG0nGXMFpWxMuJsMWqZOmqXb2hQKYsr8Hkt\n+ayZKTd4avfu84lOBUaDJAb44ZCDEMr0uI2Mtp2A4G+RznfUPrMwVY17GANbHN1F\nB2Co/eO3BdMIaZdengNyRyCC5ki8+ErGbDiOcHmbbkeBDwIrHGRh/7o2tsj3pRQ5\nmNVTZfp4E7TEWMizekpWIBK2MBjUDwnbwjEOw/+A4oAEFPgpV7LzXOyS8anGyueo\nATKbBFQ0/McDY0W1cy07OdtBDCvUHvsk4OEsZaQkOFQdC5p7BVlh+PSSQ1kJHTsd\nEBCBmIb6CD3+E+a7er1w28hvrYrRTSoW/gjT+MwUl3fK87FEqZwaJbixvQBEfiQV\nMkmpjjgfSsucv0Mo23jKLOoi2+C2rRff64ezKhQwi7Q6i8HoM599H3asZgM63CYX\nAuFtnzYFyzyULyVhnTzdDpErSwHHxzpN3OzNJMRdpA/bnsi8b4OjjEQXu5fwMqvD\nQHcj4E1Plx42uwSdvcPBX7RZIsQx7ruHpWkYde/1HwTP2u244LFk0Qf+dZfUnl4u\n68drsB4N/pEXTIN9v8R6o3wh/p1xAVn98Mr6Bs6wZJ4lZiXlwK08mAcmZr+2uucH\nUQ6k3pcx0pLqMl4FTztG\n=8YdE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDM2YzM2NWJkNjA0OWIyMWUxMzFkYzkwYmQxNmY4NGQxZGIxMDg0NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a","sha":"fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a"}],"sha":"36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/36c365bd6049b21e131dc90bd16f84d1db108460"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:09Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(testing): run cypress and playwright unit tests with vitest (#37179)\n\nStacked on #37178.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/cypress` and `@nx/playwright` unit tests run on Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run their unit tests on Vitest through the inferred\n`@nx/vitest` target. They reuse the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts` unchanged. Each\n`vitest.config.mts` copies `packages/react`''s. Each `project.json`\ndeclares the shared setup files as `test` inputs. `jest.config.cts` is\ndeleted in both.\n\n| Package | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median (jest →\nvitest) | Runner-reported, median (jest → vitest) |\n| ---------- | --------------------- |\n-------------------------------------- |\n--------------------------------------- |\n| cypress | 388 → 388 | 49.4s → 5.1s | 48.2s → 4.1s |\n| playwright | 264 → 264 | 26.3s → 16.4s | 25.3s → 15.5s |\n\nTiming method: 3 alternating rounds (jest on a detached checkout of the\nbase branch, vitest on this branch), `NX_DAEMON=true pnpm nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies`, daemon warmed after every\ncheckout. Load average 3.8-6.6 during the runs. Playwright stays bounded\nby `wait-for-webserver.impl.spec.ts`, whose real-time waits take about\n14s on their own.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **Config files loaded through `loadConfigFile`** (cypress\n`plugin.spec.ts` and `convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`, playwright\n`convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`). `loadConfigFile` `require`s the config,\nso `vi.mock`/`vi.doMock` never reach it. These now use `mockCjsModule`,\nwith `resetCjsMocks` in `afterEach`. In cypress `plugin.spec.ts`, the\n`vi.mock` inside a helper was also hoisted to the top of the file, where\nit crashed.\n- **cypress `cypress.impl.spec.ts`**. The spec reassigned properties on\n`require(''@nx/devkit'')`. The executor imports devkit as ESM, so under\nvitest those writes landed on a different module instance. It now\nimports the automocked namespace and configures `runExecutor`,\n`readTargetOptions`, `stripIndents` and `parseTargetString` with\n`vi.mocked(...)`. The `detect-port` factory returns `{ default: fn }`\nwith the fn from `vi.hoisted`, replacing `jest.requireMock`.\n- **cypress `component-configuration.spec.ts`**. A sync\n`jest.requireActual` inside a test is now `await vi.importActual`.\n- **playwright `webserver-readiness.spec.ts`**. The config fixtures\n`require(''@nx/devkit/internal'').applyDaemonEnvFromClient`. Under vitest,\nthat CJS require loads a second copy with its own apply state, separate\nfrom the one the source reads. The `loadConfigWithProbeEnv` suite now\nregisters the ESM namespace with `mockCjsModule` for its duration, so\nboth sides share one instance.\n\nSpecs that only mention `jest` in strings were left alone (for example\ncypress `rewrite-internal-subpath-imports.spec.ts`, which tests\nrewriting user `jest.mock(...)` calls).\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\n- cypress: 1 `.snap` file was regenerated from a pristine tree. The\nvalue diff finds 1 key and 0 value changes, and only the key separator\nchanged. One inline `toThrowErrorMatchingInlineSnapshot` changed format\nonly (`\"msg\"` → `[Error: msg]`).\n- playwright: only inline snapshots, and none changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p cypress playwright jest\n--skip-nx-cache` passes. `jest` is the still-on-jest canary.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two repeat `nx test` runs of each package are green, with test counts\nequal to the jest baseline.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"d7f68e42bdd82fcdc3ac8debf4ccab577fc39e47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/d7f68e42bdd82fcdc3ac8debf4ccab577fc39e47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a","verification":{"payload":"tree d7f68e42bdd82fcdc3ac8debf4ccab577fc39e47\nparent 9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438949 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438949 -0400\n\nchore(testing): run cypress and playwright unit tests with vitest (#37179)\n\nStacked on #37178.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/cypress` and `@nx/playwright` unit tests run on Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run their unit tests on Vitest through the inferred\n`@nx/vitest` target. They reuse the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts` unchanged. Each\n`vitest.config.mts` copies `packages/react`''s. Each `project.json`\ndeclares the shared setup files as `test` inputs. `jest.config.cts` is\ndeleted in both.\n\n| Package | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median (jest →\nvitest) | Runner-reported, median (jest → vitest) |\n| ---------- | --------------------- |\n-------------------------------------- |\n--------------------------------------- |\n| cypress | 388 → 388 | 49.4s → 5.1s | 48.2s → 4.1s |\n| playwright | 264 → 264 | 26.3s → 16.4s | 25.3s → 15.5s |\n\nTiming method: 3 alternating rounds (jest on a detached checkout of the\nbase branch, vitest on this branch), `NX_DAEMON=true pnpm nx test <p>\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies`, daemon warmed after every\ncheckout. Load average 3.8-6.6 during the runs. Playwright stays bounded\nby `wait-for-webserver.impl.spec.ts`, whose real-time waits take about\n14s on their own.\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **Config files loaded through `loadConfigFile`** (cypress\n`plugin.spec.ts` and `convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`, playwright\n`convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`). `loadConfigFile` `require`s the config,\nso `vi.mock`/`vi.doMock` never reach it. These now use `mockCjsModule`,\nwith `resetCjsMocks` in `afterEach`. In cypress `plugin.spec.ts`, the\n`vi.mock` inside a helper was also hoisted to the top of the file, where\nit crashed.\n- **cypress `cypress.impl.spec.ts`**. The spec reassigned properties on\n`require(''@nx/devkit'')`. The executor imports devkit as ESM, so under\nvitest those writes landed on a different module instance. It now\nimports the automocked namespace and configures `runExecutor`,\n`readTargetOptions`, `stripIndents` and `parseTargetString` with\n`vi.mocked(...)`. The `detect-port` factory returns `{ default: fn }`\nwith the fn from `vi.hoisted`, replacing `jest.requireMock`.\n- **cypress `component-configuration.spec.ts`**. A sync\n`jest.requireActual` inside a test is now `await vi.importActual`.\n- **playwright `webserver-readiness.spec.ts`**. The config fixtures\n`require(''@nx/devkit/internal'').applyDaemonEnvFromClient`. Under vitest,\nthat CJS require loads a second copy with its own apply state, separate\nfrom the one the source reads. The `loadConfigWithProbeEnv` suite now\nregisters the ESM namespace with `mockCjsModule` for its duration, so\nboth sides share one instance.\n\nSpecs that only mention `jest` in strings were left alone (for example\ncypress `rewrite-internal-subpath-imports.spec.ts`, which tests\nrewriting user `jest.mock(...)` calls).\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\n- cypress: 1 `.snap` file was regenerated from a pristine tree. The\nvalue diff finds 1 key and 0 value changes, and only the key separator\nchanged. One inline `toThrowErrorMatchingInlineSnapshot` changed format\nonly (`\"msg\"` → `[Error: msg]`).\n- playwright: only inline snapshots, and none changed.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p cypress playwright jest\n--skip-nx-cache` passes. `jest` is the still-on-jest canary.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two repeat `nx test` runs of each package are green, with test counts\nequal to the jest baseline.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABOYQAAGf83XXDqRtRtKCPoebiljX\nzWBbH7V/suUgQZlGYOe44BAzxzOIB7u9A28RQRozznu3PoYgQzrYOztoOtCEVAKt\nFSC6SEHT8tQBpVIsNFSKLmy+NXVKrI5XQaSpkxs4yYx4fCrnVBRRVLpJg5ROZo8E\n8JWRQ6/Om9Xz5qB2ZjM0FRn+8hMbhtN6ugajqAUfXRSOFX7jeLdHAUVKw/N0mAfJ\n/Rv1LW+pXFfmTTOSX6CV64v73qm1dAfGsQ34HTMlgqxSBF38GREHH2zZYEoPf79l\n9Crt1k0WZpf+wk9SzzBKRZJ+WHfBxjb9svbs9/IlnA3wG8s7MuJwgXjkyryraxvS\nqm4GWbC7t+unVWu67ehvugQJqQ2MJE4mYdKEYFw7wjKb3fuCRPvy1N/+Avj1QhSC\nbuh0dIGdgIFB7fZpciujGO00krSQoVlFL/VPwCj3fEkeK8YzCtv0v6FclYpuiE0Q\n1Kik5AG6Z9pV+kD0WVv7NTIRSSO3VSDJJ/EwA0rVv+v5y/IOPbPTPETdAncTvi5f\nLcLImT0hjfCVIzjkaZZI78bGjN1k9JhriOA6we8rcVaIcBEV+4hlEyfHRseBvFk2\nZY2KcBp4gUEBmdDbWPIt/qqv3pxmGiosj7WVh8llbA/hHvEYmAHwG5vcff+gr0P9\nMVATi4c+Y8ITF0pnvzNd\n=dK6y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGZhZDkxOGZmYjhlZTM5MTgwZDM2M2JhZDJkNGM1NTQ4ZjgzNDZlMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194","sha":"9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194"}],"sha":"fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/fad918ffb8ee39180d363bad2d4c5548f8346e2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:09Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:09:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): run web, vite, webpack, vitest, rollup and esbuild unit tests with vitest (#37178)\n\nStacked on #37177.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe unit tests of `@nx/web`, `@nx/vite`, `@nx/webpack`, `@nx/vitest`,\n`@nx/rollup` and `@nx/esbuild` run on Jest. The six suites take about\n139s of wall time together.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAll six run on Vitest 4 through the inferred `@nx/vitest` plugin. They\nreuse the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`. Test counts are unchanged, and\ntogether they take about 22s.\n\n| Project | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median (jest →\nvitest) | Runner time, median (jest → vitest) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| web | 73 → 73 | 45.20s → 3.56s | 44.12s → 2.62s |\n| vite | 327 → 327 | 43.53s → 4.70s | 42.50s → 3.76s |\n| webpack | 170 → 170 | 18.99s → 4.38s | 17.96s → 3.47s |\n| vitest | 241 → 241 | 9.35s → 3.58s | 8.34s → 2.69s |\n| rollup | 184 → 184 | 17.02s → 3.58s | 16.02s → 2.68s |\n| esbuild | 40 → 40 | 4.57s → 2.49s | 3.58s → 1.54s |\n\nHow we measured: 3 rounds that alternate between Jest (a detached\ncheckout of the base branch) and Vitest (this branch). Each run is\n`NX_DAEMON=true nx test <p> --skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies`,\nand the daemon is warmed after every checkout. The machine was quiet:\nthe 1-minute load average was 2.6–7.6 for every run. Raw numbers per\nround:\n\n- Jest wall: web 45.29/45.08/45.20, vite 43.80/43.53/43.49, webpack\n18.98/18.99/19.02, vitest 9.35/9.35/9.35, rollup 17.07/17.00/17.02,\nesbuild 4.64/4.56/4.57\n- Vitest wall: web 3.56/3.98/3.55, vite 4.67/4.70/4.76, webpack\n4.36/4.45/4.38, vitest 3.56/3.61/3.58, rollup 3.58/3.62/3.58, esbuild\n2.49/2.42/2.50\n\n### What changed per package\n\nEach package gets the same pieces:\n\n- a `vitest.config.mts` copied from `packages/react`\n- the shared `test.inputs` block\n- `vitest/globals` in `tsconfig.spec.json`\n- `jest.config.cts` deleted\n\nNone of the jest configs had settings beyond the preset. Then:\n\n- the `jest.*` → `vi.*` codemod. Migration specs that assert on\n`jest.mock(...)` text were left alone.\n- the hand fixes below\n- snapshots regenerated\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **web, static-serve spec:** `expect(...).rejects` was not awaited. The\ninline snapshot moves from `\"msg\"` to `[Error: msg]`, which is a\nserializer change only.\n- **vite, `nx-tsconfig-paths.plugin.spec.ts`:**\n- `jest.replaceProperty(devkit, ''workspaceRoot'', ...)` becomes a\n`vi.mock(''@nx/devkit'')` getter. This is the same pattern the js\n`prune-lockfile` spec uses.\n- The spec also strips the non-default `require.extensions` keys during\neach test. `tsconfig-paths` probes every `require.extensions` key. The\nshared setup''s swc-node hook adds `.ts`, so `tsconfig-paths` finds\n`dir/index.ts` and returns the extensionless directory. Plain node and\njest''s sandbox don''t have `.ts` there, so the plugin used to fall\nthrough to its own resolver.\n- **vite, configuration spec:** it spied on\n`require(''@nx/devkit/internal'').confirmationPrompt`, but that export\ncan''t be redefined, and the source imports it through ESM. The spec now\nmocks it with `vi.mock` and a pass-through `vi.fn`.\n- **vite, configuration spec:** the `test.each` table title\n`\"$unitTestRunner\"` became `$unitTestRunner` so vitest doesn''t\ndouble-quote it.\n- **webpack, convert-to-inferred and plugin specs:** `loadConfigFile`\n`require`s `webpack.config.js`, so the virtual `vi.doMock`/`vi.mock`\nnever applied. These use `mockCjsModule` + `resetCjsMocks` now, the same\nas the rspack spec. The lazy `Proxy` + `requireActual` mock of\n`nx/src/devkit-internals` became the async `importActual` factory that\nrspack uses.\n- **webpack, deprecation spec:** `jest.isolateModules` becomes\n`vi.resetModules()` + dynamic `import()`, with `vi.restoreAllMocks()`\nbetween tests.\n- **vitest, plugin spec:** `jest.requireMock(''vitest/node'')` becomes\n`await import(''vitest/node'')`, which returns the registered mock.\n- **rollup, update-package-json spec:** the spy on\n`require(''fs'').writeFileSync` never reached the ESM import. The spec now\nuses a module-level `vi.mock(''fs'')` instead.\n- **rollup, plugin spec:** the plugin `require`s\n`rollup/loadConfigFile`, so the spec mocks it with `mockCjsModule`.\n- **esbuild, normalize spec:** the codemod left a sync `vi.mock<T>(...,\n() => { await ... })` factory, so the factory is now `async`.\n`jest.MockedFunction` becomes `MockedFunction`.\n\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` is **not** changed.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\nWe regenerated every `.snap` from pristine copies with `vitest run -u`\nand compared values to the Jest originals after normalizing keys. The\nresult is 0 value diffs across 11 files and 63 keys. The only renames\nare the 5 `unitTestRunner` table keys in vite, and they pair 1:1 with\nidentical values.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p web vite webpack vitest\nrollup esbuild jest --skip-nx-cache` passes. The `jest` project stays on\nJest as the canary: 437 tests pass.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two more `nx run-many -t test` runs of the six packages both pass with\nthe same counts.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"906aa75142cc1e06d34fa9bbfbd3813d8ad52ee2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/906aa75142cc1e06d34fa9bbfbd3813d8ad52ee2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194","verification":{"payload":"tree 906aa75142cc1e06d34fa9bbfbd3813d8ad52ee2\nparent ce7d1ddc617fcc95f8f84b0bae9e1a12c5dfdbf3\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790438949 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790438949 -0400\n\nchore(repo): run web, vite, webpack, vitest, rollup and esbuild unit tests with vitest (#37178)\n\nStacked on #37177.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe unit tests of `@nx/web`, `@nx/vite`, `@nx/webpack`, `@nx/vitest`,\n`@nx/rollup` and `@nx/esbuild` run on Jest. The six suites take about\n139s of wall time together.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAll six run on Vitest 4 through the inferred `@nx/vitest` plugin. They\nreuse the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts` and\n`tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`. Test counts are unchanged, and\ntogether they take about 22s.\n\n| Project | Tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall, median (jest →\nvitest) | Runner time, median (jest → vitest) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| web | 73 → 73 | 45.20s → 3.56s | 44.12s → 2.62s |\n| vite | 327 → 327 | 43.53s → 4.70s | 42.50s → 3.76s |\n| webpack | 170 → 170 | 18.99s → 4.38s | 17.96s → 3.47s |\n| vitest | 241 → 241 | 9.35s → 3.58s | 8.34s → 2.69s |\n| rollup | 184 → 184 | 17.02s → 3.58s | 16.02s → 2.68s |\n| esbuild | 40 → 40 | 4.57s → 2.49s | 3.58s → 1.54s |\n\nHow we measured: 3 rounds that alternate between Jest (a detached\ncheckout of the base branch) and Vitest (this branch). Each run is\n`NX_DAEMON=true nx test <p> --skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies`,\nand the daemon is warmed after every checkout. The machine was quiet:\nthe 1-minute load average was 2.6–7.6 for every run. Raw numbers per\nround:\n\n- Jest wall: web 45.29/45.08/45.20, vite 43.80/43.53/43.49, webpack\n18.98/18.99/19.02, vitest 9.35/9.35/9.35, rollup 17.07/17.00/17.02,\nesbuild 4.64/4.56/4.57\n- Vitest wall: web 3.56/3.98/3.55, vite 4.67/4.70/4.76, webpack\n4.36/4.45/4.38, vitest 3.56/3.61/3.58, rollup 3.58/3.62/3.58, esbuild\n2.49/2.42/2.50\n\n### What changed per package\n\nEach package gets the same pieces:\n\n- a `vitest.config.mts` copied from `packages/react`\n- the shared `test.inputs` block\n- `vitest/globals` in `tsconfig.spec.json`\n- `jest.config.cts` deleted\n\nNone of the jest configs had settings beyond the preset. Then:\n\n- the `jest.*` → `vi.*` codemod. Migration specs that assert on\n`jest.mock(...)` text were left alone.\n- the hand fixes below\n- snapshots regenerated\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **web, static-serve spec:** `expect(...).rejects` was not awaited. The\ninline snapshot moves from `\"msg\"` to `[Error: msg]`, which is a\nserializer change only.\n- **vite, `nx-tsconfig-paths.plugin.spec.ts`:**\n- `jest.replaceProperty(devkit, ''workspaceRoot'', ...)` becomes a\n`vi.mock(''@nx/devkit'')` getter. This is the same pattern the js\n`prune-lockfile` spec uses.\n- The spec also strips the non-default `require.extensions` keys during\neach test. `tsconfig-paths` probes every `require.extensions` key. The\nshared setup''s swc-node hook adds `.ts`, so `tsconfig-paths` finds\n`dir/index.ts` and returns the extensionless directory. Plain node and\njest''s sandbox don''t have `.ts` there, so the plugin used to fall\nthrough to its own resolver.\n- **vite, configuration spec:** it spied on\n`require(''@nx/devkit/internal'').confirmationPrompt`, but that export\ncan''t be redefined, and the source imports it through ESM. The spec now\nmocks it with `vi.mock` and a pass-through `vi.fn`.\n- **vite, configuration spec:** the `test.each` table title\n`\"$unitTestRunner\"` became `$unitTestRunner` so vitest doesn''t\ndouble-quote it.\n- **webpack, convert-to-inferred and plugin specs:** `loadConfigFile`\n`require`s `webpack.config.js`, so the virtual `vi.doMock`/`vi.mock`\nnever applied. These use `mockCjsModule` + `resetCjsMocks` now, the same\nas the rspack spec. The lazy `Proxy` + `requireActual` mock of\n`nx/src/devkit-internals` became the async `importActual` factory that\nrspack uses.\n- **webpack, deprecation spec:** `jest.isolateModules` becomes\n`vi.resetModules()` + dynamic `import()`, with `vi.restoreAllMocks()`\nbetween tests.\n- **vitest, plugin spec:** `jest.requireMock(''vitest/node'')` becomes\n`await import(''vitest/node'')`, which returns the registered mock.\n- **rollup, update-package-json spec:** the spy on\n`require(''fs'').writeFileSync` never reached the ESM import. The spec now\nuses a module-level `vi.mock(''fs'')` instead.\n- **rollup, plugin spec:** the plugin `require`s\n`rollup/loadConfigFile`, so the spec mocks it with `mockCjsModule`.\n- **esbuild, normalize spec:** the codemod left a sync `vi.mock<T>(...,\n() => { await ... })` factory, so the factory is now `async`.\n`jest.MockedFunction` becomes `MockedFunction`.\n\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` is **not** changed.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\nWe regenerated every `.snap` from pristine copies with `vitest run -u`\nand compared values to the Jest originals after normalizing keys. The\nresult is 0 value diffs across 11 files and 63 keys. The only renames\nare the 5 `unitTestRunner` table keys in vite, and they pair 1:1 with\nidentical values.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p web vite webpack vitest\nrollup esbuild jest --skip-nx-cache` passes. The `jest` project stays on\nJest as the canary: 437 tests pass.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean.\n- Two more `nx run-many -t test` runs of the six packages both pass with\nthe same counts.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqt+4lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApysQAKOmobQ39CEqPtrqsm7CPM/t\n2ZrSLbXEufhj1oRkf6ssuwA7b2nYJU07jvuVno6hZq+CtjFKVW5AhlE24nOES9jc\nW79O8L7F9N2VjbaKGV4KFSIQC3ji9Ny3HRjQ8s1KErsfmyhj2R/ACtWuWIZVIhhe\n/RDG+PPuc8vtKKZTo9Xm0kFDVSMgiFAH4dVd3rA1uM0+hyI2xm/w4Rf7QfF25xU6\nyAR+e/bkxYpPQ6n58e//G2DgvrTko6iQzeWZpWqYDmMJV60wGwMe0HKlshZQ6iED\n3NymQfQccSfo+BCHb9sgujxjrSb7UnxI+5L2o1+yXqieE1z6j2lOn0V8qdFRxs8e\nF3deyn3J8/uyf2e0wh7qPWCvI7v5hr/hj/fIDltzNPZ8vcgbFTyFyPEQI2vPGIZS\n/PM4rFQQ72B5gdUPvgX1BsKn0VitsISCHeMOs3bRDbll0VfUTObMIiu7P0NQVPCX\nk83Kd9+1+HY1eGfFrIeZOj95gZCUoEUCgmo18G5HhMyvh98gZKgFp9tJBWZqB0q8\n5uN2ybTP9U0YHgcCiZ8jEuhFP4zJTHF1P054cxJtzzPAz3RcExVgEegfzNMl24LM\nXeUilzQFGruP74CxEQP9XdzAgTVQAlZyEZ4p/cP33oGr7i82BLu2bkz2hnPPkCTu\nyu+F3tt7M7BH0pSInn2k\n=KZie\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T16:09:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDlmNDBhMTA5MjEwY2E1NjFiZWY5ZDg2MGQ3NWI0YzgyNjMyZjkxOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/ce7d1ddc617fcc95f8f84b0bae9e1a12c5dfdbf3","sha":"ce7d1ddc617fcc95f8f84b0bae9e1a12c5dfdbf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/ce7d1ddc617fcc95f8f84b0bae9e1a12c5dfdbf3"}],"sha":"9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9f40a109210ca561bef9d860d75b4c82632f9194"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/ce7d1ddc617fcc95f8f84b0bae9e1a12c5dfdbf3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:59:21Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:59:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(devkit): run devkit unit tests with vitest (#37177)\n\nStacked on #37174.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/devkit` unit tests (`devkit:test`) run on Jest.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`devkit:test` runs on Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from\n`packages/devkit/vitest.config.mts`, using the shared\n`tools/vitest/setup.mts` and `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`. The\nshared setup is **not** changed.\n\n| | Jest (base) | Vitest (this PR) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 601 (600 passed, 1 todo), 42 files | 601 (600 passed, 1 todo),\n42 files |\n| `nx test devkit` wall, median of 3 | 17.1s | 7.2s |\n| Runner-reported time, median of 3 | 16.0s | 6.1s |\n\nPer-file test counts match Jest exactly. Timing method: 3 rounds,\nalternating a detached checkout of `chore/eslint-oxlint-vitest` (Jest)\nwith this branch (Vitest), `nx show projects` twice after each checkout\nto warm the daemon, then one `NX_DAEMON=true nx test devkit\n--skip-nx-cache --excludeTaskDependencies` under `caffeinate -i`, on a\nquiet 8-core machine (load 3.8–4.9). Raw wall: Jest 17.7 / 17.1 / 17.1s,\nVitest 7.1 / 7.2 / 7.5s.\n\n### What the vitest config reproduces from `jest.config.cts`\n\n- `setupFiles: [jest-setup-nx-workspace-data-dir.js]` → renamed to\n`vitest-setup-nx-workspace-data-dir.cjs` and loaded through `execArgv:\n[''--require'', …]`. That way `NX_WORKSPACE_DATA_DIRECTORY` is set before\nany nx module computes `workspaceDataDirectory`. I checked that the ESM\nand CJS copies of `nx/src/utils/cache-directory` both see it. Vitest\nstops forks with SIGTERM, which skips `exit` handlers. The file now also\ncleans up on SIGTERM, so no temp dir is left behind per spec file. (Jest\nleft 42 per run.)\n- `modulePathIgnorePatterns: [''<rootDir>/dist/'']` → `exclude:\n[''dist/**'']`.\n- `moduleNameMapper` for `@schematics/angular/collection.json` /\n`@angular-devkit/schematics/tools` → no alias needed. The only user was\n`invoke-nx-generator.spec.ts`, which calls\n`require.resolve(''@schematics/angular/collection.json'')`. The package''s\nexports map only exposes `./*.js`, so the spec now finds\n`collection.json` beside the package''s `package.json`.\n`@angular-devkit/schematics/tools` resolves normally under node (the\npackage has no exports map).\n\n### Hand fixes\n\n- **Missing exports mocked as `undefined`** (`format-files-nx-skew`,\n`ignore-nx-skew`, `e2e-web-server-info-utils`,\n`find-plugin-for-config-file`). Vitest throws when code reads an export\nthat a mock factory did not return. An older nx''s CJS module reads that\nexport as `undefined`, so the factories now list those names as\n`undefined`. The skew specs'' \"guards the simulation itself\" checks read\nthe mocked module through `await import` rather than `require` (which\nbypasses `vi.mock`). The jest-only `{ virtual: true }` mock option is\ngone.\n- **`jest.isolateModules`** in `config-utils.spec.ts` →\n`vi.resetModules()` + `vi.doMock` + dynamic `import()`, with `doUnmock`\nin `finally`.\n- **Real `ensurePackage` under test** (`ensure-package.spec.ts`,\n`package-json.spec.ts`). The shared setup stubs `ensurePackage` at its\nsource path, and these specs test that function directly, so they\n`vi.unmock(''./package-json'')`. Jest''s setup only mocked the `@nx/devkit`\nspecifier, so these specs always ran the real code.\n- **Unit-test workspace root is an empty scratch dir**\n(`installed-version`, `version-floor`). The resolvable-package case now\nresolves `semver` from the spec''s directory. The two\n`FsTree(workspaceRoot)` cases seed an in-memory `package.json` (nothing\nis written to disk).\n- **Latent test bug** in `add-plugin.spec.ts`: `fail(''Should have thrown\nan error'')` sat inside a `try { } catch {}`. `fail` is not defined, so\nthe `ReferenceError` was swallowed, and the test would have passed even\nif nothing threw. It now asserts `.rejects.toThrow()` (and passes).\n- `vi.fn<Promise<string>, []>()` → `vi.fn<() => Promise<string>>()` in\n`require-esm-race.spec.ts`. Jest''s generic arity was left behind by the\ncodemod.\n- Stale jest-specific comments were updated (`format-files.spec.ts`,\n`ignore-nx-skew.spec.ts`, `config-utils.spec.ts`).\n- `update-deep-imports.spec.ts` is untouched: its `jest.*` hits are\nfixture strings for the migration.\n\n### Snapshots\n\n- `generate-files.spec.ts.snap`: the only change is the `// Vitest\nSnapshot` header. Snapshot values match (6/6 keys, 0 value diffs).\n- Inline `toThrowErrorMatchingInlineSnapshot`: format-only (`\"msg\"` →\n`[Error: msg]`).\n- `aggregate-log-util.spec.ts` inline snapshots: the bold ANSI codes\n(`[1m`/`[22m`) Jest recorded are gone. The shared setup pins\n`NO_COLOR=1`, and the text is otherwise identical.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,build-base,copy-assets -p\ndevkit jest --skip-nx-cache` passes. `jest` (packages/jest) is the\nstill-on-jest canary: 437 tests.\n- `nx sync:check` is clean. Two repeat `nx test devkit --skip-nx-cache`\nruns are green (601/601).\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` vitest note lists `packages/devkit`.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cad5cc6be78fcd85136e56e4a46b692ae480761","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/9cad5cc6be78fcd85136e56e4a46b692ae480761"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/ce7d1ddc617fcc95f8f84b0bae9e1a12c5dfdbf3","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cad5cc6be78fcd85136e56e4a46b692ae480761\nparent 6e2b778e4eca78fa84f263830ba63807d4238e9d\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790434761 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790434761 -0400\n\nchore(devkit): run devkit unit tests with vitest (#37177)\n\nStacked on #37174.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/devkit` u