url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/8e5b27731b9a7f9587a5643e807b4d259be3a41c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/2cfeb623a8cdc1dab6064fbddaa41293588ac340/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:05:08Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:05:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(storybook): run storybook unit tests with vitest (#37172)\n\nStacked on #37171.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/storybook` unit tests run on Jest\n(`packages/storybook/jest.config.cts`, `jest.preset.js`).\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`@nx/storybook` unit tests run on Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from\n`packages/storybook/vitest.config.mts`. The config is the same as\n`packages/js` and `packages/react`: the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts`\nand `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`, forks pool, 35s timeout.\n`test.inputs` names the shared setup files. `jest.config.cts` is\ndeleted.\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 227 (12 files) | 227 (12 files) |\n| `nx test storybook` wall time (median of 3) | 146.6s | 5.3s |\n| Runner-reported time (median of 3) | 145.4s | 4.2s |\n\nTiming method: 3 alternating rounds on the same machine. Jest ran on a\ndetached checkout of the base branch. Vitest ran on this branch. The\ndaemon was on and warmed with two `nx show projects` calls after each\ncheckout. Each run used `nx test storybook --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies`.\n\nRaw numbers (wall / runner):\n- jest: 146.56 / 145.38, 146.59 / 145.46, 146.26 / 145.14\n- vitest: 5.58 / 4.19, 5.25 / 4.20, 5.24 / 4.17\n\n### Hand fixes after the codemod\n\n- **CJS-loaded configs** (`plugin.spec.ts`,\n`convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`, `configuration-nested.spec.ts`):\n`loadConfigFile` and `getInstalledStorybookVersion` load files with\n`require()`, and `vi.mock`/`vi.doMock` can''t reach that channel. These\nnow use `mockCjsModule`/`resetCjsMocks`. In `plugin.spec.ts` the\n`vi.mock` sat inside a helper, where vitest hoists it and it crashes the\nfile. I checked that the convert-to-inferred mock applies: a bogus\nangular framework in the mock fails all 6 tests.\n- **`@swc/helpers` in the plugin spec''s temp workspace**\n(`plugin.spec.ts`): two tests load real `main.ts` files that `import` a\nbase config. The swc-node hook compiles them with `importHelpers`. A\ntemp root outside the repo can''t resolve\n`@swc/helpers/_/_interop_require_default`, so `loadConfigFile` threw and\nthe plugin skipped the addon. The spec now symlinks the repo''s\n`@swc/helpers` into the temp root. This stays local to the spec, so the\nshared setup is unchanged.\n- **Non-identifier JSON keys** (`utilities.spec.ts`): vite only exposes\nJSON keys that are valid identifiers as named exports. So `import * as x\nfrom ''*.json''` dropped `react-swc` and `nextapp-swc`. The spec now reads\nthrough `default`, the same pattern `configuration.spec.ts` already\nuses.\n- **`%p` in `test.each` titles** (`configuration.spec.ts`): vitest has\nno `%p`. All 20 cases in each block got the same name, so snapshots were\nkeyed by a shared counter. The titles now use `%j`, which renders the\nsame `\"apps/.../.storybook/\"` text jest printed.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\nAll 4 `.snap` files were regenerated from pristine copies. There are 55\nkeys before and after. After normalizing the describe separator, 0\nvalues differ and no keys are missing or extra.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,copy-assets,build-base -p\nstorybook devkit --skip-nx-cache`: green. `devkit` is the still-on-jest\ncanary.\n- `nx sync:check`: up to date.\n- Two more `nx test storybook --skip-nx-cache` runs: 227/227 both times.\nA single-file run (`nx run storybook:test --\nsrc/utils/utilities.spec.ts`) also works.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a613c8e94d5b03c3ce1f2150da2992aa7c5237ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/a613c8e94d5b03c3ce1f2150da2992aa7c5237ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/2cfeb623a8cdc1dab6064fbddaa41293588ac340","verification":{"payload":"tree a613c8e94d5b03c3ce1f2150da2992aa7c5237ef\nparent 484d84dfd94875114ae9ccbb255f99c2f4cf054b\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790352308 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790352308 -0400\n\nchore(storybook): run storybook unit tests with vitest (#37172)\n\nStacked on #37171.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/storybook` unit tests run on Jest\n(`packages/storybook/jest.config.cts`, `jest.preset.js`).\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`@nx/storybook` unit tests run on Vitest, inferred by `@nx/vitest` from\n`packages/storybook/vitest.config.mts`. The config is the same as\n`packages/js` and `packages/react`: the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts`\nand `tools/vitest/nx-source-resolver.mts`, forks pool, 35s timeout.\n`test.inputs` names the shared setup files. `jest.config.cts` is\ndeleted.\n\n| | Jest | Vitest |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tests | 227 (12 files) | 227 (12 files) |\n| `nx test storybook` wall time (median of 3) | 146.6s | 5.3s |\n| Runner-reported time (median of 3) | 145.4s | 4.2s |\n\nTiming method: 3 alternating rounds on the same machine. Jest ran on a\ndetached checkout of the base branch. Vitest ran on this branch. The\ndaemon was on and warmed with two `nx show projects` calls after each\ncheckout. Each run used `nx test storybook --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies`.\n\nRaw numbers (wall / runner):\n- jest: 146.56 / 145.38, 146.59 / 145.46, 146.26 / 145.14\n- vitest: 5.58 / 4.19, 5.25 / 4.20, 5.24 / 4.17\n\n### Hand fixes after the codemod\n\n- **CJS-loaded configs** (`plugin.spec.ts`,\n`convert-to-inferred.spec.ts`, `configuration-nested.spec.ts`):\n`loadConfigFile` and `getInstalledStorybookVersion` load files with\n`require()`, and `vi.mock`/`vi.doMock` can''t reach that channel. These\nnow use `mockCjsModule`/`resetCjsMocks`. In `plugin.spec.ts` the\n`vi.mock` sat inside a helper, where vitest hoists it and it crashes the\nfile. I checked that the convert-to-inferred mock applies: a bogus\nangular framework in the mock fails all 6 tests.\n- **`@swc/helpers` in the plugin spec''s temp workspace**\n(`plugin.spec.ts`): two tests load real `main.ts` files that `import` a\nbase config. The swc-node hook compiles them with `importHelpers`. A\ntemp root outside the repo can''t resolve\n`@swc/helpers/_/_interop_require_default`, so `loadConfigFile` threw and\nthe plugin skipped the addon. The spec now symlinks the repo''s\n`@swc/helpers` into the temp root. This stays local to the spec, so the\nshared setup is unchanged.\n- **Non-identifier JSON keys** (`utilities.spec.ts`): vite only exposes\nJSON keys that are valid identifiers as named exports. So `import * as x\nfrom ''*.json''` dropped `react-swc` and `nextapp-swc`. The spec now reads\nthrough `default`, the same pattern `configuration.spec.ts` already\nuses.\n- **`%p` in `test.each` titles** (`configuration.spec.ts`): vitest has\nno `%p`. All 20 cases in each block got the same name, so snapshots were\nkeyed by a shared counter. The titles now use `%j`, which renders the\nsame `\"apps/.../.storybook/\"` text jest printed.\n\n### Snapshot parity\n\nAll 4 `.snap` files were regenerated from pristine copies. There are 55\nkeys before and after. After normalizing the describe separator, 0\nvalues differ and no keys are missing or extra.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint,copy-assets,build-base -p\nstorybook devkit --skip-nx-cache`: green. `devkit` is the still-on-jest\ncanary.\n- `nx sync:check`: up to date.\n- Two more `nx test storybook --skip-nx-cache` runs: 227/227 both times.\nA single-file run (`nx run storybook:test --\nsrc/utils/utilities.spec.ts`) also works.\n- `tools/vitest/setup.mts` is unchanged.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtpu0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADfoQAC49nR+bFghfhHUXg6RjXZ97\nH9fcgDPnkUvHpoaglH9xFF6hfVg3fk+NtbJAGl4ezvkFoKpnIH06+phQRrJQrFyR\ntsvDPDfz6Mi1jw6IoU5VLP9E8gV3lDG6/MDyJEWbdT2V87degGnAisnTIexM8oi3\nwgYERKOQWMGr6X1WaCNCgmW3pa2docZixppA7Zq9IteHOJVej0eNBBLqjQOQew9Y\nwE9SM1cZPcv/mg3gF3CfFXMWc6cl43aFpS6XFXbkpCa0JwvRyeA8LQ2Ds0JVMIJq\