sts-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtnXhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0SEQABbdUGw9MRpm9nuaGtRx35uQ\n2Sz4V7Do+fpltF4eXgFqfCdCd6gt87QRWx81BxtmrRbwnCh7QXIvoW5caKdCGO5c\nxrgpD4rm0XM/bk2mjZAhILicMqO/0EauvZGJjMWxYLvcMD6zN+dz/1GT1KIUT7Pi\nIx3gUwXP2FMXrj8Wz3yIJFRzyqko8jqMcR8nZG98hCAZMLf6HTc/f22gGg15umhS\nmY3QDMQCzNaszCpVSjQI1HMuNIuoAnzHi0tnnXTBjktKmfSqFfW8Fyj+96xWHa8m\nPXZP5XEggk04DIHHu+HeFxuOTh0Jc2zmSPRPPkvkNJ93PJFIdLUmEX9evvDb8lFX\nN5HwiSvnSwYzMJ+z1Q5PJJKnf6EXFxso8hXBl1wxOO/x6+DKLsz1kA9TB8zaFJ4Q\nUWe9VhJoBFL/IVEmZK/HII57v0MolCDYqQQkHNMX8QPOyeOTesBLNKAgbUKAOXm2\nhCl/2ziWFZ2EHzfvOQJiwNaqnOCRZRqoofBIte1Se0+DDGLaRVy5AfKgMeDcL5hQ\n5uXb4zVehxTX98QrpD4fcXO4S2TMt8/0keLu3jp1LuRhhiVbqSXRQ1icySYHTK14\nyivsSQH+cxpFoRSpys9nx9ce5TREs75JBJgm7hRsjHqWnQWY/Xn6BDWUkosdsBdE\ni74j9OhLIHC2JD5QVSfZ\n=+72Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T13:23:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/9f1046e14c0e9a53ab6e7200d89b900a4b9a6bed","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDlmMTA0NmUxNGMwZTlhNTNhYjZlNzIwMGQ4OWI5MDBhNGI5YTZiZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266","sha":"3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266"}],"sha":"9f1046e14c0e9a53ab6e7200d89b900a4b9a6bed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/9f1046e14c0e9a53ab6e7200d89b900a4b9a6bed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:23:44Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:23:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): run angular and react unit tests with vitest (#37162)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/angular` and `@nx/react` unit tests run on Jest. They are the two\nslowest unit suites in the repo, so `dynamic-changesets.yaml` pins their\n`test` targets to a dedicated `linux-extra-large` agent, one at a time.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run their unit tests on Vitest 4, inferred by `@nx/vitest`\nand loading the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts`. Test counts are\nunchanged, and the dedicated-agent assignment rule is removed, so they\ndistribute like any other task.\n\n| package | tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall time |\nrunner-reported time |\n| ------- | --------------------- | ------------------- |\n-------------------- |\n| react   | 564 → 564 (44 files) | 289.0s → 14.4s | 287.5s → 12.9s |\n| angular | 1528 → 1528 (110 files) | 235.2s → 24.0s | 233.3s → 22.6s |\n\nTimings are medians of 3 rounds of `nx test <pkg> --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies` with a warm Nx daemon, alternating jest and\nvitest within each round, on an 8-core machine with some other load\n(±~20%). Runner time is jest''s `Time` / vitest''s `Duration`.\n\nBeyond the `jest.*` → `vi.*` codemod:\n\n- **Modules the source loads with `require()`** are mocked with\n`mockCjsModule` (from #37157), since `vi.mock` only reaches the ESM\ngraph: `@nx/cypress/internal` in the Cypress component-testing\ngenerators (plus `@nx/devkit` and `readCachedProjectGraph`, which it\nreaches on the CJS channel), `fs` for `nxE2EPreset`, `@nx/eslint` loaded\nthrough `ensurePackage`, and the react-router config that\n`loadConfigFile` requires.\n- **Angular''s `test-setup.ts`** wraps `@angular-devkit`''s\n`readJsonWorkspace` on the CJS channel (the schematics `require` it). It\nimports the `cjs-mock` helper directly rather than the\n`internal-testing-utils` barrel: modules a setup file loads are cached\nbefore a spec''s `vi.mock` applies, and the barrel pulls in\n`nx/src/devkit-internals`, which silently defeated spec mocks of\n`readFileMapCache`.\n- **Shared setup (`tools/vitest/setup.mts`)**:\n- also mocks `ensurePackage` where it is defined. A spec''s own\n`vi.mock(''@nx/devkit'')` (e.g. via `mock-project-graph`) replaces the\nsetup''s mock and spreads the real module, which made `ensurePackage`\ninstall `@nx/oxlint` into a temp dir.\n- the `require` hook maps `./x.js` to `./x.ts` inside `packages/`, so\nESM-style source such as `@nx/oxlint` loads on the CJS channel.\n- Three specs spied on `require(''@nx/devkit'')` while the generator uses\nthe ESM import; they now spy on the ESM namespace.\n- `route-utils.spec.ts` used interpolated `toMatchInlineSnapshot` inside\n`describe.each`, which vitest rejects; those two assertions are now\nexact `toBe` checks against the same strings.\n- `vi.mock` inside a helper function is hoisted by vitest (not by jest),\nso `router-plugin.spec.ts`''s helper now registers its mock with\n`mockCjsModule`.\n- The codemod skipped two string-only migration specs\n(`rewrite-internal-subpath-imports`) whose fixtures contain\n`jest.mock(...)` user code.\n- **Snapshots**: all 18 react and 25 angular `.snap` files are rekeyed\nonly. Every value (133 react, 380 angular) matches the jest originals\nafter normalizing the key separator. 18 react keys from `describe.each`\ntitles changed shape (vitest quotes/truncates interpolated values) and\nwere matched by position. Three SCAM inline snapshots change only from\n`\"msg\"` to `[Error: msg]` (vitest''s `toThrowErrorMatchingInlineSnapshot`\nserializer).\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p angular react workspace\nrspack rsbuild devkit --skip-nx-cache` — green (the shared setup\nchanged, so the earlier vitest packages were re-run; devkit''s 600 jest\ntests as a canary)\n- `nx sync:check` — clean\n- Two further repeat runs of angular + react — green\n- Rebased onto master with `@nx/vitest` 23.3.0-beta.5: `nx show project\nangular` lists `tools/vitest/setup.mts` as an inferred input (nx#36920);\nthe `tools/vitest/**/*` glob stays for the resolver and future helpers,\nand the migration skill says so\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","tree":{"sha":"7d10efc25d0a9f5715b8618de98c45f7921b9e28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/7d10efc25d0a9f5715b8618de98c45f7921b9e28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d10efc25d0a9f5715b8618de98c45f7921b9e28\nparent 396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790342624 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790342624 -0400\n\nchore(repo): run angular and react unit tests with vitest (#37162)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`@nx/angular` and `@nx/react` unit tests run on Jest. They are the two\nslowest unit suites in the repo, so `dynamic-changesets.yaml` pins their\n`test` targets to a dedicated `linux-extra-large` agent, one at a time.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nBoth packages run their unit tests on Vitest 4, inferred by `@nx/vitest`\nand loading the shared `tools/vitest/setup.mts`. Test counts are\nunchanged, and the dedicated-agent assignment rule is removed, so they\ndistribute like any other task.\n\n| package | tests (jest → vitest) | `nx test` wall time |\nrunner-reported time |\n| ------- | --------------------- | ------------------- |\n-------------------- |\n| react   | 564 → 564 (44 files) | 289.0s → 14.4s | 287.5s → 12.9s |\n| angular | 1528 → 1528 (110 files) | 235.2s → 24.0s | 233.3s → 22.6s |\n\nTimings are medians of 3 rounds of `nx test <pkg> --skip-nx-cache\n--excludeTaskDependencies` with a warm Nx daemon, alternating jest and\nvitest within each round, on an 8-core machine with some other load\n(±~20%). Runner time is jest''s `Time` / vitest''s `Duration`.\n\nBeyond the `jest.*` → `vi.*` codemod:\n\n- **Modules the source loads with `require()`** are mocked with\n`mockCjsModule` (from #37157), since `vi.mock` only reaches the ESM\ngraph: `@nx/cypress/internal` in the Cypress component-testing\ngenerators (plus `@nx/devkit` and `readCachedProjectGraph`, which it\nreaches on the CJS channel), `fs` for `nxE2EPreset`, `@nx/eslint` loaded\nthrough `ensurePackage`, and the react-router config that\n`loadConfigFile` requires.\n- **Angular''s `test-setup.ts`** wraps `@angular-devkit`''s\n`readJsonWorkspace` on the CJS channel (the schematics `require` it). It\nimports the `cjs-mock` helper directly rather than the\n`internal-testing-utils` barrel: modules a setup file loads are cached\nbefore a spec''s `vi.mock` applies, and the barrel pulls in\n`nx/src/devkit-internals`, which silently defeated spec mocks of\n`readFileMapCache`.\n- **Shared setup (`tools/vitest/setup.mts`)**:\n- also mocks `ensurePackage` where it is defined. A spec''s own\n`vi.mock(''@nx/devkit'')` (e.g. via `mock-project-graph`) replaces the\nsetup''s mock and spreads the real module, which made `ensurePackage`\ninstall `@nx/oxlint` into a temp dir.\n- the `require` hook maps `./x.js` to `./x.ts` inside `packages/`, so\nESM-style source such as `@nx/oxlint` loads on the CJS channel.\n- Three specs spied on `require(''@nx/devkit'')` while the generator uses\nthe ESM import; they now spy on the ESM namespace.\n- `route-utils.spec.ts` used interpolated `toMatchInlineSnapshot` inside\n`describe.each`, which vitest rejects; those two assertions are now\nexact `toBe` checks against the same strings.\n- `vi.mock` inside a helper function is hoisted by vitest (not by jest),\nso `router-plugin.spec.ts`''s helper now registers its mock with\n`mockCjsModule`.\n- The codemod skipped two string-only migration specs\n(`rewrite-internal-subpath-imports`) whose fixtures contain\n`jest.mock(...)` user code.\n- **Snapshots**: all 18 react and 25 angular `.snap` files are rekeyed\nonly. Every value (133 react, 380 angular) matches the jest originals\nafter normalizing the key separator. 18 react keys from `describe.each`\ntitles changed shape (vitest quotes/truncates interpolated values) and\nwere matched by position. Three SCAM inline snapshots change only from\n`\"msg\"` to `[Error: msg]` (vitest''s `toThrowErrorMatchingInlineSnapshot`\nserializer).\n\n### Verification\n\n- `nx run-many -t test,build,lint,oxlint -p angular react workspace\nrspack rsbuild devkit --skip-nx-cache` — green (the shared setup\nchanged, so the earlier vitest packages were re-run; devkit''s 600 jest\ntests as a canary)\n- `nx sync:check` — clean\n- Two further repeat runs of angular + react — green\n- Rebased onto master with `@nx/vitest` 23.3.0-beta.5: `nx show project\nangular` lists `tools/vitest/setup.mts` as an inferred input (nx#36920);\nthe `tools/vitest/**/*` glob stays for the resolver and future helpers,\nand the migration skill says so\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nN/A\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/Run-rspack-and-rsbuild-unit-tests-with-vitest-4a161f55\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtnXgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqlYQAGvg4Vn+UtKUYDat86M5koEH\n7kWD3oYHG6y56RHwjwsrXPE/ThMAqNBxWTiHlcCF2w8Jn5IM0ZbottgVW3a9cS1g\nN3790o/eWc1Jfpjyl9Q02vDbyoplhVI7aiUNmpC6Bx7E69fUmYbBttSz5yEzosSa\nFonB4KA1CYZ0aOgXU+21T+nEYzG97j2FrW2w9PphKhxXUParYMP6eJ5e+FLJotNn\nD7VDnfQyROuvupVneB0csWy2IhXlqvBxGxKOlVSu+rrB4G8TZRYlXVuMNBa1xScU\njsGfESaHGIj2vGVJxs4DfCt5QrsheOvfHOy8x46YgduDxQ/oiN1ycn6HQhACRnmP\nvhXxV15kg3lA2RpY6lyqbT5P0s/Jg/zlbR2ABqs7+B8q8JmujXOm3Vn+9ITOOe33\nRvkvpiVZ0BcJ30nM26Sm8EPE998r0PBnIM3OAeJ1McuB3rPC9rU/Ug2Pzb32aSVj\nuARYWozXFUTdHKZRr38YquHZLYxxsBllA9DU2l18ZDg6KV4Oi0T1lIlLLUncrO0a\nGpJ96XDWG1eBpbuQI4I0OA0xQ8t+i0GvGOliULGNOnv/XDojvUsh17k0biHwSG9t\nUbreqjC4c9uofnfmFrTjEIH52oEdf9HuzDZMr54yUG1D8oqqBte9DUi1FWuLIZEK\njvRO73om8kKBAYf+HVWk\n=98La\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T13:23:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDNmNmVjY2IxNmRkODVhYzI3OTkyMDEzOTFlYTBiYjE0OTE2NjYyNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0","sha":"396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0"}],"sha":"3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/3f6eccb16dd85ac2799201391ea0bb1491666266"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8104246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/FrozenPandaz","id":8104246,"login":"FrozenPandaz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDQyNDY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FrozenPandaz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T12:37:22Z","email":"jasonjean1993@gmail.com","name":"Jason Jean"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T12:37:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(core): hash tasks from Nx Cloud I/O snapshots (#37036)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nA task''s hash is computed from the inputs its target declares. When\nthose declarations are wider than what the task reads (most\n`default`/`production` filesets), unrelated edits miss the cache; when\nthey are narrower, stale results are served. Nx Cloud already records\nwhat each task actually read and wrote (I/O snapshots), but nx cannot\nuse them.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nSplit out of #36823, after #37017 (continuous-dependency inputs), #37025\n(`includeIgnored`) and #36853 (`sandbox` target configuration).\n\n**Opt-in, CI only.** Off unless a CI run sets `NX_IO_SNAPSHOTS=true` (or\nthe Nx Cloud client''s `NX_CLOUD_USE_IO_SNAPSHOTS=true`) in a workspace\nthat uses Nx Cloud (Cloud config in `nx.json`, or a Cloud token in the\nrun''s env). Outside CI both are ignored, so local runs always hash from\ndeclared inputs. `NX_NO_CLOUD`, `neverConnectToCloud` and `--no-cloud`\nturn it off. Without it, every plan holds the same instructions as\nbefore. One thing still differs: a disk-backed file group of more than 8\nglobs (a large `includeIgnored` input) is named by its count and a\ndigest, and that name orders it in the hash. So a task with two such\ngroups can change its hash once, on upgrading to this version, alongside\nthe misses the upgrade''s own package versions cause. It''s stable from\nthen on.\n\n**Store.** Once per run, nx asks the Nx Cloud client (`readIoSnapshots`)\nfor the snapshot set in effect for HEAD and stores it in the workspace\ndatabase as a version keyed by commit and fetch time: one row for the\nresolution, one row per task for its entry, written in one transaction.\nVersions are never pruned, so a run can always read the one it is pinned\nto: the database is not kept between CI runs, and `nx reset` clears it.\nA recently fetched set for HEAD is served from the database without a\nrequest. When the read fails (offline, unauthorized, bad response, no\nclient), the run hashes natively; it never reuses an older set, and it\nwarns only on `unauthorized`, `invalid-response` and `write-failed`.\nCommit selection, auth and transport live in the Nx Cloud client; nx has\nno HTTP client of its own. The fetch and write always happen in the nx\nprocess, which has the full environment the Nx Cloud client reads\n(`NX_CLOUD_API`, the CI execution id), under a file lock beside the\ndatabase: processes that miss together fetch once, and the rest use the\nset it stored. With the daemon, hash requests carry the set''s version,\nso a run keeps hashing from the set it started with even if the same\ncommit is re-imported mid-run; a set reopened from the database is read\nby task id as the planner asks, so a run costs the tasks it touches\nrather than the workspace''s whole set (a fresh import already holds\nevery entry). Up-front plan reuse keys on the set''s commit and fetch\ntime.\n\n**DTE agents.** Agents run tasks through `runDiscreteTasks` and\n`runContinuousTasks`, which re-hash each task, so they now take an\noptional snapshot set from the caller: its observed outputs join the\ntask outputs and tasks hash from it, as on the main job. nx never\nfetches on this path; without a set it hashes natively. The new\n`nx/nx-cloud-internals` entry point exports two functions for this.\n`importIoSnapshots(commit, snapshots)` stores a set the Nx Cloud client\nread and returns that handle. `openIoSnapshots(commit, fetchedAt)`\nreopens the stored version, so an agent imports once and its workers\nshare the set. The client probes for these two exports to tell whether\nnx hashes from snapshots itself (nrwl/ocean#13236).\n\n**Engine.** A task with an eligible entry hashes the files it actually\nread instead of its declared filesets: one disk-backed group per owning\nproject, each carrying the declared negations every visit of that\nproject shares (natively each visit is its own fileset), plus an\n`io-snapshot:<digest>` marker (the digest of the task''s own observed\noutputs, so snapshot keys never collide with native ones). Only file\ninputs are replaced: declared filesets (`includeIgnored` ones included,\nfrom own, dependency and `{ input, projects }` inputs), and\n`dependentTasksOutputFiles`, whose files count through the recorded\nreads of those outputs. Env, runtime and external-dependency\ninstructions stay, including those a `{ input, projects }` input brings\nin. Reads under `node_modules` are left out (native never hashes them as\nfiles), as are `nx.json`, `.gitignore` and `.nxignore` (the always-on\ninstruction hashes them whole). A lockfile the task read is hashed as a\nfile, since an `externalDependencies` list or an `@nx/*` executor hashes\nonly a few packages. A declared `{json}` file and the root tsconfig are\nhashed whole from the trace, since their native instructions cover only\nselected fields and a stripped tsconfig; those instructions survive only\nif the trace read them. Continuous dependencies are spliced in after the\nreplacement: each from its own eligible entry the same way, with its own\nmarker, or from its declared inputs when it has none. A task that hashes\nnatively (`backfill: false` included) hashes its continuous dependencies\nnatively too.\n\nEligibility is decided in Rust, per task. A task falls back to native\nhashing when it sets `sandbox.enabled: false` or `sandbox.backfill:\nfalse` (read off the task, so agents agree with the main job), its\nexecutor ships a custom hasher, it has no entry, a read would leave the\nworkspace, or a read, negations included, is not a valid files glob. A\ndeclared `includeIgnored` group is still validated, so its error fires\nas it does natively, but not hashed: ignored files the task read hash\nthrough its observed-read group. Reads of another task''s outputs defer\nthe task until those producers ran. Observed writes join the task''s\noutputs before hashing; negations and writes under `node_modules`, `.nx`\nor `.git` are never added.\n\n**Cost.** Measured on this repo (335 tasks) during development: with no\nset, hashing time is unchanged (up-front batch of 146 tasks 44.3 vs 44.6\nms median, a lazy hash 39 ms on both). With a set loaded (47k observed\nreads), the up-front batch takes 93 ms and a lazy hash 34 ms, against 78\nand 36 ms native. The deferral check, eligibility, owner attribution and\nper-task matching are linear in the observed reads, and a large file\ngroup''s hash-details key is a count plus a digest. Loading a set reads\none row plus the entries of the tasks planned: a four-task run against a\n5,000-task, 44 MB set loads in under a millisecond. Importing takes 18\nms for this repo and 360 ms for the 5,000-task set, once per fetch.\n\nDisplay (`nx show`, `nx graph`, the run summary) follows in a separate\nPR.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4858, NXC-4846, NXC-4861\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/NXC-4846-snapshot-resolution-in-Nx-core-618d13d8\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: FrozenPandaz <FrozenPandaz@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e000960534aacd707a50472feb6d93939d6bf02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/7e000960534aacd707a50472feb6d93939d6bf02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e000960534aacd707a50472feb6d93939d6bf02\nparent d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c\nauthor Jason Jean <jasonjean1993@gmail.com> 1790339842 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790339842 -0400\n\nfeat(core): hash tasks from Nx Cloud I/O snapshots (#37036)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nA task''s hash is computed from the inputs its target declares. When\nthose declarations are wider than what the task reads (most\n`default`/`production` filesets), unrelated edits miss the cache; when\nthey are narrower, stale results are served. Nx Cloud already records\nwhat each task actually read and wrote (I/O snapshots), but nx cannot\nuse them.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nSplit out of #36823, after #37017 (continuous-dependency inputs), #37025\n(`includeIgnored`) and #36853 (`sandbox` target configuration).\n\n**Opt-in, CI only.** Off unless a CI run sets `NX_IO_SNAPSHOTS=true` (or\nthe Nx Cloud client''s `NX_CLOUD_USE_IO_SNAPSHOTS=true`) in a workspace\nthat uses Nx Cloud (Cloud config in `nx.json`, or a Cloud token in the\nrun''s env). Outside CI both are ignored, so local runs always hash from\ndeclared inputs. `NX_NO_CLOUD`, `neverConnectToCloud` and `--no-cloud`\nturn it off. Without it, every plan holds the same instructions as\nbefore. One thing still differs: a disk-backed file group of more than 8\nglobs (a large `includeIgnored` input) is named by its count and a\ndigest, and that name orders it in the hash. So a task with two such\ngroups can change its hash once, on upgrading to this version, alongside\nthe misses the upgrade''s own package versions cause. It''s stable from\nthen on.\n\n**Store.** Once per run, nx asks the Nx Cloud client (`readIoSnapshots`)\nfor the snapshot set in effect for HEAD and stores it in the workspace\ndatabase as a version keyed by commit and fetch time: one row for the\nresolution, one row per task for its entry, written in one transaction.\nVersions are never pruned, so a run can always read the one it is pinned\nto: the database is not kept between CI runs, and `nx reset` clears it.\nA recently fetched set for HEAD is served from the database without a\nrequest. When the read fails (offline, unauthorized, bad response, no\nclient), the run hashes natively; it never reuses an older set, and it\nwarns only on `unauthorized`, `invalid-response` and `write-failed`.\nCommit selection, auth and transport live in the Nx Cloud client; nx has\nno HTTP client of its own. The fetch and write always happen in the nx\nprocess, which has the full environment the Nx Cloud client reads\n(`NX_CLOUD_API`, the CI execution id), under a file lock beside the\ndatabase: processes that miss together fetch once, and the rest use the\nset it stored. With the daemon, hash requests carry the set''s version,\nso a run keeps hashing from the set it started with even if the same\ncommit is re-imported mid-run; a set reopened from the database is read\nby task id as the planner asks, so a run costs the tasks it touches\nrather than the workspace''s whole set (a fresh import already holds\nevery entry). Up-front plan reuse keys on the set''s commit and fetch\ntime.\n\n**DTE agents.** Agents run tasks through `runDiscreteTasks` and\n`runContinuousTasks`, which re-hash each task, so they now take an\noptional snapshot set from the caller: its observed outputs join the\ntask outputs and tasks hash from it, as on the main job. nx never\nfetches on this path; without a set it hashes natively. The new\n`nx/nx-cloud-internals` entry point exports two functions for this.\n`importIoSnapshots(commit, snapshots)` stores a set the Nx Cloud client\nread and returns that handle. `openIoSnapshots(commit, fetchedAt)`\nreopens the stored version, so an agent imports once and its workers\nshare the set. The client probes for these two exports to tell whether\nnx hashes from snapshots itself (nrwl/ocean#13236).\n\n**Engine.** A task with an eligible entry hashes the files it actually\nread instead of its declared filesets: one disk-backed group per owning\nproject, each carrying the declared negations every visit of that\nproject shares (natively each visit is its own fileset), plus an\n`io-snapshot:<digest>` marker (the digest of the task''s own observed\noutputs, so snapshot keys never collide with native ones). Only file\ninputs are replaced: declared filesets (`includeIgnored` ones included,\nfrom own, dependency and `{ input, projects }` inputs), and\n`dependentTasksOutputFiles`, whose files count through the recorded\nreads of those outputs. Env, runtime and external-dependency\ninstructions stay, including those a `{ input, projects }` input brings\nin. Reads under `node_modules` are left out (native never hashes them as\nfiles), as are `nx.json`, `.gitignore` and `.nxignore` (the always-on\ninstruction hashes them whole). A lockfile the task read is hashed as a\nfile, since an `externalDependencies` list or an `@nx/*` executor hashes\nonly a few packages. A declared `{json}` file and the root tsconfig are\nhashed whole from the trace, since their native instructions cover only\nselected fields and a stripped tsconfig; those instructions survive only\nif the trace read them. Continuous dependencies are spliced in after the\nreplacement: each from its own eligible entry the same way, with its own\nmarker, or from its declared inputs when it has none. A task that hashes\nnatively (`backfill: false` included) hashes its continuous dependencies\nnatively too.\n\nEligibility is decided in Rust, per task. A task falls back to native\nhashing when it sets `sandbox.enabled: false` or `sandbox.backfill:\nfalse` (read off the task, so agents agree with the main job), its\nexecutor ships a custom hasher, it has no entry, a read would leave the\nworkspace, or a read, negations included, is not a valid files glob. A\ndeclared `includeIgnored` group is still validated, so its error fires\nas it does natively, but not hashed: ignored files the task read hash\nthrough its observed-read group. Reads of another task''s outputs defer\nthe task until those producers ran. Observed writes join the task''s\noutputs before hashing; negations and writes under `node_modules`, `.nx`\nor `.git` are never added.\n\n**Cost.** Measured on this repo (335 tasks) during development: with no\nset, hashing time is unchanged (up-front batch of 146 tasks 44.3 vs 44.6\nms median, a lazy hash 39 ms on both). With a set loaded (47k observed\nreads), the up-front batch takes 93 ms and a lazy hash 34 ms, against 78\nand 36 ms native. The deferral check, eligibility, owner attribution and\nper-task matching are linear in the observed reads, and a large file\ngroup''s hash-details key is a count plus a digest. Loading a set reads\none row plus the entries of the tasks planned: a four-task run against a\n5,000-task, 44 MB set loads in under a millisecond. Importing takes 18\nms for this repo and 360 ms for the 5,000-task set, once per fetch.\n\nDisplay (`nx show`, `nx graph`, the run summary) follows in a separate\nPR.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-4858, NXC-4846, NXC-4861\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/6a061dcb561c062131116eca/sessions/NXC-4846-snapshot-resolution-in-Nx-core-618d13d8\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: FrozenPandaz <FrozenPandaz@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtmsCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlTIQAKm0DYv1+75FhlvKayilj2vn\n2ShwXmSm6s3ed4HXuMNt4JYrrj0gA7yp74oKF001y13Yl9wFk8B9Bh40EGBtPy7q\n1iddUT4IuYrUcwMk7d9ZQobtd4aVBR9JTn9MmDw3VzFfppoa0HqWELca5/CKMclu\nlEYOnEUsWOtrILTANPBRE5S9WaIwOWyeS9KlDu7fenX5Zv/TM/MTOfGSFsLnX+C+\n9Vbfq/OAQoZQWg18SyjEIMscEkx/5IworqdHvcmSkgStKEL1um2FmjOE73enLcja\nrAZpHURX9ncUR0Ac1tvpqUyQvejmBHEAcWqWc7mQ+qoGAfQ7l7YDhykV5Obq+G/S\n9GlGoUETz9+BrBsY/ZiZYN3liAFETJx8rCFCAgIiaiZeP3wd5RGzEPX8JLT2wgJt\nMomrrFXYuQwUDU9Nez1u07o12jIAY4jASVddi1re2YOCqs/XR/2ImzxMMyBwCZIb\nidJWvSscXIaWtx6WkQPjKgA8ZRzt15gGpQS/j7sz1uMfwN9+zGqPmqPvuS+3Rk8V\n8mg6RXddGgxqBBeUFyZJSonh6o5mgtrzlWt0J3PNl36QINe+BuUWXU56on4REytg\ndnjc8M1HzT3Geg0tWWw518X+kqGQ7EsB4/PvCmqBuCP1IOSgEyhAzr/9G2llb3Ah\n0jLhYMpVsqR5URHXAByp\n=WZ+7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T12:37:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKDM5NmRhZWFmMmQyNjU0YjFmNmZkMDUwMmMzMWMyMTc2NDA1YzdhYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c","sha":"d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c"}],"sha":"396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/396daeaf2d2654b1f6fd0502c31c2176405c7ab0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4440385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nixallover","id":4440385,"login":"nixallover","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0NDAzODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nixallover","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:02:55Z","email":"nicole.oliver.42@gmail.com","name":"Nicole Oliver"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:02:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(nx-dev): adopt one UTM convention for Nx Cloud links (#36888)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nThe 34 links from the docs site and nx.dev into the Nx Cloud app tag\nthemselves inconsistently, and two of the four UTM fields carry the\nwrong kind of value:\n\n| Field | Today |\n| --- | --- |\n| `utm_source` | `nx-dev` (24) and `nx-docs` (9) — the same property\nspelled two ways. All of these links live on the docs site or nx.dev,\nbut 22 docs-site links report `nx-dev`. |\n| `utm_medium` | `website` (30), plus `homepage_links`,\n`documentation-header`, `header`. The last three are page positions, not\nchannels. |\n| `utm_campaign` | 28 distinct values, almost all page topics\n(`remote-cache`, `flaky-tasks`, `access-tokens`, …). Because campaign is\neffectively unique per link, it can never roll up — the campaign report\nis just a list of links. |\n| `utm_content` | 1 use. Effectively unused, despite being the field\nintended for exactly the placement data sitting in `campaign`. |\n\nOne CTA — the mobile header button in\n`ui-common/src/lib/headers/header.tsx` — carries no parameters at all,\nso its clicks arrive at Nx Cloud unattributed.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nOne convention across all 34 links, with cardinality rising left to\nright:\n\n| Field | Meaning | Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `utm_source` | originating property | `nx-docs` (31), `nx-dev` (3) |\n| `utm_medium` | unchanged | `website` (34) |\n| `utm_campaign` | intent | `nx-cloud-signup` (31), `nx-cloud-login`,\n`nx-cloud-demo`, `single-tenant` |\n| `utm_content` | placement | 30 values (`docs-header`, `mobile-header`,\n`remote-cache`, …) |\n\n**No granularity is lost.** Placement previously lived in `campaign` on\nthe docs site and in `medium` on nx.dev; both now move to `content`, so\nevery existing distinction survives — it just moves to the field meant\nto hold it. This also corrects the 22 docs-site links that reported\n`utm_source=nx-dev`, and tags the mobile header CTA to sit alongside its\ndesktop twin (`content=mobile-header` vs `content=header`).\n\n`utm_campaign` is derived mechanically from the destination path rather\nthan chosen per link:\n\n```\n/get-started, /setup/connect-workspace/*  -> nx-cloud-signup\n/demo/*                                   -> nx-cloud-demo\n/  (app root, sign-in)                    -> nx-cloud-login\n/powerpack/request/trial                  -> powerpack-trial\n/powerpack/purchase                       -> powerpack-purchase\n```\n\n### On `utm_medium`\n\n`medium` keeps its current value of `website` and is deliberately left\nout of scope here. Strictly, UTM `medium` is the acquisition channel\n(`email`, `cpc`, `paid_social`, …), and a constant `website` duplicates\nwhat `source` already says. Changing it would touch every link a second\ntime for no reporting gain today, so this PR leaves it alone and\nconfines itself to the two fields that are actively broken: `campaign`\nand `content`.\n\nBecause `medium` is unchanged, the 30 docs-site links churn only on\n`source`, `campaign`, and `content`.\n\n### What stays untagged\n\n23 links to Nx Cloud are deliberately left without parameters, because\nthey are navigation for existing customers rather than conversions:\n\n| Destination | Count |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/go/organization/add-ons` | 12 |\n| `/go/workspace/settings/self-healing-ci` | 3 |\n| `/go/organization/{edit,conformance-rules}`, `/go/workspace/settings`\n| 3 |\n| `/orgs` | 1 |\n| `nx.app/privacy`, `cloud.nx.app/privacy` | 2 |\n| release-note references | 2 |\n\nAll of these require an existing Nx Cloud account. Tagging them would\nstart a new session and overwrite the visitor''s original acquisition\nsource for no reporting gain.\n\n### Scope\n\nA pure query-string rewrite: 29 files, every changed line a UTM\nparameter, plus one Markdown table realignment in\n`getting-started/intro.mdoc` where the longer URL widened a column. No\nprose, headings, link text, or page structure changed.\n\n**Deliberately out of scope**, worth follow-ups:\n\n- 7 CLI links in `packages/nx` and `packages/next` still use\n`utm_medium=cli`.\n- The live nx.dev marketing pages have the same problem\n(`medium=header`, `nx-cloud-plans`, `nx-cloud-hero`), plus several\nuntagged CTAs on `/nx-cloud`, `/pricing`, and `/contact`.\n- 19 links use a dotted `utm_source=nx.dev` instead of `nx-dev`. All\npoint at third parties (x.com, GitHub, YouTube, Bluesky) rather than Nx\nCloud, so they are a separate spelling cleanup.\n- No enforcement helper yet. Convention alone is how the current drift\nhappened; a shared URL builder is the durable fix.\n\n### Verification\n\nVerified by parsing the committed files: 34 links, `utm_medium` has\nexactly one distinct value, `utm_campaign` has 4, and no Nx Cloud link\non the docs site retains `utm_source=nx-dev`. (Other non-`website`\nmediums found under `nx-dev/nx-dev/public/documentation` are gitignored\nbuild output, not source.)\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Vale could not be run locally — its binary comes from `mise`, which\ncrashes in this sandbox. The docs style pass was done by hand instead.\nThe only style-guide rules touching this diff are the **Links** section\nand **Line length**; no links were added or removed (a pure\nsubstitution), no URL is broken across a line, and long URL lines are\nexempt under \"Don''t break links across lines.\" CI Vale should be treated\nas the authority.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNo linked issue — internal analytics taxonomy cleanup.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://snapshot.app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/69cdc268b6aa527e4129c2b4/sessions/docs-get-started-dcd55ec4\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc55b75d9d64271efd7958c1bbe4a930bf138296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/bc55b75d9d64271efd7958c1bbe4a930bf138296"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c","verification":{"payload":"tree bc55b75d9d64271efd7958c1bbe4a930bf138296\nparent f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d\nauthor Nicole Oliver <nicole.oliver.42@gmail.com> 1790272975 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790272975 -0700\n\ndocs(nx-dev): adopt one UTM convention for Nx Cloud links (#36888)\n\n