` is derived mechanically from the destination path rather\nthan chosen per link:\n\n```\n/get-started, /setup/connect-workspace/*  -> nx-cloud-signup\n/demo/*                                   -> nx-cloud-demo\n/  (app root, sign-in)                    -> nx-cloud-login\n/powerpack/request/trial                  -> powerpack-trial\n/powerpack/purchase                       -> powerpack-purchase\n```\n\n### On `utm_medium`\n\n`medium` keeps its current value of `website` and is deliberately left\nout of scope here. Strictly, UTM `medium` is the acquisition channel\n(`email`, `cpc`, `paid_social`, …), and a constant `website` duplicates\nwhat `source` already says. Changing it would touch every link a second\ntime for no reporting gain today, so this PR leaves it alone and\nconfines itself to the two fields that are actively broken: `campaign`\nand `content`.\n\nBecause `medium` is unchanged, the 30 docs-site links churn only on\n`source`, `campaign`, and `content`.\n\n### What stays untagged\n\n23 links to Nx Cloud are deliberately left without parameters, because\nthey are navigation for existing customers rather than conversions:\n\n| Destination | Count |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/go/organization/add-ons` | 12 |\n| `/go/workspace/settings/self-healing-ci` | 3 |\n| `/go/organization/{edit,conformance-rules}`, `/go/workspace/settings`\n| 3 |\n| `/orgs` | 1 |\n| `nx.app/privacy`, `cloud.nx.app/privacy` | 2 |\n| release-note references | 2 |\n\nAll of these require an existing Nx Cloud account. Tagging them would\nstart a new session and overwrite the visitor''s original acquisition\nsource for no reporting gain.\n\n### Scope\n\nA pure query-string rewrite: 29 files, every changed line a UTM\nparameter, plus one Markdown table realignment in\n`getting-started/intro.mdoc` where the longer URL widened a column. No\nprose, headings, link text, or page structure changed.\n\n**Deliberately out of scope**, worth follow-ups:\n\n- 7 CLI links in `packages/nx` and `packages/next` still use\n`utm_medium=cli`.\n- The live nx.dev marketing pages have the same problem\n(`medium=header`, `nx-cloud-plans`, `nx-cloud-hero`), plus several\nuntagged CTAs on `/nx-cloud`, `/pricing`, and `/contact`.\n- 19 links use a dotted `utm_source=nx.dev` instead of `nx-dev`. All\npoint at third parties (x.com, GitHub, YouTube, Bluesky) rather than Nx\nCloud, so they are a separate spelling cleanup.\n- No enforcement helper yet. Convention alone is how the current drift\nhappened; a shared URL builder is the durable fix.\n\n### Verification\n\nVerified by parsing the committed files: 34 links, `utm_medium` has\nexactly one distinct value, `utm_campaign` has 4, and no Nx Cloud link\non the docs site retains `utm_source=nx-dev`. (Other non-`website`\nmediums found under `nx-dev/nx-dev/public/documentation` are gitignored\nbuild output, not source.)\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Vale could not be run locally — its binary comes from `mise`, which\ncrashes in this sandbox. The docs style pass was done by hand instead.\nThe only style-guide rules touching this diff are the **Links** section\nand **Line length**; no links were added or removed (a pure\nsubstitution), no URL is broken across a line, and long URL lines are\nexempt under \"Don''t break links across lines.\" CI Vale should be treated\nas the authority.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNo linked issue — internal analytics taxonomy cleanup.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- polygraph-session-start -->\n---\n<p><a\nhref=\"https://snapshot.app.trypolygraph.com/orgs/69cdc268b6aa527e4129c2b4/sessions/docs-get-started-dcd55ec4\">View\nPolygraph session ↗</a></p>\n<!-- polygraph-session-end -->\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtWXPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG4oQAEh1mzgrAt0rtn1tRse+KRwT\nT3+cVXDwo9TxIp9tfaV82cwshfrxGmRRf0AvU7d/BagRtvIf68qNwSNJE1sLIoj7\nRjDzWZXve+CDPYUzxHaK88m7oUnjX2ZWsO+b/WQ6/e8GrjaJF3ghmUXRjMW1521h\nlsJ4Vh7qu1E/hDulTpObbn1Ar1Ap2zLguhngHzRDcer9iZlvswEXGwyX2QvUgI1a\neuVMiKSI8OC6jE5OR9bD82yY/zG2Aul6mto5U+Ljren4kTxOTG4NcXALXP9/sv49\nnTbtxXBfPJ1yXRndMVvijMGpCCiwLeUXGczFQfLP5hXv/uQy7Wyq+7sqrTl05laR\nK8ylFvpa2LuL35YDMMd0RknafZLJqSJ7S5u4sD4A+aILkQmavK3tjkJJoLo6jOr7\n3x/1QlHxZCc7pNfYr+CJZ79b5+iFVx35ypjwMGfgbDTR4MnP6U0m3RqMEbPTdzJD\nfqVViMrQe3HezggS45gDiHdbRsFEm2X1mb3sgjqs+OVhiT6HrnFDTNgyORXwjxdL\nUmMcB4U1zMqWX6hpHw0MHEMDzrlQMKoyw4dUc47nkEbZbIXqT0ztTOXGInhs06vY\nZH17tSNUEnqjj/05GbdUXfrclaXVuV99WLUy3+aazlhGfk0s/LY20zvjwH/+rKnd\nZTQ0s9sqHVqbdKGFwbpH\n=EHHr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:02:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNoAKGQ1YWJkMDc5YjdkMTgzOTg4NmJlNDBjMGMyNWZmMDZkZGE1OTBiMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d","sha":"f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d"}],"sha":"d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/d5abd079b7d1839886be40c0c25ff06dda590b0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12051310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leosvelperez","id":12051310,"login":"leosvelperez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDUxMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leosvelperez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/commits/f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T17:50:43Z","email":"leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com","name":"Leosvel Pérez Espinosa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T17:50:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): narrow workspace glob searches to literal directory prefixes (#37126)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWorkspace glob queries and directory listings copy and scan every\nworkspace file, even when searching inside one project. Jest and\nPlaywright repeat this work to discover tests for inferred CI targets\nduring graph construction.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nRead only the relevant directory range from the existing ordered file\nmap. For example, a Jest search under `e2e/react/` examines that\nproject''s files rather than every workspace file.\n\n- Reuse `partition_glob` after glob conversion, so the prefix follows\nthe patterns the matcher receives.\n- Cache the prefix with its matcher and reuse both throughout the query,\navoiding repeated calculation and lookup.\n- Share `get_child_files` across globbing, directory listings, hashing,\nand deletion to avoid duplicate directory traversal logic.\n\nThe original matcher determines results and exclusions. Broad or\nambiguous patterns retain the full scan, preserving matching semantics,\norder, duplicates, and watcher/archive freshness.\n\n### File discovery\n\nBenchmarks compare master `47c1a2212e61` with these production changes:\noptimized native builds, Apple M2 Max, 96 GiB RAM, macOS arm64, Node\n26.7.0. Each comparison uses seven alternating before/after pairs;\noutputs matched and no samples were discarded. Before/after values are\nmedian timings. Changes summarize the differences measured within each\npaired run.\n\nEach row times the first execution of all listed calls from one plugin\nworker against an initialized file index. Configuration loading,\nstartup, and initial indexing are excluded.\n\n| File discovery during graph construction | Before | After | Median\npaired saving |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Nx: Jest searches in 32 projects | 65.35 ms | 5.46 ms | 59.93 ms\n(91.6%) |\n| Nx: Jest searches in another 3 projects | 6.30 ms | 0.70 ms | 5.60 ms\n(88.8%) |\n| Nx: 2 Playwright directory listings | 3.44 ms | 0.08 ms | 3.35 ms\n(97.8%) |\n| 317-project workspace: 3 Jest searches | 8.15 ms | 0.78 ms | 7.35 ms\n(90.5%) |\n| 317-project workspace: 2 Playwright directory listings | 4.70 ms |\n0.15 ms | 4.55 ms (96.8%) |\n\nAll seven pairs improved. These discovery timings cover part of plugin\nexecution; worker savings are not additive.\n\n### Complete graph construction\n\nThese timings measure the graph API in fresh Node processes with the\ndaemon disabled. Cold means empty Nx caches.\n\n| Cold graph construction | Before | After | Median paired change |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Nx, 150 projects | 7,320.5 ms | 7,111.7 ms | 208.9 ms faster (2.85%);\nimproved in 6/7 pairs |\n| 317-project workspace | 8,676.9 ms | 8,721.3 ms | 115.0 ms slower\n(1.33%); inconclusive |\n| 636-project workspace, no scoped discovery | 2,045.8 ms | 2,029.8 ms |\n28.1 ms faster (1.37%); inconclusive |\n\nThe other workspaces'' paired runs went in both directions, with\ndifferences reaching hundreds of milliseconds. That makes run-to-run\nnoise a plausible explanation for the small median graph differences.\nWhen no search can be narrowed, the same files are scanned; the measured\nadditional work is negligible at graph scale: 0.067 ms for Nx''s 37\nmatcher constructions, 0.638 ms for the first 636-root fallback query,\nand less than 1 ms in other broad/configuration controls. Those median\ncosts do not explain a 115 ms graph slowdown on their own, so we expect\nlittle graph-time change where no searches benefit from narrowing.\n\nWarm and edited graph results were mixed: cached graphs skip most Jest\ndiscovery, and other plugins can dominate graph time. These results\nsupport faster scoped discovery, without a general graph-speed or\ntask-hashing claim.\n\nMatcher-construction controls added 0.05-0.16 MiB of process memory\ngrowth after garbage collection.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5031\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b720b8fab006a4bea8aba736a579454f8bc98e3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/trees/b720b8fab006a4bea8aba736a579454f8bc98e3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nrwl/nx/git/commits/f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d","verification":{"payload":"tree b720b8fab006a4bea8aba736a579454f8bc98e3d\nparent 6c0f1996cc9c460ef8e159201bcf594b27581403\nauthor Leosvel Pérez Espinosa <leosvel.perez.espinosa@gmail.com> 1790272243 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790272243 -0400\n\nfix(core): narrow workspace glob searches to literal directory prefixes (#37126)\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nWorkspace glob queries and directory listings copy and scan every\nworkspace file, even when searching inside one project. Jest and\nPlaywright repeat this work to discover tests for inferred CI targets\nduring graph construction.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nRead only the relevant directory range from the existing ordered file\nmap. For example, a Jest search under `e2e/react/` examines that\nproject''s files rather than every workspace file.\n\n- Reuse `partition_glob` after glob conversion, so the prefix follows\nthe patterns the matcher receives.\n- Cache the prefix with its matcher and reuse both throughout the query,\navoiding repeated calculation and lookup.\n- Share `get_child_files` across globbing, directory listings, hashing,\nand deletion to avoid duplicate directory traversal logic.\n\nThe original matcher determines results and exclusions. Broad or\nambiguous patterns retain the full scan, preserving matching semantics,\norder, duplicates, and watcher/archive freshness.\n\n### File discovery\n\nBenchmarks compare master `47c1a2212e61` with these production changes:\noptimized native builds, Apple M2 Max, 96 GiB RAM, macOS arm64, Node\n26.7.0. Each comparison uses seven alternating before/after pairs;\noutputs matched and no samples were discarded. Before/after values are\nmedian timings. Changes summarize the differences measured within each\npaired run.\n\nEach row times the first execution of all listed calls from one plugin\nworker against an initialized file index. Configuration loading,\nstartup, and initial indexing are excluded.\n\n| File discovery during graph construction | Before | After | Median\npaired saving |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Nx: Jest searches in 32 projects | 65.35 ms | 5.46 ms | 59.93 ms\n(91.6%) |\n| Nx: Jest searches in another 3 projects | 6.30 ms | 0.70 ms | 5.60 ms\n(88.8%) |\n| Nx: 2 Playwright directory listings | 3.44 ms | 0.08 ms | 3.35 ms\n(97.8%) |\n| 317-project workspace: 3 Jest searches | 8.15 ms | 0.78 ms | 7.35 ms\n(90.5%) |\n| 317-project workspace: 2 Playwright directory listings | 4.70 ms |\n0.15 ms | 4.55 ms (96.8%) |\n\nAll seven pairs improved. These discovery timings cover part of plugin\nexecution; worker savings are not additive.\n\n### Complete graph construction\n\nThese timings measure the graph API in fresh Node processes with the\ndaemon disabled. Cold means empty Nx caches.\n\n| Cold graph construction | Before | After | Median paired change |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Nx, 150 projects | 7,320.5 ms | 7,111.7 ms | 208.9 ms faster (2.85%);\nimproved in 6/7 pairs |\n| 317-project workspace | 8,676.9 ms | 8,721.3 ms | 115.0 ms slower\n(1.33%); inconclusive |\n| 636-project workspace, no scoped discovery | 2,045.8 ms | 2,029.8 ms |\n28.1 ms faster (1.37%); inconclusive |\n\nThe other workspaces'' paired runs went in both directions, with\ndifferences reaching hundreds of milliseconds. That makes run-to-run\nnoise a plausible explanation for the small median graph differences.\nWhen no search can be narrowed, the same files are scanned; the measured\nadditional work is negligible at graph scale: 0.067 ms for Nx''s 37\nmatcher constructions, 0.638 ms for the first 636-root fallback query,\nand less than 1 ms in other broad/configuration controls. Those median\ncosts do not explain a 115 ms graph slowdown on their own, so we expect\nlittle graph-time change where no searches benefit from narrowing.\n\nWarm and edited graph results were mixed: cached graphs skip most Jest\ndiscovery, and other plugins can dominate graph time. These results\nsupport faster scoped discovery, without a general graph-speed or\ntask-hashing claim.\n\nMatcher-construction controls added 0.05-0.16 MiB of process memory\ngrowth after garbage collection.\n\n## Related Issue(s)\n\nNXC-5031\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: nx-cloud[bot] <71083854+nx-cloud[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtWLzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAncEQAHJ+ARhtJ2d/B0JeANXFy8Bl\n+xc7C9hvD+nB0TMUNjmEwZQKQOpcg84nriN4AJYKelkumQkIR6ttWI7z8uVWzBM+\nYdqIMGg3TqJnFyp80z63tB39miNkDinESddNb2FCwh5BukadA4NjTXHKPRdTT1qq\n1ZIJ8f0P8nMdJG18W/DeM+s+KQYjMxGWLAajdfzw3lZzGXQLNiWqo9qQEcjcgQr0\nuJF//EuVoLA1GpKeLJFoj707uoAdhNmA8qkO6UCmyO4tE5GZbWJXlfhLsu78gIvO\ngD8/lNeg8XwE2jAllvsJpxLBl1uJC4TFRVEzl6+fCsjLuezyknffLXpexyzqj4uH\npyqegzvbdChy/zbpaCvr/bXJ2YvJbQXQfrfuCHx3urTAzMVfxCFHbQc1/imikJil\nNLWIR8wD4D8o0oJaSkoHYdkfCRaECFQxQuqQY6nidf8HS5u2wTJm+5EU3aqHZDy4\nx929c5VI7jrHqTuIQEWVpRFyF737gYxCRR5GdHeVXGF8Uht8F9odxoUrGISqHbLJ\n6oiLOew8B1w0K/iH6RpB9Y7gpp95xRzBYV526M+dBAbyBqsYrgRMPSTUO2ngtf2D\npZ/hRsFmTWjDimbWbz888FckLJMzG1gXXsTRg6VqCjFezW96du6p7x8jzOc3Aahp\nSc99mIzmeDefaARpp/Wf\n=/k5E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T17:50:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nrwl/nx/commit/f10a66f737cd5a89a5ec6dc634f4c78b9843617d","node_id":"C_kwDOBfbSFNo